#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_1.tres
msgid "A Small Hunt"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_1.tres
msgid ""
"Ever since the Shattering, the cats of the shards have had to adapt to the new environment. The transition was surprisingly easy, especially for the strays, who were already used to foraging for food.\n"
"\n"
"The settlers notice one such cat standing motionless by the water's edge, waiting for just the right moment to pounce on a toad, who is blissfully unaware of the mortal danger it is in."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_1.tres
msgid "Learn patience from the cat."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_1.tres
msgid ""
"A monk among the settlers launches into a sermon illustrating the value of patience on the path to enlightenment.\n"
"\n"
"Before he can get a few words out, the cat makes a half-hearted swipe at the toad, misses entirely, and immediately begins grooming its paw with intense focus. It projects an air of absolute certainty that it meant to do exactly that."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_1.tres
msgid "Save the toad."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_1.tres
msgid ""
"A settler yells out, trying to alert the toad, and succeeds in scaring both animals.\n"
"\n"
"The toad quickly disappears into the water.\n"
"\n"
"The cat, once recovered from a momentary panic, shoots the settlers a profound look of disapproval and slowly walks away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_1.tres
msgid "Help the cat catch the toad."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_1.tres
msgid ""
"A settler approaches the toad, hoping to block its path of retreat.\n"
"\n"
"Instead, the toad is alerted by the movement and leaps off the rock, quickly disappearing into the water.\n"
"\n"
"The cat shoots the settlers a profound look of disapproval before slowly walking away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_1.tres
msgid "Leave the animals alone."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#. Property: goals[]
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_1.tres
#: quests/companion/quest_companion_cat.tres
msgid "Observe a cat hunting."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_1.tres
msgid "The cat is pleased to be left undisturbed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_1.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers look on as the cat finally makes its move.\n"
"\n"
"Despite its lightning-fast swipe, the toad manages to escape. The cat looks sheepish for just a moment, before immediately beginning to groom its paw with intense focus. It projects an air of absolute certainty that it meant to do exactly that."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_2.tres
msgid "Market Cats"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_2.tres
msgid ""
"The market's roofs have become a home for many stray cats. They started showing up out of the wilderness one by one, and by now every stall has its own stall cat.\n"
"\n"
"The merchants consider the cats to be good luck charms, spirits blessing their businesses. As such, whenever cats from competing shops squabble, everyone watches with bated breath; the winning cat is thought to bring great luck to the business it patronizes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_2.tres
msgid "Declare the luckiest cat the town's patron spirit."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_2.tres
msgid ""
"The mayor declares that the luckiest cat is to be the town's patron spirit.\n"
"\n"
"As a result, traders start baiting the cats into fights, each eager to be associated with the town mascot.\n"
"\n"
"Folks begin putting wagers on the fights. Some traders begin to file their cats' claws, or even dress them in armor.\n"
"\n"
"The competition continues to escalate until finally, the local monks decide that a line has been crossed, and usher all the cats back to the wilderness."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_2.tres
msgid "Mandate compensation for the cats."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_2.tres
msgid "Get the cats fed"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_2.tres
msgid "The cats feel pampered and appreciative."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_2.tres
msgid ""
"The town council declares that the cats must be compensated for their blessings with at least two meals per day.\n"
"\n"
"The merchants grumble but acquiesce, afraid of losing patronage.\n"
"\n"
"Soon the cats grow plump and lazy, and the fights gradually dwindle."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_2.tres
msgid "Merge stalls to pool the blessings."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_2.tres
msgid ""
"An enterprising merchant comes up with an idea: if two stalls are merged, they will have two cats, and therefore double the blessings.\n"
"\n"
"At first she has trouble convincing the others, but after the first merged stall ends up with a monopoly on sake sales, the rest of the merchants catch on, planting the seeds of a cartel economy in the shard's future."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_2.tres
msgid "Ask scholars to explain the symbolism."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_2.tres
msgid ""
"Scholars are called to study the cats' blessings. They consult old books and come back with an explanation.\n"
"\n"
"They claim that the cats are fighting over territory and food, not to bestow divine economic favor.\n"
"\n"
"Most merchants refuse to believe this, but the excitement surrounding the fights soon fades, and few people pay attention to it anymore."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_3.tres
msgid "The Windowsill Cat"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_3.tres
msgid ""
"A grumpy-looking stray tomcat has been regularly showing up at the farmhouse.\n"
"\n"
"Every day at dusk he climbs up to the second floor, slips in through the open window, and makes himself comfortable on the windowsill. He spends the evening relaxed, looking over the fields with his eyes half-closed.\n"
"\n"
"The farmers haven't tried approaching the cat yet, wary of his grumpy looks, and he hasn't tried approaching anyone either."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_3.tres
msgid "Pet the cat."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_3.tres
msgid ""
"One of the farmers tries to approach the cat.\n"
"\n"
"The cat gets up, gives the approaching farmer a judging look, shakes his paw, and jumps out of the window, never to be seen again."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_3.tres
msgid "Put down a blanket on the windowsill."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_3.tres
msgid "Adopt a cat"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_3.tres
msgid "The cat decided to live at the farmhouse from now on."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_3.tres
msgid ""
"The farmers wait for the cat to depart that night, and the next day put down a warm blanket on the windowsill.\n"
"\n"
"When the cat shows up, he seems taken aback for a moment, but soon settles in as usual.\n"
"\n"
"Later that night, a farmer finds the cat fast asleep on the blanket."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_3.tres
msgid "Keep the shutters closed in the future."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_3.tres
msgid ""
"The farmers shoo the cat away and keep the second floor shutters closed from now on.\n"
"\n"
"The cat shows up a few more times, but finding no way in, eventually moves on."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_3.tres
msgid "Leave the cat alone."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/cat/event_companion_cat_3.tres
msgid ""
"The farmers decide that the cat isn't ready for an introduction yet.\n"
"\n"
"They keep ignoring him, and one day he stops showing up."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_1.tres
msgid "A Noisy Flock"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_1.tres
msgid ""
"The sky above the beach is filled with cranes, crossing the sea to their feeding grounds.\n"
"\n"
"The massive flock is incredibly loud, their constant calls echoing off the rocks all day.\n"
"\n"
"The villagers are rubbing their temples and debating how to reclaim their peace and quiet."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_1.tres
msgid "Use smoke to drive them away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_1.tres
msgid ""
"The villagers pile damp seaweed onto fire pits to create clouds of thick smoke that fill the beach.\n"
"\n"
"The tactic works, and the birds adjust their route to avoid the noxious hazard.\n"
"\n"
"However, the wind blows the smoke directly back into the village, leaving everyone's eyes watering."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_1.tres
msgid "Fly kites shaped like large birds of prey."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_1.tres
msgid ""
"The craftspeople quickly assemble kites painted with fierce eyes and sharp beaks.\n"
"\n"
"The false predators easily spook the cranes into avoiding the area."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_1.tres
msgid "Declare the bird calls to be voices of spirits."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_1.tres
msgid ""
"Instead of fighting the flock, the priests declare the sudden arrival to be an auspicious sign.\n"
"\n"
"They call on the locals to appease the spirits by folding intricate paper cranes, and leaving them as offerings at the shrine.\n"
"\n"
"The real birds remain just as loud, but the villagers find the noise much more tolerable now that it is considered holy."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_1.tres
msgid "Make a lot of noise to scare them off."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_1.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers grab pots, pans, and wooden spoons, marching down to the beach to create a terrible racket.\n"
"\n"
"The cranes are offended by the commotion and eventually fly away.\n"
"\n"
"The villagers win the battle for the beach, but end up with even worse headaches than they started with."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_2.tres
msgid "Sibling Rivalry"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_2.tres
msgid ""
"Deep in the wildlife sanctuary, a forester has been observing a crane nest in an old pine.\n"
"\n"
"Two chicks have hatched, but they fight relentlessly. The forester notes that the parent crane seems to favor the stronger chick, offering it most of the food.\n"
"\n"
"It is a harsh reality of nature, but the forester is determined to see both of the fuzzy little creatures survive the season."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_2.tres
msgid "Swap the two chicks regularly."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_2.tres
msgid "Save a crane chick"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_2.tres
msgid "A crane chick is saved."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_2.tres
msgid ""
"The forester sets up a warm, padded basket at the base of the tree. Whenever the parent leaves to forage, she climbs up and swaps the bullied chick for the rested one.\n"
"\n"
"It is exhausting, precarious work, but she prevents the sibling fights, and manages to trick the parent into feeding both chicks equally until they are old enough to fend for themselves."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_2.tres
msgid "Take the weaker chick and raise it."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_2.tres
msgid ""
"Accepting that the two chicks will not cease fighting on their own, the forester carefully removes the weaker chick.\n"
"\n"
"She keeps it in a warm, padded basket and nurtures it carefully.\n"
"\n"
"The chick clearly thinks the forester is a strange, large bird, but it imprints on her completely and survives to fly off within a few months."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_2.tres
msgid "Regularly leave rice in the nest."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_2.tres
msgid ""
"The forester pours portions of rice into the nest every day, hoping the extra food will keep both chicks full.\n"
"\n"
"Unfortunately, this diet proves inadequate for the hatchlings, and neither survives the season."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_2.tres
msgid "Let nature take its course."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_2.tres
msgid ""
"The forester sighs and steps back, deciding it is not her place to interfere with the wild.\n"
"\n"
"Nature is highly efficient, but not always kind.\n"
"\n"
"The stronger chick thrives under the undivided attention of its parent, while the weaker one soon perishes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_3.tres
msgid "The Crane Dance"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_3.tres
msgid ""
"A lone crane has been standing perfectly still in a shallow pool by the rice paddy all day.\n"
"\n"
"The bird refuses to hunt or move, looking like a slender statue rising from the water. The farmers are beginning to find its endless patience a bit eerie.\n"
"\n"
"Just before dusk, a second crane glides down from the sky, and the two immediately spring to life. They bow to one another, spread their wings, and begin a complex, leaping dance."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_3.tres
msgid "Play the flute to accompany the dance."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_3.tres
msgid ""
"Moved by the display, a well-meaning farmer pulls a bamboo flute from his belt and plays a trilling melody.\n"
"\n"
"The sharp noise spooks the birds and they instantly take flight."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_3.tres
msgid "Choreograph a dance based on their movements."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_3.tres
msgid "Learn from the cranes"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_3.tres
msgid "The settlers have learned from the cranes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_3.tres
msgid ""
"The farmers watch the deep bows and elegant leaps in quiet awe, trying to memorize the pattern.\n"
"\n"
"They adapt the birds' motions into a graceful dance, which becomes a frequent sight during wedding ceremonies."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_3.tres
msgid "Stand back and enjoy the show."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_3.tres
msgid ""
"The farmers lean on their tools, wiping the sweat from their brows, and watch.\n"
"\n"
"It is a rare moment of pure elegance in an otherwise muddy, backbreaking workday.\n"
"\n"
"They find the dedication of the mating pair inspiring."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_3.tres
msgid "Give them some privacy."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/crane/event_companion_crane_3.tres
msgid ""
"The farmers decide that it is rude to stare at a private reunion.\n"
"\n"
"They gather their tools and move to the other side of the paddy to finish their chores.\n"
"\n"
"The elegant dancers are soon gone, and the episode is quickly forgotten."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_1.tres
msgid "Deer Incursion"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_1.tres
msgid ""
"The fruit trees hang heavy with pears and plums. So heavy, in fact, that some have fallen on the ground and attracted deer from the nearby forest. The fruit pickers are now constantly accosted by hungry deer asking for sweet treats.\n"
"\n"
"They have long stopped being skittish, and have all but claimed the grove as their home. The fruit pickers are getting more annoyed by the day."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_1.tres
msgid "Let the deer stay, but withhold the fruit."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_1.tres
msgid ""
"The deer eventually learn that the only fruit they're getting is what they can find on the ground.\n"
"\n"
"They still visit the grove regularly, but they eventually stop pestering the workers."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_1.tres
msgid "Share the fruit willingly."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_1.tres
msgid ""
"The deer are encouraged by the easily obtained food, and continue to frequent the grove.\n"
"\n"
"Now that the fruit has become their main diet, who knows how they'll fare when the harvest season passes..."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_1.tres
msgid "Build fences around the grove."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_1.tres
msgid ""
"Simple bamboo fences are built, surrounding the grove.\n"
"\n"
"At first the deterrent seems to work, but soon the deer learn to simply leap over them, and the pestering persists."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_1.tres
msgid "Gently shoo the deer out of the grove."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_1.tres
msgid ""
"The deer flee into the woods.\n"
"\n"
"Work resumes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_2.tres
msgid "Boundaries"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_2.tres
msgid ""
"Each evening a pair of deer approach the watchpost and stand looking at the settlers going about their tasks. They never cross into the town proper, although a leap could easily carry them across the simple bamboo fences.\n"
"\n"
"Several townspeople find the behavior odd, perhaps even eerie, and have complained to the guards, asking them to keep wildlife away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_2.tres
msgid "Remove the fences entirely."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_2.tres
msgid "Welcome the deer into the town"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_2.tres
msgid "The deer feel welcomed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_2.tres
msgid ""
"The fence is taken down.\n"
"\n"
"For a while, the deer continue to stay by the watchpost, but eventually they grow more confident and start roaming the streets.\n"
"\n"
"A few townspeople grumble, but most find the new neighbors charming."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_2.tres
msgid "Raise the fence to block the view."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_2.tres
msgid ""
"The fence is rebuilt, taller and harder to see through.\n"
"\n"
"The deer eventually stop coming, but more importantly, the new fence keeps the more dangerous wildlife away as well."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_2.tres
msgid "Place a feeding trough outside the watchpost."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_2.tres
msgid ""
"A trough is placed by the wall and the guards refill it with leftovers once in a while.\n"
"\n"
"The deer still come every night, but rather than staring at the settlers, they eat and leave."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_2.tres
msgid "Do nothing and let things be."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_3.tres
msgid "Deer at the Shrine"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_3.tres
msgid ""
"The hermit maintaining the shrine has noticed deer regularly wandering out of the forest to graze nearby. He is sure that these are no ordinary animals, but spirits staking a claim on the area.\n"
"\n"
"Perhaps the shrine could be dedicated to them, or their interest could be acknowledged with offerings."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_3.tres
msgid "Leave offerings of incense."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_3.tres
msgid ""
"The hermit visits the local town to trade most of his supplies for incense, and leaves bowls of it slowly smoldering by the shrine.\n"
"\n"
"The deer vanish the very next day, driven away by the strong scent."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_3.tres
msgid "Let the deer roam undisturbed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_3.tres
msgid "The deer feel comfortable."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_3.tres
msgid ""
"The shrine remains untouched, and the deer continue their visits.\n"
"\n"
"One particularly friendly deer starts sleeping on the hermit's porch."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_3.tres
msgid "Carve the shrine in the shape of the deer."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/deer/event_companion_deer_3.tres
msgid ""
"The hermit works long hours to reshape the stone. The result may not be a masterpiece, but no one could mistake it for anything but a deer.\n"
"\n"
"Once the locals learn of the new deer shrine, many visit to pay their respects.\n"
"\n"
"Ironically, all the activity ends up driving the deer back into the forest."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_1.tres
msgid "Lumber Yard Assistant"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_1.tres
msgid ""
"One of the woodworkers has inherited an old dog from her father, who has become her constant companion.\n"
"\n"
"In its younger days, the dog helped drag logs to the lumber yard, and carry planks to the storage shed, but now it's too old to do such hard labor. Still, it insists on following the woodworker around.\n"
"\n"
"The woman has to decide how to deal with the mild annoyance of a dog always getting in the way."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_1.tres
msgid "Leave it at home."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_1.tres
msgid ""
"The dog is locked inside all day while the woman is working.\n"
"\n"
"Neighbors report hearing quiet whining coming from the house all day, only punctuated by the occasional mournful howl."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_1.tres
msgid "Set it to guard the lumber yard."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_1.tres
msgid ""
"The woman asks the dog to stand guard outside of the lumber yard, showering it with praise at the end of each day.\n"
"\n"
"The dog seems excited to remain useful despite its advanced age."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_1.tres
msgid "Teach it to pull a saw."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_1.tres
msgid ""
"The woman spends several days trying to train the dog in the art of sawing.\n"
"\n"
"The dog listens politely, wags its tail, but completely fails to follow the instructions.\n"
"\n"
"Most of the time it gets bored and ends up falling asleep on a pile of logs."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_1.tres
msgid "Give the dog away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_1.tres
msgid ""
"The woman decides that she is no longer able to take care of an elderly dog, given her busy job.\n"
"\n"
"The dog is rehomed to a nice family on the other side of the settlement.\n"
"\n"
"It looks on mournfully as the woman walks away for the last time."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_2.tres
msgid "Sleeping Rough"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_2.tres
msgid ""
"The night guards have stumbled upon an old man sleeping on the street, huddled beneath a frayed straw mat with a sorry-looking dog.\n"
"\n"
"They offer to let him sleep in the common dining hall, but they refuse to let the dog in, citing very strict rules about muddy paws and fleas.\n"
"\n"
"The man sits up, shivering, and looks between the warm glow of the hall and the steadfast animal at his side."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_2.tres
msgid "Leave the dog outside the hall."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_2.tres
msgid ""
"The man takes the offer, leaving the dog by the entrance.\n"
"\n"
"The hearth is warm, and the floor is dry, but the man barely sleeps.\n"
"\n"
"Every time the wind howls, he looks toward the door, wondering how his friend is doing.\n"
"\n"
"By dawn the guilt overwhelms him and he takes off, with the dog walking alongside."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_2.tres
msgid "Refuse the offer."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_2.tres
msgid "Remain loyal to the dog"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_2.tres
msgid "The dog appreciates the loyalty."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_2.tres
msgid ""
"The man shakes his head and pulls the straw mat a little higher over the dog.\n"
"\n"
"The guards sigh, muttering about stubborn fools, and walk away.\n"
"\n"
"The street is cold, but as the man curls tighter around the dog, the chill seems to lose its bite."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_2.tres
msgid "Accept then sneak the dog in."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_2.tres
msgid ""
"The man agrees, but the moment the guards walk away, he ushers the dog inside.\n"
"\n"
"The plan works perfectly until the dog spots a dropped rice cake under a table and makes a dive for it, upending a bench in the process.\n"
"\n"
"The guards promptly return, alarmed by the clatter, and the man ends up back on the street."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_2.tres
msgid "Let the dog go."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_2.tres
msgid ""
"Deciding the street is no place for a loyal beast, the man stands up, points toward the edge of town, and firmly tells the dog to leave.\n"
"\n"
"The dog whines, confused, but eventually trots away into the dark, looking back over its shoulder."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_3.tres
msgid "A Panicked Dog"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_3.tres
msgid ""
"The town council chairman is organizing the records when his dog companion, usually a calm and friendly creature, suddenly becomes agitated.\n"
"\n"
"It barks loudly and keeps tugging at his robe, trying to drag him outside.\n"
"\n"
"Nothing the man does seems to calm the dog, and it is becoming more and more aggressive."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_3.tres
msgid "Distract the dog with food."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_3.tres
msgid ""
"The chairman pours some beans into the dog's bowl. The dog hesitates, but then lets go of the robe.\n"
"\n"
"A moment later, the ground heaves as a mild earthquake rattles the hall.\n"
"\n"
"Both the man and the dog manage to scramble under a heavy desk, but end up with a few scrapes and bruises."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_3.tres
msgid "Lock the dog in another room until it calms down."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_3.tres
msgid ""
"Deciding that the dog may be rabid, the chairman locks the animal in a sturdy storeroom.\n"
"\n"
"A moment later, the ground shakes.\n"
"\n"
"The chairman barely stumbles out of the hall before the ceiling caves in.\n"
"\n"
"The dog is less fortunate."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_3.tres
msgid "Follow the dog outside."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_3.tres
msgid ""
"The chairman decides to trust the animal's sudden urgency over his own common sense.\n"
"\n"
"He lets the dog drag him out of the building, just as the ground starts shaking.\n"
"\n"
"They watch from a safe distance as the roof of the hall buckles and promptly caves in."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_3.tres
msgid "Shout loudly to scare the dog away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/dog/event_companion_dog_3.tres
msgid ""
"The chairman loses his patience, waving his arms and shouting for the dog to get out.\n"
"\n"
"Startled, the animal lets go of the robe and bolts out the door.\n"
"\n"
"A moment later, the ground shakes and the roof starts to buckle.\n"
"\n"
"The chairman scrambles outside, but not before a falling timber catches him on the shoulder."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_1.tres
msgid "Curious Stones"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_1.tres
msgid ""
"A few of the monks from the Ember Monastery opt for the long trek up the mountain to visit this cave, located just below the tip of the volcano.\n"
"\n"
"The cave is too hot to get very far in, but they do come upon a curious find: flat stones that shine with an iridescent gleam in the torchlight."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_1.tres
msgid "Preserve these as relics at the monastery."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_1.tres
msgid ""
"The stones are carried back to the monastery.\n"
"\n"
"There they are placed on pedestals, and the whole area is sectioned off with sacred ropes.\n"
"\n"
"Visitors are not allowed to approach, and nosy scholars are particularly cautioned to stay away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_1.tres
msgid "Study the stones, even if it damages them."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_1.tres
msgid "A dragon scale has been identified."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_1.tres
msgid ""
"The monks study the rocks carefully back at the monastery.\n"
"\n"
"They chip away crusted-on sediment and wipe off the remaining dust with coarse brushes. Finally, they soak them in vinegar and rinse them in water.\n"
"\n"
"Once so cleaned, the shape and luster of the stones become unmistakable. These are clearly the scales of a very large creature. \"Dragonscales,\" the monks declare."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_1.tres
msgid "Make the stones into rosaries."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_1.tres
msgid ""
"The stones are cleaned and polished smooth. Holes are drilled into them, and the resulting beads are strung onto strings, which the monks who had explored the cave now carry.\n"
"\n"
"Visitors to the monastery often comment on the beauty of the rosaries, which are unlike anything seen anywhere else on the shard."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_1.tres
msgid "Leave the stones in the cave."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_1.tres
msgid "The monks leave the stones in the cave and start their trek back down the slopes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_2.tres
msgid "The Writing on the Wall"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_2.tres
msgid ""
"The Ember monks come across a cave not far from their monastery, strikingly similar to one seen by Ember monks from another shard. It is clearly not a natural formation, the walls too smooth and the entrance too carefully carved.\n"
"\n"
"The other cave of this kind was too hot to explore, but this one is further away from the tip of the volcano, and therefore much cooler. There are, however, faint rumblings coming from within."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_2.tres
msgid "Explore deeper into the cave."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_2.tres
msgid "Discover the dragon's message"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_2.tres
msgid "Words of warning have been translated."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_2.tres
msgid ""
"The monks descend deep into the shafts. As they explore, they find messages on the wall, carved neatly, almost like placards. The script is old, from long before the Shattering.\n"
"\n"
"It takes days to interpret the glyphs, and the monks have to fill in the gaps, but the tale they tell is familiar. They speak of the pillars of the earth turning unstable, of poison rising from the ground when the heart of the mountain is pierced. They caution not to ignore the signs, and promise the end of days for those who let greed disturb the balance of nature.\n"
"\n"
"The monks adopt this wisdom into their teachings, and thank the dragon spirit for its wise counsel."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_2.tres
msgid "Listen to the rumblings."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_2.tres
msgid ""
"The monks set a watch, taking turns to listen to the sounds coming from within the cave.\n"
"\n"
"Soon they notice a pattern. Whenever a particularly loud rumble is heard, it is soon followed by a small eruption from the volcano.\n"
"\n"
"From now on, they are able to predict these, and decide when an evacuation is in order."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_2.tres
msgid "Leave an offering to appease whoever's inside."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_2.tres
msgid ""
"Unwilling to disturb whoever dwells within the cave, the monks leave offerings of grain and incense at the entrance. Occasionally these disappear during the night.\n"
"\n"
"Although the mysterious inhabitant remains elusive, the monks are proud to have a patron spirit."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_2.tres
msgid "Stay safely away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_2.tres
msgid "The monks decide to prioritize safety and leave the cave alone. Pilgrims occasionally wander close, but the monks never allow them to enter, fearful of dangers that may lie within."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_3.tres
msgid "A Vision of the Dragon"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_3.tres
msgid ""
"The Ember monks come upon what has become a famous sight. A cave entrance carved into the side of the volcano. Such caves have been found on many other shards, and have long been revered as the abodes of dragons.\n"
"\n"
"This particular cave is filled with a foul-smelling miasma."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_3.tres
msgid "Explore the cave despite the miasma."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_3.tres
msgid "Communed with the dragon spirit."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_3.tres
msgid ""
"The monks venture into the cave, braving the miasma. After hours of waiting, their fellows suspect the worst and mount a rescue mission.\n"
"\n"
"They find the original explorers passed out, and quickly drag them out into fresh air. When the monks finally awaken, they share their story, punctuated by violent coughing fits.\n"
"\n"
"Soon after they entered the cave, they felt a divine presence. A sense of peace bloomed in their mind, and the dragon spirit appeared to them. It commended them on their courage, and spoke of the Enlightened One's commandments. If the world is to be restored, it said, the people must make an accord with nature, a vow to keep the balance and honor the spirits of the earth."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_3.tres
msgid "Try to clear the air with bellows."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_3.tres
msgid ""
"The monks return back to the settlement and bring back with them many sets of bellows.\n"
"\n"
"They work for hours pumping the miasma out, but the moment they stop, the cave immediately starts filling back up with bad air.\n"
"\n"
"After a day of attempts, they give up and decide to leave the cave unexplored."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_3.tres
msgid "Cleanse the miasma with fire."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_3.tres
msgid ""
"The monks ignite torches and throw them into the cave.\n"
"\n"
"The results are immediate. A jet of flame erupts from the cave, blowing the hapless monks away.\n"
"\n"
"Thankfully everyone survives, but they wisely conclude that the dragon must not appreciate such forceful attempts to enter its abode."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_3.tres
msgid "Retreat to safety."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/dragon/event_companion_dragon_3.tres
msgid "The monks leave the cave exploration for another day, hoping that the miasma will have cleared by then."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#. Property: text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_1.tres
#: events/system/scenes/event_scene.tscn
msgid "A Spooked Fox"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_1.tres
msgid ""
"A group of settlers walking at night by the river hear a rustle in the reeds. They follow it to the source, and discover a lone fox, hesitating at the edge of the river.\n"
"\n"
"The fox seems to have been too engrossed in its hunt to notice them approaching, and is now surrounded by villagers who are just as surprised as it is."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_1.tres
msgid "Pretend to look away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_1.tres
msgid ""
"The villagers turn around and start slowly walking away.\n"
"\n"
"The fox visibly relaxes, gives the river one last look, then follows the people for a while, before disappearing into the night."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_1.tres
msgid "Try to pet the fox."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_1.tres
msgid ""
"The villagers approach the fox from all directions, causing it to panic, clawing at the intruders.\n"
"\n"
"It manages to escape in the commotion, but not without leaving a nasty scratch on one of the villagers' arms."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_1.tres
msgid "Toss food at the fox."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_1.tres
msgid ""
"One of the villagers tosses a rice ball in the fox's direction, but that only startles it further.\n"
"\n"
"Before anyone can react, the fox bolts away into the reeds, never to be seen again."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_1.tres
msgid "Stand very still."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_1.tres
msgid ""
"After a prolonged staring contest, the fox decides that there's no escape for it but to jump into the river.\n"
"\n"
"Luckily, the current is gentle here, by the bank, so after a moment of struggle the fox relaxes and drifts downstream, eventually jumping out at the next bend, soaked and annoyed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_2.tres
msgid "A Fox Pointer"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_2.tres
msgid ""
"Rumors spread about foxes appearing at night by the riverside. Townspeople suspect they have a burrow nearby, but the more interesting rumors claim that these foxes are spirits, guarding the trees.\n"
"\n"
"One night, someone notices a group of foxes gathered under a willow. They seem to be plotting something, and one of them appears to be pointing towards the stream with its paw."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_2.tres
msgid "Send a scouting team in the pointed direction."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_2.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers consider the fox's pointing a sign from the Enlightened One.\n"
"\n"
"Early the next morning, a group of settlers gathers bags of rations, crosses the river, and takes off in the pointed direction.\n"
"\n"
"Days later they return empty-handed, having failed to find anything of note."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_2.tres
msgid "Build a bridge over the spot the fox is pointing to."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_2.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers consider the fox's pointing a sign from the Enlightened One.\n"
"\n"
"Early the next morning they gather their tools and start building a new bridge over the exact spot that the fox was pointing at.\n"
"\n"
"Once finished, the bridge will surely make the river safer to cross, but all the construction noises end up driving the foxes away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_2.tres
msgid "Approach the foxes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_2.tres
msgid ""
"The foxes have other ideas. It seems that they consider the humans a danger to their home, so most of them snarl and stand their ground.\n"
"\n"
"As the settlers get closer, though, they scatter. The fox which was pointing is noticeably limping."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_2.tres
msgid "Stay hidden and observe the foxes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_2.tres
msgid "Get a fox to trust humans"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_2.tres
msgid "Some foxes begin to see people as potential allies."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_2.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers hide behind the willows, away from the foxes, and observe.\n"
"\n"
"By midnight, most of the foxes depart, but the one who was pointing remains sitting. Soon the reason becomes apparent. There's a large splinter stuck in the fox's front paw, and it is trying to get it out, unsuccessfully.\n"
"\n"
"It's too tired and hurt to run away when one of the settlers approaches, so after a minor struggle, the splinter is removed and the fox hobbles away, presumably grateful."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_3.tres
msgid "Guarding the Granaries"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_3.tres
msgid ""
"Settlers have been hearing rustling outside the granaries at night, though they are yet to notice anything missing.\n"
"\n"
"One evening, a patrol spots a group of foxes running up the road on the outskirts of the settlement. The guards suspect they are the ones responsible for the noise around the granaries."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_3.tres
msgid "Build lanterns to keep the road lit."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_3.tres
msgid ""
"The guards decide to let the foxes go this time, and instead invest in a long-term deterrent.\n"
"\n"
"They hire masons to erect stone lanterns along the path, lit every night. The foxes no longer show up, and the granaries remain quiet. Some townsfolk whisper that their spirits must have been appeased."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_3.tres
msgid "Set up baited traps."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_3.tres
msgid ""
"The guards decide to let the foxes go this time, and instead invest in a long-term deterrent.\n"
"\n"
"Simple traps are set around the granaries and the path leading up the settlement.\n"
"\n"
"The very next night, all the traps are sprung, the food is gone, but the foxes are nowhere to be found.\n"
"\n"
"Food starts to go missing from the granaries."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_3.tres
msgid "Stalk them from a distance."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_3.tres
msgid "The foxes have gained a new food source."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_3.tres
msgid ""
"The guards follow the foxes, keeping their distance.\n"
"\n"
"Once the foxes reach the settlement, they make a beeline for the granary. The guards wait patiently, and eventually spot the foxes running back into the marshes, carrying rats in their mouths."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_3.tres
msgid "Chase them."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/fox/event_companion_fox_3.tres
msgid "The guards rush at the foxes, but the beasts are far too fast, quickly scattering into the wilderness."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_1.tres
msgid "Riverside Sorrow"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_1.tres
msgid ""
"A local poet has become fascinated by a frog living on the riverbank. Every day, he stands by the river and watches it jumping up towards the willow branches. The frog misses every time, splashing back into the water with a dull plop.\n"
"\n"
"He has come to believe that the frog is a reincarnation of his late wife, who would often sit by this very willow, playing her koto."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_1.tres
msgid "Write a poem about the frog."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_1.tres
msgid "The man is inspired by the frog."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_1.tres
msgid ""
"The man decides to focus on the amphibian itself, rather than his lost love. He thinks for a moment, then writes:\n"
"\n"
"The river flowing\n"
"The willow is still weeping\n"
"Missed once again\n"
"\n"
"He chuckles at the pun, inspired by the frog's unbothered cycle. The creature doesn't seem to care that it keeps missing.\n"
"\n"
"He walks home, head filled with puns to incorporate into his future poems."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_1.tres
msgid "Write a poem about the wife."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_1.tres
msgid ""
"The man embraces his grief, dedicating a poem to his wife's memory:\n"
"\n"
"The koto's sound\n"
"had soothed the willow's weeping\n"
"Now it is silent\n"
"\n"
"Tears well in his eyes, the verse only deepening his sorrow.\n"
"\n"
"He remains by the riverbank, lost in his memories, as the frog splashes into the water once more."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_1.tres
msgid "Marry the frog."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_1.tres
msgid ""
"The local priest is taken aback by the man's request. Still, he eventually agrees, hoping the ritual will help the poet move on from his sorrow.\n"
"\n"
"It does not. The man treats the ceremony with absolute solemnity, and as the days pass, his grip on reality slips further and further."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_1.tres
msgid "Try to move on."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_1.tres
msgid ""
"The man's friends gently but firmly tell him that his wife is gone, and getting obsessed with a frog will not bring her back.\n"
"\n"
"He bristles at their bluntness. To him, their practical advice just proves that no one understands the depth of his loss.\n"
"\n"
"He turns his back on friendship, isolating himself further in his grief."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_2.tres
msgid "Nothing Goes to Waste"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_2.tres
msgid ""
"The lotus plantation has become home to a large number of frogs. Every other leaf seems to harbor a tiny amphibian.\n"
"\n"
"One of the artisans notices a frog molting. Rather than discarding an empty husk, the frog pulls the skin off its limbs and stuffs it right back into its mouth."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_2.tres
msgid "Study the behavior."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_2.tres
msgid "Learn from the frog"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_2.tres
msgid "The artisans learn from the frog."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_2.tres
msgid ""
"The artisan fixes her eyes on the frog, unwilling to let irrational disgust rule her behavior.\n"
"\n"
"As she sees the creature avoiding waste to such an extent, she contemplates her work. To weave a single thread of lotus silk, they break hundreds of stems, discarding a huge amount of plant matter.\n"
"\n"
"She resolves to find a use for the byproducts of her craft."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_2.tres
msgid "Rid the pond of these unclean creatures."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_2.tres
msgid ""
"The artisan calls her fellow workers and describes the foul scene she witnessed.\n"
"\n"
"With some effort, they are convinced that the foul creatures cannot be allowed to remain.\n"
"\n"
"Instead of following the regular work schedule, they spend the next day wading through the pond and shooing away every frog that can be found."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_2.tres
msgid "Let the creature finish its meal in peace."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_2.tres
msgid "The artisan shrugs at the odd behavior and moves on, letting nature take its course."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_2.tres
msgid "Look away in mild disgust."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_2.tres
msgid ""
"The artisan cringes and looks away.\n"
"\n"
"The image stays in her mind, though. She wakes up at night from a nightmare of eating a bowl of noodles and realizing that she is slurping up moist, sticky frog skin."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_3.tres
msgid "A Grim Feast"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_3.tres
msgid ""
"By the side of the trail is a murky pond teeming with tadpoles. One of the tadpoles floats lifelessly on the surface.\n"
"\n"
"A nearby frog suddenly lashes out its tongue, snaps up the dead tadpole, and swallows it whole.\n"
"\n"
"The settlers are horrified by this act of cannibalism."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_3.tres
msgid "Explain it as practical animal behavior."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_3.tres
msgid "Some settlers gain an appreciation for natural cycles."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_3.tres
msgid ""
"A scholar explains that animals do not follow human sensibilities, and in nature, a dead tadpole would just go to waste.\n"
"\n"
"Rather than accuse the frog of cannibalism, she commends it for making the best use of its resources.\n"
"\n"
"The settlers nod, but few are truly convinced."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_3.tres
msgid "Identify the frog as an evil spirit."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_3.tres
msgid ""
"A priest is quick to resolve the confusion. This frog, he explains, is nothing but an evil spirit.\n"
"\n"
"He throws a handful of mud towards the animal, and it quickly hops away, disappearing into the reeds.\n"
"\n"
"The monster thus banished, the settlers breathe a sigh of relief."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_3.tres
msgid "Rescue the remaining tadpoles."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_3.tres
msgid ""
"Horrified by the cannibalism, a few settlers scoop up the living tadpoles into a bucket and relocate them to a pond on the other side of the path.\n"
"\n"
"It makes them feel good to have rescued the helpless victims."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_3.tres
msgid "Chase the frog away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/frog/event_companion_frog_3.tres
msgid ""
"A settler throws a handful of mud towards the animal, appalled by its behavior, but it quickly hops away, disappearing into the reeds.\n"
"\n"
"Saved from confronting the bizarre behavior, the settlers breathe a sigh of relief."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_1.tres
msgid "Caught in the Hemp"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_1.tres
msgid ""
"When the laborers come to collect the processed hemp, they find several of the bundles tangled together. Something appears to be caught in them, though it's hard to tell what.\n"
"\n"
"It would take a while to untangle the foul-smelling bundles, and the retters are loath to brave the stench for that long."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_1.tres
msgid "Drag all the hemp out before untangling it."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_1.tres
msgid ""
"The workers drag all the hemp onto dry land, and leave it to dry out.\n"
"\n"
"In the evening, the tangled bundles are unraveled to reveal a carp that had gotten caught in the long strands. Unfortunately, it is too late to save the fish."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_1.tres
msgid "Try to untangle the bundles in the water."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_1.tres
msgid "The carp was saved."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_1.tres
msgid ""
"One of the workers ties several layers of cloth around their face and wades into the water.\n"
"\n"
"It is hard work, but eventually the bundles are untangled, releasing a carp that was stuck between them, who eagerly swims away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_1.tres
msgid "Cut the bundles apart."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_1.tres
msgid ""
"An impatient retter takes a large knife and hacks at the bundles, which quickly unravel.\n"
"\n"
"Whatever had gotten caught in the hemp remains a mystery."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_1.tres
msgid "Leave the tangled bundles alone."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_1.tres
msgid ""
"The tangled bundles are left in the water, and eventually disappear into the lakebed.\n"
"\n"
"Whatever had gotten caught in the hemp remains a mystery."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_2.tres
msgid "Swimming Past the Boats"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_2.tres
msgid ""
"Folks crossing the pontoon bridge notice a carp trying to swim upstream past them. Since the boats are tied together so tightly, the carp is unable to get through.\n"
"\n"
"For some reason the stubborn fish hasn't realized that it can swim under the boats, and instead keeps ramming them, trying to get them to move out of its way."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_2.tres
msgid "Untie the boats to let the carp through."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_2.tres
msgid "Let the carp through"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_2.tres
msgid "The carp continues its journey."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_2.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers untie one of the boats to make a gap for the carp to get through.\n"
"\n"
"This works, and the carp safely passes the bridge, continuing its journey upstream.\n"
"\n"
"However, the action comes at a cost. Before the settlers are able to tie the boats back together, the river pushes them apart, the two sections quickly ending up on opposing banks. Although no one is hurt, it takes considerable effort to put the bridge back together."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_2.tres
msgid "Catch the carp and move it over."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_2.tres
msgid "It takes the settlers some time to catch the slippery fish, but once they do, it is quickly transported to the other side, and continues its journey upstream."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_2.tres
msgid "Throw some rice into the water."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_2.tres
msgid ""
"The carp is distracted by the rice, and starts eating.\n"
"\n"
"By the time it's full, it decides to abandon its quest and turns back downstream."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_2.tres
msgid "Leave the carp alone."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_2.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers laugh and keep walking.\n"
"\n"
"The fish continues its struggle."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_3.tres
msgid "Braving the Waterfall"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_3.tres
msgid ""
"Settlers having a picnic by the bottom of the cliff notice a curious scene. A carp has somehow gotten stuck in the little pool at the foot of the waterfall, and is desperately trying to swim up the torrent.\n"
"\n"
"The poor fish keeps jumping out into the falling stream only to plop back down into the water. It swims in a circle for a moment, then repeats its attempt. At one point it somehow ends up on a higher ledge, only to be immediately washed back down."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_3.tres
msgid "Grab the fish and throw it up the waterfall."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_3.tres
msgid ""
"One of the settlers grabs the carp and hurls it upwards, hoping to help it along.\n"
"\n"
"Things do not go as planned. The fish hits a ledge, bounces back, and falls into a crack in the cliff wall. Efforts to get it out end in failure."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_3.tres
msgid "Keep the fish away from the waterfall."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_3.tres
msgid ""
"A child picks up a rice ball and uses it to lure the fish to the edge of the pond.\n"
"\n"
"Every time the fish swims back, the child repeats her tactic.\n"
"\n"
"Eventually the carp learns to associate food with staying away from the stream. It will probably be safe for now, but its dream is left forgotten."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_3.tres
msgid "Draw the scene."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_3.tres
msgid "The carp's dream remains alive."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_3.tres
msgid ""
"One of the settlers picks up a piece of charcoal and draws the carp, capturing its perseverance.\n"
"\n"
"This memento is sure to inspire the settlers to continue on their challenging journey."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_3.tres
msgid "Leave the fish to its attempts."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/koi/event_companion_koi_3.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers don't interfere.\n"
"\n"
"The carp continues its endless struggle."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_1.tres
msgid "A Simian Omen"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_1.tres
msgid ""
"The island shrine is a popular spot for visitors, who arrive regularly to leave offerings and enjoy the breeze.\n"
"\n"
"Recently, a troop of monkeys has claimed the temple porch. One particularly vocal macaque has climbed a wooden pillar. It is shrieking and pointing frantically at a platter of fruit left as an offering on the altar.\n"
"\n"
"The priests are stroking their chins and debating the theological implications of the monkey's behavior."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_1.tres
msgid "Consider the offering inauspicious."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_1.tres
msgid ""
"The head priest concludes that the monkey is a divine messenger, sent to warn them that the fruit is impure.\n"
"\n"
"The priests carefully dispose of the offering and begin a lengthy purification ritual.\n"
"\n"
"The monkey watches them throw the fruit away, deeply disappointed in human intelligence."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_1.tres
msgid "Give the fruit to the yelling monkey."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_1.tres
msgid "The monkeys are fed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_1.tres
msgid ""
"A settler walks up to the altar, grabs a pear, and tosses it to the monkey.\n"
"\n"
"The monkey catches the fruit, lets out a happy chirp, and begins to gnaw on it.\n"
"\n"
"The priests look mildly annoyed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_1.tres
msgid "Dedicate the shrine to the monkey spirits."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_1.tres
msgid ""
"The priests decide to name the monkeys the shrine's patron deities.\n"
"\n"
"They begin pampering the animals, presenting them with elaborate offerings and sweet treats.\n"
"\n"
"The monkeys grow progressively bolder. Soon they are stealing hats and throwing pinecones at the visitors, forcing the priests to start turning pilgrims away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_1.tres
msgid "Ignore the monkeys."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_1.tres
msgid ""
"The priests decide to ignore the distraction.\n"
"\n"
"The monkeys, offended by the lack of attention, escalate the tantrum.\n"
"\n"
"Before anyone can stop them, they grab several holy scrolls and an incense burner, and scatter them all around the courtyards before fleeing into the canopy."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_2.tres
msgid "The Moon Reflected"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_2.tres
msgid ""
"The evening air around the hot springs is thick with steam. A few settlers are relaxing by the water, watching a monkey hanging precariously from a low branch.\n"
"\n"
"The creature is stretching its long arm downward, desperately trying to grab the bright reflection of the moon on the still surface of the pool."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_2.tres
msgid "Discuss the illusory nature of ambition."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_2.tres
msgid ""
"A scholar seizes the moment to deliver an impromptu lecture.\n"
"\n"
"\"Behold,\" he announces to the bathers, \"a perfect metaphor for human craving. We reach for illusions, grasping...\"\n"
"\n"
"His speech is cut short when the monkey loses its grip and plummets into the spring, splashing water all over the scholar's robes and eliciting a few stifled chuckles from his audience."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_2.tres
msgid "Splash water at the monkey."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_2.tres
msgid "Amuse the monkey"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_2.tres
msgid "The monkey is amused."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_2.tres
msgid ""
"A playful settler scoops up a handful of water and splashes the monkey.\n"
"\n"
"The animal reaches into the water and splashes it right back at the settlers.\n"
"\n"
"A chaotic water fight breaks out, leaving everyone soaked and laughing."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_2.tres
msgid "Give the monkey a mirror."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_2.tres
msgid ""
"A settler fetches a hand mirror and angles it to reflect the moon directly into the monkey's face.\n"
"\n"
"The monkey promptly snatches the mirror.\n"
"\n"
"It spends the next hour completely mesmerized, tilting it this way and that and occasionally trying to bite its own reflection."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_2.tres
msgid "Throw a pebble to shatter the image."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_2.tres
msgid ""
"Annoyed by the distraction, a settler tosses a pebble into the center of the reflection, shattering the moon into a dozen ripples.\n"
"\n"
"The monkey chitters in annoyance and retreats high into the canopy."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_3.tres
msgid "A Wrestling Match"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_3.tres
msgid ""
"Several settlers are enjoying a picnic on the riverbank under the blooming cherry trees.\n"
"\n"
"The peaceful atmosphere is abruptly interrupted when two monkeys tumble out of the bushes, locked in a wrestling match.\n"
"\n"
"They roll around on the petals, tugging at each other's ears and kicking up dirt right next to the picnic blankets."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_3.tres
msgid "Break up the fight."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_3.tres
msgid ""
"A stern settler steps forward and tries to pull the animals apart.\n"
"\n"
"The monkeys immediately stop fighting each other, and turn their attention to the human instead.\n"
"\n"
"The settler spends the rest of the picnic running up and down the riverbank, relentlessly chased by two little angry macaques."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_3.tres
msgid "Take bets on the winner."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_3.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers gather around, cheering and placing wagers on which monkey will pin the other.\n"
"\n"
"Just as the bets are finalized, a large butterfly flutters over the grass.\n"
"\n"
"Both monkeys stop, release their grips, and chase the insect back into the bushes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_3.tres
msgid "Study their grappling techniques."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_3.tres
msgid ""
"A local monk observes the brawl with intense focus, praising the animals' fluid movements and calling on the picnickers to learn from their natural technique.\n"
"\n"
"Once the monkeys notice a strange man pointing at them, they seem to take offense and charge at him.\n"
"\n"
"The monk spends the rest of the picnic running up and down the riverbank, relentlessly chased by two little angry macaques."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_3.tres
msgid "Start wrestling too."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_3.tres
msgid "The settlers have join in with the monkeys' antics."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/monkey/event_companion_monkey_3.tres
msgid ""
"Deciding to join in on the fun, two young settlers drop to the grass and begin their own exaggerated, comical wrestling match.\n"
"\n"
"The onlookers burst into laughter, distracting the monkeys, who are instantly interested and promptly sit down to join the audience in watching the show."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_1.tres
msgid "The Gourd Guardian"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_1.tres
msgid ""
"A part of the kudzu plantation has been sectioned off for growing bottle gourds. This morning, a crowd gathers around one of the trellises to gawk at an uninvited visitor.\n"
"\n"
"A large snake is curling around one of the bamboo poles, hissing whenever anyone approaches. It seems to be guarding a large unripe gourd, hanging heavy from the vines.\n"
"\n"
"The villagers are nervous and want the creature gone immediately."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_1.tres
msgid "Use a mirror to scare the snake with a bright beam."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_1.tres
msgid ""
"An inventive woman among the crowd takes out a mirror and uses it to reflect the sunlight right into the snake's eyes.\n"
"\n"
"The snake startles, uncoils, and flees deeper into the field, clearly unhappy."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_1.tres
msgid "Knock the snake off with a pole."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_1.tres
msgid ""
"Before the farmers can intervene, one of the townsfolk detaches a bamboo pole from the trellis and nudges the snake with it until it drops into the grass and slithers away.\n"
"\n"
"The crowd is satisfied, but the farm has lost a pest controller."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_1.tres
msgid "Snatch the gourd."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_1.tres
msgid ""
"Deciding to save the harvest from the creature, a bold onlooker reaches for the gourd.\n"
"\n"
"The snake strikes faster than the eye can follow, and the brave settler is left with a painful bite. At least he's lucky that this snake isn't venomous.\n"
"\n"
"The crowd learns its lesson and quickly disperses."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_1.tres
msgid "Keep away from the snake."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_1.tres
msgid "The dangerous situation is safely resolved."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_1.tres
msgid ""
"The farmers convince the crowd to let the snake be.\n"
"\n"
"The gourds are still unripe, they reason, and by the time harvest comes, the snake will have left.\n"
"\n"
"The crowd remains afraid, but eventually disperses, deciding to let the farmers be responsible for the problem."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_2.tres
msgid "The Warm Fruit"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_2.tres
msgid ""
"A merchant has left several of his prized melons out on his market stand during his midday break, only to come back to a sleek little snake curling around them.\n"
"\n"
"It seems the snake has found the warm fruit inviting and decided to take a nap. It awakens when the merchant approaches, and stares up at him, unwilling to part with its claimed spot."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_2.tres
msgid "Leave the snake undisturbed until dusk."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_2.tres
msgid "Retrieve the snake's treasure safely"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_2.tres
msgid "The snake's treasure is retrieved safely."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_2.tres
msgid ""
"The merchant decides to wait until the sun sets, hoping that the snake will leave once the melons cool down.\n"
"\n"
"The plan succeeds, and by the time the market closes and he checks on the melons again, the snake is nowhere to be seen.\t"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_2.tres
msgid "Lure the snake away with a hot stone."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_2.tres
msgid ""
"The merchant picks up a large, hot stone from the ground and sets it in front of the snake.\n"
"\n"
"It only takes a few minutes before the snake gives up the melons, sensing the greater warmth, and lazily transfers itself to the rock."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_2.tres
msgid "Offer the snake as a free bonus with melon purchase."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_2.tres
msgid ""
"The merchant puts up a sign advertising a new bargain: one free snake with every two melons purchased, while supplies last.\n"
"\n"
"To his surprise, no one takes him up on the offer, but it does cause a buzz among the marketgoers."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_2.tres
msgid "Tip the stand over."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_2.tres
msgid ""
"Lacking any patience, the merchant kicks the stand, tipping it over.\n"
"\n"
"The snake slithers away unharmed, if annoyed, but the melons hit the stones with a splat and shatter into a pile of wet debris."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_3.tres
msgid "A Guarded Treasure"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_3.tres
msgid ""
"While exploring the dusty halls of the ruined outpost, the settlers find a room filled with remarkably preserved furniture, decorated with gold and jeweled inlays.\n"
"\n"
"Just as they are about to collect all this treasure, a massive snake slithers out from behind a painted screen."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_3.tres
msgid "Leave the treasure to its guardian."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_3.tres
msgid "The snake is left with its hoard."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_3.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers bow respectfully and back away, deciding that some treasures are not meant to be claimed.\n"
"\n"
"They adopt the patient, watchful snake as a symbol of keeping things hidden until the time is right."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_3.tres
msgid "Leave the screen and take the rest."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_3.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers rush to claim the furniture, but the snake is faster.\n"
"\n"
"A scuffle ensues.\n"
"\n"
"The snake is wounded, one of the settlers is injured, and the treasures remain untouched."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_3.tres
msgid "Drive the snake away with torches."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_3.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers wave open flames at the snake.\n"
"\n"
"It hisses and retreats into a corner of the room.\n"
"\n"
"The treasure is claimed, but the room is now full of smoke, no longer a welcoming habitat for the reptile."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_3.tres
msgid "Flee in terror."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/snake/event_companion_snake_3.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers run screaming from the outpost, declaring it a monster's den.\n"
"\n"
"It will be a while before anyone will brave these rooms again."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_1.tres
msgid "Feline Pest Control"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_1.tres
msgid ""
"Today, the tea pavilion is a battlefield. A cat is chasing a large, exceptionally hairy spider around the room, knocking cups and scratching the delicate paper screens.\n"
"\n"
"The spider seems to be winning so far, holding its ground against a beast fifty times its size, but the feline is not giving up."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_1.tres
msgid "Grab the spider and deposit it outside."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_1.tres
msgid "The spider is saved."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_1.tres
msgid ""
"Despite her fear of spiders, the tea maker bends down and snatches the arachnid before the cat can strike.\n"
"\n"
"She endures the unsettling sensation of eight prickly legs scrambling over her bare skin, but calmly deposits the spider on the porch.\n"
"\n"
"The battle is finished, and the spider survives to spin another day."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_1.tres
msgid "Cheer the cat on."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_1.tres
msgid ""
"The chase goes on for a while yet, but finally the cat pounces, sealing the spider's fate.\n"
"\n"
"The aftermath leaves a whole tea set strewn all around the tea house, and one of the paper screens seriously damaged.\n"
"\n"
"The cat looks exceedingly pleased with itself though."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_1.tres
msgid "Trap the spider under a cup."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_1.tres
msgid ""
"The tea maker calmly places a cup over the creature, slides a thick piece of parchment underneath, and escorts the angry arachnid outside.\n"
"\n"
"It is a sensible, highly effective, and utterly unadventurous solution."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_1.tres
msgid "Flee the pavilion."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_1.tres
msgid ""
"The tea maker follows her instinct and flees, leaving the problem to her cat companion.\n"
"\n"
"Once the hubbub dies down, she returns to find a whole tea set strewn all around the tea house, and one of the paper screens seriously damaged.\n"
"\n"
"The cat looks exceedingly pleased with itself though."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_2.tres
msgid "A Webbed Habitat"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_2.tres
msgid ""
"While exploring a damp cavern, the expedition stumbles upon a pre-Shattering scroll in an airtight case, perfectly preserved.\n"
"\n"
"The caves extend further, into deep tunnels, bound to contain more ancient artifacts, but the way forward lies through a thick, silvery labyrinth of spiderwebs.\n"
"\n"
"The spiders themselves are large, watchful, and currently sitting motionless in the dark. Retrieving the lost knowledge will lead through their domain."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_2.tres
msgid "Wade through the webs."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_2.tres
msgid "Preserve the habitat"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_2.tres
msgid "The spider habitat is preserved."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_2.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers push through the sticky silk, enduring the terrifying feeling of heavy spiders dropping onto their shoulders and crawling across their backs.\n"
"\n"
"They retrieve a cache of ancient scrolls without destroying the nest, but everyone is jittery for days afterwards."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_2.tres
msgid "Burn the webs away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_2.tres
msgid ""
"Torches make quick work of the silk.\n"
"\n"
"Unfortunately, the fire quickly spreads despite the dampness, and when the blaze dies down, all that can be found in the cave is ash.\n"
"\n"
"The spiders and the ancient scrolls alike are lost."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_2.tres
msgid "Send in armored guards."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_2.tres
msgid ""
"Clad in thick coats and heavy gloves, the guards sweep the webs away.\n"
"\n"
"The scrolls are retrieved successfully.\n"
"\n"
"The spiders flee deeper into the rock, displaced but alive."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_2.tres
msgid "Take the single scroll and leave."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_2.tres
msgid ""
"The cave is left undisturbed.\n"
"\n"
"The settlers decide that no knowledge is worth braving the creepy arachnids."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_3.tres
msgid "The Antidote"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_3.tres
msgid ""
"The town has been plagued by painful spider bites. What's worse, they seem to put victims into a depression that lasts for days.\n"
"\n"
"An apothecary has finally identified the exact type of spider responsible for the affliction, and one is now hanging on its web in her hut.\n"
"\n"
"She thinks she could use its venom to brew an antidote, but extracting it from such an aggressive creature is a delicate matter."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_3.tres
msgid "Coax it to bite a resin-coated stick."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_3.tres
msgid "An uneasy alliance is forged."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_3.tres
msgid ""
"The apothecary carefully agitates the spider until it strikes the stick, leaving heavy beads of precious venom behind on the resin.\n"
"\n"
"The apothecary collects it, and successfully produces a cure.\n"
"\n"
"The spider is kept around for future extractions, left mostly to its devices."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_3.tres
msgid "Suffer a bite to extract the venom."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_3.tres
msgid ""
"The apothecary offers her bare arm to the spider.\n"
"\n"
"The bite is agonizing, and she has to push through an all-consuming feeling of hopelessness to continue the project.\n"
"\n"
"She squeezes enough of the venom out of the wound to successfully produce a cure, but spends the next week barely leaving the hut."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_3.tres
msgid "Crush the spider to extract the venom."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_3.tres
msgid ""
"It is messy work, but it gets the job done.\n"
"\n"
"The town gets an antidote, but the creature is destroyed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_3.tres
msgid "Release the spider far away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/spider/event_companion_spider_3.tres
msgid ""
"The apothecary refuses to risk an extraction, dumping the spider back into the swamp.\n"
"\n"
"The town will simply have to endure the bites for the time being."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_1.tres
msgid "Flashes in the Deep"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_1.tres
msgid ""
"Kelp gatherers pulling up their daily harvest are reporting sudden red flashes darting deep among the dark green fronds below.\n"
"\n"
"Some fear it is a warning from the sea spirits, unwilling to share the bounty, while others find the colorful display quite festive.\n"
"\n"
"Neither group has yet been able to identify what exactly these flashes are."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_1.tres
msgid "Leave the next harvest to the spirits."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_1.tres
msgid ""
"The workers decide that red is the color of fire, blood, and things that do not belong underwater. The spirits must be making a threat.\n"
"\n"
"They take the next few days off, hoping the flashes will disappear.\n"
"\n"
"They do not."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_1.tres
msgid "Consider the flashes a lucky sign."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_1.tres
msgid "The settlers encounter the sea bream."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_1.tres
msgid ""
"A few workers spend the afternoon leaning over the edge of their boats, looking for the flashes.\n"
"\n"
"The source turns out to be large, very red fish: sea bream.\n"
"\n"
"Something else they notice is that the kelp grows thickest wherever these sea bream gather, marking these fish as a sign of abundance among the kelp gatherers."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_1.tres
msgid "Try to get rid of them."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_1.tres
msgid ""
"The workers decide that whatever these flashes are, they must be harmful.\n"
"\n"
"On their next trip out, they jab their oars down into the water, trying to push the flashes away.\n"
"\n"
"This turns out to be effective, and within days, the flashes stop showing up."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_1.tres
msgid "Ignore the flashes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_1.tres
msgid ""
"The workers agree that whatever is flashing down there is none of their business.\n"
"\n"
"They haul up their kelp and keep their eyes on the horizon."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_2.tres
msgid "Delicious Shapes"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_2.tres
msgid ""
"The local bakers have spent the past month coming up with a perfect steamed bun.\n"
"\n"
"They have grown an exceptional yeast that produces soft, fluffy dough, and perfected a rich sweet red bean paste as a filling.\n"
"\n"
"All that remains is to decide how to shape the bun to ensure its popularity."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_2.tres
msgid "Shape it into a sea bream."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_2.tres
msgid "Make the sea bream a symbol of celebration"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_2.tres
msgid "The sea bream becomes a symbol of celebration."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_2.tres
msgid ""
"The bakers shape the buns into the plump, red fish often seen near the kelp farms.\n"
"\n"
"The first few customers are puzzled by the choice, but it sparks interest, and soon the townsfolk are lining up in queues every morning to get their fresh fish-shaped buns.\n"
"\n"
"The treat is now a staple at festivals, and the sea bream becomes a common symbol of celebration."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_2.tres
msgid "Shape it into a lotus flower."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_2.tres
msgid ""
"The buns are shaped then snipped in a circular pattern that creates petals once the dough rises.\n"
"\n"
"The result is a beautiful, elegant bun that many consider too pretty to actually eat."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_2.tres
msgid "Shape it perfectly round, like the moon."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_2.tres
msgid ""
"The bakers stick to the classics. The round buns sell well enough, but they lack novelty.\n"
"\n"
"Within days the interest wanes and the townsfolk are in the grip of a new snack fad, completely forgetting about the perfectly adequate bean buns."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_2.tres
msgid "Shape it into a maple leaf."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_2.tres
msgid ""
"The leaf shape is a modest success, particularly among the local scholars and priests who appreciate the seasonal poetry of it.\n"
"\n"
"It becomes a refined snack meant for quiet contemplation, but the common townsfolk consider it pretentious."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_3.tres
msgid "Calling a Boat"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_3.tres
msgid ""
"The shipwrights have finally finished their latest vessel.\n"
"\n"
"It is a sturdy, wide-bellied cargo ship built to haul heavy crates across the rougher waters of the shard.\n"
"\n"
"The workers are gathered around, debating what name will bring the ship the most fortune."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_3.tres
msgid "Name it after the carp."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_3.tres
msgid ""
"The ship is named the Koi, to honor the persevering carp, in a loud ceremony full of celebratory toasts.\n"
"\n"
"As the cheering dies down, a young deckhand points out that carp live in fresh water, and taking one out to sea doesn't make much sense."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_3.tres
msgid "Name it after the sea bream."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_3.tres
msgid "The sea bream is honored."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_3.tres
msgid ""
"The ship is named the Tai, after the plump red fish which has become a symbol of abundance.\n"
"\n"
"The name fits the wide, sturdy vessel perfectly as it sits low in the water, heavy with cargo.\n"
"\n"
"The sea bream is well on its way to being adopted as the patron spirit of good fortune."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_3.tres
msgid "Name it after the dragon."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_3.tres
msgid ""
"The ship is named the Ryū, after the sleek flowing shape of the sky dragons of legend.\n"
"\n"
"The name sounds impressive, and the workers spend a long time carving a magnificent figurehead to mount at the front of the bow.\n"
"\n"
"However, the heavy cargo ship makes for a very chubby, slow-moving dragon, and the crews of smaller vessels sometimes make fun of the Dragon for being slower than even their tiny boats."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_3.tres
msgid "Name it after the wind."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tai/event_companion_tai_3.tres
msgid ""
"The ship is named the Kaze, after the wind that animates its sails.\n"
"\n"
"However, during its very first trip out of the harbor, a sudden gale catches the rigging and tears away the sail.\n"
"\n"
"It is quickly reattached, but the crew snicker about the irony of being foiled by one's own namesake."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_1.tres
msgid "Contented Lethargy"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_1.tres
msgid ""
"One night, farmers stumble upon a chubby tanuki sitting in the middle of their field.\n"
"\n"
"The animal seems content, patting its belly and wistfully looking up at the moon. It is surrounded by a circle of trampled buckwheat, clearly picked clean of grain.\n"
"\n"
"On the one hand, the farmers want to banish the pest. On the other hand, many of them can empathize with the contented lethargy the animal must be experiencing."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_1.tres
msgid "Chase it away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_1.tres
msgid ""
"The farmers wave their arms and shout.\n"
"\n"
"The creature attempts a dignified retreat, immediately foiled by its perfectly round shape. It awkwardly waddles into the brush, bouncing slightly with every step.\n"
"\n"
"A particularly stern farmer, having never seen a tanuki before, demands it be declared an Invasive Alien Species of Shard Concern."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_1.tres
msgid "Give it more food."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_1.tres
msgid ""
"A farmer approaches the tanuki with a handful of grain.\n"
"\n"
"The creature slowly lowers its head, gives a deep sigh, then looks back at the moon.\n"
"\n"
"The farmer retreats, feeling slightly judged."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_1.tres
msgid "Sit next to it."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_1.tres
msgid ""
"All four farmers sit next to it, mimicking its posture.\n"
"\n"
"The tanuki doesn't react immediately, but soon looks around, confused.\n"
"\n"
"It eventually decides to get away from these odd mimicking creatures."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_1.tres
#: events/generic/charcoal_theft/event_charcoal_theft.tres
msgid "Let it be."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_1.tres
msgid "The tanuki enjoys its reverie."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_1.tres
msgid ""
"The farmers decide to leave the trespasser to its midnight digestion.\n"
"\n"
"The creature remains perfectly still, its paws resting on its round belly.\n"
"\n"
"As the moonlight hits its face, one farmer swears the plump little thief is smiling."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_2.tres
msgid "Drunken Stumbling"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_2.tres
msgid ""
"The brewers at the lodge have recently found some of their aging vats broken, the precious liquid spilled all around them.\n"
"\n"
"One night they hide, hoping to catch the thief. By midnight they hear a rustling from behind the lodge, and rush to find the culprit.\n"
"\n"
"They are greeted by a tanuki stumbling away into the dark, only to be caught in the vines. The animal turns around, a look of sheepish confusion on its face."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_2.tres
msgid "Untangle the little criminal."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_2.tres
msgid "Help the tanuki"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_2.tres
msgid "The tanuki appreciates the help."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_2.tres
msgid ""
"A brave brewer steps forward, murmuring soft words of reassurance, and carefully unwinds the vines from the creature's legs.\n"
"\n"
"The animal freezes for a moment, but once freed, it gives the brewer a glazed look, then slowly ambles away into the darkness, hiccuping the entire time."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_2.tres
msgid "Cut away the vines."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_2.tres
msgid ""
"A brewer fetches her harvesting knife and snips the vines away.\n"
"\n"
"The animal freezes for a moment, but once freed, it gives the brewer a glazed look, then slowly ambles away into the darkness, hiccuping the entire time."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_2.tres
msgid "Give it some food to go with the drink."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_2.tres
msgid ""
"A brewer takes pity on the creature and tosses it a dried plum to soak up the alcohol.\n"
"\n"
"The animal sniffs it, takes a tentative bite, and immediately throws up.\n"
"\n"
"Its belly having contracted, it finally gets through the vines and scrambles away in shame."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_2.tres
msgid "Leave it tangled as a lesson."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_2.tres
msgid ""
"The brewers decide that a night in the vines is exactly the sort of punishment a thief deserves.\n"
"\n"
"When morning comes, the creature is still there, having simply given up and fallen fast asleep."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_3.tres
msgid "A Pilgrim By Moonlight"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_3.tres
msgid ""
"An apprentice working late into the night is greeted by an odd sight. A tanuki approaches the door, walking on its hind legs, with a scarf tied around its head.\n"
"\n"
"The animal looks eerily human-like in the moonlight, a diminutive pilgrim who lost his way in the night.\n"
"\n"
"The apprentice wonders if it's a sign from the Enlightened One."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#. Property: label
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_3.tres
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_hawk_chick.tres
msgid "Adopt it."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_3.tres
msgid ""
"The apprentice coaxes the creature inside.\n"
"\n"
"The animal accepts the hospitality, falling asleep by the loom. The moment the sun rises, though, it bolts out the door.\n"
"\n"
"It leaves behind a lingering, musky stench that takes days to dissipate."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_3.tres
msgid "Pray to it."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_3.tres
msgid ""
"Overwhelmed by the eerie sight, the apprentice drops to his knees and begins loudly chanting a half-remembered prayer.\n"
"\n"
"The creature stops dead in its tracks, clearly unnerved by this strange human behavior.\n"
"\n"
"It turns around and rapidly scurries back into the woods, its headscarf flashing white in the moonlight."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_3.tres
msgid "Examine the scarf."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_3.tres
msgid "The tanuki is happy to be freed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_3.tres
msgid ""
"Gathering his courage, the apprentice steps closer and reaches for the cloth.\n"
"\n"
"The creature freezes, allowing him to carefully untie the knot. It turns out the animal had managed to get its head stuck in one of the silk cloths hung out to dry. Freed from its makeshift headwear, the animal chirps in relief and bounds away.\n"
"\n"
"Ever since, the weavers often hear it cheerfully rummaging around on the edge of the settlement at night."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_3.tres
msgid "Pretend it's not there."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tanuki/event_companion_tanuki_3.tres
msgid ""
"The apprentice closes his eyes, rubs them vigorously, and decides that staying late has finally broken his mind.\n"
"\n"
"He turns his back and focuses on the work. When he finally dares to look again, the yard is empty.\n"
"\n"
"He will spend the rest of his life wondering if the tiny pilgrim was real."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_1.tres
msgid "A Painting Come to Life"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_1.tres
msgid ""
"A traveling artist recently painted a remarkably lifelike image of a tiger on a screen at the little forest shrine.\n"
"\n"
"The townsfolk greatly admire the masterful work, but lately, deep, rumbling roars have been heard coming from the shrine at night.\n"
"\n"
"Rumors are spreading, claiming that the painted beast steps out of its frame at night, and folks have been avoiding the shrine."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_1.tres
msgid "Keep watch in the dark to discover the truth."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_1.tres
msgid "Encountered a real live tiger."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_1.tres
msgid ""
"A few brave settlers hide in the bushes near the shrine.\n"
"\n"
"Just past midnight, a massive, very real tiger walks into the clearing. It sniffs the painting, lets out a roar, and lays down to rest.\n"
"\n"
"The danger remains, but thanks to the settlers' bravery, they are now aware of their fearsome neighbor."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_1.tres
msgid "Remove the cursed painting."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_1.tres
msgid ""
"Assuming the painting to be the source of the trouble, the settlers take it out and store it in a locked cellar.\n"
"\n"
"The next night, the same roars are heard from the forest, but sounding perhaps even louder and more annoyed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_1.tres
msgid "Build a fence around the shrine."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_1.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers spend an afternoon erecting a bamboo fence to keep whatever is making the noise inside.\n"
"\n"
"The next morning they find the fence destroyed, splintered as if hit by a falling boulder."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_1.tres
msgid "Avoid the shrine after dusk."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_1.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers decide to avoid the danger, but their imaginations continue to run wild.\n"
"\n"
"Soon folks are terrified of stepping into the woods even during the day, convinced that paper tigers are waiting to pounce."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_2.tres
msgid "Under the Same Moon"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_2.tres
msgid ""
"A local poet likes to sit at the edge of the cliff to find inspiration in the night sky.\n"
"\n"
"Tonight, the view is particularly breathtaking, with red maple leaves dancing on the wind.\n"
"\n"
"However, the evening is interrupted when a tiger pads out onto the cliff's edge, playing with the leaves and staring at the moon."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_2.tres
msgid "Remain on the cliff."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_2.tres
msgid "Show the tiger courage"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_2.tres
msgid "The settlers have shown the tiger courage."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_2.tres
msgid ""
"The poet swallows hard but remains still, unwilling to show the tiger a hint of fear.\n"
"\n"
"For an hour, human and beast sit side by side, admiring the moon.\n"
"\n"
"The experience provides the poet with enough inspiration for a long time."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_2.tres
msgid "Recite a booming verse to the beast's majesty."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_2.tres
msgid ""
"The poet stands up and delivers a dramatic verse in a low growl, to match the tiger's fierce nature.\n"
"\n"
"The tiger listens intently and seems to relax long enough for the poet to slowly walk away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_2.tres
msgid "Flee back down the path."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_2.tres
msgid ""
"The poet jumps up and sprints toward the settlement.\n"
"\n"
"This triggers the tiger's hunting instinct, and it bounds after the terrified poet, effortlessly keeping pace all the way to the tree line before losing interest and wandering off."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_2.tres
msgid "Jump down from the cliff."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_2.tres
msgid ""
"In a panic, the poet decides that the only way to survive the predator is to jump down.\n"
"\n"
"He survives the incident with a broken leg and a life-long fear of wildlife."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_3.tres
msgid "A Mourning Beast"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_3.tres
msgid ""
"Heavy rains have turned the bottom of the quarry into a muddy pit. In this pit, huddled under a small overhang of ivy, is a tiger.\n"
"\n"
"The beast has been there for days, looking miserable, occasionally emitting sorrowful moans. A wildlife warden reports that it had recently lost its cubs to a rockslide."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_3.tres
msgid "Roar a fierce challenge down into the quarry."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_3.tres
msgid "The tiger's spirit is reinvigorated."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_3.tres
msgid ""
"A brave settler steps to the edge of the pit, cups her hands, and lets out a booming roar.\n"
"\n"
"The tiger snaps to attention, its eyes flashing with renewed intensity.\n"
"\n"
"It rises to the challenge, and lets out a deafening roar, before proudly stalking away into the wilderness."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_3.tres
msgid "Build a makeshift roof to keep the rain off."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_3.tres
msgid ""
"The townsfolk tie some bamboo together into a canopy above the ivy overhang.\n"
"\n"
"The tiger doesn't seem to notice, and continues to sit in the cold dampness, whimpering once in a while.\n"
"\n"
"Rarely can a physical solution fix a mental problem."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_3.tres
msgid "Scare the beast away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_3.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers throw pebbles down, trying to scare the tiger away.\n"
"\n"
"The beast watches the falling rocks with disinterest, shifts its position closer to the wall, but continues to sit in the cold dampness, whimpering once in a while."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_3.tres
msgid "Leave the beast to its misery."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/tiger/event_companion_tiger_3.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers agree to stay out of the quarry until the tiger decides to leave.\n"
"\n"
"The tiger remains in the quarry for days, inconsolable in its grief.\n"
"\n"
"It leaves eventually, stepping softly, its shoulders hunched and its gaze fixed on the ground."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_1.tres
msgid "Trailing Seaweed"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_1.tres
msgid ""
"The waters of the coral garden are clear enough to spot several turtles swimming lazily among the reefs.\n"
"\n"
"One of the turtles is sporting a long cape of green algae trailing from its shell.\n"
"\n"
"The settlers are greatly impressed by the unusual sight, and someone mentions hearing stories from their grandparents about such turtles."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_1.tres
msgid "Tell the tale of the straw cape turtle."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_1.tres
msgid "The tale of the straw cape turtle is told."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_1.tres
msgid ""
"A young diver recounts the old tale, as told to her by her grandparents.\n"
"\n"
"According to legend, a turtle which lives ten thousand years grows a tail of seaweed that looks like a straw cape. This cape is proof that the turtle had reached complete harmony with nature and became enlightened.\n"
"\n"
"So can humans, the story seems to suggest, attain enlightenment by moving slowly and carefully through life."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_1.tres
msgid "Clean the algae off the turtle's shell."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_1.tres
msgid ""
"A few well-meaning swimmers carefully catch the turtle and scrape the heavy algae away.\n"
"\n"
"The turtle looks completely unbothered, but it doesn't seem to benefit from the grooming in any way either."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_1.tres
msgid "Capture the sight in a painting."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_1.tres
msgid ""
"An artist quickly mixes some green and brown ink, capturing the majestic creature on parchment.\n"
"\n"
"The work is easy, as the subject was moving so slowly that it might as well have been still."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_1.tres
msgid "Leave the turtles to their swim."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_1.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers watch until the turtles slowly disappear behind a reef.\n"
"\n"
"It is a peaceful sight, but there is work to be done."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_2.tres
msgid "Studying All Night"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_2.tres
msgid ""
"A diligent student has been sitting outside the archives all night, frantically studying for his apprenticeship exam.\n"
"\n"
"He is exhausted, his eyes are blurry, and the words stopped making sense hours ago.\n"
"\n"
"A small turtle slowly climbs the slope beside him, moving at a remarkably consistent, unhurried pace."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_2.tres
msgid "Ask the turtle for study advice."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_2.tres
msgid ""
"The delirious student asks the turtle to quiz him on the scroll's contents.\n"
"\n"
"The turtle completely ignores the man and continues its slow trek up the hill."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_2.tres
msgid "Pet the turtle."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_2.tres
msgid ""
"The student reaches out and pats the turtle on the shell.\n"
"\n"
"The turtle doesn't seem to notice, or perhaps chooses not to.\n"
"\n"
"The man sighs and goes back to staring blankly at the scroll."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_2.tres
msgid "Continue studying through sheer willpower."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_2.tres
msgid ""
"Inspired by the turtle's relentless progress, the student vows to finish reading.\n"
"\n"
"He forces his eyes open, reads two more lines, then passes out face-first into the hydrangea bush."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_2.tres
msgid "Go to sleep."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_2.tres
msgid "Learn not to rush"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_2.tres
msgid "The student has learned not to rush."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_2.tres
msgid ""
"Inspired by the turtle's unrushed effort, the student decides to pace himself.\n"
"\n"
"He rolls up his scroll and lies down, falling asleep within minutes.\n"
"\n"
"He will retain more knowledge after a good rest."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_3.tres
msgid "A Grand Design"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_3.tres
msgid ""
"The architect of the waterwheel has been sitting by the town's resident turtle, daydreaming of future projects.\n"
"\n"
"In his imagination, a sprawling, magnificent castle rises from the ground.\n"
"\n"
"His daydream, however, is spoiled by realizing that such a project is bound to take multiple lifetimes to finish."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_3.tres
msgid "Downsize the project to be more manageable."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_3.tres
msgid ""
"The architect lets go of the outer wall, then the inner one, then the towers, and ends up with little more than a rampart.\n"
"\n"
"It is a practical design, feasible to build in a few years, but he can't help feeling that he'd let his dream go."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_3.tres
msgid "Break the project down into stages."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_3.tres
msgid "The settlers have learned to take the long-term view."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_3.tres
msgid ""
"Looking at the ancient turtle, the architect considers the long term.\n"
"\n"
"Even if he can't finish the project within his lifetime, he would leave behind a legacy for future generations.\n"
"\n"
"He starts breaking the design down into stages, imagining the plans he would have to hand down to his successors to ensure its success."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_3.tres
msgid "Design a way for the castle to move on wheels."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_3.tres
msgid ""
"Inspired by the turtle carrying its home, the architect begins imagining a fortress that rolls on massive wooden wheels.\n"
"\n"
"It takes about five minutes of math for him to realize the idea is completely absurd, but the image is highly entertaining."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_3.tres
msgid "Abandon the project entirely."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/companions/turtle/event_companion_turtle_3.tres
msgid ""
"Defeated by the brevity of human existence, the architect discards the idea.\n"
"\n"
"He decides to stick to designing practical constructions, buildable in a month, and leaves the grand dreams behind."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/alekon/event_alekon.tres
msgid ""
"The lead artisan of the bureau was commissioned to carve a great statue of the Enlightened One. After a month of work he unveils his masterpiece, to the astonishment of everyone present.\n"
"\n"
"When questioned, the artisan claims that the Enlightened One had appeared to him in a dream in this exact shape, and asked him about the meaning of life."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/alekon/event_alekon.tres
msgid "Pay your respects."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/alekon/event_alekon.tres
msgid ""
"Each member of the expedition takes a turn to walk up to the statue and bow.\n"
"\n"
"Somehow, the sheer strangeness of the creature fills them with an immense feeling of inspiration and the desire to go out into the world and create unique and beautiful things."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/basket_weaver/event_basket_weaver.tres
msgid "An Ominous Basket"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/basket_weaver/event_basket_weaver.tres
msgid ""
"The basket weavers are working diligently, winding the slender yellow stalks into simple yet sturdy shapes.\n"
"\n"
"The master weaver inspects his apprentices' handiwork, setting another basket down when something around its rim catches his eye.\n"
"\n"
"He squints for a moment, then his eyes widen. The woven pattern seems to form tiny glyphs. They read: [i]\"lanterns follow not\"[/i]."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/basket_weaver/event_basket_weaver.tres
msgid "Show others the message."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/basket_weaver/event_basket_weaver.tres
msgid ""
"The master weaver summons his favorite apprentice and asks him to read the glyphs. The boy cocks his head, looking at the master in confusion.\n"
"\n"
"The master, suspecting a prank, grows angry. He holds the basket up in front of the entire hut, demanding that each worker step forward to inspect it.\n"
"\n"
"When nobody else admits to seeing the glyphs, he grows pale. He laughs, a bit too loudly, then asks everyone to return to work.\n"
"\n"
"For the rest of the day, his fingers keep returning to the basket, tracing the edge."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/basket_weaver/event_basket_weaver.tres
msgid "Compare the basket to other baskets."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/basket_weaver/event_basket_weaver.tres
msgid ""
"The master lines all the baskets he has inspected into a row, and starts to compare them, searching for any sign of glyphs or hidden messages.\n"
"\n"
"The workers look on, glancing at the master nervously.\n"
"\n"
"By the time the inspection is done, the master realizes that many of the common weave patterns look like glyph shapes, if one tries hard enough to see the parallels. He laughs at his superstitiousness, and feels relieved for the rest of the day."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/basket_weaver/event_basket_weaver.tres
msgid "Search for the lanterns."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/basket_weaver/event_basket_weaver.tres
msgid ""
"The weaver, with trembling hands, writes the message down on a piece of paper and tucks it into his sleeve.\n"
"\n"
"Later, when the moon rises over the swamp, he steps out into the dark to begin his search.\n"
"\n"
"He is found the next morning at the edge of a bog, confused and mumbling to himself, the message still in his sleeve."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/basket_weaver/event_basket_weaver.tres
msgid "Examine the message more closely."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/basket_weaver/event_basket_weaver.tres
msgid ""
"The weaver looks intently at the spot where he saw the strange message, twisting the edge of the basket this way and that to see more clearly.\n"
"\n"
"Startled, he watches as the glyphs morph into different shapes. First they appear as lanterns, then as a path through tall reeds.\n"
"\n"
"He is absorbed in watching the images for the rest of the day."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/big_dry_tree/event_big_dry_tree.tres
msgid "The Old Cherry Tree"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/big_dry_tree/event_big_dry_tree.tres
msgid ""
"Deep in the forest, the woodcutters pause at the foot of a towering tree, easily the largest they've ever seen.\n"
"\n"
"The bark is scarred, and most of the limbs are either broken or bare. A few birds nest in hollows once shaped by age or lightning.\n"
"\n"
"The tree is not dead, though. Two thin branches are lush with pink petals, reaching for the light."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/big_dry_tree/event_big_dry_tree.tres
msgid "Fell the tree for timber."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/big_dry_tree/event_big_dry_tree.tres
msgid ""
"The work takes all day.\n"
"\n"
"The trunk cracks like thunder, and its fall shakes the forest floor.\n"
"\n"
"The wood is strong, aged, and clean.\n"
"\n"
"But something changes. Birds avoid the clearing now."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/big_dry_tree/event_big_dry_tree.tres
msgid "Prune just enough to help it grow."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/big_dry_tree/event_big_dry_tree.tres
msgid ""
"The dead limbs are removed with care, no more than necessary.\n"
"\n"
"When the last one falls, the young shoots already look freer. The sun reaches the bark in places it hasn't touched in years."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/big_dry_tree/event_big_dry_tree.tres
msgid "Establish a care routine."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/big_dry_tree/event_big_dry_tree.tres
msgid ""
"A schedule is made. Each week, a few woodcutters visit to check the roots and trim dead branches.\n"
"\n"
"They put a small sign to mark the tree as maintained.\n"
"\n"
"Soon, such signs start appearing all around the forest."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/big_dry_tree/event_big_dry_tree.tres
msgid "Leave the tree untouched."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/big_dry_tree/event_big_dry_tree.tres
msgid ""
"The woodcutters continue on.\n"
"\n"
"The tree stands unchanged, or perhaps changing too slowly to notice."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/bird_man/event_bird_man.tres
msgid "The Bird Man"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/bird_man/event_bird_man.tres
msgid ""
"When the expedition first encountered bird nests on the cliffs, one of the settlers felt a particular affinity with the birds.\n"
"\n"
"Only a few days later, he declared that he was a bird, reborn in the wrong vessel. He now spends his days crouching at the edge of the cliff, his robe shaped to resemble plumage.\n"
"\n"
"The other settlers are concerned, but though peculiar, he understands his physical limitations and seems harmless."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/bird_man/event_bird_man.tres
msgid "Have the artisans craft him proper plumage."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/bird_man/event_bird_man.tres
msgid ""
"If he is to be a bird, he shouldn't have to make do with a frayed robe.\n"
"\n"
"The artisans meticulously fold, layer, and dye paper to create a magnificent cloak of artificial feathers.\n"
"\n"
"When he spreads his arms against the wind, he cries with joy as his spirit soars."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/bird_man/event_bird_man.tres
msgid "Formally recognize his spirit as a patron deity."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/bird_man/event_bird_man.tres
msgid ""
"The Enlightened One's blessings work in mysterious ways, the monks declare. Perhaps a sky-bound fragment of the divine spirit tumbled into a human frame.\n"
"\n"
"A small shrine is dedicated to the new avian patron god in a small ceremony.\n"
"\n"
"The settlers now awake each dawn to the trilling song of the bird man, out on the cliff."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/bird_man/event_bird_man.tres
msgid "Ask if he needs help."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/bird_man/event_bird_man.tres
msgid ""
"When asked, the bird man indicates that he needs a nest for himself, one large enough for a human.\n"
"\n"
"His friends set to work under his guidance, bringing woven reeds, dried moss, and bits of cloth.\n"
"\n"
"The result is the strangest nest any of them had seen, but the bird man finds it perfectly comfortable."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/bird_man/event_bird_man.tres
msgid "Leave him undisturbed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/bird_man/event_bird_man.tres
msgid ""
"The world is strange enough without demanding everyone fit into the same mold.\n"
"\n"
"The community agrees to let him be, ensuring someone checks up on him once in a while."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/blossom_study/event_blossom_study.tres
msgid "Roots of Wonder"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/blossom_study/event_blossom_study.tres
msgid ""
"The flowers here bloom without end. Even as petals fly off in the wind, new ones begin sprouting.\n"
"\n"
"Locals admire the view in awe, but a scholar claims the secret of this renewal lies under the soil.\n"
"\n"
"She proposes digging up the plants, stalk, root, and all.\n"
"\n"
"\"We might learn something to restore other lands,\" she argues.\n"
"\n"
"The ranger, however, worries that the flowers may stop growing back once disturbed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/blossom_study/event_blossom_study.tres
msgid "Approve full excavation."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/blossom_study/event_blossom_study.tres
msgid ""
"The scholar gets her way, and digs with obsessive care.\n"
"\n"
"Her notes speak of twinned seeds, taking turns to sprout, one resting while the other blooms.\n"
"\n"
"But the flowers don't grow back. The seeds she replants remain inert, and the field loses some of its magic.\n"
"\n"
"Still, the seeds are preserved. Perhaps they will still sprout one day."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/blossom_study/event_blossom_study.tres
msgid "Allow study of a single plant."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/generic/blossom_study/event_blossom_study.tres
msgid "A chance of discovery"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#. Property: outcome_text
#: events/generic/blossom_study/event_blossom_study.tres
#: events/generic/school/event_school.tres
#: events/landmark/mirage_gate/event_mirage_gate.tres
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_big_tree.tres
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_swamp_bridge.tres
msgid "<overridden>"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/blossom_study/event_blossom_study.tres
msgid "Capture them in a painting."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/blossom_study/event_blossom_study.tres
msgid ""
"Painters set to work, capturing every angle and hue.\n"
"\n"
"Still, the scholar sighs, admitting sketches can't reveal the truth beneath the soil."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/blossom_study/event_blossom_study.tres
msgid "Forbid any study."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/blossom_study/event_blossom_study.tres
msgid ""
"The scholar is asked to leave the field untouched.\n"
"\n"
"She storms off with a few muttered protests.\n"
"\n"
"The blossoms continue their gentle sway."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#. Property: name
#: events/generic/boat_festival/event_boat_festival.tres
#: stage/spots/lake/upgrade_lake_3_boat_festival.tres
msgid "Boat Festival"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/boat_festival/event_boat_festival.tres
msgid ""
"The lake is still in the pale light of dawn. A few settlers have taken sailboats out to catch the morning breeze.\n"
"\n"
"Several canoes are tied by the shore, one loaded with baskets and sailcloth.\n"
"\n"
"\"In the Old World, we used to launch boats with painted sails to mark a year's guiding glyph.\" One settler reminisces. \"But perhaps it is not yet time for such extravagance.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/boat_festival/event_boat_festival.tres
msgid "Host a guiding boat festival."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/boat_festival/event_boat_festival.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers sing as they sew.\n"
"\n"
"The sails are painted with a guiding glyph to carry forward.\n"
"\n"
"As the sun sets, boats are pushed out into the lake, floating away.\n"
"\n"
"\"We'll remember that one,\" an old shipwright remarks."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/boat_festival/event_boat_festival.tres
msgid "Paint the sailcloth for a future festival."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/boat_festival/event_boat_festival.tres
msgid ""
"New sails are painted and hung to dry, flapping in the breeze.\n"
"\n"
"It will be a while before they are used. Perhaps by next year there'll be enough boats to host the festival."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/boat_festival/event_boat_festival.tres
msgid "Host a small gathering to share stories of old boat festivals."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/boat_festival/event_boat_festival.tres
msgid ""
"Settlers gather to hear old festival tales, how boats once symbolized promises to future generations.\n"
"\n"
"Someone traces a glyph in the dirt."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/boat_festival/event_boat_festival.tres
msgid "Pass the day in quiet contemplation."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/bonded_rocks/event_bonded_rocks.tres
msgid "Unequal Rocks"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/bonded_rocks/event_bonded_rocks.tres
msgid ""
"Soon after the great rocks were tied with a rope and declared to be a married couple, some settlers began to complain.\n"
"\n"
"Since the rocks are unequal in size, they say, they represent an unequal relationship.\n"
"\n"
"Several people volunteer to resolve the problem."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/bonded_rocks/event_bonded_rocks.tres
msgid "Let a poet resolve it."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/bonded_rocks/event_bonded_rocks.tres
msgid ""
"The poet stands before the crowd and recites a verse declaring that harmony is found not in being the same, but in being together.\n"
"\n"
"The crowd doesn't seem entirely convinced, but they seem content with having been acknowledged."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/bonded_rocks/event_bonded_rocks.tres
msgid "Let a scribe resolve it."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/bonded_rocks/event_bonded_rocks.tres
msgid ""
"The scribe drafts some documents and holds a small ceremony in front of the rocks.\n"
"\n"
"Henceforth, he declares, these rocks are to be called the Mother and Child."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/bonded_rocks/event_bonded_rocks.tres
msgid "Let a mason resolve it."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/bonded_rocks/event_bonded_rocks.tres
msgid ""
"The mason is eager to get to work. He gathers his crew and they set to carving the bigger rock down.\n"
"\n"
"Days later, the two rocks are exactly the same size, though one is covered in chisel marks."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/bonded_rocks/event_bonded_rocks.tres
msgid "Ignore the complaints."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/bonded_rocks/event_bonded_rocks.tres
msgid ""
"The town council declares the issue invalid and refuses to address it.\n"
"\n"
"The complaints soon dissipate, but an air of dissatisfaction remains."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/bone_girl/event_bone_girl.tres
msgid "Bone Research"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/bone_girl/event_bone_girl.tres
msgid ""
"A young woman has taken to spending all her time at the ancient boneyard out in the wasteland.\n"
"\n"
"As soon as she finishes her morning chores, she arrives to wander among the bones, lost in thought, imagining the great creatures that once walked these lands.\n"
"\n"
"She begins sketching the giant bones, and fitting fragments together. Before long the settlers are giving her strange looks and calling her Bone Girl behind her back."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/bone_girl/event_bone_girl.tres
msgid "Continue visiting the boneyard."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/bone_girl/event_bone_girl.tres
msgid ""
"Unconcerned with public image, the young woman refuses to give up her visits, and they grow longer and more frequent instead.\n"
"\n"
"Her most exciting discovery comes when she starts noticing bits of metal embedded in many of the bones. Some look like splinters, while others resemble little jagged flowers."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/bone_girl/event_bone_girl.tres
msgid "Try to make the visits practical."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/bone_girl/event_bone_girl.tres
msgid ""
"The woman tries to make her trips to the boneyard more practical.\n"
"\n"
"She chooses the largest, heaviest bones and brings them to the artisans to be made into tools.\n"
"\n"
"The settlers become more accepting of her eccentricity, but she worries that the mysterious creatures are being reduced to scrap."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/bone_girl/event_bone_girl.tres
msgid "Seek advice."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/bone_girl/event_bone_girl.tres
msgid ""
"The woman turns to a passing scholar for advice.\n"
"\n"
"She is surprised when he shows great interest in her sketches and discusses her ideas with clear excitement. They spend days studying the bones together, before he has to leave.\n"
"\n"
"She will one day hear of the great bone scholar who had discovered a treasure trove of bones in the wasteland, all by himself."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/bone_girl/event_bone_girl.tres
msgid "Stop going to the boneyard."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/bone_girl/event_bone_girl.tres
msgid ""
"The young woman gives in to the social pressure and stops wandering among the ancient bones.\n"
"\n"
"She resolves to take up more acceptable pastimes, like cooking and mending clothes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/book_drying/event_book_drying.tres
msgid "The Book of Beasts"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/book_drying/event_book_drying.tres
msgid ""
"The librarians are airing the entire archive, hanging books on strings to let the damp pages dry. \n"
"\n"
"One of the helpers, a bright child, laughs in delight as one of the books reveals page upon page of colorful illustrations depicting strange-looking beasts. \n"
"\n"
"One page shows a yellow squirrel with feathered wings. Another, a big blue horse with an improbably long snout. The boy, however, is most fascinated by a giant, wide-eyed creature with pointed ears peeking through a row of reeds.\n"
"\n"
"He asks a librarian what sort of creature this is."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/book_drying/event_book_drying.tres
msgid "It is an evil spirit."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/book_drying/event_book_drying.tres
msgid ""
"The boy nods solemnly. He asks the local priests about spirits and ghosts, and begins studying old manuscripts describing possessions and exorcisms.\n"
"\n"
"Soon he sets out to seek a monastery and become a novice monk."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/book_drying/event_book_drying.tres
msgid "It is an ancient beast."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/book_drying/event_book_drying.tres
msgid ""
"The librarian admits that nobody here knows what those creatures are, but she thinks they are ancient beasts, ones who used to roam these lands before the Shattering.\n"
"\n"
"This sparks a lifelong passion of history in the boy. Someday he will uncover many mysteries lost in the mists of the past."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/book_drying/event_book_drying.tres
msgid "It is an imaginary monster."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/book_drying/event_book_drying.tres
msgid ""
"The librarian explains that these are fairy-tale monsters that an artist imagined.\n"
"\n"
"Spurred by the revelation that one is free to come up with imaginary beasts, the boy starts spending his days drawing his own creatures. Dogs with wings, birds with books in their beaks, and brightly colored tigers with flowers around their necks."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/book_drying/event_book_drying.tres
msgid "Tell him to put the book away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/book_drying/event_book_drying.tres
msgid ""
"The librarian sternly instructs the boy to put the book back on its string, explaining that the paper is too damp to handle.\n"
"\n"
"The boy will not be back to the library for a long time."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/broken_bamboo/event_broken_bamboo.tres
msgid "Broken Stalks"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/broken_bamboo/event_broken_bamboo.tres
msgid ""
"At dawn, the bamboo grove lies unsettled. Several of the younger stalks have been snapped halfway up.\n"
"\n"
"No claw marks or footprints mar the ground. Only the wind whistles through hollowed joints, rustling the leaves in its wake.\n"
"\n"
"It could be last night's rainstorm, or wild beasts, or perhaps travelers taking a shortcut.\n"
"\n"
"The broken stalks lie waiting. It seems wrong to leave them untouched."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/broken_bamboo/event_broken_bamboo.tres
msgid "Whittle the broken bamboo into chopsticks."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/broken_bamboo/event_broken_bamboo.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers gather the fallen stalks, trimming them down into simple tools.\n"
"\n"
"A hundred slender pairs of chopsticks take shape.\n"
"\n"
"Whatever caused the damage, life must go on."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/broken_bamboo/event_broken_bamboo.tres
msgid "Build a tipping fountain."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/broken_bamboo/event_broken_bamboo.tres
msgid "A simple shishi-odoshi is built beside the grove's footpath: a hollow tube, filling with water until it tips with a sharp, deliberate knock. One can't help but listen for it."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/broken_bamboo/event_broken_bamboo.tres
msgid "Carve a shakuhachi flute from the bamboo."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/broken_bamboo/event_broken_bamboo.tres
msgid ""
"A few stalks, strong and straight, are chosen with care.\n"
"\n"
"The soft rasp of carving blades soon gives way to the first tentative notes of a shakuhachi flute.\n"
"\n"
"Several musicians hold a performance in the grove at dusk."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/broken_bamboo/event_broken_bamboo.tres
msgid "Store the bamboo for future use."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/broken_bamboo/event_broken_bamboo.tres
msgid ""
"The broken pieces are bundled carefully and stacked at the foot of the hill.\n"
"\n"
"There they rest, waiting for future carvers to decide their fate."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/census/event_census.tres
msgid "The Census"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/census/event_census.tres
msgid ""
"The first official act of the new Assembly Hall is to conduct a census of the population. It's time to record who settled down, who moved on with the expedition, and how the land will be tended.\n"
"\n"
"One settler brings a preserved scroll to show they've stewarded land before. Another proposes communal use, with simple census tags to track imbalance. A third calls for precise allotments, granting full ownership.\n"
"\n"
"They disagree, but all seek a system that endures."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/census/event_census.tres
msgid "Respect the old claim."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/generic/census/event_census.tres
msgid "Shard culture may be affected"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/census/event_census.tres
msgid ""
"The scroll is added to the public record as precedent, and a copy is sent on with the expedition for redundancy.\n"
"\n"
"The claimant is assigned to manage land allocation at will, and trusted to dole out lots fairly and impartially.\n"
"\n"
"Most of the gathered express doubts."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/census/event_census.tres
msgid "Share everything and let the census track balance."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/census/event_census.tres
msgid ""
"Wooden tags are inscribed with parcel numbers and kept at the assembly hall.\n"
"\n"
"Anyone can take a tag to start a farm or dig a well.\n"
"\n"
"Progress will be audited at a regular schedule, and when tags run out, the assembly will decide which ones should be returned to the pool, to give others a chance to do something different with the land."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/census/event_census.tres
msgid "Impose a fixed record. Equal parcels, equal weight."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/census/event_census.tres
msgid ""
"Most of the land is divided among those present. It will be bought, sold, or passed on from parent to child. Those not present for the meeting are assigned parcels at random.\n"
"\n"
"Precise records of ownership are stamped with official seals and stored in the Assembly Hall for future magistrates to resolve disputes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/census/event_census.tres
msgid "Move on without making a decision."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/census/event_census.tres
msgid ""
"The meeting continues long into the night, but the debate remains unresolved.\n"
"\n"
"For now, whoever has laid a claim keeps their land, but future assemblies are sure to challenge them again and again."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/charcoal_theft/event_charcoal_theft.tres
msgid "Charcoal Theft"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/charcoal_theft/event_charcoal_theft.tres
msgid ""
"Charcoal has been vanishing from the camp. Never in bulk, but just enough to notice.\n"
"\n"
"At first, the workers thought it was miscounted and blamed each other.\n"
"\n"
"Last night, a burner followed faint footprints to a clearing, where the ashes of a tiny fire and a pile of woven reeds suggest that someone has been camping out in the open swamp."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/charcoal_theft/event_charcoal_theft.tres
msgid "Set a trap to catch the thief."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/charcoal_theft/event_charcoal_theft.tres
msgid ""
"The snare is crude but effective.\n"
"\n"
"When the intruder stumbles into it, she screams.\n"
"\n"
"An old woman, face smeared, eyes wild. She fights like a cornered animal and escapes in the scuffle.\n"
"\n"
"She drops something in her flight, though: a charcoal-stained tooth, painted black and polished smooth."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/charcoal_theft/event_charcoal_theft.tres
msgid "Leave food and charcoal deliberately."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/charcoal_theft/event_charcoal_theft.tres
msgid ""
"A bundle is left each night with no demands, and always gone by the morning.\n"
"\n"
"Days pass.\n"
"\n"
"One morning, the bundles are untouched, but in their place is a cracked cup holding a charcoal-stained tooth, painted black and polished smooth."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/charcoal_theft/event_charcoal_theft.tres
msgid "Post guards to protect the supplies."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/charcoal_theft/event_charcoal_theft.tres
msgid ""
"The guards keep watch in shifts.\n"
"\n"
"One night, someone rustles in the brush, then flees.\n"
"\n"
"The thefts stop, and the camp returns to its rhythm."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/charcoal_theft/event_charcoal_theft.tres
msgid ""
"The thefts continue.\n"
"\n"
"Bundles vanish, and the burners continue to grumble.\n"
"\n"
"No more signs appear in the clearing, but the tracks remain."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/cicada/event_cicada_1.tres
msgid "The Sparrow and the Cicada"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/cicada/event_cicada_1.tres
msgid ""
"A sparrow dives on a cicada in a sudden motion that seems to split the air in two.\n"
"\n"
"Settlers pause mid-step, enthralled. It is an everyday occurrence, yet it feels significant.\n"
"\n"
"There's a brief moment to intervene."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/cicada/event_cicada_1.tres
msgid "Save the cicada from the sparrow."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/generic/cicada/event_cicada_1.tres
msgid "The cicada may return the favor"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/cicada/event_cicada_1.tres
msgid ""
"Hands rise, clapping sharply.\n"
"\n"
"The sparrow startles, its quarry escapes, and the air fills with a self-satisfied cry of survival.\n"
"\n"
"It won't be the last cicada the settlers see on this shard."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/cicada/event_cicada_1.tres
msgid "Study the interaction."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/cicada/event_cicada_1.tres
msgid ""
"The cicada is easily caught mid-air, and the sparrow lands on the ground, the prey secure in its beak.\n"
"\n"
"After methodically pulling off the cicada's legs, the sparrow enjoys its meal, emits a satisfied chirrup, and flies away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/cicada/event_cicada_1.tres
msgid "Meditate on the balance of nature."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/cicada/event_cicada_1.tres
msgid ""
"The cicada is caught. The sparrow flies on. The grass continues to sway in the wind.\n"
"\n"
"All things in nature rise and fall.\n"
"\n"
"Perhaps beauty lies in the transition."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/cicada/event_cicada_1.tres
msgid "Ignore the chase."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/cicada/event_cicada_2.tres
msgid "An Empty Husk"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/cicada/event_cicada_2.tres
msgid ""
"At the base of a willow, a fragile cicada shell clings to the bark.\n"
"\n"
"The cicada is gone. In its place is a perfect empty husk, intact and light as paper.\n"
"\n"
"The wind is whistling faintly through it."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/cicada/event_cicada_2.tres
msgid "Take the shell as a memento."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/cicada/event_cicada_2.tres
msgid ""
"The shell remains intact.\n"
"\n"
"It is bound to inspire the expedition later."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/cicada/event_cicada_2.tres
msgid "Study the shell."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/cicada/event_cicada_2.tres
msgid ""
"A painter smudges ink onto the shell and takes an imprint.\n"
"\n"
"The lines are sharp and precise, as if the cicada is alive on the paper."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/cicada/event_cicada_2.tres
msgid "Meditate on the transformation."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/cicada/event_cicada_2.tres
msgid ""
"A monk sits by the willow, meditating on the husk.\n"
"\n"
"Although the shell is empty, what grew from it lives elsewhere, freer for the dropped burden."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/clay_basket/event_clay_basket.tres
msgid "A Basket of Clay"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/clay_basket/event_clay_basket.tres
msgid ""
"A local teenager, cheeks dusted with clay, arrives at the kiln with a basket of handmade bowls, almost too large for him to carry alone.\n"
"\n"
"He is too timid to say anything. He just sets them down and looks hopeful.\n"
"\n"
"The bowls are crooked, thick-lipped, and none quite match.\n"
"\n"
"The master potter rubs her chin."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/clay_basket/event_clay_basket.tres
msgid "Suggest turning them into cooking pots."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/clay_basket/event_clay_basket.tres
msgid ""
"The master potter inspects each piece, nods, and says, \"Not for tea. But these'll hold soup just fine.\"\n"
"\n"
"The teen laughs, then asks for more clay."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/clay_basket/event_clay_basket.tres
msgid "Offer to teach the kid."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/clay_basket/event_clay_basket.tres
msgid ""
"\"You've got a spark,\" the potter says. \"If you're willing to learn, I'll teach you to throw a bowl that sings.\"\n"
"\n"
"The teen blinks, then grins wider than the kiln mouth."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/clay_basket/event_clay_basket.tres
msgid "Fire them all as-is and offer kind words."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/clay_basket/event_clay_basket.tres
msgid ""
"The kiln glows late into the night.\n"
"\n"
"In the morning, the teen returns to find his clumsy bowls fired and neatly stacked.\n"
"\n"
"A note rests on top of the stack, thanking the youngster for his patronage.\n"
"\n"
"It won't be the last time he visits the kiln."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/clay_basket/event_clay_basket.tres
msgid "Tell the teen they aren't worth firing."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/clay_basket/event_clay_basket.tres
msgid ""
"\"Not this time,\" the potter says. \"Maybe next.\"\n"
"\n"
"The teen shrugs and carries the crate back home."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/crystallobotany/event_crystallobotany.tres
msgid "A Breakthrough in Crystallobotany"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/crystallobotany/event_crystallobotany.tres
msgid ""
"The swamp path turns rigid underfoot. A crystal-crusted lily pad shimmers on stagnant water. A crystal squirrel perches motionless on a branch. A settler cries out after stepping on a bed of crystallized mushrooms.\n"
"\n"
"In front of a ramshackle hut, the alchemist is elbow-deep in a great steaming cauldron.\n"
"\n"
"\"It began with moss. Then algae. Now root, stem, flower, and beast!\" He breaks off a branch and gestures excitedly. \"Try it! The bigger the ingredient, the bigger the reaction!\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/crystallobotany/event_crystallobotany.tres
msgid "Throw a twig into the cauldron."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/generic/crystallobotany/event_crystallobotany.tres
msgid "A mild gamble"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/crystallobotany/event_crystallobotany.tres
msgid "<will be overridden>"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/crystallobotany/event_crystallobotany.tres
msgid "Tear off a petal and throw it into the cauldron."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/generic/crystallobotany/event_crystallobotany.tres
msgid "A medium gamble"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/crystallobotany/event_crystallobotany.tres
msgid "Throw the entire branch into the cauldron."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/generic/crystallobotany/event_crystallobotany.tres
msgid "A risky gamble"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/crystallobotany/event_crystallobotany.tres
msgid "Use the Dead Branch."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/crystallobotany/event_crystallobotany.tres
msgid ""
"The branch doesn't seem to react at first, but a minute later crystals start growing around its tip.\n"
"\n"
"\"Smart,\" the alchemist nods, \"it must be safer with a dead one.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/crystallobotany/event_crystallobotany.tres
msgid "Do not engage with the madman."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/desert_archive/event_desert_archive.tres
msgid "Beneath the Sands"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/desert_archive/event_desert_archive.tres
msgid ""
"Buried in the sand behind a storage space of an old ruin is a chamber full of scrolls. Most appear to be from shortly before the Shattering, but a few fragments are much older, written in an unfamiliar script.\n"
"\n"
"It seems that historians were researching an even older civilization here. Translated fragments declare strange laws banning weapons of unclear nature. Redrawn maps show cities the size of a shard.\n"
"\n"
"The settlement's scholars ponder what to do with this treasure trove."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/desert_archive/event_desert_archive.tres
msgid "Leave a mark and seal the place once more."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/desert_archive/event_desert_archive.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers leave a scroll of their own, a contribution to this treasure trove of knowledge.\n"
"\n"
"The chamber is then resealed, the entrance hidden again under the sand.\n"
"\n"
"Someday people wiser than us will make use of this archive."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/desert_archive/event_desert_archive.tres
msgid "Let an eager scholar copy everything she can."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/desert_archive/event_desert_archive.tres
msgid ""
"The scholar starts frantically transcribing every record she sees.\n"
"\n"
"When she runs out of paper, she starts writing directly on the fabric of her robe.\n"
"\n"
"\"I don't understand it all,\" she says. \"But I'll find someone who will.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/desert_archive/event_desert_archive.tres
msgid "Explore deeper into the archive."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/desert_archive/event_desert_archive.tres
msgid ""
"The scholars clear the rubble of a collapsed wall and find a stair leading down into the darkness.\n"
"\n"
"At the bottom they find another chamber. This one is filled with stacks of stone tiles, many covered in unusual geometric patterns.\n"
"\n"
"It seems that the tiles were once part of a mosaic, but too many are missing to even guess at what the full image was meant to depict."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/desert_archive/event_desert_archive.tres
msgid "Let the lead scholar decide."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/desert_archive/event_desert_archive.tres
msgid ""
"The lead scholar steps forward without asking. He lifts a wooden seal from among the scrolls and drops it into his sleeve.\n"
"\n"
"\"This will make a wonderful addition to my collection,\" he says."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/desert_cassava/event_desert_cassava.tres
msgid "The Sandstorm"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/desert_cassava/event_desert_cassava.tres
msgid ""
"The settlement is halfway through the cassava harvest when the chief priest emerges from the shrine in distress. He has interpreted the color of the sky at dawn and the howling of the wind as a warning: a great sandstorm is coming and the village must pull out every cassava root by sunset.\n"
"\n"
"The head farmer disagrees. He has spent his life reading wind, soil, and plant signs. Storm or not, he insists that the cassava is safer left underground until it can be processed properly.\n"
"\n"
"The settlers are divided. The priest has been right before, but the farmer's experience is what keeps their granaries full.\n"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/desert_cassava/event_desert_cassava.tres
msgid "Listen to the priest."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/desert_cassava/event_desert_cassava.tres
msgid ""
"Panicked, the whole settlement rushes into the fields and tears up every cassava root they can find before sunset.\n"
"\n"
"When the storm strikes, the untouched crops remain undamaged, while the harvested roots are now bruised and already beginning to spoil."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/desert_cassava/event_desert_cassava.tres
msgid "Trust the head farmer."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/desert_cassava/event_desert_cassava.tres
msgid ""
"The farmer agrees that the storm may occur, but insists that the safest place for most of the cassava is still underground.\n"
"\n"
"\"We should reinforce the granary walls and cover the irrigation channels instead,\" he says, \"before the storm reaches us.\"\n"
"\n"
"As winds howl through the village, the tubers remain safe underground, and the preparations save time spent on cleanup afterwards."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/desert_cassava/event_desert_cassava.tres
msgid "Test the prophecy."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/desert_cassava/event_desert_cassava.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers send scouts to the dunes to verify the priest's warning.\n"
"\n"
"By the time they see the storm headed for the village, it is too late to act.\n"
"\n"
"When the dust settles, the cassava roots remain mostly underground, but the irrigation channels are choked with sand."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/desert_cassava/event_desert_cassava.tres
msgid "Wait out the storm inside."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/desert_cassava/event_desert_cassava.tres
msgid ""
"Too frightened to act, the villagers decide to shelter and wait for the storm to pass.\n"
"\n"
"No one risks being caught in the open, but the fields are left unprotected.\n"
"\n"
"When the dust settles, the cassava roots remain safe underground, but the irrigation channels are choked with sand."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/desert_pub/event_desert_pub.tres
msgid "The Desert Pub"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/desert_pub/event_desert_pub.tres
msgid ""
"This evening the pub is full. Locals drift in, eager for news from the road from merchants in dusty robes.\n"
"\n"
"A stranger sits in the corner, ignored as the drink and conversation flow. His long face remains shadowed, only a prominent nose sticking out, and oddly large eyes catching the lamplight. Finally, he stands up and begins to tell a story.\n"
"\n"
"The patrons roar with laughter at his retelling of the Magic Teapot, and refill his cup time and again.\n"
"\n"
"As his tongue loosens, the tales begin to change. He now speaks of a white city, its turrets shimmering in the sunlight, its lotus ponds filling the air with a sweet fragrance. His eyes get misty as he describes the scent of rain on white stone and the brothers he left behind."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/desert_pub/event_desert_pub.tres
msgid "Let the storyteller continue."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/desert_pub/event_desert_pub.tres
msgid ""
"Most of the patrons are too deep in their cups, but the innkeeper keeps her ears open.\n"
"\n"
"She lets the storyteller speak until his cup drops from his hand, writing down every word she can remember of his tale."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/desert_pub/event_desert_pub.tres
msgid "Keep the storyteller safe."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/desert_pub/event_desert_pub.tres
msgid ""
"Noticing the heaviness of the storyteller's sleeve, several shady characters continue plying him with drink. When he is finally unable to stand, they offer to take him to his lodging.\n"
"\n"
"The innkeeper intervenes, however, claiming that this honored guest is her responsibility. She shoos the other patrons away and walks him back herself.\n"
"\n"
"As the strange man leaves the next morning, he deposits several coins with unfamiliar writing in the innkeeper's hand. \"I've no more use for these,\" he says."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/desert_pub/event_desert_pub.tres
msgid "Ask the storyteller about his brothers."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/desert_pub/event_desert_pub.tres
msgid ""
"Curious, the innkeeper asks to hear more about the stranger's family. \"I wish I could go back,\" he says, as tears fill his eyes.\n"
"\n"
"He suddenly looks up from his drink, his eyes regaining focus. With a nod at the innkeeper, he excuses himself and walks back to his lodgings."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/desert_pub/event_desert_pub.tres
msgid "Ignore the drunkard."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/desert_pub/event_desert_pub.tres
msgid ""
"The innkeeper lets the stories pass with the night.\n"
"\n"
"Some of the patrons speak amongst themselves, wondering about the strange tale, but the traveler is gone as the first sunrays shine through the palms."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/driftwood/event_driftwood.tres
msgid "Odd Driftwood"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/driftwood/event_driftwood.tres
msgid ""
"Over several days, new pieces of driftwood make it to the shoal with an uncanny regularity.\n"
"\n"
"They aren't the usual planks or branches, though, but solid wood shaped like tools. A mallet with no joints. A sickle with no metal parts.\n"
"\n"
"The driftwood gatherers swear they've never seen anything like this before, and say that sea spirits must be sharing tools with their new neighbors."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/driftwood/event_driftwood.tres
msgid "Leave a ceremonial gift in return."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/driftwood/event_driftwood.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers leave bowls of rice and a cup of sake on the shore for the tide to claim.\n"
"\n"
"The offering is gone by morning.\n"
"\n"
"A few days later, a large tree branch washes onto the shore. Tucked between its forked twigs are several pre-Shattering coins."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/driftwood/event_driftwood.tres
msgid "Carve the odd driftwood into dice."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/driftwood/event_driftwood.tres
msgid ""
"The wood is waterlogged, yet satisfying to carve.\n"
"\n"
"A pair of dice is finished in no time.\n"
"\n"
"The first roll comes up six. So does the second."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/driftwood/event_driftwood.tres
msgid "Throw the pieces back."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/driftwood/event_driftwood.tres
msgid ""
"One by one, the tools are cast into the waves.\n"
"\n"
"They float away, but some return later the same day.\n"
"\n"
"Other such tools keep showing up, but few pay them any mind.\n"
"\n"
"Perhaps a ship with a very creative carver on board had sunk into the sea."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/driftwood/event_driftwood.tres
msgid "Throw the inkstick into the sea."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/driftwood/event_driftwood.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers cast a single inkstick into the waves, which quickly disappears.\n"
"\n"
"The next day a peculiarly sharpened stake is found on the beach."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/driftwood/event_driftwood.tres
msgid "Leave them alone."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/driftwood/event_driftwood.tres
msgid ""
"The tide rises and falls.\n"
"\n"
"The driftwood floats on, untouched.\n"
"\n"
"Over time, the tools disappear one by one, and the incident is forgotten."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/dyer_workshop/event_dyer_workshop.tres
msgid "The Tapestry"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/dyer_workshop/event_dyer_workshop.tres
msgid ""
"The dyes from this workshop come out richer than any the locals have seen before.\n"
"\n"
"Inspired by them, a young apprentice wants to turn her humble tapestry project into a masterpiece, a great landscape depicting the whole lake and its surroundings, deep blue giving way to warm tans and lively greens, dotted with bright splashes of pink.\n"
"\n"
"Her mentor advocates restraint, as cloth and dyes are both precious."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/dyer_workshop/event_dyer_workshop.tres
msgid "Finish the tapestry."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/dyer_workshop/event_dyer_workshop.tres
msgid ""
"The apprentice meticulously gathers remnants, spindles, and half-finished bolts.\n"
"\n"
"No grand tapestry is made, but nothing is wasted.\n"
"\n"
"Perhaps one day these fragments will be put together into an even more impressive project."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/dyer_workshop/event_dyer_workshop.tres
msgid "Carefully prepare the cloth for future projects."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/dyer_workshop/event_dyer_workshop.tres
msgid ""
"The apprentice meticulously gathers remnants, spindles, and half-finished bolts.\n"
"\n"
"No grand tapestry is made, but nothing is wasted.\n"
"\n"
"Perhaps one day these fragments will serve as a canvas for an even more impressive project."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/dyer_workshop/event_dyer_workshop.tres
msgid "Save the dyes for more practical work."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/dyer_workshop/event_dyer_workshop.tres
msgid ""
"The apprentice leaves the dyes untouched.\n"
"\n"
"No grand tapestry is made, but nothing is wasted.\n"
"\n"
"The saved dyes are destined to color many a settler's robe in the days ahead."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/dyer_workshop/event_dyer_workshop.tres
msgid "Hang the unfinished tapestry as it is."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/dyer_workshop/event_dyer_workshop.tres
msgid ""
"The apprentice cuts her project short, leaving the tapestry with a simple indigo pattern.\n"
"\n"
"It hangs by the entrance now. Perhaps it is a reminder of dreams postponed, or of waste prevented."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/ember_monastery/event_ember_monastery.tres
msgid "The Ember Trial"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/ember_monastery/event_ember_monastery.tres
msgid ""
"The path to the Ember Monastery is a long one, and the final approach requires more than just walking.\n"
"\n"
"This last stretch of the path is made of old fossils, glowing with heat.\n"
"\n"
"A solemn nun is standing on one of the glowing stones.\n"
"\n"
"She explains that visitors are invited to steel their resolve and make their own choice for how to traverse this path."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/ember_monastery/event_ember_monastery.tres
msgid "Judge the heat by the cracks in the bones."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/ember_monastery/event_ember_monastery.tres
msgid ""
"One settler kneels at the edge and studies the coals.\n"
"\n"
"Patterns emerge where heat has split the bone-flecked stones.\n"
"\n"
"\"The future may seem obscure, but there are always signs for us to read,\" he says, as he steps on the path."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/ember_monastery/event_ember_monastery.tres
msgid "Inscribe protective charms on paper before stepping forward."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/ember_monastery/event_ember_monastery.tres
msgid ""
"Each settler draws a single line on a strip of paper.\n"
"\n"
"They fold them gently, and carry them as they step onto the glowing path.\n"
"\n"
"\"With this protection,\" a settler says, \"we will remember that the pain will pass.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/ember_monastery/event_ember_monastery.tres
msgid "Throw tools onto the coals and walk on them."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/ember_monastery/event_ember_monastery.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers throw pins, fasteners, and scraps of iron onto the path.\n"
"\n"
"The metal digs into skin, but it grants them just enough time to escape the heat.\n"
"\n"
"On the other side, one settler retrieves a single molten pin.\n"
"\n"
"\"We'll shape it again,\" she says. \"We'll shape everything again.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/ember_monastery/event_ember_monastery.tres
msgid "Spread ash over the coals and walk on them."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/generic/ember_monastery/event_ember_monastery.tres
msgid "Get one of the Ember Order relics."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/ember_monastery/event_ember_monastery.tres
msgid ""
"One of the expedition members is an initiate in the Ember Order.\n"
"\n"
"She knows the trick the monks are expected to perform, and simply covers the glowing stones with a layer of ash, leaving a safe path for her comrades to follow.\n"
"\n"
"The monks send her off with one of the monastery's relics to spread the teachings."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/ember_monastery/event_ember_monastery.tres
msgid "Step away from the coals."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/ember_monastery/event_ember_monastery.tres
msgid ""
"The nun bows.\n"
"\n"
"\"Another time,\" she says."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/firewood_coppice/event_firewood_coppice.tres
msgid "What the Fire Leaves"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/firewood_coppice/event_firewood_coppice.tres
msgid ""
"The gatherers worked hard, perhaps too hard. Piles of firewood line the coppice edge, and bundles of kindling have replaced chairs and tables in the camp.\n"
"\n"
"There's more wood than the settlers can store in the sheds, and more than the kitchens can use in a year. It will rot if left in the open.\n"
"\n"
"Some suggest burning it now, while others want to put it to better use."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/firewood_coppice/event_firewood_coppice.tres
msgid "Char it carefully into ritual sticks."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/firewood_coppice/event_firewood_coppice.tres
msgid ""
"Slow fires are set in shallow pits, turning the excess wood into light, porous charcoal rods.\n"
"\n"
"Artists keep some to draw with."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/firewood_coppice/event_firewood_coppice.tres
msgid "Tend a long, low flame."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/firewood_coppice/event_firewood_coppice.tres
msgid ""
"The fire is banked in a clay ring and fed just enough. It smolders for days: no blaze, just embers and smoke.\n"
"\n"
"It becomes a place to warm hands and share stories. Some say it will keep burning long after the wood is gone."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/firewood_coppice/event_firewood_coppice.tres
msgid "Burn it all in a great communal bonfire."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/firewood_coppice/event_firewood_coppice.tres
msgid ""
"Flames leap high into the dusk. Someone starts a song. Soon, drums join in. The coppice glows, keeping shadows and worries away.\n"
"\n"
"Little is left of the wood by the time the fire dies, but the settlers will long remember this bonfire."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/firewood_coppice/event_firewood_coppice.tres
msgid "Use it to lay a wooden path into the coppice."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/firewood_coppice/event_firewood_coppice.tres
msgid ""
"The logs are split and laid with care. By morning, there's a dry, clear path from the settlement to the grove.\n"
"\n"
"It may be mundane, but it gets people where they need to go."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/forest_monastery/event_forest_monastery.tres
msgid "Insufficiently Holy Trees"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/forest_monastery/event_forest_monastery.tres
msgid ""
"This monastery of the Order of Growth was established in a copse of cherry trees, perhaps cultivated once, but wild now. They bloom briefly and produce bitter fruit.\n"
"\n"
"Many of the monks argue that they should instead replant the area with traditional cedar trees. Some object to needlessly cutting wild trees, suggesting that it should be enough to just sanctify them, or even to graft cedar branches."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/forest_monastery/event_forest_monastery.tres
msgid "Replace them with traditional cedar."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/forest_monastery/event_forest_monastery.tres
msgid ""
"The trees are felled and cut into logs for the temple hearths.\n"
"\n"
"In their place, cedar saplings are planted. Perhaps in ten years, the monastery will be surrounded by trees again.\n"
"\n"
"Some of the monks who objected to the plan save the cherry pits, hoping to revive the copse elsewhere someday."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/forest_monastery/event_forest_monastery.tres
msgid "Sanctify the existing trees."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/forest_monastery/event_forest_monastery.tres
msgid ""
"The monks wrap moss-green robes around the cherry trees and tie them with heavy braided ropes, symbolically ordaining them as part of the order.\n"
"\n"
"The trees do not seem to mind, and it deters vermin."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/forest_monastery/event_forest_monastery.tres
msgid "Graft cedar branches onto the trees."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/forest_monastery/event_forest_monastery.tres
msgid ""
"The monks make cuts in the cherry trees, and bind branches from sacred cedars to the wounds.\n"
"\n"
"Within days, the bound branches wither.\n"
"\n"
"\"Of the pine tree learn from the pine tree. Of the bamboo learn from the bamboo,\" quotes one of the monks."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/forest_monastery/event_forest_monastery.tres
msgid "Plant the grounds with seeds from the talisman pouch."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/forest_monastery/event_forest_monastery.tres
msgid ""
"One of the monks reminds the abbot that the Enlightened One had entrusted them with their seed pouches for just such an occasion.\n"
"\n"
"Instead of felling the cherry trees or planting cedars, the initiates walk the grounds emptying surplus seed pouches to let divine will guide regrowth.\n"
"\n"
"One of the pouches turns out to be filled with odd twinned seeds that the monks had never seen before."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/forest_monastery/event_forest_monastery.tres
msgid "Leave the trees as is."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/forest_monastery/event_forest_monastery.tres
msgid ""
"The monks endlessly debate the plan, but failing to come to a consensus, they leave the trees alone.\n"
"\n"
"\"The forest is not there to serve us,\" the head monk concedes. \"We should let nature take its course.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/forgotten_pouch/event_forgotten_pouch.tres
msgid "Forgotten Pouch"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/forgotten_pouch/event_forgotten_pouch.tres
msgid ""
"The rest stop is quiet, save for birdsong and breeze. But someone was here recently, and forgot something.\n"
"\n"
"A pouch lies on the bench, a modest thing with no markings. It doesn't seem to contain much, so perhaps its absence won't even be noticed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/forgotten_pouch/event_forgotten_pouch.tres
msgid "Keep the pouch."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/forgotten_pouch/event_forgotten_pouch.tres
msgid "\"There's no proof it belonged to anyone,\" one settler reasons, slipping it into their pack. \"No reason for letting it go to waste.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/forgotten_pouch/event_forgotten_pouch.tres
msgid "Search for the owner."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/forgotten_pouch/event_forgotten_pouch.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers follow a trail of flattened grass and catch up to a traveler by the next ridge.\n"
"\n"
"She smiles in relief at the sight of the pouch.\n"
"\n"
"\"You didn't have to go through all this trouble,\" she says. \"But I'm so grateful that you did.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/forgotten_pouch/event_forgotten_pouch.tres
msgid "Build a little lost-and-found box."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/forgotten_pouch/event_forgotten_pouch.tres
msgid ""
"It won't solve everything, but it's a start.\n"
"\n"
"The settlers leave a tiny wooden box with a polite sign, and trust that it will be put to good use."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/forgotten_pouch/event_forgotten_pouch.tres
msgid "Leave it be."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/forgotten_pouch/event_forgotten_pouch.tres
msgid ""
"Maybe its owner will return. Maybe it was left on purpose.\n"
"\n"
"Either way, the pouch remains on the bench."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/giant_butterbur/event_giant_butterbur.tres
msgid "The Giant Butterbur"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/giant_butterbur/event_giant_butterbur.tres
msgid ""
"The butterbur plants were meant to be a modest patch for cough medicine. Something in the soil disagreed with that plan, though.\n"
"\n"
"The stems have surged to the height of a house, and the leaves are now vast green parasols, casting the entire garden in deep, cool shade.\n"
"\n"
"The herbalist measures a stem and notes that the hollow core could fit a kettle. \"Is it a miracle of vitality,\" she wonders, \"or a very large mistake?\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/giant_butterbur/event_giant_butterbur.tres
msgid "Process it into medicine for the town."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/giant_butterbur/event_giant_butterbur.tres
msgid ""
"The herbalist assembles a crew and brings ladders to harvest the leaves. They are dried, ground, and mixed with honey to temper the bitterness.\n"
"\n"
"The taste is still challenging, but the sheer volume means that every cough, ache, and fever in the settlement will be treated for the next year."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/giant_butterbur/event_giant_butterbur.tres
msgid "Distill into a potent extract."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/generic/giant_butterbur/event_giant_butterbur.tres
msgid "The shard culture may be affected"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/giant_butterbur/event_giant_butterbur.tres
msgid ""
"The herbalist selects the most potent roots and the juiciest leaves. They are boiled down, strained, and boiled again until only a thick, dark resin remains.\n"
"\n"
"There's enough to last the settlement for a long while, so some of the resin is packed into small jars to send on with the expedition."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/giant_butterbur/event_giant_butterbur.tres
msgid "Harvest the seeds."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/giant_butterbur/event_giant_butterbur.tres
msgid ""
"The flowers are the size of a person's head, heavy with pollen.\n"
"\n"
"The settlers carefully collect the seeds, wondering if they will grow so huge in other soils, or if this was a singular quirk of this specific place.\n"
"\n"
"Either way, the potential is now stored in a pouch, waiting for a new home."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/giant_butterbur/event_giant_butterbur.tres
msgid "Cook a feast for the whole settlement."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/giant_butterbur/event_giant_butterbur.tres
msgid ""
"The stems are chopped like timber and boiled in the largest cauldrons available.\n"
"\n"
"The expectations are high, but the results are... educational. A settler describes it as similar to chewing on warm rope, and the bitterness lingers in the mouth long after the meal is finished.\n"
"\n"
"\"Well,\" the cook sighs, dumping the leftovers. \"At least we know why the rodents didn't eat it.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/grumpy_rabbits/event_grumpy_rabbits.tres
msgid "The Grumpy Rabbits"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/grumpy_rabbits/event_grumpy_rabbits.tres
msgid ""
"The settlement's architect is surveying the planned location for the town's new warehouse as a full moon rises above. Lost in thought, he catches movement out of the corner of his eye, and is startled to see two white rabbits glaring at him.\n"
"\n"
"They stand still as statues, their red eyes staring accusingly into his very soul. The man laughs nervously and steps past them, but the rabbits' gaze follows.\n"
"\n"
"Looking closely, he notices with a sinking feeling the dark mouths of several burrows.\n"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/grumpy_rabbits/event_grumpy_rabbits.tres
msgid "Cancel the project."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/grumpy_rabbits/event_grumpy_rabbits.tres
msgid ""
"The architect decides to cancel the building project, afraid to disturb the burrows.\n"
"\n"
"The settlers complain, grumbling that they have been reduced to taking orders from rabbits."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/grumpy_rabbits/event_grumpy_rabbits.tres
msgid "Build around the burrows."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/grumpy_rabbits/event_grumpy_rabbits.tres
msgid ""
"The architect revises his plan. The warehouse will now stand on stilts, leaving the burrows beneath untouched.\n"
"\n"
"The design proves effective beyond its original intent. It keeps the grain away from hungry rodents, and the air gap prevents moisture from seeping through the floorboards and spreading rot."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/grumpy_rabbits/event_grumpy_rabbits.tres
msgid "Build a rabbit shrine instead."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/grumpy_rabbits/event_grumpy_rabbits.tres
msgid ""
"Haunted by the rabbits' accusing stares, the architect halts construction on the warehouse and begins a new project.\n"
"\n"
"The result is a set of tiny white shrines, marking the entrances to the rabbits' warren.\n"
"\n"
"Settlers leave little piles of hay in front of the shrines as offerings to the town's new patron deities."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/grumpy_rabbits/event_grumpy_rabbits.tres
msgid "Continue the project."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/grumpy_rabbits/event_grumpy_rabbits.tres
msgid ""
"The project continues as planned, and the settlement gains much-needed storage space.\n"
"\n"
"Still, the architect cannot shake the memory of the rabbits' glaring eyes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/hanging_monastery/event_hanging_monastery.tres
msgid "A Snap in the Chain"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hanging_monastery/event_hanging_monastery.tres
msgid ""
"During routine maintenance, one of the brothers slipped. A link in the chain securing the building to the cliff cracked and gave way beneath his hammer.\n"
"\n"
"Thankfully, the platform held.\n"
"\n"
"Together, the smiths forged a new link before dawn.\n"
"\n"
"Now, as the sunrise gilds the canyon walls, a heavy stillness settles over the common hall. It is time to decide what consequences should follow this mistake."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hanging_monastery/event_hanging_monastery.tres
msgid "Let the monk continue with the same responsibilities."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/hanging_monastery/event_hanging_monastery.tres
msgid ""
"The snapped chain is entrusted to the very hand that broke it.\n"
"\n"
"The monk studies each link as though it were scripture. He will remember every scratch on the chain's surface for the rest of his life.\n"
"\n"
"When the monastery's Acceptance Bell is rung at dusk, the monks feel that a fracture has been avoided."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hanging_monastery/event_hanging_monastery.tres
msgid "Make it a shared duty: four brothers at every check."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/hanging_monastery/event_hanging_monastery.tres
msgid ""
"From now on, chain maintenance is never a lone task. Four pairs of eyes inspect each link, as it is passed from hand to hand.\n"
"\n"
"The chains hold steadier, and the inspection becomes a ritual of responsibility."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hanging_monastery/event_hanging_monastery.tres
msgid "Chastise the monk to sharpen his resolve."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/hanging_monastery/event_hanging_monastery.tres
msgid ""
"The monk is admonished before his brothers and sisters, reminding him that a slip here could mean death.\n"
"\n"
"From now on his hammer strikes become measured and fearful. He ties his hammer to his sash with a cord, which he rubs before every strike."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hanging_monastery/event_hanging_monastery.tres
msgid "Prioritize unity."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/hanging_monastery/event_hanging_monastery.tres
msgid ""
"The abbot holds a meeting to address the incident.\n"
"\n"
"He explains that to blame a single individual betrays the very principle of unity that their rings symbolize.\n"
"\n"
"From now on, the monk who made the mistake is to lead a maintenance team, sharing with them the wisdom gained from his own mistake."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hanging_monastery/event_hanging_monastery.tres
#: events/generic/silver_mine/event_silver_mine.tres
msgid "Ignore the incident."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/hanging_monastery/event_hanging_monastery.tres
msgid ""
"Nothing is said aloud. Gossip passes among the brothers, but soon dissipates.\n"
"\n"
"In the days that follow, distant creaks can be heard in the hall, which are also ignored."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/hill_beacon/event_hill_beacon.tres
msgid "The Missing Flame"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hill_beacon/event_hill_beacon.tres
msgid ""
"A festival is underway celebrating a successful harvest. The settlers dance and feast all day.\n"
"\n"
"Once the sun sinks below the horizon, they climb the tallest hill and light the beacon, a signal that all is well and the harvest was plentiful. They watch the darkening hills, waiting for the next town over to light their own flame, but no flame appears.\n"
"\n"
"An alarmed councilor, perhaps impelled by the feast's ample drinks, raises an alarm, certain that their neighbors must be in trouble."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hill_beacon/event_hill_beacon.tres
msgid "Send a small party to investigate."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/hill_beacon/event_hill_beacon.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts are reluctant to leave the feast, but the councilor urges them incessantly, insisting that waiting may cost lives.\n"
"\n"
"With festival lanterns in tow, they trudge through the dark path.\n"
"\n"
"When they finally reach the neighboring settlement, they find it safe. A recent landslide had made the hilltop inaccessible, and since the harvest was disappointing, the villagers didn't bother repairing the stairs to light their beacon."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hill_beacon/event_hill_beacon.tres
#: events/generic/sick_apothecary/event_sick_apothecary.tres
msgid "Wait until morning."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/hill_beacon/event_hill_beacon.tres
msgid ""
"Cooler heads prevail and the anxious councilor is convinced to wait until morning to send out runners to the other settlement. Rushing into the darkness will only create more danger, they argue.\n"
"\n"
"As the first light creeps up the hill, a trader from the neighboring settlement arrives.\n"
"\n"
"She explains that her town is well, but a recent landslide had made the hilltop inaccessible, and since the harvest was disappointing, the villagers didn't bother repairing the stairs to light their beacon."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hill_beacon/event_hill_beacon.tres
msgid "Take drastic measures."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/hill_beacon/event_hill_beacon.tres
msgid ""
"The anxious councilor declares the festival closed and sends a town crier through the village with an alarm bell, declaring that the neighboring town has mysteriously disappeared, perhaps taken over by an evil spirit.\n"
"\n"
"Families hurry indoors as the gates are barred, and the hillside paths are blocked with carts.\n"
"\n"
"Near dawn, an exhausted messenger from the neighboring town arrives bringing news. Spooked by the barricades, he ends up turning around and heading back home."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hill_beacon/event_hill_beacon.tres
msgid "Continue the festival as if nothing happened."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/hill_beacon/event_hill_beacon.tres
msgid ""
"The revelry continues, but the councilor's anxiety spreads among the settlers.\n"
"\n"
"Even as they eat, drink, and sing beneath the hilltop flame, they can't help but glance uneasily, searching for a light among the dark landscape.\n"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/hollow_heart/event_hollow_heart.tres
msgid "The Hollow Heart"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hollow_heart/event_hollow_heart.tres
msgid ""
"The grandfather of the grove, a massive tree that has sheltered countless picnics, has begun to lean.\n"
"\n"
"On closer inspection the caretaker finds that the trunk has rotted, and much of it is hollow. It now stands as an empty shell, waiting for the first strong gale to snap it like a dried reed.\n"
"\n"
"Opinions on how to deal with it are divided: a builder wants to fill it, a gardener wants to prop it, and nervous visitors just want it gone before it falls and hurts someone."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hollow_heart/event_hollow_heart.tres
msgid "Pack the hollow with sand."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/hollow_heart/event_hollow_heart.tres
msgid ""
"The void is filled with gravel and sand, packed tight until the trunk is solid again.\n"
"\n"
"It is safe from falling, anchored by its heavy new core.\n"
"\n"
"However, soon the leaves turn brown and drop, leaving a standing skeleton of branches. It remains as a monument, undeniable and sturdy, but it no longer sings in the wind."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hollow_heart/event_hollow_heart.tres
msgid "Cut it down and replace it with a sapling."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/hollow_heart/event_hollow_heart.tres
msgid ""
"The cycle must turn. The old giant is felled with reverence, its fall shaking the whole grove.\n"
"\n"
"In the center of the fresh stump, a young sapling is planted, bathed in sunlight that hasn't touched this patch of earth for centuries.\n"
"\n"
"The wood of the elder is cut into small blocks and given to the settlers. \"A memento of the elder,\" the caretaker says, \"while we wait for the new one to grow.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hollow_heart/event_hollow_heart.tres
msgid "Prop it up with bamboo crutches."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/hollow_heart/event_hollow_heart.tres
msgid ""
"A lattice of bamboo poles is constructed, tucked under the heaviest boughs like crutches.\n"
"\n"
"The tree leans on them, looking like a weary elder supported by dutiful grandchildren.\n"
"\n"
"It is frail, but it lives on to witness years to come."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hollow_heart/event_hollow_heart.tres
msgid "Fell the tree before it hurts someone."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/hollow_heart/event_hollow_heart.tres
msgid ""
"Axes ring out, and the giant is quickly felled.\n"
"\n"
"The danger is gone, but there is a conspicuous gap in the canopy now, a scar of light among the rustling crowns."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/hull_pile/event_hull_pile.tres
msgid "The Hull Pile"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hull_pile/event_hull_pile.tres
msgid ""
"The threshing is finished, the grain safely stored in the granary, and the hulls gathered in huge piles. The wind rattles through the piles with a dry, whispering sound.\n"
"\n"
"The settlers, exhausted from the harvest, complain of backaches, claiming that the straw mats offer little relief from the hard, cold ground of the new world.\n"
"\n"
"A seamstress offers to make pillows out of the hulls. \"They hold their shape,\" she explains, \"and they breathe.\"\n"
"\n"
"The farmers are tempted, but they could also compost the hulls so the soil remains fertile, though that will take some effort."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hull_pile/event_hull_pile.tres
msgid "Sew pillows for the community."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/hull_pile/event_hull_pile.tres
msgid ""
"The seamstress works late, stitching rough cloth into sacks.\n"
"\n"
"The hulls are stuffed inside, creating firm, cool cushions that cradle the head.\n"
"\n"
"That night, for the first time, the farmers get a good night's sleep. The soil may be hungry, but the people are rested."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hull_pile/event_hull_pile.tres
msgid "Plow the hulls back into the earth"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/hull_pile/event_hull_pile.tres
msgid ""
"The farmers resist the temptation, and get to work again.\n"
"\n"
"The mountain of hulls is leveled and turned into the soil. Some look on wistfully as the potential comfort is buried in the mud.\n"
"\n"
"\"We eat first,\" a farmer says, rubbing a sore shoulder. \"We sleep later.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hull_pile/event_hull_pile.tres
msgid "Spread the hulls on the earthen floors."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/hull_pile/event_hull_pile.tres
msgid ""
"The hulls are spread inside every dwelling, carpets to soften the hard ground.\n"
"\n"
"The damp cold no longer seeps into the sleeping mats, but it is dusty, and the sound of skittering is now an ever-present nuisance."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hull_pile/event_hull_pile.tres
msgid "Burn the hulls."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/hull_pile/event_hull_pile.tres
msgid ""
"The farmers are too tired to put it more effort. They opt for the quickest way to clear the field instead.\n"
"\n"
"The pile is lit, filling the settlement with heavy, pungent smoke for days."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/hungry_monk/event_hungry_monk.tres
msgid "The Hungry Monk"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hungry_monk/event_hungry_monk.tres
msgid ""
"A monk has been at the noodle stall for hours, eating box after box of noodles.\n"
"\n"
"The cook is starting to look at him askance as a towering stack of empty boxes continues to grow, but is wary of offending a customer.\n"
"\n"
"Before long, the monk requests yet another serving."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hungry_monk/event_hungry_monk.tres
msgid "Serve him another box."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_outcome_hint
#: events/generic/hungry_monk/event_hungry_monk.tres
msgid "The feast continues..."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hungry_monk/event_hungry_monk.tres
msgid "Mix a lot of wasabi into the next box."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/hungry_monk/event_hungry_monk.tres
msgid ""
"The cook grinds a massive pile of wasabi and mixes it straight into the noodles.\n"
"\n"
"The monk takes a hearty slurp. His eyes bulge, his face turns red, and he abruptly remembers an urgent appointment, fleeing the stall."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hungry_monk/event_hungry_monk.tres
msgid "Curtly demand payment for the food already consumed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/hungry_monk/event_hungry_monk.tres
msgid ""
"The cook taps the counter and points at the staggering stack of empty boxes.\n"
"\n"
"The monk blinks in surprise, as if the concept of currency had never occurred to him.\n"
"\n"
"He rummages through his deep robes, produces a handful of coins, and leaves with a slightly wounded expression."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hungry_monk/event_hungry_monk.tres
msgid "Serve him an empty box."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/hungry_monk/event_hungry_monk.tres
msgid ""
"The cook places an empty wooden box before the monk with absolute solemnity.\n"
"\n"
"The monk stares at it for a moment, then lets out a booming laugh.\n"
"\n"
"He bows to the cook, and declares his hunger completely cured."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hungry_monk/event_hungry_monk.tres
msgid "The monk quickly polishes off the noodles and asks for another box."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_outcome_hint
#: events/generic/hungry_monk/event_hungry_monk.tres
msgid "The feast still continues..."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hungry_monk/event_hungry_monk.tres
msgid "The monk eats this portion as well, but remains hungry, asking for another portion."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_outcome_hint
#: events/generic/hungry_monk/event_hungry_monk.tres
msgid "Will the feast ever end?"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/hungry_monk/event_hungry_monk.tres
msgid "The monk seems almost done, but asks for another box to properly end the meal."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/hungry_monk/event_hungry_monk.tres
msgid ""
"After this final box, the monk finally lets out a contented sigh.\n"
"\n"
"He stacks the box atop the tower and waddles away towards the horizon."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/ikebana/event_ikebana.tres
msgid "Flower Arrangement"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/ikebana/event_ikebana.tres
msgid ""
"The garden's master florist is preparing an arrangement for the township's founding ceremony.\n"
"\n"
"She must choose the anchor, a single strong branch reaching up into the heavens. Everything else will bend and flow around this anchor to complete the arrangement.\n"
"\n"
"She studies the available choices, noting the true essence of each branch."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/ikebana/event_ikebana.tres
msgid "Choose the twisted pine, a strong, sacred vessel."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/ikebana/event_ikebana.tres
msgid ""
"The florist selects the heavy, gnarled pine branch. It is evergreen and unyielding, scarred by harsh seasons, yet stronger for it.\n"
"\n"
"She boldly angles this anchor branch upward, and to complement its harshness, adds a line of stiff, golden grass reaching out from the arrangement.\n"
"\n"
"Finally, she places a massive chrysanthemum on a bed of moss, the soft bloom safely sheltered beneath the protective canopy of the evergreen."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/ikebana/event_ikebana.tres
msgid "Choose the budding plum, a promise of blooms to come."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/ikebana/event_ikebana.tres
msgid ""
"The florist selects the slender plum branch, dry but for a few tight, pink buds.\n"
"\n"
"She anchors it completely vertical, emphasizing the starkness of the wood, and supports it with a line of pale reeds bowing away leaving a wedge of empty space.\n"
"\n"
"Finally, she adds broad, dark green leaves just above the water level, drawing the eye to the tiny buds, waiting to bloom."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/ikebana/event_ikebana.tres
msgid "Choose the supple willow, graceful in its resilience."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/ikebana/event_ikebana.tres
msgid ""
"The florist selects the supple willow. She coaxes the main stem upward before letting its trailing foliage cascade over the lip of the basin.\n"
"\n"
"To harmonize with the weeping figure, she adds bellflowers that trail closely along the willow's arch.\n"
"\n"
"Finally, she places a cluster of smooth, water-worn stones at the base, to emphasize the resilience in yielding to the flow."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/ikebana/event_ikebana.tres
msgid "Choose a dead branch of unclear origin."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/ikebana/event_ikebana.tres
msgid ""
"The florist selects the withered piece of wood, fated to never bloom again.\n"
"\n"
"She anchors it firmly, treating its twisted form with reverence. Around the base, she places fleshy succulents and tall, crimson wildflowers wrapped intimately around the lifeless wood.\n"
"\n"
"The result is a striking contrast, vibrant new life rising from the unchangeable bones of the past."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/iron_wreck/event_iron_wreck.tres
msgid ""
"The huge metal beast stands forlorn among the dry cracks of the wasteland. Even before the Shattering, these giants were considered ancient, the remnants of a civilization long gone.\n"
"\n"
"Until recently, settlers have avoided coming near them, afraid to disturb ancient curses, but today a group of adventurers and scholars have decided to explore one.\n"
"\n"
"Inside they find the decayed remains of levers and gears, most now fused to the metal walls. One wall is full of racks containing large metal eggs. A few are noticeably heavier."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/iron_wreck/event_iron_wreck.tres
msgid "Retrieve an egg."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/iron_wreck/event_iron_wreck.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers pick the heaviest, best-preserved egg. Its surface is ridged, and a ring of raised metal runs along the middle.\n"
"\n"
"The egg is packed carefully and sent off with the expedition for further study."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/iron_wreck/event_iron_wreck.tres
msgid "Study the construction."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/iron_wreck/event_iron_wreck.tres
msgid ""
"The scholars among the group study the structure of the walls. They find them made of two layers of thick metal plates, held together by rivets as thick as a person's arm.\n"
"\n"
"The metal from which the plates are made is covered with a layer of grime, but once cleaned, the rough surface gleams with a dull silvery sheen. Attempts to scratch it yield no results."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/iron_wreck/event_iron_wreck.tres
msgid "Search for inscriptions."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/iron_wreck/event_iron_wreck.tres
msgid ""
"The scholars among the group study the inside of the giant beast looking for sign of writing, but if any inscriptions ever graced the walls, they no longer survive.\n"
"\n"
"Further search, however, uncovers a compartment with several sheets of a thick, waxy material that resembles smooth paper. On it are detailed drawings of complex mechanisms."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#. Property: label
#: events/generic/iron_wreck/event_iron_wreck.tres
#: events/landmark/mirage_gate/event_mirage_gate.tres
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_hawk_chick.tres
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_water_goat.tres
msgid "Leave it alone."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/iron_wreck/event_iron_wreck.tres
msgid "The group decides to leave the beast alone, letting it continue its vigil over the wasteland."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/kite_fight/event_kite_fight.tres
msgid "The Kite Fight"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/kite_fight/event_kite_fight.tres
msgid ""
"The wind is strong today, but the mood on the field is heated.\n"
"\n"
"Two groups of settlers, the millers and the potters, are engaged in a kite battle. Their strings are coated in glue and crushed pottery shards, designed to saw through an opponent's line.\n"
"\n"
"Wagers are piling up on the sidelines. \"It's all in good fun,\" a young miller argues, bandaging a cut on his finger. \"And besides, they insulted our flour.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/kite_fight/event_kite_fight.tres
msgid "Turn it into an aesthetic competition."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/kite_fight/event_kite_fight.tres
msgid ""
"The town chief intervenes, declaring that cutting strings is easy, but building a masterpiece is hard.\n"
"\n"
"The abrasive strings are replaced, and instead, the kites are judged on stability and paintwork.\n"
"\n"
"The millers end up victorious, with a massive kite depicting their old teacher comically glaring down on the field.\n"
"\n"
"The kite catches the wind perfectly, and is left floating motionless, as if pinned to the sky."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/kite_fight/event_kite_fight.tres
msgid "Ban the abrasive strings."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/kite_fight/event_kite_fight.tres
msgid ""
"\"We cannot afford injured hands,\" the safety warden declares. \"And this rivalry is bound to escalate.\"\n"
"\n"
"The jagged strings are confiscated and replaced with plain hemp. The wagered goods are returned to their owners.\n"
"\n"
"The settlers fly their kites in polite, distinct circles. It is undeniably safer, but many will miss the excitement that punctuated their months of hard labor."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/kite_fight/event_kite_fight.tres
msgid "Coordinate a synchronized display."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/kite_fight/event_kite_fight.tres
msgid ""
"The competitors are challenged not to cut lines, but to line up their kites perfectly parallel.\n"
"\n"
"The new challenge requires intense focus and cooperation, but soon, more groups join in, and the sky is covered with kites dancing in perfect unison.\n"
"\n"
"When the display finally lands, an impromptu celebration breaks out, uniting the former rivals by the difficulty of the challenge."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/kite_fight/event_kite_fight.tres
msgid "Let the rivalry play out."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/kite_fight/event_kite_fight.tres
msgid ""
"The crowd stands back and watches the kites dive and swoop like hawks.\n"
"\n"
"A sharp snap echoes across the field as the potters' line is severed, their kite drifting helplessly into the sky, as cheers and groans erupt.\n"
"\n"
"The rivalry is bound to escalate, but for a moment, everyone forgot the hardship of their daily labor in the thrill of the fight."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/kudzu_harvest/event_kudzu_harvest.tres
msgid "Kudzu Harvest"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/kudzu_harvest/event_kudzu_harvest.tres
msgid ""
"The kudzu harvest has been more than plentiful. The vines threatened to swallow the toolshed by the time they were ripe, and the tubers have grown to the size of a person's thigh.\n"
"\n"
"The tubers can be ground into starch, while the vines could be turned into fiber for baskets or paper.\n"
"\n"
"There aren't enough farmers to process everything, so the settlers have to decide what to focus on."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/kudzu_harvest/event_kudzu_harvest.tres
msgid "Refine the starch and make delicate cakes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/kudzu_harvest/event_kudzu_harvest.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers grind the tubers and wash the starch repeatedly in fresh water until it is chalk-white.\n"
"\n"
"The starch is pressed into nuggets, steamed, and dusted with soybean flour, resulting in sweet, wobbly treats.\n"
"\n"
"\"It's like eating a cloud that fell in the mud,\" a child laughs, poking one of the cakes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/kudzu_harvest/event_kudzu_harvest.tres
msgid "Make baskets out of the vines."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/kudzu_harvest/event_kudzu_harvest.tres
msgid ""
"The tubers are left to compost, returning their nutrients to the soil.\n"
"\n"
"Instead, the settlers harvest the vines, splitting and boiling them to loosen the fibers.\n"
"\n"
"These are then made into sturdy baskets, perfect for holding harvests yet to come."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/kudzu_harvest/event_kudzu_harvest.tres
msgid "Process the stems into paper."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/kudzu_harvest/event_kudzu_harvest.tres
msgid ""
"The tubers are left untouched, ready to sprout again, while the vines are cut.\n"
"\n"
"The woody stems are boiled and beaten into a pulp, then mixed into a slurry. Craftspeople use screens to form thin sheets and dry them into paper.\n"
"\n"
"This paper will be used to make painted screens and sliding doors, perfect to keep houses cool while adding a touch of refinement."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/kudzu_harvest/event_kudzu_harvest.tres
msgid "Boil the tubers into a hearty survival paste."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/kudzu_harvest/event_kudzu_harvest.tres
msgid ""
"There is no time for fancy sweets. The tubers are boiled down into a thick, flavorless, but incredibly filling glue.\n"
"\n"
"It is not a meal anyone will sing songs about, but it will keep the hunger away for a long time."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/laundry/event_laundry.tres
msgid "Laundry Service"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/laundry/event_laundry.tres
msgid ""
"The cloth rinsers are done with their work early today.\n"
"\n"
"They offer to handle the expedition's laundry."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/laundry/event_laundry.tres
msgid "Wash the dirty veil."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/laundry/event_laundry.tres
msgid ""
"The rinsers are puzzled when the only garment they receive is a wedding veil.\n"
"\n"
"Perhaps an explorer couple married during the expedition, they suppose.\n"
"\n"
"The veil is quickly washed in the lake, rinsed again in a bucket of well water, and finally rubbed with yuzu peel. It has never been cleaner."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/laundry/event_laundry.tres
msgid "Wash the overperfumed sleeve."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/laundry/event_laundry.tres
msgid ""
"The rinsers are confused when presented with a single sleeve, not even attached to a robe.\n"
"\n"
"It takes all day to wash away the stench of perfume clinging to the cloth, and by the end there's still a trace remaining, but it is certainly a big improvement."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/laundry/event_laundry.tres
msgid "Wash the ink off a robe."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/laundry/event_laundry.tres
msgid ""
"The rinsers are surprised to receive only a single robe, and surprised again to find it covered in strange and unfamiliar glyphs.\n"
"\n"
"Still, they have a job, and they take it seriously.\n"
"\n"
"After a few washes the ink is mostly gone. It looks more like a single abstract pattern now."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/laundry/event_laundry.tres
msgid "Wash assorted robes and underclothes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/laundry/event_laundry.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers are taken aback by the mountain of garments they receive, but they persevere.\n"
"\n"
"They work late into the night, and the expeditions members are amazed to wake up to stacks and stacks of clean, neatly folded clothes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/leaning_rampart/event_leaning_rampart.tres
msgid "The Crumbling Rampart"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/leaning_rampart/event_leaning_rampart.tres
msgid ""
"One of the old ramparts was too ramshackle to restore when the outpost was resettled, but now it has started to crumble piece by piece.\n"
"\n"
"The stones shift underfoot, and each gust of wind brings a faint groan from the structure. If left alone, it will fall.\n"
"\n"
"Shall we let it fall on our terms, or its own?"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/leaning_rampart/event_leaning_rampart.tres
msgid "Dismantle it."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/leaning_rampart/event_leaning_rampart.tres
msgid ""
"The collapse is carefully planned: bracing, guiding, and disassembling one layer at a time.\n"
"\n"
"It's dirty, brutal work, but when the last stone is pried loose, something glimmers within the wall's hollow: a green, sharp-edged lump of jade."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/leaning_rampart/event_leaning_rampart.tres
msgid "Patch it with scavenged pieces."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/leaning_rampart/event_leaning_rampart.tres
msgid ""
"Workers scour the ruins for usable remnants: broken tiles, crooked beams, and stones just the right size to fit the cracks.\n"
"\n"
"It isn't elegant, but it holds.\n"
"\n"
"In the end, more tiles are found than needed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/leaning_rampart/event_leaning_rampart.tres
msgid "Rebuild it properly."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/leaning_rampart/event_leaning_rampart.tres
msgid ""
"Resources are brought from the nearby settlement. Proper tools, sturdy timber, hewn stone.\n"
"\n"
"As the final tile is laid, the workers look on in pride.\n"
"\n"
"This piece of the past is no longer a ruin."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/leaning_rampart/event_leaning_rampart.tres
msgid "Do nothing."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/leaning_rampart/event_leaning_rampart.tres
msgid ""
"The wall groans, shivers, then settles.\n"
"\n"
"For a while, it still stands. But weeks later, during a windstorm, it collapses with a crack like thunder.\n"
"\n"
"No one is hurt, but some of the shelters lose their windbreak."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/leaving_hive/event_leaving_hive.tres
msgid "A Hum in the Air"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/leaving_hive/event_leaving_hive.tres
msgid ""
"At first, the beekeepers think it is a swarm, but more and more bees join in, producing a hum loud enough to wake the locals.\n"
"\n"
"One of the older hives is absconding. It isn't clear what prompted them to leave, but it's too late to stop them.\n"
"\n"
"Perhaps the hive had grown too full, or mites have infested their home. Or maybe the bees had simply decided they didn't like the scenery."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/leaving_hive/event_leaving_hive.tres
msgid "Study the empty hive."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/leaving_hive/event_leaving_hive.tres
msgid ""
"The beekeepers inspect the empty hive for damage.\n"
"\n"
"There's no sign of mites or other parasites, but they find the cells uncapped and emptied, the wax caps jagged, as if chewed through. It appears that this hive has been robbed by bees from another hive.\n"
"\n"
"The remaining hives are spread further apart, to discourage such unneighborly conduct."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/leaving_hive/event_leaving_hive.tres
msgid "Set new hives to welcome the swarm."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/leaving_hive/event_leaving_hive.tres
msgid ""
"It is a scramble to fetch empty hives from storage and spread them around the meadow, but the keepers are fast enough.\n"
"\n"
"The bees stop on a nearby bush for a while, but eventually make their way to one of the new hives, the one furthest from their old home.\n"
"\n"
"The old, empty hive is retired."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/leaving_hive/event_leaving_hive.tres
msgid "Compose a poem for the occasion."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/leaving_hive/event_leaving_hive.tres
msgid ""
"At twilight, the settlers gather near the old hive. One of them steps forward and recites a short verse:\n"
"\n"
"The hive is empty.\n"
"Fragrant still, but echoless.\n"
"One bee circles back\n"
"As if to remind,\n"
"Every ending is a start."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/leaving_hive/event_leaving_hive.tres
msgid "Collect the leftover honey."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/leaving_hive/event_leaving_hive.tres
msgid ""
"The hive left behind is light. Still, a few honeycombs remain, sweet and clean.\n"
"\n"
"The harvest is very modest, but at least it isn't a complete loss."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/lotus_lovers/event_lotus_lovers.tres
msgid "The Lotus Decision"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/lotus_lovers/event_lotus_lovers.tres
msgid ""
"The air above the lake is fresh with the sweet, subtle scent of lotus blooms. A couple is standing on the stone bridge, gazing silently at the green expanse below.\n"
"\n"
"A courier had arrived from the capital with extraordinary news: one of the women has been offered the position of Head Record-Keeper, her lifelong dream. However, her partner cannot leave her ailing grandmother, who is much too frail for a trek to the capital.\n"
"\n"
"Silence stretches as neither has the courage to voice the decision they must make before the courier departs at dawn."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/lotus_lovers/event_lotus_lovers.tres
msgid "Decline the position to stay together."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/lotus_lovers/event_lotus_lovers.tres
msgid ""
"The scholar delivers her decision to the courier with a pang of grief, but the pain will soften in the warm embrace awaiting her at home.\n"
"\n"
"She has decided to lead a life of wistful, quiet contentment.\n"
"\n"
"The grand archives will have to be filled by someone else."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/lotus_lovers/event_lotus_lovers.tres
msgid "Attempt a long-distance relationship."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/lotus_lovers/event_lotus_lovers.tres
msgid ""
"The desperate lovers refuse to say goodbye. They make a pact: one will go to the capital to secure a future, while the other stays to ensure her grandmother lives out her life in comfort.\n"
"\n"
"Before they part, they unspool a length of red thread and tie it around each other's wrists. The small gesture is a promise for them to hold onto when their love is far away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/lotus_lovers/event_lotus_lovers.tres
msgid "Elope to the capital together."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/lotus_lovers/event_lotus_lovers.tres
msgid ""
"In the dead of night, they pack a single bag and slip away. Their trip is uneventful, and the scholar promptly assumes her new position.\n"
"\n"
"Not a month passes before a letter arrives, announcing that the grandmother had passed away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/lotus_lovers/event_lotus_lovers.tres
msgid "End the relationship so each can fulfill their duty."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/lotus_lovers/event_lotus_lovers.tres
msgid ""
"They stand on the bridge and face the harsh reality of the world they live in. Love alone cannot cure the grandmother, or fill the archives.\n"
"\n"
"They hold each other one last time, tears falling onto the broad green leaves below, and walk away carrying the heavy, hollow weight of duty."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/magic_mushrooms/event_magic_mushrooms.tres
msgid "Little Blue Figures"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/magic_mushrooms/event_magic_mushrooms.tres
msgid ""
"The foragers have discovered a new kind of mushroom in the glade. Plump, brown, and juicy, they sizzle when cooked and fill the air with a glorious aroma.\n"
"\n"
"As these mushrooms become a major food source in the budding settlement, several settlers report that they start seeing spirits after their meals, little blue figures flitting around.\n"
"\n"
"The priests are overjoyed at this window into the spirit world, but the healers claim that these visions are dangerous, and demand the mushrooms be banned."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/magic_mushrooms/event_magic_mushrooms.tres
msgid "Continue using the mushrooms as a staple food."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/magic_mushrooms/event_magic_mushrooms.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers continue to harvest the mushrooms, consuming them almost daily.\n"
"\n"
"Only a few people suffer the strange visions, and once the novelty wears off, they mostly ignore them.\n"
"\n"
"The mushrooms do become a draw for pilgrims eager to commune with the spirits, though most are disappointed when they end up unaffected."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/magic_mushrooms/event_magic_mushrooms.tres
msgid "Only use the mushrooms during spiritual ceremonies."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/magic_mushrooms/event_magic_mushrooms.tres
msgid ""
"The local priests adopt the mushrooms into their spirit communion ceremonies. The rare few who can see the spirits consult them about portents and omens, sharing their knowledge with the rest of the order, and incidentally quickly rising to positions of leadership.\n"
"\n"
"A little mushroom-shaped shrine is built, and pilgrims arrive regularly to pay their respects to the little blue people guarding this town."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/magic_mushrooms/event_magic_mushrooms.tres
msgid "Ban the mushrooms completely."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/magic_mushrooms/event_magic_mushrooms.tres
msgid ""
"The healers insist that the mushrooms are dangerous. Who knows what these spirits might make people do.\n"
"\n"
"After some deliberation, the town council assents and consumption of these mushrooms is declared banned, punishable by exile."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/magic_mushrooms/event_magic_mushrooms.tres
msgid "Discourage their use, but leave the decision up to each person."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/magic_mushrooms/event_magic_mushrooms.tres
msgid ""
"Once the effects of the mushrooms become widely known, most settlers turn to other foods, wary of being among the few who get affected.\n"
"\n"
"Some who received visions from the mushrooms still consume them, but tend to do so in secret, afraid of being judged."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/mapping/event_mapping.tres
msgid "Lines on a Map"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/mapping/event_mapping.tres
msgid ""
"The guild is planning its own expedition to map the shard, and compose one grand, official map.\n"
"\n"
"As the explorers look out across the landscape, a debate breaks out.\n"
"\n"
"Some argue the map should be precise, with every river and valley marked. Others say it must highlight fertile lands and safe routes. A few grin and suggest a more thrilling approach: mark the mysteries, the rumored beasts, the unexplained ruins.\n"
"\n"
"A veteran shrugs and says, \"Why not just let everyone draw what they've seen?\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/mapping/event_mapping.tres
msgid "Focus on accurate geography."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/mapping/event_mapping.tres
msgid ""
"Journals are unpacked, sketches compared, and arguments are held over the length of each stream.\n"
"\n"
"When the ink dries, the map is a marvel of precision, peaks, canyons, and trails laid out with confidence.\n"
"\n"
"It may not be exciting, but it will help travelers find their way."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/mapping/event_mapping.tres
msgid "Highlight the most fertile and habitable lands."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/mapping/event_mapping.tres
msgid ""
"The map blooms with green patches and golden marks: places where the soil is rich, the winds are kind, and fresh water flows.\n"
"\n"
"Paths between them are carefully drawn.\n"
"\n"
"It may not tempt explorers, but settlers will follow this map like a promise."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/mapping/event_mapping.tres
msgid "Emphasize sites of danger, mystery, and excitement."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/generic/mapping/event_mapping.tres
msgid "Get a <term:card.dare> or <term:card.perilous> <term_lower:glyph>"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/mapping/event_mapping.tres
msgid ""
"The map is filled with swirling marks and jagged notations: cave entrances, spots where past explorers disappeared, and alleged habitats of mythical beasts.\n"
"\n"
"Still, this mess of guesswork and outright fiction can't help but instill a thrill for exploration."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/mapping/event_mapping.tres
msgid "Let each adventurer mark what they remember."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/mapping/event_mapping.tres
msgid ""
"The map becomes a patchwork of memory: a wrong turn that led to a waterfall, a shortcut that required a rope, a pond that one settler insists is shaped like a bear.\n"
"\n"
"It's not consistent. It's not entirely useful. But it's genuine, in its own way."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/mary_poppins/event_mary_poppins.tres
msgid "When the Wind Changes"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/mary_poppins/event_mary_poppins.tres
msgid ""
"Onlookers gawk as a young woman drifts down from the sky, her hand gripping an umbrella. She folds it and taps it against her shoulder.\n"
"\n"
"Despite her rich dress, she introduces herself as a nun. When questioned about her arrival, she curtly replies \"I never explain anything.\"\n"
"\n"
"She takes one glance at the notice board, then walks to the house of a widowed merchant, accepting a job as his children's tutor. Before the sun sets, she decides to take the children on an outing.\n"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/mary_poppins/event_mary_poppins.tres
msgid "Take them to the wilderness."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/mary_poppins/event_mary_poppins.tres
msgid ""
"The nun takes the children away from the town and makes them contemplate the trees for hours.\n"
"\n"
"The trips repeat daily. The children kneel on the ground and learn to calm their minds, letting racing thoughts pass, like leaves floating down the stream.\n"
"\n"
"She makes them chop wood and carry water, until they are too tired to get into trouble.\n"
"\n"
"One day, her lessons delivered, she leaves. \"The wind has changed,\" she says."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/mary_poppins/event_mary_poppins.tres
msgid "Take them to the mountains."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/mary_poppins/event_mary_poppins.tres
msgid ""
"The nun takes the children to the highlands, away from the bustle of the town.\n"
"\n"
"She makes them contemplate their surroundings: the does grazing down by the stream, the rays of sunshine, fading as the sun sinks below the horizon, the Cloud Sea stretching far into the distance.\n"
"\n"
"As the trips repeat, she makes them vocalize sacred sounds at different pitches, and teaches them holy chants. When a storm comes during one such trip, she leads them in a chant enumerating the practices most favored by the Enlightened One.\n"
"\n"
"One day the settlers find the merchant's house empty, with no sign of him, the children, or the nun."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/mary_poppins/event_mary_poppins.tres
msgid "Take them through the town."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/mary_poppins/event_mary_poppins.tres
msgid ""
"The nun listens as the merchant lists rules that his children must follow, gives schedules for their lessons, and lays out the plan for them to take over the family business.\n"
"\n"
"Once the father leaves, the nun gathers his ledgers, ties them to bamboo poles, and strides into the square with the children in tow. They spend the rest of the day flying these kites, before finally letting the wind claim them.\n"
"\n"
"The next day the merchant discovers his ledgers gone. Furious, he disowns the children on the spot and sends them off with the nun to her monastery."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/material_science/event_material_science.tres
msgid "Material Science"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/material_science/event_material_science.tres
msgid ""
"The forge's master smith is hosting a group of scholars from another settlement. Together, they are studying a variety of metals and exploring ways to create new alloys.\n"
"\n"
"Although their learning is exemplary, their experiments are limited by the lack of raw materials.\n"
"\n"
"They would welcome contributions of exotic substances to study."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/material_science/event_material_science.tres
msgid "Contribute the Heavy Chunk."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/material_science/event_material_science.tres
msgid ""
"The smith is immediately impressed by the malleability of the strange material, and the ease with which it melts, but he finds that it lacks the solidity needed for most practical applications.\n"
"\n"
"He tries mixing it into a variety of alloys, until he hit upon a discovery. Mixed with antimony, it retains its low melting point, and becomes sturdy when cooled.\n"
"\n"
"The scholars quickly find a use for the new alloy: a much more durable replacement for wooden printing blocks, which can be be cast into far more intricate shapes than a carver could ever hope to produce."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/material_science/event_material_science.tres
msgid "Contribute the Metal Egg."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/material_science/event_material_science.tres
msgid ""
"The smith studies the egg until he determines that the ring around its center is a much softer metal, removable with relative ease.\n"
"\n"
"Inside is a waxy substance of unknown composition that burns brightly when heated.\n"
"\n"
"Perhaps such eggs could be harvested to make fireworks."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/material_science/event_material_science.tres
msgid "Contribute the Curious Stone."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/material_science/event_material_science.tres
msgid ""
"The smith examines the scale-shaped stone and quickly determines that it isn't a metal, despite the sheen.\n"
"\n"
"The scholars go one step further, and confirm that the substance is incredibly hard, able to scratch any surface they try it on. However, it is brittle enough to be easily crushed. The resulting powder is a phenomenal abrasive, able to polish any other material without wearing over time."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/material_science/event_material_science.tres
msgid "Leave them to their studies."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/material_science/event_material_science.tres
msgid ""
"The group continues their studies.\n"
"\n"
"Perhaps in time they will revolutionize the technology on this shard."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/moistened_sleeves/event_moistened_sleeves.tres
msgid "The Tale of Moistened Sleeves"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/moistened_sleeves/event_moistened_sleeves.tres
msgid ""
"Every morning at the Storytellers Camp, the same young man takes the stage.\n"
"\n"
"The scion of a long, noble family from the Old World, he performs traditional koto pieces that sound suspiciously similar, recites breathless poetry about women whose names change nightly, and weeps loudly into the sleeves of his over-perfumed robes.\n"
"\n"
"At first, the settlers were sympathetic. Then the headaches started."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/moistened_sleeves/event_moistened_sleeves.tres
msgid "Convince him that perfumed robes are out of fashion."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/moistened_sleeves/event_moistened_sleeves.tres
msgid ""
"A few settlers quietly suggest that the floral cloud around him is actually [i]very last era[/i].\n"
"\n"
"This strikes him like a lightning bolt of revelation.\n"
"\n"
"The next time he arrives in stark undyed cloth, proclaiming a new era of \"pure scentlessness\" and \"emotionally astringent aestheticism\".\n"
"\n"
"He still cries into his sleeves, but now they're hempen."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/moistened_sleeves/event_moistened_sleeves.tres
msgid "Mention that his latest \"lost love\" is alive nearby."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/moistened_sleeves/event_moistened_sleeves.tres
msgid ""
"As he sobs while reciting \"Cicada Shells and the Echo of Her Name\", someone offhandedly remarks that the woman he's invoking - Lady Yukako, this week - is reportedly thriving in a nearby settlement.\n"
"\n"
"His eyes widen, his sleeve halfway to his face. \"Then... perhaps I must... make amends!\" he cries.\n"
"\n"
"He dramatically dons his travel cloak, weeps into his sleeve one final time, and sets off. In the direction away from the aforementioned settlement.\n"
"\n"
"He doesn't even stop to pick up his koto."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/moistened_sleeves/event_moistened_sleeves.tres
msgid "Convince him that the poems must be recorded."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/moistened_sleeves/event_moistened_sleeves.tres
msgid ""
"A group of settlers, stone-faced, praise his genius and suggest the world is not ready to lose such brilliance.\n"
"\n"
"\"The verses... must be preserved!\" He gasps, and retreats to his tent for days.\n"
"\n"
"A week later, a bound manuscript appears at the campfire. The title reads: \"Moonlight on a Frozen Sleeve: 213 Verses of Divine Despair.\"\n"
"\n"
"No one musters the patience to read past the introduction."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/moistened_sleeves/event_moistened_sleeves.tres
msgid "Grin and bear it."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/moistened_sleeves/event_moistened_sleeves.tres
msgid ""
"The performances continue.\n"
"\n"
"One morning he arrives wearing three layers of sleeves (\"to contain the moisture\").\n"
"\n"
"Another day, he presents a new form of poetry based on sobbing rhythm alone.\n"
"\n"
"Many stop coming to the campfire. Newcomers ask whether it's normal for poems to last over forty stanzas.\n"
"\n"
"The koto goes mysteriously missing."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/moss_art/event_moss_art.tres
msgid "The Moss Dragon"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/moss_art/event_moss_art.tres
msgid ""
"Two men are gathering moss in the canyon, sitting in large baskets suspended by ropes. As one of them prepares to scrape another handful from the wet stone, he pauses and looks at the wall in surprise.\n"
"\n"
"Further along the cliff face the moss is cleared in a pattern that looks strikingly like a dragon tied into a knot, its scales clumps of raised moss."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/moss_art/event_moss_art.tres
msgid "Add to the image."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/moss_art/event_moss_art.tres
msgid ""
"The men's faces break out into grins, and they take turns adding details to the dragon.\n"
"\n"
"One scrapes away a line, forking it at the end, and suddenly the dragon has a long curled tongue.\n"
"\n"
"The other presses two clumps of moss into place and the dragon looks on, cross-eyed.\n"
"\n"
"They laugh so hard their baskets begin to sway."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/moss_art/event_moss_art.tres
msgid "Declare it a work of art."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/moss_art/event_moss_art.tres
msgid ""
"The men decide that the image must be the work of a great artist.\n"
"\n"
"They return to the settlement to tell their fellow settlers of the strange artwork they found on the canyon wall.\n"
"\n"
"Before the day ends, there's a queue of people lined up for a chance to go down in the baskets and admire the sight."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/moss_art/event_moss_art.tres
msgid "Consider it a message from the spirits."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/moss_art/event_moss_art.tres
msgid ""
"The men see a deeper message in the image.\n"
"\n"
"The canyon's spirit is widely known to grant wisdom through the cracks in the wall, so this pattern cannot be a coincidence.\n"
"\n"
"When they consult the local priestess, she confirms their guess. The dragon represents wisdom, she explains, so the spirit is saying that scholars have tied wisdom into knots, preventing the common people from learning."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/moss_art/event_moss_art.tres
msgid "Remove the moss dragon."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/moss_art/event_moss_art.tres
msgid ""
"After the initial surprise wears out, the men decide that some of the village youths must have tried to prank them.\n"
"\n"
"They grumble as they scrape every last bit of moss that makes up the pattern."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/mulberries/event_mulberries.tres
msgid "Multipurpose Mulberries"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/mulberries/event_mulberries.tres
msgid ""
"The mulberry harvest is shared between the humans, who collect the berries, and the silkworms, who feast on the leaves.\n"
"\n"
"The silkworm carers want to pluck most of the leaves for their worms, but leaving the bushes bare risks stunting their growth and leading to a poor berry harvest.\n"
"\n"
"The mulberries are one of the only sweet treats that the scrubland provides, and the settlers are eagerly awaiting their arrival."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/mulberries/event_mulberries.tres
msgid "Favor the silkworms."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/mulberries/event_mulberries.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers prioritize their silk production, and decide to risk a poor berry harvest.\n"
"\n"
"The bushes are stripped bare, the berries doomed to wither on the vine.\n"
"\n"
"The folks harvesting the leaves do manage to pluck the occasional early ripened ones as they work."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/mulberries/event_mulberries.tres
msgid "Wait until the berry harvest before plucking the leaves."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/mulberries/event_mulberries.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers forbid leaf harvesting until the berries are ripe.\n"
"\n"
"Once the berries are gathered, the silkworm carers pluck the leaves.\n"
"\n"
"Unfortunately, the silkworms refuse these, unimpressed by their lack of freshness."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/mulberries/event_mulberries.tres
msgid "Leave the bushes with the best berries unplucked."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/mulberries/event_mulberries.tres
msgid ""
"The farmers carefully inspect each bush and mark ones that seem likely to produce the most berries. The harvest will be meager, but it's an efficient use of resources.\n"
"\n"
"The unmarked bushes are sacrificed to the worms."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/mulberries/event_mulberries.tres
msgid "Favor the berries."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/mulberries/event_mulberries.tres
msgid ""
"The silkworms are put on a strict diet and indoctrinated into an ascetic lifestyle.\n"
"\n"
"When the berries ripen, the settlers will fill their pantries with mulberry wine and stuff themselves with millet dumplings topped with fresh berries."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/pale_weaver/event_pale_weaver.tres
msgid "The Pale Weaver"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/pale_weaver/event_pale_weaver.tres
msgid ""
"Women are weaving tatami mats as the cool evening breeze rustles the trees, scattering a flock of birds into the sunset. Each woman warms her fingers inside her sleeve before taking up a new bundle of reeds.\n"
"\n"
"They laugh softly as they discuss the latest happenings, exchanging comments and little jokes. Despite their light manner, all but one of them are hiding grief.\n"
"\n"
"One smiles faintly, however, her skin pale yet her nose and cheeks bright red. She coughs into her sleeve before joining in the laughter."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/pale_weaver/event_pale_weaver.tres
msgid "Confront her."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/pale_weaver/event_pale_weaver.tres
msgid ""
"The weavers confront their friend about her sickness. The pale woman smiles gently, looking relieved. \"I suppose there's no use hiding it,\" she says.\n"
"\n"
"The next day, she is not there at her usual spot.\n"
"\n"
"At her hut, the weavers find her heavy traveling robe missing, and the rice sacks suspiciously light."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/pale_weaver/event_pale_weaver.tres
msgid "Lighten her workload."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/pale_weaver/event_pale_weaver.tres
msgid ""
"The pale weaver's friends pretend not to notice when she coughs or pauses to catch her breath.\n"
"\n"
"They give her the lightest bundles, and pass her the softest reeds to weave. A small mercy."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/pale_weaver/event_pale_weaver.tres
msgid "Isolate her."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/pale_weaver/event_pale_weaver.tres
msgid ""
"The women love their friend, but they fear contagion.\n"
"\n"
"They inform the settlement's healer, who gently instructs the ailing woman to stay away from public places until she gets better.\n"
"\n"
"The funeral is held the following month."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/pale_weaver/event_pale_weaver.tres
msgid "Let her keep her peace."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/pale_weaver/event_pale_weaver.tres
msgid "The friends are careful not to speak of sadness or endings. The women let her laugh, weave, and pretend as long as she can."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/persimmons/event_persimmons.tres
msgid "The Fallen Fruit"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/persimmons/event_persimmons.tres
msgid ""
"The harvest was late. By the time anyone noticed, the grove's bounty had begun to fall.\n"
"\n"
"Bright persimmons now lie bruised and soft beneath the trees, their skins splitting in the sun.\n"
"\n"
"There's enough food in the stores, but the elders remember lean winters, and say letting this much spoil is a betrayal.\n"
"\n"
"Youngsters point to the scent of ferment and the slowly gathering wasps, and suggest that the fruit has already chosen its fate."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/persimmons/event_persimmons.tres
msgid "Burn the fruit as a ceremonial offering."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/persimmons/event_persimmons.tres
msgid ""
"The fallen fruit is gathered into neat mounds.\n"
"\n"
"Fire is lit, and prayers are murmured, some old, some invented on the spot.\n"
"\n"
"The ashes smell faintly of sugar.\n"
"\n"
"The elders shake their heads, saying at least it should have fed someone.\n"
"\n"
"The younger settlers mutter that spirits belong in the Old World."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/persimmons/event_persimmons.tres
msgid "Leave the fruit for the animals."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/persimmons/event_persimmons.tres
msgid ""
"The fruit is left where it lies.\n"
"\n"
"Over the weeks, deer wander close. Birds come at dawn. A few wild boars dig in the piles.\n"
"\n"
"The locals avoid the grove until all the fruit is eaten."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/persimmons/event_persimmons.tres
msgid "Sort and mulch what can't be saved."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/persimmons/event_persimmons.tres
msgid ""
"Settlers carefully gather the firm fruit and lay the rest in compost pits.\n"
"\n"
"The scent changes, inviting grumbles from the townspeople.\n"
"\n"
"When the soil is turned weeks later, it's already richer."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/persimmons/event_persimmons.tres
msgid "Gather everything and store it."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/persimmons/event_persimmons.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers work hard, filling baskets and jars and sealed clay urns.\n"
"\n"
"Some of the fruit is still good, but not much.\n"
"\n"
"By the end of the week, the smell of rot seeps into the granary, inviting flies. It is soon unofficially renamed \"the sticky room\"."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/petroglyph_cave/event_petroglyph_cave.tres
msgid "Into the Petroglyph Cave"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/petroglyph_cave/event_petroglyph_cave.tres
msgid ""
"Curious settlers shuffle into the petroglyph cave. The main chamber is large, the walls covered with a variety of glyphs. Someone in ages past has reinforced the ceiling, and the wood still holds despite the dampness.\n"
"\n"
"The cave narrows in the back, leading deeper into the dark. The symbols there are fainter, the carvings subtler, but it seems others once descended further."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/petroglyph_cave/event_petroglyph_cave.tres
msgid "Follow the faint sound of water."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/petroglyph_cave/event_petroglyph_cave.tres
msgid ""
"The most adventurous of the group trace the drip, step by step. The passage narrows, then widens sharply.\n"
"\n"
"An underground river rushes through the stone, vanishing into a spiraling whirlpool.\n"
"\n"
"Etched above it is a glyph everyone recognizes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/petroglyph_cave/event_petroglyph_cave.tres
msgid "Search for sources of light."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/petroglyph_cave/event_petroglyph_cave.tres
msgid ""
"A few enterprising settlers block the way behind to shut out light, then wait.\n"
"\n"
"Slowly, a faint, greenish light becomes visible in the darkness.\n"
"\n"
"As they descend, glowing fungi mark a sloping tunnel. Beyond it are more glyphs carved into damp pebbles.\n"
"\n"
"One of the glyphs is glowing. It appears that a strange lichen has grown within the carving, giving it a soft green glow."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/petroglyph_cave/event_petroglyph_cave.tres
msgid "Secure a route downward."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/petroglyph_cave/event_petroglyph_cave.tres
msgid ""
"A crack in the rock quickly expands into a shaft disappearing into the darkness below.\n"
"\n"
"Safety experts rig a descent with rope and wedges. It's slow going, but steady.\n"
"\n"
"At the bottom is a new chamber. Half-finished statues litter the cave floor: animal limbs, human faces, and shapes none of the settlers recognize.\n"
"\n"
"One of these stands out in particular: a peculiarly accurate heart carved from a single piece of stone."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/petroglyph_cave/event_petroglyph_cave.tres
msgid "Stay near the surface and record the findings."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/petroglyph_cave/event_petroglyph_cave.tres
msgid ""
"Everyone remains in the main chamber, mapping every symbol and comparing their forms to modern glyphs.\n"
"\n"
"The mystery won't be solved yet, but the record will endure."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/reservoir_of_leisure/event_reservoir_of_leisure.tres
msgid "A Reservoir of Leisure"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/reservoir_of_leisure/event_reservoir_of_leisure.tres
msgid ""
"The reservoir was built to hold back disaster, but it has grown to serve as a place of leisure instead.\n"
"\n"
"Stalls line the banks, selling juicy dumplings and cold barley tea. The air is filled with the rustle of leaves and relaxed chatter.\n"
"\n"
"A safety warden frowns at the crowd, tapping his ledger. \"If a fire starts, these benches will block the bucket brigade. This is a hazard, not a park.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"If a fire starts, we'll douse it with tea!\" the keeper laughs. \"Come, sit!\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/reservoir_of_leisure/event_reservoir_of_leisure.tres
msgid "Let the stalls remain."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/reservoir_of_leisure/event_reservoir_of_leisure.tres
msgid ""
"The safety warden shrugs his shoulders and plops down onto a crowded bench.\n"
"\n"
"The stall keeper serves tea for the whole crowd, pouring from a huge jug until the tea spills into the saucers below.\n"
"\n"
"\"There is time for strictness,\" he says, \"but there must also be time for excess.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/reservoir_of_leisure/event_reservoir_of_leisure.tres
msgid "Move the stalls onto floating platforms."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/reservoir_of_leisure/event_reservoir_of_leisure.tres
msgid ""
"A craftswoman from the crowd comes up with a compromise: lash empty barrels and timber together, pushing the stalls out onto the water itself.\n"
"\n"
"Customers now balance on makeshift pontoons, dipping their feet directly into the cool reservoir while they eat.\n"
"\n"
"The banks are clear for the fire brigade, and the floating tea stalls quickly become the talk of the town."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/reservoir_of_leisure/event_reservoir_of_leisure.tres
msgid "Rearrange the stalls to ensure access."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/reservoir_of_leisure/event_reservoir_of_leisure.tres
msgid ""
"The stalls are allowed to remain, but the wardens insist that they be moved to leave clear access paths.\n"
"\n"
"Fire lanes are set up with bamboo fences, which soon become adorned with festive lanterns.\n"
"\n"
"The crowd flows smoothly, the wardens have their clear paths, and the stall owners find they can serve customers even faster."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/reservoir_of_leisure/event_reservoir_of_leisure.tres
msgid "Clear all stalls from the banks."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/reservoir_of_leisure/event_reservoir_of_leisure.tres
msgid ""
"The warden remains unconvinced and orders the stalls moved away.\n"
"\n"
"\"The risk is too great to ignore,\" he insists.\n"
"\n"
"Reluctantly, the settlers help the stall keepers pack up their bowls and carts, and the crowd soon disperses, grumbling about the heat."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/river_festival_flood/event_river_festival_flood.tres
msgid "When the River Rose"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/river_festival_flood/event_river_festival_flood.tres
msgid ""
"The rains came hard this season.\n"
"\n"
"The river swelled, spilled, and took more than it should have. A few homes were washed away. Stores of grain, precious records, and whole crates of tools were swallowed up.\n"
"\n"
"As festival season arrives, settlers debate whether the celebration should be canceled, or if this is the time it is needed most."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/river_festival_flood/event_river_festival_flood.tres
msgid "Use expedition resources to host the festival."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/river_festival_flood/event_river_festival_flood.tres
msgid ""
"Donations are gathered from across the land.\n"
"\n"
"The expedition members help shape the floats, craft new lanterns from spare scrolls, and pass bowls of simple but warm food along the river's edge.\n"
"\n"
"The festival is smaller in size, but not in spirit.\n"
"\n"
"Grief softens as singing resounds along the muddy banks."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/river_festival_flood/event_river_festival_flood.tres
msgid "Cancel the festival to focus on recovery."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/river_festival_flood/event_river_festival_flood.tres
msgid ""
"No lanterns are lit. No river songs are sung.\n"
"\n"
"Instead, walls are mended, floors swept, and water lines rerouted.\n"
"\n"
"Even the rice paper from the lanterns is recycled for screens, leaving behind empty frames resting by the riverside."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/river_festival_flood/event_river_festival_flood.tres
msgid "Hold a tiny ceremony."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/river_festival_flood/event_river_festival_flood.tres
msgid ""
"The ceremony is performed in the evening, with all th settlers gathered on the bank.\n"
"\n"
"It consists of a single lit lantern floating away down the stream, and a half-forgotten song chanted by the priest."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/river_festival_flood/event_river_festival_flood.tres
msgid "Hold the festival as if nothing happened."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/river_festival_flood/event_river_festival_flood.tres
msgid ""
"Decorations hang limp from broken rafters.\n"
"\n"
"The food runs out before sundown.\n"
"\n"
"A few lanterns sputter out, and more than a few sink.\n"
"\n"
"Whispers of \"this is a waste\" and \"we should've waited\" spread through the town."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#. Property: name
#: events/generic/rocks_reply/event_rocks_reply.tres
#: stage/spots/canyon/upgrade_canyon_3_rocks_reply.tres
msgid "The Rock's Reply"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/rocks_reply/event_rocks_reply.tres
msgid ""
"The cracks in the wall of this canyon look suspiciously like written characters. Folks claim that if one carves a question at dusk, by sunrise new cracks will appear as a response.\n"
"\n"
"Several of the settlers want to give this a try, each with a different question to ask."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/rocks_reply/event_rocks_reply.tres
msgid "Choose the one who fears death."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/rocks_reply/event_rocks_reply.tres
msgid ""
"Their question is clear, almost clinical: when, how, and why.\n"
"\n"
"At dawn, the wall bears new cracks: five parallel lines. Just enough to know the stone understood.\n"
"\n"
"The settler says nothing and simply sits down, dejected. When he stands up, he has a little splinter of stone in his hand."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/rocks_reply/event_rocks_reply.tres
msgid "Choose the one who wonders about the wall's nature."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/rocks_reply/event_rocks_reply.tres
msgid ""
"\"What are you?\" the question reads, simple and to the point.\n"
"\n"
"The cracks that appear at dawn are complicated, but a scholar is willing to study them.\n"
"\n"
"After hours of tracing and comparison, she finally declares success. The cracks, she says, bear a striking resemblance to an ancient form of a familiar glyph."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/rocks_reply/event_rocks_reply.tres
msgid "Choose the one seeking safety."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/rocks_reply/event_rocks_reply.tres
msgid ""
"The settler carves a careful plea: \"How do we best protect the expedition?\"\n"
"\n"
"That night, new cracks appear. At first no one is able to make any sense of them, but finally someone suggests that they are a map with a marked path. Once followed, the expedition finds itself on a ridge with perfect sightlines, ideal for studying the whole canyon."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/rocks_reply/event_rocks_reply.tres
msgid "Watch the wall all night."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/generic/rocks_reply/event_rocks_reply.tres
msgid "Chance of a choice of high rarity glyphs"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/rocks_reply/event_rocks_reply.tres
msgid ""
"The expedition camps by the canyon wall, setting a watch through the night. When the dawn arrives, the wall appears unchanged.\n"
"\n"
"Some say they saw movement in the dust, and copy what they thought the pattern looked like."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/ropeways/event_ropeways.tres
msgid "The Flying Baskets"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/ropeways/event_ropeways.tres
msgid ""
"The settlement is separated from its fields by a deep valley. The villagers have stretched ropes between the cliffs and attached baskets that could be pulled from one side to the other. \n"
"\n"
"As harvest time approaches, the villagers face a new problem. The children of the settlement have discovered that playing in the baskets is their favorite way to pass the time. They spend their entire days racing each other across the gorge and inventing new games in their baskets.\n"
"\n"
"The farmers shake their heads in exasperation as baskets are left stranded on the wrong side of the valley. Their harvest loads end up delayed, the fruits and vegetables left to wilt in the sun."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/ropeways/event_ropeways.tres
msgid "Allow the children to continue."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/ropeways/event_ropeways.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers decide that the ropeways belong to all of the village, not just the farmers.\n"
"\n"
"The children delight in their freedom, racing across the valley like birds in their flying baskets.\n"
"\n"
"One child in particular becomes highly skilled at maintaining the ropes and pulleys, having spent so much time fiddling with them."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/ropeways/event_ropeways.tres
msgid "Craft additional baskets."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/ropeways/event_ropeways.tres
msgid ""
"The farmers gather wood and rope, and commission extra baskets from the artisans.\n"
"\n"
"The work takes time, but soon there are enough baskets to carry both harvests and children with no delays, making the sky ropeways busier than ever."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/ropeways/event_ropeways.tres
msgid "Give the children responsibilities."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/ropeways/event_ropeways.tres
msgid ""
"Rather than banning the games, the villagers appoint the children as keepers of the ropeways. It becomes their duty to ensure the baskets are available whenever the harvests arrive.\n"
"\n"
"At first the children complain about the responsibility. But soon, they begin competing to see who can move the most loads across the valley each day. The adults and children alike look on with pride at the ingenuity.\n"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/ropeways/event_ropeways.tres
msgid "Forbid the games."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/ropeways/event_ropeways.tres
msgid ""
"The villagers prohibit the children from using the sky ropeways for games anymore.\n"
"\n"
"The harvest work resumes as it always has, but the farmers miss the sound of the merry laughter that used to echo among the rocks."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/salt_gatherers/event_salt_gatherers.tres
msgid "The Salt Sisters"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/salt_gatherers/event_salt_gatherers.tres
msgid ""
"Every morning, salters head to the flats to fill their buckets with pale crystals and bring back the treasure to the village by sundown.\n"
"\n"
"Among these salters are two sisters. The elder, Akiko, works without complaint and returns home with salt crusting her sleeves and sandals every evening. The younger, Haruko, often leaves her bucket half-filled, and spends her time tracing patterns on the ground with a length of string. When merchants come into town, she often leaves her sister behind, and spends her day convincing the merchants to buy more salt.\n"
"\n"
"Akiko resents working alone on market days, while Haruko insists that a merchant's first impression is worth more than a bucket of salt."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/salt_gatherers/event_salt_gatherers.tres
msgid "Akiko is right."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/salt_gatherers/event_salt_gatherers.tres
msgid ""
"Akiko lays down her buckets and refuses to return to the flats until Haruko agrees to work beside her, even on market days.\n"
"\n"
"The buckets remain empty for a time, with neither sister agreeing to work at all. At last, Haruko rolls up her sleeves and joins in the work. She proves herself to be industrious, and soon she is bringing back more salt than most of the salters.\n"
"\n"
"Akiko's anger softens, but the merchants find no familiar face to greet them. Some pass through the town without even stopping."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/salt_gatherers/event_salt_gatherers.tres
msgid "Haruko is right."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/salt_gatherers/event_salt_gatherers.tres
msgid ""
"Haruko is allowed to focus on trade while Akiko pairs up with another salter.\n"
"\n"
"Her new partner is a serious man, who says little and works steadily. In him she finds a kindred soul, who understands the importance of a worker's duty."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/salt_gatherers/event_salt_gatherers.tres
msgid "Consult a village elder."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/salt_gatherers/event_salt_gatherers.tres
msgid ""
"The sisters decide to seek advice from a village elder. The elder listens for a while, then proposes that they exchange responsibilities until the next full moon.\n"
"\n"
"Haruko returns home every day with aching shoulders, while Akiko quickly learns that merchants rarely agree on anything and that a single misplaced word can spoil an entire afternoon of bargaining.\n"
"\n"
"When the full moon finally rises, both sisters return to their tasks, never mentioning the argument again."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/salt_gatherers/event_salt_gatherers.tres
msgid "Let the argument go unresolved."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/salt_gatherers/event_salt_gatherers.tres
msgid ""
"The sisters fail to come to an agreement. Haruko continues to avoid work out on the salt flats, while Akiko grows more and more irate.\n"
"\n"
"The issue comes to a head one day, as the two sisters unload their resentment.\n"
"\n"
"They are still feuding to this day."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/scarlet_curse/event_scarlet_curse.tres
msgid "The Scarlet Curse"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/scarlet_curse/event_scarlet_curse.tres
msgid ""
"After a heavy rain, a landslide has exposed a vein of brilliant red stone. The master potter, rubbing it between his fingers, realizes it stains like no paint they have ever used.\n"
"\n"
"He instructs his apprentices to grind the stone and mix it with lacquer. The master uses it to paint intricate designs onto the pots, the dazzling vermilion shining.\n"
"\n"
"Soon the potters develop coughs. They become irritable, and complain of dizziness. The workshop stops using the paint at once, but stacks of red pottery still line every wall."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/scarlet_curse/event_scarlet_curse.tres
msgid "Destroy the red pots."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/scarlet_curse/event_scarlet_curse.tres
msgid ""
"The apprentices demand that the cursed pottery be destroyed. The other workers agree, and further insist that the fragments be buried so nobody else can get sick.\n"
"\n"
"The master potter is sad to watch his works of art disappear into the ground, but he hides his trembling hands in his sleeves and breathes a sigh of relief."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/scarlet_curse/event_scarlet_curse.tres
msgid "Only use the pottery as decoration."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/scarlet_curse/event_scarlet_curse.tres
msgid ""
"The master potter is unwilling to destroy or seal away his works of art. Instead he offers the red plates and pots to the local shrine, in return for a promise to only use them for decoration.\n"
"\n"
"The plates are placed on high shelves behind the altar, where the whole settlement can admire them."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/scarlet_curse/event_scarlet_curse.tres
msgid "Ritually purify the vessels."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/scarlet_curse/event_scarlet_curse.tres
msgid ""
"The master potter refuses to destroy his beautiful works. Cloudy-headed and stumbling, he calls a priest instead, and commissions an elaborate ritual to banish the evil spirits haunting the pottery.\n"
"\n"
"The symptoms fade soon afterwards."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/scarlet_curse/event_scarlet_curse.tres
msgid "Sell the pottery to travelers."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/scarlet_curse/event_scarlet_curse.tres
msgid ""
"Unwilling to let his hard work go to waste, the master saves the pottery.\n"
"\n"
"The next time a merchant passes through town, he will sell them cheaply, to at least recover the cost of clay."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/school/event_school.tres
msgid "The Future of Education"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/school/event_school.tres
msgid ""
"A ruin has been renovated into a brand new school, and all that remains is to choose the head teacher.\n"
"\n"
"One option is the local beekeeper, a soft-spoken woman who knows songs and stories, and has herbs to soothe any ailment.\n"
"\n"
"The other candidate is a monk trained at the Haven, a master of rhetoric and arithmetic. He believes the children are capable of more, but he is strict and often impatient."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/school/event_school.tres
msgid "Choose the scholar."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/school/event_school.tres
msgid ""
"The parents decide to invest in rigor, discipline, and a future outside of the settlement.\n"
"\n"
"The cleverest students thrive under the monk's strict instruction, but the ones less interested in scholarship begin to dread their lessons, and resent being sent home with scrolls full of assignments."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/school/event_school.tres
msgid "Choose the beekeeper."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/school/event_school.tres
msgid ""
"The parents prioritize the children's peace of mind, and hope that by choosing the wise woman, they would preserve the old folk wisdom.\n"
"\n"
"The new teacher is gentle. She gives extra attention to the most anxious students, and brings honeycomb to class.\n"
"\n"
"The more ambitious pupils, however, soon grow restless."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/school/event_school.tres
msgid "Let the children decide."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/generic/school/event_school.tres
msgid "A random teacher is chosen"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/school/event_school.tres
msgid "Ask them to share the duties."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/school/event_school.tres
msgid ""
"The parents ask the two candidates to teach together.\n"
"\n"
"By the third day, half of the lesson is taken up by the teachers arguing about the best way to run a school.\n"
"\n"
"The constant disagreement leaves the children confused, eroding their trust in education before they have a chance to start learning."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/sick_apothecary/event_sick_apothecary.tres
msgid "The Sick Apothecary"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/sick_apothecary/event_sick_apothecary.tres
msgid ""
"Lantern light burns dimly across the dark water outside the apothecary's hut, hidden by reeds that almost reach above the roof.\n"
"\n"
"The young apothecary, working late into the night, is nursing a persistent cough. Luckily, when she inherited the job, with it came shelves full of medicines, bundled herbs, and jars of bitter powders.\n"
"\n"
"As the night wears on, her cough fades, but the room begins to tilt. The black cat lounging beside the hearth blinks at her, its eyes narrowing.\n"
"\n"
"\"Good evening,\" it says."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/sick_apothecary/event_sick_apothecary.tres
msgid "Question the cat."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/sick_apothecary/event_sick_apothecary.tres
msgid ""
"The apothecary demands to know how the cat is able to speak.\n"
"\n"
"The cat only grins in response. Its shadow, dancing upon the wall in the firelight, keeps growing until it towers over her menacingly.\n"
"\n"
"The woman backs away from the dark spirit, huddling in the corner of the hut. She recites chants until dawn, when sleep finally overcomes her."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/sick_apothecary/event_sick_apothecary.tres
msgid "Look through her mother's book."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/sick_apothecary/event_sick_apothecary.tres
msgid ""
"The woman looks from the cat to the bottle on the shelf, realizing she must have taken the wrong kind of medicine.\n"
"\n"
"Intent on learning what it is she has imbibed, she leafs through the worn and smudged pages of her mother's recipe book.\n"
"\n"
"Maybe if she combined that potion with a few drops of…\n"
"\n"
"Soon, her mind is buzzing with ideas. Inspired, she spends the rest of the night working out a new tincture."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/sick_apothecary/event_sick_apothecary.tres
msgid "Get some fresh air."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/sick_apothecary/event_sick_apothecary.tres
msgid ""
"Longing to feel the wind on her face and the ground beneath her feet, the apothecary puts on a heavier robe and leaves the cat at the warm hearth.\n"
"\n"
"She looks up at the dark sky, the clouds low and heavy. Frogs croak in the distance as rain washes down her face.\n"
"\n"
"She stands there for a long while, slowly regaining a sense of inner peace."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/sick_apothecary/event_sick_apothecary.tres
msgid ""
"The apothecary decides to pretend that nothing is wrong.\n"
"\n"
"She sits up straight in her chair and pours herself some tea. She ignores the cat's commentary, which becomes increasingly rude.\n"
"\n"
"If she can remain calm, maybe the strange effects will pass by morning."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/silk_weaver/event_silk_weaver.tres
msgid "A Different Weave"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/silk_weaver/event_silk_weaver.tres
msgid ""
"One of the weavers spins thread that doesn't match. Unlike the traditional reserved palette, they weave a rainbow of threads in wild patterns.\n"
"\n"
"They don't boast or argue, but they don't follow the traditions either. Their cloth shimmers with iridescent silk: garish to some, beautiful to others.\n"
"\n"
"Murmurs spread among the workers. Someone asks if it's time to decide what kind of weaving belongs here."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/silk_weaver/event_silk_weaver.tres
msgid "Use their cloth in the hut's banner."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/generic/silk_weaver/event_silk_weaver.tres
msgid "Gain one of two silk relics<related_term:relic.silk_loop><related_term:relic.silk_thread>"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/silk_weaver/event_silk_weaver.tres
msgid ""
"The brightest piece is cut and stitched together with more traditional pieces into a banner above the door.\n"
"\n"
"Settlers nod as they pass beneath it, some stopping to trace the threads.\n"
"\n"
"The weaver continues to experiment, weaving strands of gold and silver into the next piece."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/silk_weaver/event_silk_weaver.tres
msgid "Ask them why they weave this way."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/silk_weaver/event_silk_weaver.tres
msgid ""
"The weaver pauses.\n"
"\n"
"\"Because it feels like me,\" they say. \"And I want to make something that feels like me... and still holds.\"\n"
"\n"
"They offer a small piece of thread. \"It's strong. Even if it's soft.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/silk_weaver/event_silk_weaver.tres
msgid "Discourage the weaver, gently but firmly."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/silk_weaver/event_silk_weaver.tres
msgid ""
"The community asks for uniformity, as customers shun such garish cloth. The weaver unrolls and unravels it by hand.\n"
"\n"
"No one challenges the decision, and before long the town has one less weaver."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/silk_weaver/event_silk_weaver.tres
msgid "Let them keep weaving."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/silk_weaver/event_silk_weaver.tres
msgid ""
"The colorful cloths dry behind the hut, where the wind still finds them, even if the settlers do not.\n"
"\n"
"They don't ask for any further accommodation.\n"
"\n"
"The loom continues to spin."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/silver_mine/event_silver_mine.tres
msgid "The Collapsed Shaft"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/silver_mine/event_silver_mine.tres
msgid ""
"The silver mine is the settlement's primary industry, supplying the whole region with gleaming rings and necklaces. The miners swing their picks from sunup to sundown to feed the hungry forges.\n"
"\n"
"This morning, the miners find the beams above their heads groaning. By the time an alarm is raised, bits of stone are raining from the ceiling. The miners barely make it out before the shaft collapses."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/silver_mine/event_silver_mine.tres
msgid "Leave this shaft and reinforce the rest."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/silver_mine/event_silver_mine.tres
msgid ""
"The miners abandon the collapsed shaft and spend days carefully inspecting the remaining shafts, reinforcing any beams that are in need of repair.\n"
"\n"
"Much time and material is spent on the effort, but they are confident that it will prevent another collapse for a long time."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/silver_mine/event_silver_mine.tres
msgid "Inspect the collapsed shaft."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/silver_mine/event_silver_mine.tres
msgid ""
"After the dust settles, the workers decide to investigate the cause of the collapse.\n"
"\n"
"The culprit turns out to be one badly knotted beam that went unnoticed when the mine was first dug.\n"
"\n"
"During their inspection, however, they are surprised to find a new seam running through the rock. This one, however, is golden."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/silver_mine/event_silver_mine.tres
msgid "Dig new shafts."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/silver_mine/event_silver_mine.tres
msgid ""
"The workers dig new shafts, leaving the cliff face full of gaping holes.\n"
"\n"
"Soon they find the local wells turning pale and gritty.\n"
"\n"
"\"A curse from the cliff spirit,\" the priest declares."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/silver_mine/event_silver_mine.tres
msgid ""
"The miners avoid the collapsed shaft but continue using the remaining ones.\n"
"\n"
"Production continues uninterrupted, but the workers begin to fear every creak and groan of the beams.\n"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/singing_quarriers/event_singing_quarriers.tres
msgid "The Singing Quarriers"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/singing_quarriers/event_singing_quarriers.tres
msgid ""
"The quarry is busy today. Two men on a ledge above swing their picks, singing loudly to keep time with each strike. The song echoes off the cliff, scattering birds from the nearby trees.\n"
"\n"
"Below, two carriers are hauling stone down the path, their faces growing sourer with every [i]dokkoisho![/i] and [i]yoi-yoi![/i] reaching them from above. They say their work is already tiresome enough. They want to hear the birds sing instead, and admire the cherry blossoms in peace."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/singing_quarriers/event_singing_quarriers.tres
msgid "Throw pebbles at the singing workers."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/singing_quarriers/event_singing_quarriers.tres
msgid ""
"The carriers, fed up with the relentless singing, begin throwing pebbles in the direction of the quarrymen.\n"
"\n"
"The songs stop at once and the workers hurl insults back.\n"
"\n"
"Soon the whole worksite is arguing, and very little work ends up finished by the end of the day."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/singing_quarriers/event_singing_quarriers.tres
msgid "Let a passing monk mediate."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/singing_quarriers/event_singing_quarriers.tres
msgid ""
"One of the granite haulers spots a monk walking by the cliff, a basket of petals in his hand. The worker bows, and asks the monk to settle the dispute. \n"
"\n"
"The monk considers, contemplating the blossoming tree standing nearby. He instructs the singers to work in silence while the tree is in bloom. Until the last petal falls from the tree, the workers must listen to the sound of birds, wind, and their picks hitting the stone."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/singing_quarriers/event_singing_quarriers.tres
msgid "Challenge the singers."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/singing_quarriers/event_singing_quarriers.tres
msgid ""
"The carriers mock the singers' lack of imagination and challenge them to come up with something original.\n"
"\n"
"The two singing quarrymen make up a teasing verse about the sour-faced carriers and their love of cherry blossoms.\n"
"\n"
"At first the carriers are furious, but soon the song becomes so silly that even they can't suppress a smile."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/singing_quarriers/event_singing_quarriers.tres
msgid "Block out the noise."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/singing_quarriers/event_singing_quarriers.tres
msgid ""
"The carriers stuff cotton in their ears with grumpy sighs.\n"
"\n"
"They continue their work in muffled silence."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/soggy_mill/event_soggy_mill.tres
msgid "Soggy Mill"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/soggy_mill/event_soggy_mill.tres
msgid ""
"A crack in the millrace caught the millers unprepared. Several sacks of freshly polished rice lie sodden by the wall.\n"
"\n"
"The millers must act quickly. If left alone, all the rice will spoil, and the rot will spread throughout the mill."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/soggy_mill/event_soggy_mill.tres
msgid "Pound the wet grain into mochi."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/soggy_mill/event_soggy_mill.tres
msgid ""
"The rice is steamed and pounded with mallets in a rhythmic ritual.\n"
"\n"
"The work takes all day, but waste is averted, and by evening stacks of cut mochi line the shelves.\n"
"\n"
"The millers grill a few for dinner, skewered on spare chopsticks."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/soggy_mill/event_soggy_mill.tres
msgid "Share it freely: porridge for all."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/soggy_mill/event_soggy_mill.tres
msgid ""
"Settlers gather in the mill yard, each handed a steaming bowl of thin porridge.\n"
"\n"
"Notches are carved into the mill beam to mark each guest.\n"
"\n"
"What could have been a waste of grain turns into an opportunity to bring everyone closer."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/soggy_mill/event_soggy_mill.tres
msgid "Spread the rice to dry as much as possible."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/soggy_mill/event_soggy_mill.tres
msgid ""
"Sacks are sliced open and the grain is spread on the warm ground, letting the wind chase away the moisture.\n"
"\n"
"Some of the rice is too far gone, but most returns to the stores, saved for seasons when grain runs low.\n"
"\n"
"The town council gives the millers small wooden tokens to cover the lost grain, redeemable for extra rice from the next harvest."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/soggy_mill/event_soggy_mill.tres
msgid "Discard the damaged rice."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/soggy_mill/event_soggy_mill.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers throw the soaked sacks into the river, eager to get rid of the mess.\n"
"\n"
"\"What a waste!\" The head miller grumbles."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/stone_quarry/event_stone_quarry.tres
msgid "The Rolling Boulder"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/stone_quarry/event_stone_quarry.tres
msgid ""
"The quarriers have developed a time-saving technique of rolling the stones they cut out down the hill instead of dragging them by hand. All day, boulders tumble down the hillside with a roaring boom.\n"
"\n"
"When one boulder rolls to a stop at the center of the settlement's main road, narrowly missing a settler towing a cart of firewood, the neighbors declare that they've had enough."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/stone_quarry/event_stone_quarry.tres
msgid "Let the nearly crushed settler decide."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/stone_quarry/event_stone_quarry.tres
msgid ""
"The shaken firewood hauler is asked to speak in front of a crowd. He declares that the quarry is a danger to everyone, and demands that work stop immediately.\n"
"\n"
"The resulting angry mob raids the worksite, confiscating all the tools and setting fire to the storage sheds."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/stone_quarry/event_stone_quarry.tres
msgid "Move the quarry."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/stone_quarry/event_stone_quarry.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers convince the quarriers to move their work to the other side of the hill, away from the settlement.\n"
"\n"
"It takes a while to set up the new worksite, but the noise complaints dwindle and no more accidents occur."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/stone_quarry/event_stone_quarry.tres
msgid "Hold a meeting about the issue."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/stone_quarry/event_stone_quarry.tres
msgid ""
"The town council calls a meeting to hear all sides of the argument and help calm tensions between the settlers.\n"
"\n"
"The result is a new law, maintaining that the quarry is only allowed to operate during the middle of the day, when most settlers are away from their homes and the roads are empty."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/stone_quarry/event_stone_quarry.tres
msgid "Ignore the protesting villagers."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/stone_quarry/event_stone_quarry.tres
msgid ""
"The quarry foremen ignore the settlers' complaints and instruct the workers to continue as usual.\n"
"\n"
"People have to learn to live with the incessant deafening booms and the risk of getting crushed by a stray boulder.\n"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/stone_soup/event_stone_soup.tres
msgid "The Master Chef"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/stone_soup/event_stone_soup.tres
msgid ""
"It is the height of the nori harvest along the seashore. Everyone contributes to the harvest. Workers with chilled fingers, their pants tied above their knees, wade between the brushwood. Children carry baskets of wet seaweed to the sorting mats. Dogs wander hopefully among the drying racks.\n"
"\n"
"Amid the bustle, a weatherworn traveler arrives, carrying an empty pot and a smooth black stone. They introduce themself as a master chef, and claim that their stone can turn any soup into culinary perfection. They ask for some nori to demonstrate."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/stone_soup/event_stone_soup.tres
msgid "Give the traveler nori scraps."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/stone_soup/event_stone_soup.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers give the travelers torn scraps of the seaweed, their intact sheets too valuable to waste on a beggar's soup.\n"
"\n"
"The traveler sips the broth and suggests that it needs a bit of earthiness. The settlers, now curious, hand over a withered carrot.\n"
"\n"
"\"Almost there,\" the traveler reassures them. \"Just needs a drop of soy sauce to reach perfection.\"\n"
"\n"
"By the time the chef is finished, the soup is flavored with miso, full of mushrooms and tofu, and has a mound of scallions on top."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/stone_soup/event_stone_soup.tres
msgid "Offer the traveler some stew instead."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/stone_soup/event_stone_soup.tres
msgid ""
"Some of the settlers take pity on the traveler, and offer them the same rich stew the workers eat, along with a steamed bun.\n"
"\n"
"The traveler eats ravenously while warming up by the fire.\n"
"\n"
"When they continue on their way, they leave the stone behind."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/stone_soup/event_stone_soup.tres
msgid "Trade the stone for supper."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/stone_soup/event_stone_soup.tres
msgid ""
"A local merchant is quick to jump on the opportunity, offering a box of nori in return for the miraculous stone.\n"
"\n"
"The traveler haggles, reluctant to part with the treasure, but eventually agrees to the trade."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/stone_soup/event_stone_soup.tres
msgid "Send the traveler away. "
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/stone_soup/event_stone_soup.tres
msgid ""
"The villagers laugh at the traveler, dismissing them as delusional.\n"
"\n"
"The settlement is too busy to bother with their nonsense."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/swamp_bridge/event_swamp_bridge.tres
msgid "The Confectioner's Letter"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/swamp_bridge/event_swamp_bridge.tres
msgid ""
"A narrow bridge raised on stilts winds through the swamp, connecting the dry islands that comprise the settlement. A young confectioner has been walking the oldest, least used, section of the bridge every dawn. Each day a new folded poem is hidden under the sweets in his basket, bound for a lucky recipient.\n"
"\n"
"This morning, just before sunrise, he finds one of the stilts rotted, and the whole section around it collapsed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/swamp_bridge/event_swamp_bridge.tres
msgid "Repair the bridge alone."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/swamp_bridge/event_swamp_bridge.tres
msgid ""
"Eager to deliver his letter and certain that few people come this way, the young confectioner sets out to repair the bridge himself. \n"
"\n"
"He puts his basket down and gathers spare bamboo. Halfway through his repair attempt, his knee bumps his basket and it tips over, spilling the contents into the muddy water.\n"
"\n"
"He watches in dismay as the carefully wrapped poem is swallowed up by the mud."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/swamp_bridge/event_swamp_bridge.tres
msgid "Recruit help."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/swamp_bridge/event_swamp_bridge.tres
msgid ""
"Reluctant to put his meager building skills to the test, the confectioner looks around for help. \n"
"\n"
"He finds a basket weaver, who hurries over and assesses the damage, her hand on her chin.\n"
"\n"
"She calls over her friend, who recounts in detail the last time the bridge collapsed.\n"
"\n"
"The friend calls his brother, who agrees that collapsing bridges are certainly a problem.\n"
"\n"
"The bridge remains unrepaired."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/swamp_bridge/event_swamp_bridge.tres
msgid "Deliver the letter some other way."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/swamp_bridge/event_swamp_bridge.tres
msgid ""
"The young man gives up on the bridge and looks for alternatives.\n"
"\n"
"He ties the letter to a pebble and hurls it with all his might towards the other side. The pebble flies through the air and disappears into the dark.\n"
"\n"
"He hopes his lover will appreciate the romantic gesture."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/swamp_bridge/event_swamp_bridge.tres
msgid "Wait for someone else to repair the bridge."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/swamp_bridge/event_swamp_bridge.tres
msgid ""
"The confectioner bemoans his lack of bridge-mending experience and starts his trek back.\n"
"\n"
"He is already running late for his other deliveries.\n"
"\n"
"He is sure his lover will understand."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/swamp_fortress/event_swamp_fortress.tres
msgid "The Sunken Fortress"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/swamp_fortress/event_swamp_fortress.tres
msgid ""
"In the swamp on the outskirts of town lies an old fortress. Maybe it was founded on unstable soil, or perhaps the Shattering has turned the area into a swamp later.\n"
"\n"
"Several floors have already been claimed by the muck, and the rest of the structure is leaning precariously to one side.\n"
"\n"
"Lately, rumors have been spreading of strange noises coming from this fortress at night, and settlers suspect that spirits have claimed the place."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/swamp_fortress/event_swamp_fortress.tres
msgid "Investigate the fortress."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/swamp_fortress/event_swamp_fortress.tres
msgid "Leave well enough alone."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/swamp_fortress/event_swamp_fortress.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers continue to avoid the fortress, leaving it to its slow journey down into the center of the shard.\n"
"\n"
"Rumors will keep spreading until someone summons the bravery to venture inside."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/swamp_fortress/event_swamp_fortress.tres
msgid ""
"A small group of adventurous settlers sets out one night to investigate the rumored noises, carrying satchels of auspicious amulets. The crumbling fortress stares them down with its dark windows, daring them to approach.\n"
"\n"
"As they climb inside through a hole left by collapsed masonry, they are greeted with a pitch-black hall, large enough that none of the other walls are visible.\n"
"\n"
"The sound of footsteps from the depth of the hall echoes against the ancient stones."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#. Property: label
#: events/generic/swamp_fortress/event_swamp_fortress.tres
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_canyon_shrine.tres
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tranquil_bay.tres
msgid "Leave an offering."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/swamp_fortress/event_swamp_fortress.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers decide to pacify the spirit with an offering. They put a sheet of paper on the floor and each person places a small offering: a pile of salt, a carving of the Enlightened One, and a few acorns.\n"
"\n"
"As soon as they turn around, they hear the approaching sound of rapid pattering, followed by a swoosh.\n"
"\n"
"They turn around to find the salt scattered, the carving tipped over, and the acorns gone. The paper now bears a muddy print."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/swamp_fortress/event_swamp_fortress.tres
msgid "Chant a protective incantation."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/swamp_fortress/event_swamp_fortress.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers bow deeply and clap their hands, announcing themselves to the spirits inhabiting the fortress.\n"
"\n"
"They chant a loud incantation asking for protection, and the rustling sounds from within the hall go quiet.\n"
"\n"
"Their mission accomplished, the settlers return back to the settlement triumphant, only for the sounds to return the following night."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/swamp_fortress/event_swamp_fortress.tres
msgid "Explore the hall with torches."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/swamp_fortress/event_swamp_fortress.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers light torches and walk deeper into the hall.\n"
"\n"
"The rustling sounds continue, but the source stays just out of reach.\n"
"\n"
"When they reach the collapsed door at the end of the hall, their nostrils are assaulted by a foul, musky stench without a clear source.\n"
"\n"
"Their path barred, the settlers return empty-handed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/swamp_fortress/event_swamp_fortress.tres
msgid "Retreat."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/swamp_fortress/event_swamp_fortress.tres
msgid "The settlers decide that they've had enough adventure for the night and quickly climb back out, leaving whoever is inside undisturbed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/swamp_lanterns/event_swamp_lanterns.tres
msgid "The Spirit of the Swamp"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/swamp_lanterns/event_swamp_lanterns.tres
msgid ""
"A young man, Hiroshi, is wandering through the rainy swamp at night, the dark trees towering over his head. The raindrops fall heavily on his sturdy umbrella as he passes between the glowing lanterns guiding him along the path.\n"
"\n"
"His younger brother, Makoto, spoke of meeting a giant, grinning spirit bounding through the trees one evening. The other children in the village are making fun of the boy, and calling him a liar.\n"
"\n"
"Hoping to uphold his brother's honor, Hiroshi presses further into the swamp's depth.\n"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/swamp_lanterns/event_swamp_lanterns.tres
msgid "Ask the spirit for help."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/swamp_lanterns/event_swamp_lanterns.tres
msgid ""
"Hiroshi stops before the tallest lantern on the path. Moss covers its cracked surface, and it leans slightly, towering over the boy. Feeling a little foolish, Hiroshi bows before it and whispers a request to the swamp spirit. \"If my brother spoke the truth, show me enough to defend him.\"\n"
"\n"
"The flame in the lantern glows brighter for a second, and Hiroshi feels the hair on his neck rise. Above him, the trees whisper as a sudden gust of wind blows the flame out.\n"
"\n"
"Still, Hiroshi's hand lantern reveals nothing but darkness."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/swamp_lanterns/event_swamp_lanterns.tres
msgid "Wait at the end of the path."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/swamp_lanterns/event_swamp_lanterns.tres
msgid ""
"Remembering how Makoto's face brightened when he told his brother of the creature's enormous grin, Hiroshi resolves to be patient.\n"
"\n"
"He leaves his umbrella beneath a large tree and steps out into the rain, waiting for the spirit of the swamp to appear.\n"
"\n"
"When he finally gives up, he finds the umbrella missing, in its place a small pile of acorns."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/swamp_lanterns/event_swamp_lanterns.tres
msgid "Venture off the main path."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/swamp_lanterns/event_swamp_lanterns.tres
msgid ""
"Having walked past the last lantern with nothing to show for it, Hiroshi decides to step off the main path. He follows the sound of a croaking frog, his own little lantern lighting his way.\n"
"\n"
"He soon finds his feet ankle-deep in water. As he raises his lantern, he catches a glimpse of a dark slanted rooftop at the edge of the black pool, half-hidden by reeds."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/swamp_lanterns/event_swamp_lanterns.tres
msgid "Give up and return home."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/swamp_lanterns/event_swamp_lanterns.tres
msgid ""
"Hiroshi grows ashamed of himself for chasing a child's story through the swamp and turns back.\n"
"\n"
"On the way home, he finds Makoto waiting at the edge of the settlement, worried about his brother. Before Hiroshi can speak, Makoto points behind him. But Hiroshi turns too late, and he sees nothing but an empty path among the dark trees."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_1.tres
msgid "The First Tea"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_1.tres
msgid ""
"The new tea house is complete, its doors open to the breeze.\n"
"\n"
"An old couple is serving tea to those moving on with the expedition. They usually serve simple green tea with a few snacks and sweets, but maybe this occasion calls for something more elaborate?"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_1.tres
msgid "Make it a proper feast."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_1.tres
msgid "Establish a custom"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_1.tres
msgid "A custom has been established."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_1.tres
msgid ""
"Snacks and sweets are preceded by soup, rice, and grilled skewers.\n"
"\n"
"Tea bowls, once emptied, are refilled with beer and rice wine.\n"
"\n"
"The ceremony turns into a lively gathering, with laughter and seconds for all."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_1.tres
msgid "Arrange it beautifully."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_1.tres
msgid ""
"Mats are re-aligned perfectly.\n"
"\n"
"Petals are gathered and arranged on the low table.\n"
"\n"
"The cups are placed carefully on folded cloth.\n"
"\n"
"Few dare to speak, afraid of interrupting the host's immaculate little ritual."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_1.tres
msgid "Focus on simplicity."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_1.tres
msgid ""
"The group sits quietly, comfortable and relaxed.\n"
"\n"
"No ritual takes place, and no meal is served.\n"
"\n"
"Discussions of settling plans give way to shared memories and quoted poems."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_1.tres
msgid "We don't have time for this."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_1.tres
msgid ""
"The fire is doused, and the vessels are set back on the shelves.\n"
"\n"
"The expedition moves on without stopping at the tea house."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2a.tres
msgid "Hearty Hospitality"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2a.tres
msgid ""
"The custom of turning tea breaks into feasts has traveled across the shard with the expedition. Now, each ceremony at the pavilion ends with more dishes than hands to carry, and more cups than lips to sip with.\n"
"\n"
"Someone pours water into three kettles at once, and another rushes to stack serving trays.\n"
"\n"
"Suddenly, a sharp cry cuts through the warm chatter. A kettle has spilled. The scald is minor, but the host is beginning to panic."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2a.tres
msgid "Limit the number of guests."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2a.tres
msgid ""
"The tea pavilion takes a day off to make new schedules.\n"
"\n"
"When it reopens, it's less bustling, but certainly better organized."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2a.tres
msgid "Make up for the disturbance with more food."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2a.tres
msgid ""
"The injured settler, plied with a tray of mochi, laughs it off.\n"
"\n"
"The host quickly regains composure and the feasts go on as usual."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2a.tres
msgid "Invest in more staff and better tools."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2a.tres
msgid ""
"A cook joins the staff, as do two more hosts.\n"
"\n"
"The teapots are replaced with fine new lacquerware.\n"
"\n"
"The old clay teapots are sent on with the expedition to make tea on the road."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2a.tres
msgid "Ignore the issue and move on."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2a.tres
msgid "The spilled kettle is righted, the burn wrapped, and the feast continues, albeit with less joy."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2b.tres
msgid "Perfect Form"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2b.tres
msgid ""
"Tea Pavilions have become places of refined elegance. Hosts in full traditional dress now guide every tea ceremony with deliberate grace: folding the cloth, whisking the foam, waiting for waterdrops to evaporate from the kettle's surface.\n"
"\n"
"But today, something feels off. The tea is the same, the gestures flawless, and yet the guests hesitate: \"This felt warmer, before...\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2b.tres
msgid "Simplify things."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2b.tres
msgid ""
"The ritual is limited to the first serving. Cups are refilled without fanfare.\n"
"\n"
"Jokes and laughter break the stiffness of the atmosphere.\n"
"\n"
"The custom evolves."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2b.tres
msgid "Preserve the ritual. It will grow meaningful again."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2b.tres
msgid ""
"The guests remain silent as the ritual continues.\n"
"\n"
"When the tea hits their lips, followed by exquisite little morsels, their eyes soften.\n"
"\n"
"\"Now I see...\" one guest murmurs."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2b.tres
msgid "Let the guests perform the ceremony."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2b.tres
msgid ""
"The host sets the whisk down into its special stand and invites a guest to try.\n"
"\n"
"The moment is awkward, unrefined, but there's a new air of excitement.\n"
"\n"
"From the drawer, the host retrieves a whisk and offers it to the guests as a memento."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2b.tres
msgid "Suggest the guests visit a different establishment."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2b.tres
msgid ""
"The tea is left to go cold.\n"
"\n"
"The guests leave in a huff.\n"
"\n"
"The host's pride is preserved."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2c.tres
msgid "A Warm Shared Moment"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2c.tres
msgid ""
"Tea Pavilions are now a place of humble, warm gatherings. At this one, a hunchbacked old woman welcomes settlers with warm tea in cracked cups.\n"
"\n"
"\"These are the only ones I have,\" she apologizes. \"Better ones might arrive next month, but I would rather share tea, even if in cracked cups.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2c.tres
msgid "Use the cracked cups."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2c.tres
msgid ""
"The tea service goes on as normal, with the cracks ignored.\n"
"\n"
"The host is relieved."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2c.tres
msgid "Offer to mend her cups."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2c.tres
msgid ""
"After tea service is finished, an artisan mixes lacquer with rice flour to fill in the chips and cracks.\n"
"\n"
"Once the paste cures, each crack is polished with gold powder.\n"
"\n"
"The host insists that the guests take one cup as a memento."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2c.tres
msgid "Offer her cups carried by the expedition."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2c.tres
msgid ""
"The host bows deeply and accepts the gift.\n"
"\n"
"The old cups go on a higher shelf, and the new ones are used for the tea service.\n"
"\n"
"When the expedition departs, there is a basket of packed lunches prepared for them."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2c.tres
msgid "Refuse the inadequate vessels."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/tea_ceremony/event_tea_ceremony_2c.tres
msgid "The host does not press. The cups are returned to their shelf, still waiting."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/trampled_blossoms/event_trampled_blossoms.tres
msgid "Trampled Blossoms"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/trampled_blossoms/event_trampled_blossoms.tres
msgid ""
"A herd of wild horses has descended upon the meadow.\n"
"\n"
"Perhaps their ancestors were once beasts of burden, but little of that docility remains. They are currently treating the magnificent blooms with the same respect as one accords common weeds.\n"
"\n"
"\"They're ruining the view,\" a settler grumbles, watching a particularly chubby pony chew on a bellflower. \"And besides, we could put these beasts to good use.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/trampled_blossoms/event_trampled_blossoms.tres
msgid "Capture the horses and put them to labor."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/trampled_blossoms/event_trampled_blossoms.tres
msgid ""
"Ropes are braided, and halters are fashioned. The boldest settlers approach, confidently surrounding the herd.\n"
"\n"
"In the ensuing scuffle, the horses express their opinion of employment with a precise application of their hind legs, leaving the hapless farmers bruised and scattered around the meadow.\n"
"\n"
"The herd disappears into the distance, leaving only hoofprints and resentment behind."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/trampled_blossoms/event_trampled_blossoms.tres
msgid "Draw them away with a better offer."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/trampled_blossoms/event_trampled_blossoms.tres
msgid ""
"Baskets of salted turnips are placed at the meadow's edge, leading away from the flowers.\n"
"\n"
"The herd politely agrees that turnips taste better, and even allows the settlers to walk among them.\n"
"\n"
"They do not stay, but before they leave, they rub against the trees, leaving tufts of coarse hair caught in the bark."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/trampled_blossoms/event_trampled_blossoms.tres
msgid "Drive them off."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/trampled_blossoms/event_trampled_blossoms.tres
msgid ""
"Settlers stand shoulder to shoulder, banging pots and singing chants. They see it as a personal boundary reinforced.\n"
"\n"
"The wall of noise pushes the herd back, away from the delicate blooms.\n"
"\n"
"The flowers are saved, but the horses are never seen again."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/trampled_blossoms/event_trampled_blossoms.tres
msgid "Feed them persimmons."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/trampled_blossoms/event_trampled_blossoms.tres
msgid ""
"Baskets of surplus persimmons are placed at the meadow's edge, leading away from the flowers.\n"
"\n"
"The herd descends on the baskets and within an hour all the persimmons are gone.\n"
"\n"
"When the horses depart, they leave behind tufts of coarse hair."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/trampled_blossoms/event_trampled_blossoms.tres
msgid "Let them graze."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/trampled_blossoms/event_trampled_blossoms.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers leave the horses alone and watch the destruction.\n"
"\n"
"Soon, only stems remain of the wildflowers, and the meadow turns into a muddy trampled mess.\n"
"\n"
"But the horses are clearly content with their full bellies, and leave behind... fertilizer."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/tree_grove_forest/event_tree_grove_forest.tres
msgid "The Cedar Glen"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/tree_grove_forest/event_tree_grove_forest.tres
msgid ""
"Deep in the forest a little glade has formed around a furrow in the ground, hushed and dappled.\n"
"\n"
"The furrow is lined with ancient, towering cedars on both sides. Moss covers the ground in a thick, plush carpet.\n"
"\n"
"The settlers sit for a while, breathing in the smells of the deep forest."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/tree_grove_forest/event_tree_grove_forest.tres
msgid "Contemplate a single tree."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/tree_grove_forest/event_tree_grove_forest.tres
msgid "As branches rustle, ideas sprout in the settlers' minds. Many now feel more attuned to the forest."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/tree_grove_forest/event_tree_grove_forest.tres
msgid "Contemplate the trees around the glade."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/tree_grove_forest/event_tree_grove_forest.tres
msgid "As the shade deepens, ideas rustle through the settlers' minds. Many now feel more attuned to the forest."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/tree_grove_forest/event_tree_grove_forest.tres
msgid "Contemplate the entire forest."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/tree_grove_forest/event_tree_grove_forest.tres
msgid ""
"A breeze stirs the cedar needles, spreading the scent of sap and sun-warmed bark.\n"
"\n"
"The settlers leave carrying a sprig. Somehow they know the forest wanted them to have it."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/tree_grove_forest/event_tree_grove_forest.tres
msgid "Bask in the peace of the glade."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/tree_grove_forest/event_tree_grove_forest.tres
msgid "The serene ambiance of the quiet glade inspires the group to forge ahead, and spread harmony around the shard."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/vacant_role/event_vacant_role.tres
msgid "The Vacant Role"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/vacant_role/event_vacant_role.tres
msgid ""
"The founder of this shard's Dragonfly Troupe passed away just the other day.\n"
"\n"
"In his later years, he only took small roles: a shopkeeper here, a wandering monk there, sometimes a silent passerby. Nonetheless, he never missed a rehearsal or let a show go unperformed.\n"
"\n"
"Now, the troupe prepares their next production. His roles are already written in, but now no one is there to perform them."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/vacant_role/event_vacant_role.tres
msgid "Quietly bang a drum in place of his lines."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/vacant_role/event_vacant_role.tres
msgid ""
"When the founder's lines arrive, no one steps forward.\n"
"\n"
"Instead, a soft, deliberate beat echoes through the stage. One strike for a greeting, two for a remark, and a triplet for a farewell.\n"
"\n"
"The crowd is surprised, but soon the news spreads among them in nudges and whispers."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/vacant_role/event_vacant_role.tres
msgid "Perform a new play about his life instead."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/vacant_role/event_vacant_role.tres
msgid ""
"The troupe rewrites everything.\n"
"\n"
"From his childhood among traveling bards to the day he put together his first stage with salvaged planks.\n"
"\n"
"The show is unpolished, and a little too dramatized, but the feeling carries through and when the final bow comes, the whole crowd erupts in shouts of \"Dragonfly!\" and a rain of paper-wrapped coins showers the stage."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/vacant_role/event_vacant_role.tres
msgid "Let troupe members take turns performing his roles."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/vacant_role/event_vacant_role.tres
msgid ""
"Each performance is slightly different.\n"
"\n"
"Sometimes his lines are echoed, sometimes adjusted, but always delivered with care. A remembered gesture is repeated, or a familiar facial expression mimicked.\n"
"\n"
"The spirit of the founder lives on in the details."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/vacant_role/event_vacant_role.tres
msgid "Have his protégé take on the roles from now on."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/vacant_role/event_vacant_role.tres
msgid ""
"The protégé bows once before stepping into costume.\n"
"\n"
"Their voice is different, their timing sharper, but the air around them shifts in that familiar way.\n"
"\n"
"The founder's most ardent admirers say the transition is too seamless, but the average audience member considers it perfect."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid "The White City"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: value
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
#: events/landmark/communal_baths/event_communal_baths.tres
#: events/landmark/endless_ruin/event_endless_ruin.tres
#: events/landmark/mirage_gate/event_mirage_gate.tres
#: events/landmark/post_road/event_post_road.tres
#: events/landmark/print_studio/event_print_studio.tres
#: events/landmark/stone_of_remembrance/event_stone_of_remembrance.tres
#: events/landmark/verse_arena/event_verse_arena.tres
msgid "false"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid ""
"Recent studies of Mirage Gates suggest that although they usually lead to strange, alien worlds, it is possible to control the destination.\n"
"\n"
"It appears that an underground control mechanism can be activated by the insertion of specific stone tablets."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid "Insert the patterned tile."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid "The settlers remove layers of sand to access the gate's navigation mechanism and insert the tile into the tablet slot. It fits snugly, and the image within the gate slowly stabilizes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid "Leave the gate alone."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid "The expedition moves on, looking back now and then at the glimpses of white spires that can occasionally be seen through the gate."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid ""
"A scout steps through and finds himself in the courtyard of a small palace. The entire place seems to be carved from pure white stone, and golden spires sparkle atop the domed roofs.\n"
"\n"
"Within moments, guards dressed in strange flowing outfits bar his way. Although their language is unfamiliar, it is clear that they are telling the scout to go back."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid "Show them a coin with the image of the palace."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid "The guards' already unusually large eyes get even larger and they briefly talk among themselves. One points to a nearby bench and walks away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid "Return empty-handed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid ""
"The scout is unable to argue, and meekly steps back through the gate.\n"
"\n"
"Perhaps someone else will uncover this mystery in the future."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid ""
"She returns with an old man, his bushy, greying beard sticking out like a halo around his face. The man greets the scout in a language that sounds much closer to ours, but it is still incomprehensible.\n"
"\n"
"The scout tries to communicate, but despite efforts on both sides, no progress is made."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid "Leave him a familiar tale written in our language."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid ""
"The old man gets animated at the sight of the scroll. He hastily takes a tiny blank book and a small charcoal-tipped rod from inside a patch sewn onto his garment, then starts drawing glyphs.\n"
"\n"
"He thrusts the book in front of the scout's face, two glyphs clearly drawn on the paper. The glyph shapes are unusual, but they are recognizable: \"Good\" and \"Meeting\".\n"
"\n"
"The scout and the old man take turns writing in the strange little book.\n"
"\n"
"\"Explorer\", the scout writes.\n"
"\"Origin location question\", the man responds.\n"
"\"Desert gate\"\n"
"\"Coin question\"\n"
"\"Foreign man\"\n"
"\"Origin palace no return\"\n"
"\n"
"It doesn't take long before they start communicating in simple sentences."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid ""
"The scout is unable to find a common tongue, and meekly steps back through the gate.\n"
"\n"
"Perhaps someone else will uncover this mystery in the future."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid "The old man looks at the scout expectantly."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid "Ask to explore the city."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid "The man writes \"Foreign person forbid\", followed by \"Isolation make peace\", then looks apologetic. \"Old fear\", he adds, underlining the glyphs."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid "Ask what this place is."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid ""
"The man writes \"Safe place ancestor flee big war\".\n"
"\n"
"He draws a crude sketch of one of the iron wrecks that explorers find in the wastelands, then makes \"shuuu-pkha\" sounds and waves his arms.\n"
"\n"
"\"Now thousand year peace,\" he writes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid "Ask to establish future communications."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid "The man writes \"I want many person forbid\" and gives a sad smile. \"Safety yes knowledge no\", he adds. Then \"gate future closed\"."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid "Leave the city forever."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid "The gate will be closed forever."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid "The gate is closed forever."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/vanishing_city/event_vanishing_city.tres
msgid ""
"Having exhausted his questions, the scouts steps back through the gate.\n"
"\n"
"Moments later, the image of the city fades and the gate goes dormant."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid "The Verdant Labyrinth"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid ""
"A group of settlers are on a stroll in the forest when they realize that they are surrounded by a dense maze of trees.\n"
"\n"
"The trunks grow so close together that the canopy blocks out the sunlight, and the trail becomes lost among ferns and winding roots.\n"
"\n"
"They can no longer tell whether the trail ahead is leading them deeper into the forest, or back toward the settlement."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid "Follow the birdsong."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid "Continue down the path."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#. Property: label
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_valley_path.tres
msgid "Follow the sound of water."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid "Try to backtrack."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers decide to abandon the maze and retrace their steps, but can't seem to agree on which way looks the most familiar.\n"
"\n"
"Paths seem to wind in all directions, and the same dense walls of greenery repeat endlessly."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid "Find a way out."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid ""
"A settler watches a squirrel scramble up a nearby trunk, and decides to follow.\n"
"\n"
"He climbs up the towering tree, and sees the settlement only a small distance away.\n"
"\n"
"Follow his directions, the group eventually makes its way out of the labyrinth."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers pause, hearing several distinct bird calls coming from different directions.\n"
"\n"
"First comes the sharp and raspy cawing of a crow. It repeats, the sound echoing among the trees.\n"
"\n"
"In response comes the low hooting of an owl.\n"
"\n"
"The calls seem farther and farther away each time."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid "Follow the crow caws."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid "Follow the owl hoots."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid ""
"Following the harsh cawing of crows, the settlers wander deeper into the forest. The birds soon approach them, flying from branch to branch and pausing every few minutes to observe.\n"
"\n"
"Before long, the path opens up to reveal a tiny house on top of a little hill. A single crow perches on the weathered orange roof.\n"
"\n"
"Inside, under layers of dust and leaves, they find a trapdoor.\n"
"\n"
"They pull and tug, but it doesn't budge."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers are led deeper into the forest. As time passes, the air grows cooler, and the trees on either side of their path slowly thin.\n"
"\n"
"By nightfall the trail ends in a grassy clearing surrounding a small pond.\n"
"\n"
"The animal tracks leading to the clearing abruptly disappear here, and dark stains cover the ground nearby.\n"
"\n"
"Looking up, the settlers see a large brown owl with enormous yellow eyes staring at them."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers follow the trail deeper into the forest.\n"
"\n"
"Trees grow closer and closer together, until the way is so dark that it is hard to tell the time of day.\n"
"\n"
"Finally, the path widens, revealing a sliver of the night sky, and splits into several distinct trails."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid "Follow the animal trail."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid "Follow the thinnest path."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid "Follow the widest path."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers follow a long path up a rocky slope.\n"
"\n"
"It takes them until dawn to reach their destination.\n"
"\n"
"Here, a crack in the hillside explodes into a rushing stream, the opening surrounded by slick, mossy stones."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid ""
"A merrily rushing brook cuts through the green maze of trees, rays of sunlight dancing off its blue waters.\n"
"\n"
"One of the settlers suggests camping here and backtracking in the morning.\n"
"\n"
"Others object, wanting to follow the stream instead, in the hope of finding a way out."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid "Follow the brook upstream."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid "Follow the brook downstream."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid "Set up camp."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid ""
"Thirst and exhaustion wins out, and the group settles in for the evening, making camp beside the stream.\n"
"\n"
"As the sun sets, they gather twigs and dry weeds to start a fire, which burns with a thick, fragrant smoke.\n"
"\n"
"Within minutes, warmth begins to spread throughout their bodies. As they lie down, the stars above twinkle brightly at them, as if wishing them goodnight."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid ""
"Following the stream downhill, the settlers eventually reach a point where they can go no farther.\n"
"\n"
"The brook rushes in a waterfall down the side of a cliff. Above, the cliff rises further, towering over the landscape.\n"
"\n"
"In the damp ground surrounding the stream, however, is an abundance of green moss and unfamiliar plants."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid "Examine the plants."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid "The settlers look around to find that not only are the mosses and grass unusual, but the trees around them are also different from anywhere else in the forest."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid "Climb the cliff."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers decide to climb up the rocky cliff, hoping to get a better view of the labyrinthine forest.\n"
"\n"
"When they reach the top, they can see the canopy spreading far beyond.\n"
"\n"
"Looking in the direction they came from, they see an enormous cedar rising far above the other trees."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid ""
"Following the thinnest trail the settlers reach a giant cedar tree with low, drooping branches.\n"
"\n"
"As they take shelter under them from the sudden downpour, they see a small opening in the trunk near the ground, a welcome refuge from the elements.\n"
"\n"
"They find themselves inside a chamber of living wood, the interior etched with winding vines and animal figures.\n"
"\n"
"Marveling at the strangeness of their shelter, one settler steps backward and stumbles. There, at the back of the chamber, is a series of steps leading underground. \n"
"\n"
"The air grows cold and damp as they descend the ancient stone staircase. At the foot of the stairs is a cave, one side leading toward a faint light."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid "Go toward the darkness."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid "Go toward the light."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers walk deeper into the cave, away from the light, the steady pattering of their footsteps echoing into the distance. \n"
"\n"
"They follow the smooth, cold walls until they round a corner and find themselves in a vast chamber.\n"
"\n"
"The hall is held up by thick pillars etched with intricate designs, their patterns gleaming in the torchlight.\n"
"\n"
"The gnarled, ancient roots of the great cedar have pushed through cracks in the ceiling, twisting around the pillars, and splitting several of them in two.\n"
"\n"
"At the far end of the chamber stands a stone altar. On it is a small figurine of an owl, covered with a layer of dust."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/verdant_labyrinth/event_verdant_labyrinth.tres
msgid ""
"As the settlers walk toward the distant light, they reach a wide underground stream.\n"
"\n"
"Following the flow of dark water, they find the stream picking up speed as it narrows. It winds its way among the slick stone, rushing past their feet toward the light.\n"
"\n"
"The pale glow in the distance gathers on the water's surface. Its source is soon revealed to be a crack in the cave's wall where the stream escapes into the forest outside."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/vinegar_tasters/event_vinegar_tasters.tres
msgid "The Vinegar Tasters"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/vinegar_tasters/event_vinegar_tasters.tres
msgid ""
"The fermentation lodge was established by restoring an old ruin where huge jars of vinegar were found. Today, the fermenters open one such jar and taste the vinegar.\n"
"\n"
"This results in a disagreement. One woman claims it is too sweet. Another that it is too sour. And the third that it is too bitter.\n"
"\n"
"They ask the chief fermenter to resolve their disagreement."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/vinegar_tasters/event_vinegar_tasters.tres
msgid "It is bitter."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/vinegar_tasters/event_vinegar_tasters.tres
msgid ""
"The chief tastes a spoonful and agrees that the vinegar has a bitter note.\n"
"\n"
"\"To expect vinegar to taste sweet is only to invite disappointment,\" she says."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/vinegar_tasters/event_vinegar_tasters.tres
msgid "It is sweet."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/vinegar_tasters/event_vinegar_tasters.tres
msgid ""
"The chief tastes a spoonful and smiles. She thinks the vinegar tastes perfect as it is.\n"
"\n"
"\"This has brewed naturally for centuries,\" she says. \"To forcefully dilute it will only spoil it.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/vinegar_tasters/event_vinegar_tasters.tres
msgid "It is sour."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/vinegar_tasters/event_vinegar_tasters.tres
msgid ""
"The chief tastes a spoonful and puckers her lips.\n"
"\n"
"\"This simply won't do,\" she says. \"It is unrefined, left to grow wild for too long.\"\n"
"\n"
"She instructs her employees to institute a daily regimen of measuring the acidity and maintaining a specific storage temperature. She follows it with a list of rules for the proper handling of jars, split into subsections based on jar size and material."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#. Property: text
#: events/generic/violent_pillar/event_violent_pillar.tres
#: run/run_end/discovery_event.tscn
#: run/run_end/discovery_survey_episode.tscn
msgid "The Painted Wound"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/violent_pillar/event_violent_pillar.tres
msgid ""
"Most of the pillars are gentle: circles, flowers, birds, abstract waves.\n"
"\n"
"But one is not. Its surface is carved and painted with violence: an angry hero plunging a sword into a dragon's head.\n"
"\n"
"Opinions are split between those saying it celebrates the strife that led to the Shattering, and those who consider it a warning.\n"
"\n"
"The former group demands it be torn down, while the latter urges caution: to destroy it is to forget."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/violent_pillar/event_violent_pillar.tres
msgid "Preserve it intact."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/violent_pillar/event_violent_pillar.tres
msgid ""
"The pillar is cleaned, but not altered.\n"
"\n"
"A sign is posted: \"This stood before we arrived.\"\n"
"\n"
"The settlers who called for its removal grumble and refuse to visit the site.\n"
"\n"
"The scholars, however, consider this a victory."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/violent_pillar/event_violent_pillar.tres
msgid "Repaint the scene with a peaceful one, in the same style."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/violent_pillar/event_violent_pillar.tres
msgid ""
"The original image is painted over, preserving the brushwork and palette.\n"
"\n"
"It now shows a harvest procession and a bonfire feast. The pillar keeps its style, but not its story.\n"
"\n"
"The protesting settlers nod, satisfied.\n"
"\n"
"The scholars shake their heads.\n"
"\n"
"Most agree it's easier to visit now."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/violent_pillar/event_violent_pillar.tres
msgid "Record it and repaint in a new style."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/violent_pillar/event_violent_pillar.tres
msgid ""
"The violent image is sketched, annotated, and stored.\n"
"\n"
"The pillar is painted anew, replacing the dragon slayer with abstract shapes in green and silver.\n"
"\n"
"The style doesn't match the others. Artists call it dishonest, but visitors are no longer disturbed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/violent_pillar/event_violent_pillar.tres
msgid "Tear the pillar down."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/violent_pillar/event_violent_pillar.tres
msgid ""
"The stone cracks loudly as it falls. The painting shatters with it.\n"
"\n"
"The pieces are left on the grass.\n"
"\n"
"Those who opposed the pillar nod in relief.\n"
"\n"
"Scholars consider it a day of loss."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/volcano/event_volcano.tres
msgid "The Fire Mountain"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/volcano/event_volcano.tres
msgid ""
"One night, the mountain splits open with a roar. Ash falls like grey snow and stones tumble down the slopes, glowing in the dark.\n"
"\n"
"The villagers flee across the last undamaged bridge leading away from the eruption, but some are still waiting to cross. A burning boulder crashes into the bridge, collapsing it and leaving families stranded on the far side.\n"
"\n"
"Under the burning sky, volunteers spring up from amongst the villagers: a group of strong youngsters claiming to be best able to help, and a group of seniors, saying they've already had long lives, and should be the ones to take the risk."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/volcano/event_volcano.tres
msgid "Let the elders mount the rescue."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/volcano/event_volcano.tres
msgid ""
"The elders' argument prevails. The volunteers wrap wet scarves around their mouths, gather torches from the shrine, and fell trees to create a makeshift bridge.\n"
"\n"
"They cross carefully, calling out to villagers on the other side, their voices lost in the roaring cataclysm.\n"
"\n"
"When the smoke clears, all of the stranded villagers are accounted for, but several of the elders are nowhere to be found."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/volcano/event_volcano.tres
msgid "Let the young guide the stranded villagers."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/volcano/event_volcano.tres
msgid ""
"The youngsters convince the crowd that they have the quickest feet and the strongest lungs. The fittest of them gather their torches, ropes, and axes, felling trees to create a makeshift bridge.\n"
"\n"
"They disappear into the smoke, moving quickly through the ruins, calling out loudly to the people lost among the wreckage. \n"
"\n"
"By daybreak, many of the rescuers return coughing and burned, but some of the families do not return at all."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/volcano/event_volcano.tres
msgid "Search for alternatives."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/volcano/event_volcano.tres
msgid ""
"The eldest woman in the settlement claims to remember an old foraging path she had used before the bridge was built.\n"
"\n"
"Despite the riskiness of the proposition, the villagers follow her up the slopes. The path is narrow, barely visible in the ashy darkness, but the elder seems to know every bend by memory.\n"
"\n"
"The group makes it through to the other side, and they manage to guide their stranded comrades back safely."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/volcano/event_volcano.tres
msgid "Let the volunteers draw lots."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/volcano/event_volcano.tres
msgid ""
"A council member in the crowd decides that there's no time for debate and thrust a basket of bamboo slips at the volunteers, telling them to draw lots.\n"
"\n"
"Those who choose slips smeared with soot place wet cloths over their mouths and head into the ashy darkness. They fell tall trees to create a makeshift bridge and rush across to search for survivors.\n"
"\n"
"Although most of the stranded villagers are saved, the rescue group, having never worked together before, soon scatters, and several of them end up trapped in the ruins."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/wedding_veil/event_wedding_veil.tres
msgid "The Lost Veil"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/wedding_veil/event_wedding_veil.tres
msgid ""
"Cranes gather in the tall grasses, bowing and calling to each other. They eat their fill of insects and rest, drinking from the shallow steppe pools.\n"
"\n"
"Today the town celebrates the birds in a Crane Festival, an auspicious day for weddings. As the sun is setting, a bride waits for the ceremony to begin. A thin white veil embroidered with cranes covers her hair, falling down her white robes.\n"
"\n"
"As she steps out beneath the streamers, a gust of wind carries the veil away, depositing it on top of a crane, who promptly gets tangled in it."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/wedding_veil/event_wedding_veil.tres
msgid "Retrieve the veil."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/wedding_veil/event_wedding_veil.tres
msgid ""
"The groom sends out runners to chase down the bird and retrieve the veil.\n"
"\n"
"Panicked, the bird manages to free itself before the men catch up to it, but the veil is torn and muddy.\n"
"\n"
"The spectacle manages to startle the entire flock. They take flight, loudly croaking their complaints."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/wedding_veil/event_wedding_veil.tres
msgid "Defuse the situation."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/wedding_veil/event_wedding_veil.tres
msgid ""
"The bride is quick to reassure the guests that the mishap is no cause for concern. She asks them to wait in peace, hoping the silence will soothe the trapped creature.\n"
"\n"
"The crowd watches intently as the bird flaps its wings a few times and takes flight, letting the veil flutter free.\n"
"\n"
"The priest in attendance remarks that it is an auspicious omen for the couple's future."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/wedding_veil/event_wedding_veil.tres
msgid "Find a replacement."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/wedding_veil/event_wedding_veil.tres
msgid ""
"The bride's sisters weave a delicate crown out of soft grass and place it on their sister's head.\n"
"\n"
"The lost veil is quickly forgotten and the ceremony proceeds with no further mishaps."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/wedding_veil/event_wedding_veil.tres
msgid "Ignore the mishap."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/wedding_veil/event_wedding_veil.tres
msgid ""
"The priest warns that losing a veil is a highly inauspicious omen, advising the couple to wait until next year's festival to wed.\n"
"\n"
"The bride and groom object, however, and the ceremony goes on despite the lost veil."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/generic/wild_monastery/event_wild_monastery.tres
msgid "The Missing Crows"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/wild_monastery/event_wild_monastery.tres
msgid ""
"This chapter of the Order of the Wilds has forged a bond with the local crows. The birds fly out to forage during the day, and return in the evening to roost on monastery grounds.\n"
"\n"
"Today, as the sun is setting, the flock is nowhere to be seen.\n"
"\n"
"The monks and nuns grow worried, proposing different plans to call the crows back, or go out looking for them in the wilderness."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/wild_monastery/event_wild_monastery.tres
msgid "Call the crows with a conch trumpet."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/wild_monastery/event_wild_monastery.tres
msgid ""
"The monks decide to blow their largest conch trumpet.\n"
"\n"
"One of the monks climbs to a high balcony and brings the shell to his lips, blowing with all his might into the wooden mouthpiece.\n"
"\n"
"An hour later the crows return. The flock is clearly disturbed, making low, knocking sounds instead of their usual lively caws. One of the birds seems to be missing."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/wild_monastery/event_wild_monastery.tres
msgid "Call them back by burning incense."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/wild_monastery/event_wild_monastery.tres
msgid ""
"The novices haul a brazier up to the temple's highest balcony, and fill it with coals and ash, placing several pellets of incense on top.\n"
"\n"
"The air instantly fills with the smell of juniper and mugwort, intimately familiar to the monks and the birds alike.\n"
"\n"
"An hour later the crows return. The flock is clearly disturbed, making low, knocking sounds instead of their usual lively caws. One of the birds seems to be missing."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/wild_monastery/event_wild_monastery.tres
msgid "Send a search party."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/wild_monastery/event_wild_monastery.tres
msgid ""
"Two nuns and a monk pack bags of seeds and walk into the wilderness.\n"
"\n"
"They follow the direction in which the crows flew off in the morning, and eventually hear familiar caws in the distance.\n"
"\n"
"They find the birds agitated. The entire flock is gathered, some on bushes, others on the ground, and cawing loudly. In the center is a dead crow."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/wild_monastery/event_wild_monastery.tres
msgid "Burn herbs from the scent bags to call them back."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/wild_monastery/event_wild_monastery.tres
msgid ""
"The novices haul a brazier up to the temple's highest balcony, and fill it with coals and ash, placing herbs from the scent bags on top.\n"
"\n"
"The air instantly fills with the smell of juniper and mugwort, intimately familiar to the monks and the birds alike.\n"
"\n"
"An hour later the crows return. The flock is clearly disturbed, making low, knocking sounds instead of their usual lively caws. One of the birds seems to be missing."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/generic/wild_monastery/event_wild_monastery.tres
msgid "Wait for the crows to return."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/generic/wild_monastery/event_wild_monastery.tres
msgid ""
"The monks trust the birds to find their way back like they do every day.\n"
"\n"
"The crows only return by dawn. The flock is clearly disturbed, making low, knocking sounds instead of their usual lively caws.\n"
"\n"
"One of the birds seems to be missing."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#. Property: title
#. Property: name
#: events/landmark/communal_baths/event_communal_baths.tres
#: shops/remove_cards/shop_remove_cards.tres
#: stage/spots/square/upgrade_square_2_bathhouse.tres
msgid "Communal Baths"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/communal_baths/event_communal_baths.tres
msgid ""
"Steam curls over the water's surface. Robes hang beside the changing screens. Buckets rest on worn floors.\n"
"\n"
"The baths are warm, but there's only space for one or two people at a time.\n"
"\n"
"\"The old baths weren't just for washing,\" someone says. \"They were for letting go of one's burdens. For clarifying one's thoughts.\"\n"
"\n"
"If we invest some effort, this humble bath could be turned into a large communal bathhouse."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/communal_baths/event_communal_baths.tres
msgid "Build a proper bathhouse."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/landmark/communal_baths/event_communal_baths.tres
msgid ""
"The new bathhouse takes time to build, but it's finally finished. Pipes gurgle. Buckets clatter. The steam stays floating, confined by the ceiling.\n"
"\n"
"When someone leaves the water, they seem just a little lighter."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/communal_baths/event_communal_baths.tres
msgid "Take turns soaking in the water."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/landmark/communal_baths/event_communal_baths.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers take turns, most opting for a brisk, functional scrub. The elders, however, tend to soak until their skin prunes.\n"
"\n"
"By the next day, everyone is rested, but many grumble about the wait."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/communal_baths/event_communal_baths.tres
msgid "Let some run the baths while others bathe."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/landmark/communal_baths/event_communal_baths.tres
msgid ""
"Buckets are passed in silence. Half the visitors fill them, heat them, and test the temperature with care. The other half lowers themselves into the pools with content sighs.\n"
"\n"
"Those who serve do not ask for thanks. Those who rest do not offer apologies. The roles shift naturally over the course of the day."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/communal_baths/event_communal_baths.tres
msgid "Let the water rest."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/landmark/communal_baths/event_communal_baths.tres
msgid ""
"The expedition leaves the baths behind.\n"
"\n"
"There is talk of trying again another day, but the plan is as substantial as the rising steam."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#. Property: title
#. Property: name
#: events/landmark/endless_ruin/event_endless_ruin.tres
#: shops/get_relics/shop_get_relics.tres
#: stage/spots/wasteland/upgrade_wasteland_3_endless_ruin.tres
msgid "Endless Ruin"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/endless_ruin/event_endless_ruin.tres
msgid ""
"The entrance yawns dark below the iron giant, leading into a catacomb of tunnels glimmering with buried glass and bits of metal.\n"
"\n"
"Down in the tunnels, makeshift beams strain under rope rigs and pulleys, as voices echo faintly from further below.\n"
"\n"
"\"This level's stable,\" an archaeologist says, as the ceiling groans in protest.\n"
"\"We could keep descending, if enough of you are willing to hold the ropes.\"\n"
"\n"
"The deeper chambers promise ancient mechanisms and forgotten knowledge, but a slipped rope strike could mean a loss of lives."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/endless_ruin/event_endless_ruin.tres
msgid "Explore the lower chambers."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/landmark/endless_ruin/event_endless_ruin.tres
msgid ""
"A team rigs lines and descends. Echoes trail behind them: metal clangs, murmurs, and the crack of loosening stone.\n"
"\n"
"They emerge scraped and winded, but triumphant. One carries a bundle wrapped in old, frayed fabric.\n"
"\n"
"\"Worth it,\" they say."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/endless_ruin/event_endless_ruin.tres
msgid "Catalog existing findings."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/landmark/endless_ruin/event_endless_ruin.tres
msgid ""
"Instead of braving the caves, the settlers dig through crates of neglected past findings.\n"
"\n"
"Pottery shards and unusually shaped stones are dusted and carefully recorded into a ledger.\n"
"\n"
"No grand discoveries today. Just orderly documenting and shared nods."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/endless_ruin/event_endless_ruin.tres
msgid "Collect fragments from the upper tunnels."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/landmark/endless_ruin/event_endless_ruin.tres
msgid ""
"The settlers collect chipped fragments of ancient tools and weapons, tablets with illegible markings, and pottery embedded in the cavern walls.\n"
"\n"
"None of these are useful by themselves, but someday they may fit into a larger puzzle."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/endless_ruin/event_endless_ruin.tres
msgid "Leave exploration for another day."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/landmark/endless_ruin/event_endless_ruin.tres
msgid ""
"The sun sets with the ruins undisturbed.\n"
"\n"
"The wind whistles through ancient corridors and buried arches.\n"
"\n"
"They'll still be here tomorrow."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/mirage_gate/event_mirage_gate.tres
msgid ""
"The gate is a simple doorway made of three enormous stones.\n"
"\n"
"From a distance, strange landscapes flicker within its opening - spires rising above alien cities, strange plants reaching for purple skies, lizards flying through the air.\n"
"\n"
"Up close, it's just weathered stone, half-sunken in sand.\n"
"\n"
"The more experienced adventurers among the expedition are sure that there's a way to pass through to the other side."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/mirage_gate/event_mirage_gate.tres
msgid "Send experienced adventurers and scholars on a survey."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/mirage_gate/event_mirage_gate.tres
msgid "Attempt to force your way through."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/landmark/mirage_gate/event_mirage_gate.tres
msgid "A dangerous gamble"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/mirage_gate/event_mirage_gate.tres
msgid "Copy the inscriptions from the gate."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/landmark/mirage_gate/event_mirage_gate.tres
msgid ""
"A scholar traces faded markings etched into the base of the gate, lines that look like writing but change under different light.\n"
"\n"
"They don't know what it means, but now it's part of the records."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#. Property: text
#. Property: title
#. Property: name
#: events/landmark/post_road/event_post_road.tres
#: hub/museum/museum_detail_event.tscn
#: hub/museum/museum_detail_survey.tscn
#: shops/connect_settlements/shop_connect_settlements.tres
#: shops/connect_settlements/shop_connect_settlements.tscn
#: stage/spots/plains/upgrade_plains_2_road.tres
msgid "Post Road"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/post_road/event_post_road.tres
msgid ""
"The path stretches further than it did yesterday.\n"
"\n"
"Settlers have begun marking it with wooden stakes and bits of painted cloth. An inn is being planned.\n"
"\n"
"An enterprising settler sets up a stall accepting messages to be delivered.\n"
"\n"
"\"If we extend the road further, there's no telling who will come,\" one settler mutters."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/post_road/event_post_road.tres
msgid "Extend the road all the way to the capital."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/landmark/post_road/event_post_road.tres
msgid ""
"The final stakes are driven in. The surface is leveled. Signposts are set up.\n"
"\n"
"Several houses will soon be converted into inns for travelers.\n"
"\n"
"\"It's open,\" someone says. \"It begins now.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/post_road/event_post_road.tres
msgid "Expand the road within the settlement."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/landmark/post_road/event_post_road.tres
msgid ""
"Rather than optimize for speed or state control, the group reroutes the road through gardens, commons, and gathering spots.\n"
"\n"
"The path becomes slower, but warmer. People pause more. Talk more.\n"
"\n"
"\"A road doesn't have to get you there fast. It just has to keep you together.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/post_road/event_post_road.tres
msgid "Split the road into forks leading into the wilderness."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/landmark/post_road/event_post_road.tres
msgid ""
"Instead of a single road, the path now splits into many forks. Some end in scenic vistas, others disappear into the rough wilderness.\n"
"\n"
"Travel is not as efficient, but it carries folks off the beaten path.\n"
"\n"
"\"The straight line was fastest. But this way, we'll actually see something.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/post_road/event_post_road.tres
msgid "Leave the road in its humble state."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/landmark/post_road/event_post_road.tres
msgid ""
"The stakes stay where they are. The grass grows back slowly.\n"
"\n"
"\"Maybe the stillness was the point,\" someone says. \"For now.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#. Property: title
#. Property: text
#. Property: name
#: events/landmark/print_studio/event_print_studio.tres
#: shops/recall_cards/shop_recall_cards.tres
#: shops/recall_cards/shop_recall_cards.tscn
#: stage/spots/building_large/upgrade_building_large_3_printer.tres
msgid "Woodblock Print Studio"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/print_studio/event_print_studio.tres
msgid ""
"The studio hums with the sound of chisels hitting wood and brushes swiping rapidly across wet paper.\n"
"\n"
"Artists, carvers, and printers are working in perfect concert to make woodblock prints worth spreading all across the shard.\n"
"\n"
"Today, they are deciding on their next project."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/print_studio/event_print_studio.tres
msgid "Reproduce past records."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/landmark/print_studio/event_print_studio.tres
msgid ""
"Old scrolls are unrolled, their ink faded and their meaning almost forgotten.\n"
"\n"
"The carvers trace every mark with reverence, careful to make perfect copies.\n"
"\n"
"When the blocks are inked and pressed, memory survives another generation."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/print_studio/event_print_studio.tres
msgid "Focus on recording local customs and events."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/landmark/print_studio/event_print_studio.tres
msgid ""
"Artists visit farmers, masons, and monks in their research, capturing ceremonies, labor methods, and local architecture.\n"
"\n"
"The carvers transform the sketches into blocks and the printers dutifully set them to paper.\n"
"\n"
"Each sheet is dated and signed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/print_studio/event_print_studio.tres
msgid "Focus on landscape paintings."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/landmark/print_studio/event_print_studio.tres
msgid ""
"The carvers hike out into the wilderness and return with stories of endless hills and uncooperative clouds.\n"
"\n"
"The resulting prints are richly colored, mist rolling in with the gradients.\n"
"\n"
"One could swear they can smell the rain when looking at one of these."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/print_studio/event_print_studio.tres
msgid "Focus on scenes of daily life."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/landmark/print_studio/event_print_studio.tres
msgid ""
"The artists linger in kitchens and marketplaces, sketching laughter, spilled tea, and the tilt of tired shoulders.\n"
"\n"
"When the prints are hung to dry, the whole settlement gathers to point and chuckle. Everyone recognizes someone they know.\n"
"\n"
"Perhaps one way to make art beloved is to make it familiar."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/stone_of_remembrance/event_stone_of_remembrance.tres
msgid ""
"The plaza smells of hot chestnuts and old wood. Someone has swept the dust from the names chiseled into the stone monument.\n"
"\n"
"\"We remember them,\" a settler says.\n"
"\"Well, some of them. And not always fondly,\" another corrects.\n"
"\n"
"A few of the younger settlers carve new names, earning glares from their elders."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/stone_of_remembrance/event_stone_of_remembrance.tres
msgid "Host a remembrance feast."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/landmark/stone_of_remembrance/event_stone_of_remembrance.tres
msgid ""
"Food is shared until everyone is full, and then full again.\n"
"\n"
"A single glyph is carved into the stone.\n"
"\n"
"\"Let this guide us,\" a council leader declares. \"Until the stone wears smooth.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/stone_of_remembrance/event_stone_of_remembrance.tres
msgid "Share stories about the inscribed names."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/landmark/stone_of_remembrance/event_stone_of_remembrance.tres
msgid ""
"Everyone sits close to the stone.\n"
"\n"
"The names are read in order, settlers sharing what they know about each person.\n"
"\n"
"The stories range from proud tales of great artisans, to memories of folks who had too much rice wine and fell asleep up in a tree. Some names remain a mystery, unknown to anyone present.\n"
"\n"
"At the end of the evening, the carvings carry a new, richer significance to the settlers."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/stone_of_remembrance/event_stone_of_remembrance.tres
msgid "Chant the names together."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/landmark/stone_of_remembrance/event_stone_of_remembrance.tres
msgid ""
"The chanting begins awkwardly, stumbling over names whose pronunciation has been lost to history.\n"
"\n"
"Soon it gains a rhythm, as pronunciations are invented on the spot, and the more puzzling names are simply skipped.\n"
"\n"
"Nothing new is learned about the lives of the ancestors, but a unity is forged among the townspeople, as keepers of this long and shared history."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/stone_of_remembrance/event_stone_of_remembrance.tres
msgid "Leave the monument undisturbed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/landmark/stone_of_remembrance/event_stone_of_remembrance.tres
msgid ""
"The stone remains untouched.\n"
"\n"
"Occasionally, someone clears the moss.\n"
"\n"
"Bowls of rice appear as offerings at the foot of the stone now and then."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#. Property: title
#. Property: name
#: events/landmark/verse_arena/event_verse_arena.tres
#: shops/heal/shop_heal.tres
#: stage/spots/square/upgrade_square_2_poet_arena.tres
msgid "Verse Arena"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/verse_arena/event_verse_arena.tres
msgid ""
"In the corner of the square several aspiring poets are gathered around a vase of flowers.\n"
"\n"
"They sit quietly, occasionally remarking on the sound of the drooping blossoms or the taste of the wind.\n"
"\n"
"Each is waiting for someone more daring to let the first verse drop."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/verse_arena/event_verse_arena.tres
msgid "Hold a formal poetry contest."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/landmark/verse_arena/event_verse_arena.tres
msgid ""
"As the poets start declaiming their verses, more and more settlers gather around them. Some sit on the benches, humming in time with the rhythm.\n"
"\n"
"By nightfall, the air holds more than words.\n"
"\n"
"Much of what was shared will fade, but it will inspire future beauty to bloom."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/verse_arena/event_verse_arena.tres
msgid "Preserve all the poems for future record."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/landmark/verse_arena/event_verse_arena.tres
msgid ""
"The scribes work through the night, recording all the verses composed by the settlement's poets.\n"
"\n"
"Each poem is copied down, line by line, stroke by stroke.\n"
"\n"
"The poets and scribes alike are exhausted, but the records remain."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/verse_arena/event_verse_arena.tres
msgid "Set the poems to music."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/landmark/verse_arena/event_verse_arena.tres
msgid ""
"Musicians from the expedition join the aspiring poets, carrying string, reed, and drum.\n"
"\n"
"The verses are transformed, lifted, and carried further than words alone could reach.\n"
"\n"
"The evening is long and filled with merriment."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/landmark/verse_arena/event_verse_arena.tres
msgid "Let the square remain quiet."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/main_quest/1_20_talisman/event_talismans.tres
msgid "Legacy Event: Talisman"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/1_20_talisman/event_talismans.tres
msgid ""
"An old monk sits on a straw mat by the shard's edge, watching the Cloud Sea stretch to the horizon.\n"
"\n"
"He has prayed for guidance every morning since he came to this shard.\n"
"\n"
"Today, he thinks he hears an answer: the Enlightened One wants the people to carry a small reminder of their purpose."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/1_20_talisman/event_talismans.tres
msgid "Choose an herbal scent bag."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_outcome_hint
#. Property: description
#: events/main_quest/1_20_talisman/event_talismans.tres
#: events/main_quest/1_30_defiled_shrine/event_defiled_shrine.tres
#: events/main_quest/1_30_shrine_ritual/event_shrine_ritual.tres
#: events/main_quest/2_10_places_of_power/event_firefox.tres
msgid "This will leave a mark on history."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/main_quest/1_20_talisman/event_talismans.tres
msgid ""
"The monk gathers herbs from the shard's edge and wraps them in cloth. The smell is faint but calming.\n"
"\n"
"\"Let the faithful smell of the wilds,\" he hears in his mind. \"Not of the grand incense and decadence of the past.\"\n"
"\n"
"The sachet is simple linen, stitched shut, hanging on a rough cord. In days to come, monks will pack these with dried mugwort, mint, and cypress shavings, to share with anyone who comes asking."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/1_20_talisman/event_talismans.tres
msgid "Choose a seed pouch."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/main_quest/1_20_talisman/event_talismans.tres
msgid ""
"The monk ties a few grains into a small pouch.\n"
"\n"
"\"Carry this pouch as a reminder: you are the seeds of this new world,\" he hears in his mind. \"Your ancestors harvested what they did not sow. You, instead, shall sow what you may not harvest.\"\n"
"\n"
"In days to come, pouches will be stitched from leftover strips of loosely woven cloth, and filled with a handful of seeds. Some will put in rice grains. Others will fill theirs with wildflower seeds. People will carry their pouches at the belt; light enough to forget, obvious enough to make a child ask what it means."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/1_20_talisman/event_talismans.tres
msgid "Choose a charcoal bead."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/main_quest/1_20_talisman/event_talismans.tres
msgid ""
"From the ashes of old fires, the monk shapes tiny beads. Each one leaves a dark mark on his fingers.\n"
"\n"
"\"Remember the ashes of the old world, lest you lose humility,\" he hears in his mind. \"If the world is to be reunited, you will have to get your hands dirty.\"\n"
"\n"
"In days to come, beads will be pressed from pure charcoal, polished until they shine. Some will hang one at their throat. Others will adorn their belts with them. The beads will spread quickly through the new towns, the people feeling as if they carry embers still faintly glowing with purpose."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/1_20_talisman/event_talismans.tres
msgid "Choose a copper ring."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/main_quest/1_20_talisman/event_talismans.tres
msgid ""
"The monk commissions simple rings hammered from scrap, rough and unadorned.\n"
"\n"
"\"Let these bands remind you that your line never ends,\" he hears in his mind. \"Though your world may have come apart, you will persevere to bring it back together.\"\n"
"\n"
"In days to come, elders and children alike will wear them. Some will even wear one on each hand. A few settlers will attach gems they carried from the Old World to theirs, but the practice won't last."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/main_quest/1_30_defiled_shrine/event_defiled_shrine.tres
msgid "Legacy Event: Defiled Shrine"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/1_30_defiled_shrine/event_defiled_shrine.tres
msgid ""
"Morning finds the shrine defiled. Fences crushed, offerings overturned, and sacred ground soiled.\n"
"\n"
"Rumors mutter of drunk settlers, stumbling home from the shrine dedication. Those formerly drunk settlers point the finger at wild beasts, drawn by food left over from the celebration.\n"
"\n"
"Monks discuss whether to set guards at the shrine, question the people, or deter the animals. Unable to settle on a solution, they meditate to receive the Enlightened One's wisdom."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/1_30_defiled_shrine/event_defiled_shrine.tres
msgid "Cull the wild animals."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/main_quest/1_30_defiled_shrine/event_defiled_shrine.tres
msgid ""
"Hunters are called. Traps are set at the forest's edge, arrows loosed into the brush.\n"
"\n"
"Soon the shrine grounds fall quieter. No shuffling can be heard from the undergrowth. No pawprints disturb the soil.\n"
"\n"
"The monks breathe easier, their peace no longer disturbed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/1_30_defiled_shrine/event_defiled_shrine.tres
msgid "Station guards and only admit monks."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/main_quest/1_30_defiled_shrine/event_defiled_shrine.tres
msgid ""
"Fences are rebuilt taller, with gates that open only to monks.\n"
"\n"
"Guards are hired to stand watch with staves at all hours.\n"
"\n"
"The sacred grounds remain protected, villagers and animals alike maintaining their distance.\n"
"\n"
"The monks breathe easier, their peace no longer disturbed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/1_30_defiled_shrine/event_defiled_shrine.tres
msgid "Question the locals."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/main_quest/1_30_defiled_shrine/event_defiled_shrine.tres
msgid ""
"The monks summon the village in, one household at a time.\n"
"\n"
"Sharp questions fall, faces pale, and denials echo hollow.\n"
"\n"
"Finally some admit the drink had erased last night's memory. Their friends confirm the crime, eager to be spared suspicion.\n"
"\n"
"The culprits are made to clean the shrine for the next month, and no further incidents occur.\n"
"\n"
"The monks breathe easier, their peace no longer disturbed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/1_30_defiled_shrine/event_defiled_shrine.tres
msgid "Forgive and move on."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/main_quest/1_30_defiled_shrine/event_defiled_shrine.tres
msgid ""
"The fences are raised again, and the grounds are swept clean.\n"
"\n"
"Those who drank in excess are the most eager to volunteer help.\n"
"\n"
"The incident is soon forgotten.\n"
"\n"
"The monks breathe easier, their peace no longer disturbed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/main_quest/1_30_shrine_ritual/event_shrine_ritual.tres
msgid "Legacy Event: Shrine Ritual"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/1_30_shrine_ritual/event_shrine_ritual.tres
msgid ""
"The shrine is raised, its roof tiles tied and its gate painted, but the monks murmur uneasily.\n"
"\n"
"\"Faith is not in the wooden beams,\" says one. \"It must be kept alive with action.\"\n"
"\n"
"The day is spent in meditation, attuning to the Enlightened One's presence.\n"
"\n"
"A ritual is needed. A simple act the people should weave into their visits. A way for the shrine to bind the people together."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/1_30_shrine_ritual/event_shrine_ritual.tres
msgid "Burn incense to appease the spirits."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/main_quest/1_30_shrine_ritual/event_shrine_ritual.tres
msgid ""
"Each visitor arrives with a stick of incense, crafted by their own hand or acquired from artisans.\n"
"\n"
"It is burned before the altar, a curl of smoke rising to meld with the others.\n"
"\n"
"The scent will cling to robes and hallways, a reminder that the spirit world is never far."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/1_30_shrine_ritual/event_shrine_ritual.tres
msgid "Contribute to a communal rice pot."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/main_quest/1_30_shrine_ritual/event_shrine_ritual.tres
msgid ""
"Each day, a monk is tasked with tending the giant cauldron.\n"
"\n"
"Visitors bring their grain in the morning, and return with bowls by lunchtime.\n"
"\n"
"No one counts what is brought or what is taken, and the shrine's blessing keeps bellies fed across the settlement."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/1_30_shrine_ritual/event_shrine_ritual.tres
msgid "Bring fallen leaves and petals to the shrine."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/main_quest/1_30_shrine_ritual/event_shrine_ritual.tres
msgid ""
"Each visitor picks up stray debris on the way to the shrine, and deposits them into a shared basket.\n"
"\n"
"The basket changes with the seasons, burning orange in the fall, and blush pink in the spring. Even in winter, twigs and acorns find their way into the basket.\n"
"\n"
"What one person drops is hardly noticed. Yet together the offerings form a living tapestry."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/1_30_shrine_ritual/event_shrine_ritual.tres
msgid "Meditate on where the water meets the gate."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/main_quest/1_30_shrine_ritual/event_shrine_ritual.tres
msgid ""
"Each visitor pauses at the shore, eyes resting on where the waterline meets the gate.\n"
"\n"
"Some days the water is below the foundation stones, ground peeking through. In rainy months the gate appears to float, the lake rising halfway up the pillars.\n"
"\n"
"Although no one keeps a record, everyone seems aware of where the line was even weeks ago."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/main_quest/2_10_places_of_power/event_firefox.tres
msgid "Legacy Event: Fox-Haunted Tree"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_10_places_of_power/event_firefox.tres
msgid ""
"The expedition ventures deep into the forest, following signs interpreted by The Scribe.\n"
"\n"
"At last they reach a vast glade, quiet and bright beneath the canopy. Moss glows faintly in the filtered light, and the air smells of rain.\n"
"\n"
"The reverie is interrupted by movement among the trees. White tails flicker, darting like stray brushstrokes in the mist. The settlers follow, until the paths twist back upon themselves.\n"
"\n"
"By the time they find their way again, night has fallen. They emerge to see an old, dry tree surrounded by foxes, dozens of them, pale as moonlight. Some swear they shine faintly.\n"
"\n"
"\"This place is haunted,\" says the Scribe. \"We must act before the curse spreads.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_10_places_of_power/event_firefox.tres
msgid "Banish the spirits with a drop of blood."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: events/main_quest/2_10_places_of_power/event_firefox.tres
msgid "<unset>"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/main_quest/2_10_places_of_power/event_firefox.tres
msgid ""
"The Scribe and his disciples surround the tree.\n"
"\n"
"A shallow cut, a whispered incantation, and the foxes scatter like embers in the wind.\n"
"\n"
"\"With our lifeblood, we have cleansed these woods,\" the Scribe declares. \"No spirit will dare set foot here again.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_10_places_of_power/event_firefox.tres
msgid "Purify the ground with salt."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/main_quest/2_10_places_of_power/event_firefox.tres
msgid ""
"Rings of salt are poured around the withered tree.\n"
"\n"
"The foxes watch from afar, silent, observing.\n"
"\n"
"\"We have claimed these woods,\" The Scribe declares. \"No spirit will dare set foot here again.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_10_places_of_power/event_firefox.tres
msgid "Record the event and leave the tree untouched."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/main_quest/2_10_places_of_power/event_firefox.tres
msgid ""
"With considerable efforts, the tired settlers convince the Scribe to let the spirits go.\n"
"\n"
"Detailed entries are made in the expedition log. Sketches are drawn.\n"
"\n"
"The foxes watch as the procession departs."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_10_places_of_power/event_firefox.tres
msgid "Cut down the tree."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/main_quest/2_10_places_of_power/event_firefox.tres
msgid ""
"The foxes scatter as glyphs are inscribed onto axes.\n"
"\n"
"The settlers make short work of the tree. It cracks at the first touch of a blade, crumbling to the ground.\n"
"\n"
"\"Now these woods are cleansed,\" the Scribe declares."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/main_quest/2_10_places_of_power/event_mq210_field.tres
msgid "Place of Power: Endless Blossoms"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/main_quest/2_10_places_of_power/event_mq210_lanterns.tres
msgid "Place of Power: Ghost Lanterns"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_field/event_consecration_field.tres
msgid "Consecration: Endless Blossoms"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_field/event_consecration_field.tres
msgid ""
"The expedition gathers at the edge of a vast meadow where petals sway gently in the breeze, bright and unending. Even the insects seem hushed, afraid to disturb this eternal spring.\n"
"\n"
"This is the place the Scribe named in his plan, a field where the world refuses to change. A place of stillness, of [i]Stability[/i].\n"
"\n"
"Disciples prepare the consecration ritual, going over the Scribe's instructions again and again."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_field/event_consecration_field.tres
msgid "Pour a circle of salt to mark the ground sacred."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_requirement_hint
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_field/event_consecration_field.tres
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_forest/event_consecration_forest.tres
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_lanterns/event_consecration_lanterns.tres
msgid "A previous choice"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_requirement_tooltip
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_field/event_consecration_field.tres
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_forest/event_consecration_forest.tres
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_lanterns/event_consecration_lanterns.tres
msgid "A previous choice: purified the fox spirits' tree with salt"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_field/event_consecration_field.tres
msgid "Offer blood to awaken the meadow."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_requirement_tooltip
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_field/event_consecration_field.tres
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_forest/event_consecration_forest.tres
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_lanterns/event_consecration_lanterns.tres
msgid "A previous choice: banished the fox spirits' by spilling blood"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_field/event_consecration_field.tres
msgid "Ignite the center to draw out the meadow's power."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_requirement_tooltip
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_field/event_consecration_field.tres
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_forest/event_consecration_forest.tres
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_lanterns/event_consecration_lanterns.tres
msgid "A previous choice: cut down the fox spirits' tree"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_field/event_consecration_field.tres
msgid "Raise a banner of constancy above the meadow."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_requirement_tooltip
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_field/event_consecration_field.tres
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_forest/event_consecration_forest.tres
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_lanterns/event_consecration_lanterns.tres
msgid "A previous choice: left the fox spirits' tree alone"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_field/event_consecration_field.tres
msgid ""
"A ring of salt is poured around the center of the field, grains glittering in the sunlight on the petals.\n"
"\n"
"By morning, the blossoms on the edges of the ring have wilted. As days pass, the effect spreads, flowers bowing in turn.\n"
"\n"
"\"The power is draining into the Enlightened One's glyphs,\" the disciples declare. \"This place has given up its energies to aid in the Reunification.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_field/event_consecration_field.tres
msgid ""
"A shallow cut is made across each disciple's palm, as they walk in a careful procession through the meadow, tracing a great glyph in a trail of red.\n"
"\n"
"Days pass as incantations are chanted. Soon, the effects begin to show.\n"
"\n"
"What once was a sea of purple begins to bloom with splotches of pale pink blossoms. The pink slowly deepens, and by the end of the week the whole meadow is ablush with scarlet.\n"
"\n"
"\"Our blood has opened the gate,\" the disciples agree. \"This place is now a channel of the Enlightened One's powers.\"\n"
"\n"
"The scent of iron hangs in the air, but none speak of it."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_field/event_consecration_field.tres
msgid ""
"A circle of blossoms is cut. Leaf and petal alike are set ablaze.\n"
"\n"
"The fire digs greedily into its meal, burning without smoke despite the wet fuel.\n"
"\n"
"Disciples meditate, tracing glyphs they see in the waves of heat rippling through the air.\n"
"\n"
"\"The sacred flames have claimed this place in the Enlightened One's name,\" they agree. \"It will power the grand ritual to come.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_field/event_consecration_field.tres
msgid ""
"A great banner inscribed with the glyph of constancy is lifted above the meadow.\n"
"\n"
"The cloth flutters, lively in a sudden gust of wind.\n"
"\n"
"\"The Scribe told us to wait for a sign,\" one disciple remarks, \"but I didn't expect it so quickly.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"The Enlightened One approves,\" says another.\n"
"\n"
"They all agree that their glyphs resonate more deeply with the shard's energies now."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_forest/event_consecration_forest.tres
msgid "Consecration: Eternal Glade"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_forest/event_consecration_forest.tres
msgid ""
"Not far from the Eternal Glade the Scribe's disciples find the vein of the forest, a narrow trough lined with ancient, towering trees on both sides. Moss covers the ground in a thick, plush carpet.\n"
"\n"
"This is the place the Scribe named in his plan, where roots draw the shard's life force to the surface. A place of [i]Life[/i], now free from the haunting of the fox spirits."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_forest/event_consecration_forest.tres
msgid "Pour holy water to consecrate the trees."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_forest/event_consecration_forest.tres
msgid "Draw sap from the trees as an offering."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_forest/event_consecration_forest.tres
msgid "Ignite the forest to cleanse it with fire."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_forest/event_consecration_forest.tres
msgid "Test and record the trees' resonance."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_forest/event_consecration_forest.tres
msgid ""
"The disciples boil herbs in salty sea water, filling pots inscribed with glyphs of life and purity. They pour the water slowly, neatly following along the forest's vein. Steam rises where the water falls, spreading into the air in ghostly ribbons.\n"
"\n"
"The trees appear unscathed, but by the next morning, the moss carpeting the forest floor darkens, curling into a slimy, brown sludge.\n"
"\n"
"\"The impurities are purged,\" the disciples declare. \"The life force now flows pure and concentrated, no longer sapped by lesser growth.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_forest/event_consecration_forest.tres
msgid ""
"Sharp stakes are driven into the oldest trees, their sap gathered in flasks beneath the punctures. The liquid runs thick, almost opaque.\n"
"\n"
"\"The trees offer their own tribute to the Enlightened One,\" a disciple declares. \"Their blood carries the power of life itself.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_forest/event_consecration_forest.tres
msgid ""
"Torches are lit, and flames soon start creeping along the underbrush. The fire burns fiercely, clouds of smoke hanging like a curtain among the trees, but it doesn't spread.\n"
"\n"
"When it finally goes out, the air is thick with ash. Charred shapes are left behind in the bark, which the disciples inscribe in their scrolls.\n"
"\n"
"\"Through the purifying fire, the Enlightened One has sent down a message for us,\" the disciples whisper. \"These glyphs will power the ritual to come.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_forest/event_consecration_forest.tres
msgid ""
"The disciples move carefully among the trees, tracing glyphs in the air and waiting for a response. Some leaves rustle, others fall. Each movement is faithfully recorded as evidence of resonance.\n"
"\n"
"By the end of the day, strips of paper hang from the tree trunks, each marked with the glyphs that resonated with each tree.\n"
"\n"
"\"We have learned which glyphs resonate with Life,\" the disciples conclude. \"The Enlightened One's grand design is becoming clearer each day.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_lanterns/event_consecration_lanterns.tres
msgid "Consecration: Ghost Lanterns"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_lanterns/event_consecration_lanterns.tres
msgid ""
"The expedition arrives at the dock, where rows of pale lanterns glow softly in the night. The water below is calm, moonlight dancing on its ripples.\n"
"\n"
"This is the place the Scribe named in his plan, a passage between worlds, a place of [i]Change[/i].\n"
"\n"
"Disciples prepare for the consecration, laying out their implements with practiced care. The air tastes faintly of salt and seaweed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_lanterns/event_consecration_lanterns.tres
msgid "Pour a trail of ash between the lanterns."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_lanterns/event_consecration_lanterns.tres
msgid "Offer blood in return for the lanterns' power."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_lanterns/event_consecration_lanterns.tres
msgid "Shatter the lanterns to release their light."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_lanterns/event_consecration_lanterns.tres
msgid "Replace the lanterns to direct their glow upward."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_lanterns/event_consecration_lanterns.tres
msgid ""
"A trail of ash is poured between the lanterns, and a great urn is emptied into the sea.\n"
"\n"
"Some of the ash sinks, but much of it rises, hanging in the air around the dock. Soon a fine mist envelops the lanterns, glowing with borrowed light.\n"
"\n"
"Disciples watch for glyphs in the mist's curls, now appearing, now dissipating. They spend the night meditating on Change and transformation.\n"
"\n"
"\"The air itself was shifting,\" one recalls. \"It let me appreciate the Enlightened One's power to change the very essence of the world.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_lanterns/event_consecration_lanterns.tres
msgid ""
"The disciples kneel between the lanterns, marking the dock with splatters of crimson. The sea ripples as they chant, echoing the rhythm of their incantations.\n"
"\n"
"Before long, the incantations evolve, words in languages unknown spilling from the tongues of the bloodied men and women. Cries follow, and laughter, and new glyphs traced in the air with hand and foot.\n"
"\n"
"Eventually exhaustion overtakes the group and they retreat, leaving unmistakable stains behind.\n"
"\n"
"\"The sea spoke through us,\" they declare in the morning. \"It is prepared to glorify the Enlightened One.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_lanterns/event_consecration_lanterns.tres
msgid ""
"Hammers fall in unison, and the first lantern shatters into the waves below. Others follow, stone crumbling like sand.\n"
"\n"
"The disciples stand among the ruins, proud of their accomplishment.\n"
"\n"
"\"The light has been set free,\" one declares in the darkness. \"It will find its way home.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/2_30_consecration_lanterns/event_consecration_lanterns.tres
msgid ""
"The disciples carefully replace each lantern with a new design, boxes they brought from the Haven, with a single opening at the top. The glow no longer spills outward, but rises, like a beacon, into the sky.\n"
"\n"
"\"Before, the energies were wasted,\" one explains. \"This will direct them heavenward, a channel for the Enlightened One's power.\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_rocks_reply/event_listen_rocks_reply.tres
msgid "The Canyon Spirit"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_rocks_reply/event_listen_rocks_reply.tres
msgid ""
"Scholars gather by the canyon walls to study the cracks in the rock face. Many of the cracks bear an uncanny resemblance to common glyphs.\n"
"\n"
"\"Look! This one says [b]temple[/b]! Or maybe [b]wait[/b]?\" a young scholar says, pointing at a jumble of cracks. \"This must be one of the signs the Scribe told us to look for! A place where the spirit of the Enlightened One speaks to us through cracks.\"\n"
"\n"
"The other scholars gather around her, eager to take a look. The decision is soon reached: we must carve a question and wait for the Enlightened One's answer."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_rocks_reply/event_listen_rocks_reply.tres
msgid "Carve \"How do we rebuild the world?\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_rocks_reply/event_listen_rocks_reply.tres
msgid ""
"The question is carved at dusk. The expedition sets up camp and spends the night beneath walls.\n"
"\n"
"At dawn, new cracks have appeared around the carving.\n"
"\n"
"It takes the scholars a while to interpret them, but finally they realize that the glyph they are looking for is an ancient form, unused since long before the Shattering."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_rocks_reply/event_listen_rocks_reply.tres
msgid "Carve \"How do we keep our people safe?\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_rocks_reply/event_listen_rocks_reply.tres
msgid "Carve \"How do we gain wisdom?\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_rocks_reply/event_listen_rocks_reply.tres
msgid "Carve \"How do we regain your favor?\""
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_rocks_reply/event_listen_rocks_reply.tres
msgid ""
"The question is carved at dusk. The expedition sets up camp and spends the night beneath the walls.\n"
"\n"
"At dawn, new cracks have appeared around the carving.\n"
"\n"
"It takes the scholars a while to interpret them, but finally they realize that the glyph they are looking for is an ancient form, unused since long before the Shattering."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_singing_cascades/event_listen_singing_cascades.tres
msgid "The Voice of Water"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_singing_cascades/event_listen_singing_cascades.tres
msgid ""
"The waterfall tumbles over countless rocky ledges with a deafening roar. Several scholars from the expedition have gathered by the pool at the foot of the falls, listening intently.\n"
"\n"
"\"This melody... a hymn from the Old World,\" one scholar whispers reverently.\n"
"\n"
"\"I can hear words,\" another says.\n"
"\n"
"\"It sounds just like the rowing songs we used to keep the rhythm,\" a retired sailor chimes in.\n"
"\n"
"The scholars are all convinced that the Enlightened One's fractured spirit is sending a message through the cascade, but none can agree what it is."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_singing_cascades/event_listen_singing_cascades.tres
msgid "It is an uplifting hymn."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: preview_description
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_singing_cascades/event_listen_singing_cascades.tres
msgid "Gain 25 maximum <term:inspiration> for the rest of the <term:run>"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_singing_cascades/event_listen_singing_cascades.tres
msgid "Gained 25 maximum <term:inspiration> for the rest of the <term:run>."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_singing_cascades/event_listen_singing_cascades.tres
msgid ""
"The scholar who first heard the hymn hums along to help the rest of the group recognize it.\n"
"\n"
"Soon everyone can hear it, and some invent verses on the spot to go with the melody.\n"
"\n"
"By the time the expedition moves on, they are newly inspired, confident that the Enlightened One had blessed their path."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_singing_cascades/event_listen_singing_cascades.tres
msgid "It is a rowing song."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: preview_description
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_singing_cascades/event_listen_singing_cascades.tres
msgid "Increase <term:hand_size> by 1 for the rest of the <term:run>"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_singing_cascades/event_listen_singing_cascades.tres
msgid "Increased <term:hand_size> by 1 for the rest of the <term:run>."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_singing_cascades/event_listen_singing_cascades.tres
msgid ""
"The retired sailor starts tapping his foot, and soon scholars are common folk alike are clapping along to the thunderous beat.\n"
"\n"
"The rhythm is relentless, driving, and incredibly catchy. The expedition adopts the beat for their labor, finding that they can handle more work when everyone is moving in perfect sync."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_singing_cascades/event_listen_singing_cascades.tres
msgid "It is words of wisdom."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: preview_description
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_singing_cascades/event_listen_singing_cascades.tres
msgid "Gain an extra <term_lower:glyph> reward after each <term:foray> the rest of the <term:run>"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_singing_cascades/event_listen_singing_cascades.tres
msgid "Gained an extra <term_lower:glyph> reward after each <term:foray> the rest of the <term:run>."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_singing_cascades/event_listen_singing_cascades.tres
msgid ""
"Ink splatters in time with the water, as the scholars frantically brush symbols onto their scrolls, transcribing what they hear.\n"
"\n"
"By the time the sun sets, they have compiled a massive list.\n"
"\n"
"Although the meaning is not immediately intelligible, the scholars are bound to find wisdom in the glyphs once they've had time to study them."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_singing_cascades/event_listen_singing_cascades.tres
msgid "It is a mathematical pattern."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: preview_description
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_singing_cascades/event_listen_singing_cascades.tres
msgid "The <term:draw_pile> will appear in order for the rest of the <term:run>"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_singing_cascades/event_listen_singing_cascades.tres
msgid "The <term:draw_pile> will appear in order for the rest of the <term:run>."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/main_quest/3_10_listen_singing_cascades/event_listen_singing_cascades.tres
msgid ""
"One of the scholars, a mathematician, begins counting the seconds between the heaviest cascades. \"Three, then five, then two,\" she mutters, drawing charts in the mud.\n"
"\n"
"Although she can't yet pinpoint the meaning in the repeating pattern, she insists that the Enlightened One must be showing them the importance of keeping precise order. \"That is how we stay in harmony with the world,\" she explains."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: event_name
#. Property: name
#. Property: text
#: events/main_quest/3_50_accord_monument/event_accord_monument.tres
#: quests/main/phase3/3_50_accord_monument/quest_main_3_50_accord_monument.tres
#: shard_types/mq_accord_monument/shard_type_mq_accord_monument.tres
#: shops/accord_monument/shop_accord_monument.tscn
msgid "The Accord Monument"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/3_50_accord_monument/event_accord_monument.tres
msgid "This town square seems like a great place to start setting up the Accord Monument. It will take a lot of work, but we can get started right now."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/3_50_accord_monument/event_accord_monument.tres
msgid "Start the project."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_result_text
#: events/main_quest/3_50_accord_monument/event_accord_monument.tres
msgid ""
"The project is started.\n"
"\n"
"Significant resources will have to be dedicated to bring it to completion."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: markedup_text
#: events/main_quest/3_50_accord_monument/event_accord_monument.tres
msgid "Leave the project for another shard."
msgstr ""

