#. TRANSLATORS: Property: record_title
#: quests/main/phase3/3_10_listen/dlg_quest_main_3_10_listen_begin.tres
msgid "Era 三: Nature's Advice"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: quests/main/phase3/3_10_listen/dlg_quest_main_3_10_listen_begin.tres
msgid ""
"PAGE: historian(STUDIO_SECONDARY), scribe(STUDIO_PRIMARY)\n"
"historian: I hear you've called a general assembly tomorrow.\n"
"historian: Have you found something new?\n"
"scribe: Indeed.\n"
"scribe: I have had a revelation.\n"
"scribe: We know that the Enlightened One has not abandoned us, so the fault must lie in our actions.\n"
"scribe: The hauntings are not what they seem.\n"
"historian: That would explain why no one can ever agree on the details...\n"
"scribe: That is because we were so quick to pacify them.\n"
"scribe: We should have observed instead.\n"
"scribe: You have seen as well as I that the spirits never take everything from us.\n"
"scribe: They merely limit our greed.\n"
"scribe: Enforce a balance.\n"
"historian: They would probably take all they can if we let them.\n"
"scribe: Only if we deserved it.\n"
"scribe: This justice...\n"
"scribe: It can only come from one source.\n"
"scribe: When the Old World shattered, the Enlightened One's divine spirit must have fractured.\n"
"scribe: Perhaps the hauntings are corrupted spirit shards...\n"
"scribe: The divine sorrow manifesting.\n"
"historian: Well, that's a grim thought.\n"
"historian: Not only are we alone, but our savior is corrupted and trying to fight us?\n"
"historian: I'm not sure I'm quite ready to give up hope just yet.\n"
"scribe: You misunderstand...\n"
"scribe: The hauntings are not the only fragments.\n"
"scribe: The Enlightened One is all around us.\n"
"scribe: In rushing rivers and ancient trees.\n"
"scribe: In shifting gales and wild beasts.\n"
"historian: Let's say you're right.\n"
"historian: What do you propose we do about it?\n"
"scribe: Have you noticed how birds always sing exactly at dawn?\n"
"scribe: Or how cicadas always emerge in thirteen year cycles?\n"
"scribe: These regularities are how the Enlightened One is communicating with us.\n"
"scribe: If we just listen, we will hear the divine will through the voice of nature."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: record_title
#: quests/main/phase3/3_10_listen/dlg_quest_main_3_10_listen_end.tres
msgid "Era 三: Nature's Advice 二"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: quests/main/phase3/3_10_listen/dlg_quest_main_3_10_listen_end.tres
msgid ""
"PAGE: scribe(PORTAL_NETWORK), AUDIENCE\n"
"scribe: We have seen the signs.\n"
"scribe: The Enlightened One does speak to us through the land.\n"
"scribe: But the fractured spirits are faint.\n"
"scribe: They do not yet trust us, or they would not appear as hauntings.\n"
"scribe: We must learn to live in harmony with the land.\n"
"scribe: To prove our worth by action, or even sacrifice.\n"
"scribe: Our efforts have broken the long silence, but we must find a place of quiet communion, out in the wilderness.\n"
"scribe: A place where the spirits of the wild feel welcome to approach us."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name
#: quests/main/phase3/3_10_listen/quest_main_3_10_listen.tres
msgid "Nature's Advice"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: goals[]
#: quests/main/phase3/3_10_listen/quest_main_3_10_listen.tres
msgid "Find a place where the voice of nature can be heard."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: goals[]
#: quests/main/phase3/3_10_listen/quest_main_3_10_listen.tres
msgid "Find a place where the wisdom of nature can be read."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: record_title
#: quests/main/phase3/3_20_wild_monastery/dlg_quest_main_3_20_wild_monastery_end.tres
msgid "Era 三: Communion with the Wilds"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: quests/main/phase3/3_20_wild_monastery/dlg_quest_main_3_20_wild_monastery_end.tres
msgid ""
"PAGE: scribe(STUDIO_PRIMARY), historian(STUDIO_SECONDARY)\n"
"scribe: The monks of the Holy Wilds have sent word.\n"
"historian: Already?\n"
"historian: Well, what do they say?\n"
"scribe: They have found fragments of the divine spirit alive and well within the beasts of the land.\n"
"scribe: Foxes and rabbits alike now roam the monastery's grounds.\n"
"scribe: If we could convince these spirits to help us, perhaps they will show us the Enlightened One's will."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name
#: quests/main/phase3/3_20_wild_monastery/quest_main_3_20_wild_monastery.tres
msgid "Communion with the Wilds"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: goals[]
#: quests/main/phase3/3_20_wild_monastery/quest_main_3_20_wild_monastery.tres
msgid "Establish the [url=shard_type:mq_wild_monastery]Holy Wilds[/url] culture on a shard."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: record_title
#: quests/main/phase3/3_30_companions/dlg_quest_main_3_30_companions_end.tres
msgid "Era 三: A Helping Paw"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: quests/main/phase3/3_30_companions/dlg_quest_main_3_30_companions_end.tres
msgid ""
"PAGE: scribe(STUDIO_PRIMARY), historian(STUDIO_SECONDARY)\n"
"scribe: The beasts of the wilds walk among us in peace.\n"
"scribe: We are finally connecting with the Enlightened One's fractured spirit.\n"
"historian: I haven't noticed anything divine about these animals yet.\n"
"historian: But perhaps it's too early to tell.\n"
"historian: And besides, it's nice not to worry about the wildlife raiding town granaries every night.\n"
"\n"
"PAGE: explorer(CONVERSATION), historian(STUDIO_SECONDARY), scribe(STUDIO_PRIMARY)\n"
"explorer: Hello there!\n"
"explorer: I hope I am not interrupting.\n"
"historian: Ah, the wanderer returns.\n"
"historian: How are the far shards doing?\n"
"historian: Get into any interesting trouble recently?\n"
"explorer: You know me, Historian.\n"
"explorer: Nothing like a bit of trouble to keep the spirit alive!\n"
"explorer: Still, I'm here on business.\n"
"explorer: I heard you are looking into the wildlife, and I've got a story I think you both should hear.\n"
"\n"
"PAGE: explorer(CONVERSATION), scribe(STUDIO_PRIMARY), historian(STUDIO_SECONDARY)\n"
"explorer: So I was camping by this waterfall.\n"
"explorer: The folks living around those parts say the waterfall's got a special fish.\n"
"explorer: Now, I know it sounds far-fetched, but they say it isn't just any fish.\n"
"explorer: They swear it's a spirit!\n"
"explorer: Apparently their ancestral legend speaks of a carp that will one day ascend a waterfall and turn into a dragon.\n"
"explorer: And this fish is a carp who can't stop jumping up the stream.\n"
"explorer: Do you think there's something in this?\n"
"scribe: A dragon...\n"
"scribe: If ever there was a beast noble enough to embody the Enlightened One's spirit, the dragon would be the obvious choice.\n"
"scribe: The ancestors had much wisdom, and for this news to reach us now, when we are looking for the Enlightened One's spirit among the beasts...\n"
"scribe: This must be a sign."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name
#: quests/main/phase3/3_30_companions/quest_main_3_30_companions.tres
msgid "A Helping Paw"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: goals[]
#: quests/main/phase3/3_30_companions/quest_main_3_30_companions.tres
msgid "Befriend an animal companion."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: record_title
#: quests/main/phase3/3_40_dragon/dlg_quest_main_3_40_dragon_end.tres
msgid "Era 三: The Tale of the Dragon"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: quests/main/phase3/3_40_dragon/dlg_quest_main_3_40_dragon_end.tres
msgid ""
"PAGE: scribe(STUDIO_PRIMARY), historian(STUDIO_SECONDARY)\n"
"scribe: The Ember monks were successful.\n"
"scribe: Their dedication to our mission was rewarded with a glorious vision of the great dragon.\n"
"historian: A vision?\n"
"historian: I was hoping we'd see the actual dragon.\n"
"scribe: We are yet unworthy.\n"
"scribe: But the Enlightened One spoke to them through the spirit, showing us the way to earn divine favor.\n"
"historian: Yes, I heard about the vow.\n"
"historian: It does make sense.\n"
"scribe: Not merely a vow, but an accord.\n"
"scribe: A Grand Accord to maintain the balance with nature, as declared in the Enlightened One's teachings.\n"
"\n"
"PAGE: scribe(SHRINE_PRIMARY), teo(SHRINE_SECONDARY)\n"
"scribe: Oh Enlightened One, we finally understand.\n"
"scribe: We cannot force the shards together with magic, nor expect nature to bend to our will.\n"
"scribe: We must prove that we have learned from the mistakes of the past.\n"
"scribe: We shall build a great monument to enshrine the Grand Accord so you can guide the world to finally heal."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name
#: quests/main/phase3/3_40_dragon/quest_main_3_40_dragon.tres
msgid "The Tale of the Dragon"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: goals[]
#: quests/main/phase3/3_40_dragon/quest_main_3_40_dragon.tres
msgid "Befriend the Carp."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: goals[]
#: quests/main/phase3/3_40_dragon/quest_main_3_40_dragon.tres
msgid "Commune with the Dragon."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: record_title
#: quests/main/phase3/3_50_accord_monument/dlg_quest_main_3_50_accord_monument_end.tres
msgid "Era 三: The Accord Monument"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: quests/main/phase3/3_50_accord_monument/dlg_quest_main_3_50_accord_monument_end.tres
msgid ""
"PAGE: monk(NONE)\n"
"monk: The monument is ready for dedication. As soon as we finish the expedition, we will start the ceremony."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: goals[]
#: quests/main/phase3/3_50_accord_monument/quest_main_3_50_accord_monument.tres
msgid "Establish an <shop:accord_monument> in a <spot:square>."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: record_title
#: quests/main/phase4/4_10_news/dlg_quest_main_4_10_news_begin.tres
msgid "Era 四: The Enlightened One Reborn"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: quests/main/phase4/4_10_news/dlg_quest_main_4_10_news_begin.tres
msgid ""
"PAGE: explorer(STUDIO_SECONDARY), scribe(STUDIO_PRIMARY)\n"
"explorer: I just returned from one of the old shards.\n"
"explorer: That place is barely holding on.\n"
"explorer: But I bring news.\n"
"scribe: Such is the fate of this doomed world.\n"
"scribe: Still, what is this news you speak of?\n"
"explorer: It is about the Enlightened One's Abode.\n"
"explorer: It's no longer alone!\n"
"scribe: What do you mean?\n"
"scribe: Did settlers from another shard lay claim to the sacred ground?\n"
"explorer: No, no, nothing like that!\n"
"explorer: Another shard drifted into it.\n"
"explorer: A barren piece of rock, completely devoid of people.\n"
"explorer: They are one landmass now.\n"
"scribe: One landmass, unified?\n"
"scribe: The shards are coming together?\n"
"scribe: When did this happen?\n"
"explorer: I heard it was a few years ago.\n"
"explorer: You know how it is these days.\n"
"explorer: No one travels around anymore.\n"
"explorer: Even a famous shard like that probably gets a dozen outsiders a year.\n"
"scribe: They didn't think to send word to the Haven, when our whole world may be changed by this?\n"
"scribe: I suppose even the monks have lost faith.\n"
"scribe: But not I.\n"
"scribe: Not anymore.\n"
"scribe: I have carried the torch since my teacher and his teachers before him, and it is finally time to reignite the flame.\n"
"scribe: This is a sign of the fractured spirit gathering its pieces.\n"
"explorer: That's exciting!\n"
"explorer: I'm going to the shard to see how it's changed.\n"
"explorer: Do you want to send a message to the monks there?\n"
"scribe: More than that.\n"
"scribe: I have a mission for you.\n"
"scribe: If the land is being reborn, then so is our guide.\n"
"scribe: Everything is part of the pattern.\n"
"scribe: A child must have been born at the exact moment the earth shook and the shards became one.\n"
"explorer: A child?\n"
"scribe: The Avatar that has been foretold.\n"
"scribe: The Enlightened One reborn in human form.\n"
"scribe: You must retrieve this child.\n"
"scribe: From this day on, to raise the Enlightened One's vessel shall be my life's duty.\n"
"scribe: To protect the Avatar before the world corrupts them.\n"
"explorer: I don't know how I can track down a child born years ago, but I'll ask the monks about it.\n"
"scribe: You must do it.\n"
"scribe: If it takes years, you must do it.\n"
"scribe: At any cost.\n"
"scribe: It is what will secure the future of our world."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name
#: quests/main/phase4/4_10_news/quest_main_4_10_news.tres
msgid "The Enlightened One Reborn"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: goals[]
#: quests/main/phase4/4_10_news/quest_main_4_10_news.tres
msgid "Retrieve the Avatar."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: record_title
#: quests/main/phase4/4_20_avatar_home/dlg_quest_main_4_20_avatar_home_begin.tres
msgid "Era 四: The Avatar's Home"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: quests/main/phase4/4_20_avatar_home/dlg_quest_main_4_20_avatar_home_begin.tres
msgid ""
"PAGE: explorer(STUDIO_SECONDARY), scribe(STUDIO_PRIMARY), avatar_child(CONVERSATION)\n"
"explorer: I've brought the child, just like you asked.\n"
"explorer: The monks say the dates match perfectly.\n"
"scribe: It is as predicted.\n"
"scribe: When the time came, the sapling sprouted.\n"
"scribe: I hope you have kept our reasons discreet.\n"
"explorer: Oh, that wasn't a problem.\n"
"explorer: I was afraid of having to lie to the parents, but they didn't object at all.\n"
"explorer: They think it's an honor to be tutored by the great Scribe.\n"
"explorer: Which is all the monks told them...\n"
"scribe: Oh, it is I who shall be tutored.\n"
"scribe: But the divine spirit must yet be dormant, in one so young.\n"
"scribe: I shall awaken it to the best of my abilities.\n"
"\n"
"PAGE: scribe(STUDIO_PRIMARY), avatar_child(CONVERSATION), explorer(STUDIO_SECONDARY)\n"
"scribe: Thank you for agreeing to come, Your Holiness.\n"
"avatar_child: ...\n"
"scribe: It must have taken great courage to leave your parents and embark on this journey.\n"
"avatar_child: It was fun going through the gate!\n"
"scribe: Someday, when you are grown, we will need no gates to connect us.\n"
"scribe: When all the shards are reunited, we shall be able to simply walk.\n"
"scribe: Do you remember a time like that?\n"
"avatar_child: I walked everywhere before!\n"
"avatar_child: We had no gates.\n"
"scribe: So you remember...\n"
"avatar_child: I walked to the shrine!\n"
"avatar_child: And the market!\n"
"avatar_child: And the well!\n"
"avatar_child: And once we even went to the forest!\n"
"scribe: ...\n"
"scribe: No matter.\n"
"scribe: The memory will return in time.\n"
"\n"
"PAGE: scribe(STUDIO_PRIMARY), explorer(STUDIO_SECONDARY), avatar_child(CONVERSATION)\n"
"scribe: It is as I thought.\n"
"scribe: The divine spirit is yet to awaken within the child.\n"
"scribe: There is much work to be done.\n"
"explorer: I'll leave you to it, then!\n"
"scribe: Not so fast.\n"
"scribe: This place is not right for the child.\n"
"scribe: I am the last scholar remaining here.\n"
"scribe: Of course there's the Historian, but she...\n"
"scribe: Her order has lost faith before I was even born.\n"
"scribe: She wishes well, but her teachings may suppress the divinity.\n"
"scribe: No, we need an untouched shard.\n"
"scribe: A place for the Avatar to hear the voices of nature.\n"
"scribe: And scholars well-versed in ancient scripture to reawaken the memories.\n"
"explorer: That sounds like a plan.\n"
"explorer: I'll be going now.\n"
"scribe: You must prepare a new expedition.\n"
"scribe: And we will be coming with you."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name
#: quests/main/phase4/4_20_avatar_home/quest_main_4_20_avatar_home.tres
#: shard_types/mq_avatar_home/shard_type_mq_avatar_home.tres
msgid "The Avatar's Home"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: goals[]
#: quests/main/phase4/4_20_avatar_home/quest_main_4_20_avatar_home.tres
msgid "Establish the [url=shard_type:mq_avatar_home]Avatar's Home[/url] culture on a shard."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: record_title
#: quests/main/phase4/4_30_scholar_hub/dlg_quest_main_4_30_scholar_hub_begin.tres
msgid "Era 四: The Ancient Tongue"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: quests/main/phase4/4_30_scholar_hub/dlg_quest_main_4_30_scholar_hub_begin.tres
msgid ""
"PAGE: explorer(MUSEUM_SECONDARY), historian(MUSEUM_PRIMARY)\n"
"historian: Good to see you back!\n"
"historian: I was starting to feel lonely with the Scribe gone.\n"
"historian: What could possess the old man to leave in such a hurry?\n"
"historian: He's barely left his studio in decades!\n"
"explorer: Oh, you're never too old to go out and explore!\n"
"historian: Well, I rather like it here myself.\n"
"historian: Besides, he left behind half of his sacred archive in my care, which has been fascinating.\n"
"explorer: You can actually read that old stuff?\n"
"historian: Well, no, not yet.\n"
"historian: But I'm close.\n"
"historian: They are almost the same glyphs we use today.\n"
"historian: But the meaning has drifted, and there's no grammar at all.\n"
"explorer: Even the Scribe said they were sacred chants whose meaning is too divine for us mortals.\n"
"historian: They were written down by people, and we're people too, so we must be able to understand them eventually.\n"
"explorer: Sounds like you've got your work cut out for you.\n"
"explorer: I'll look forward to hearing about what you find!\n"
"historian: You really can't sit still, can you?\n"
"historian: Fine, I won't bore you with the details.\n"
"historian: But I need a favor.\n"
"historian: Next time you join a settling expedition, bring a scholar from among the refugees with you.\n"
"historian: I'll have them set up a school to tackle this translation project."
msgstr ""

