#. TRANSLATORS: Property: record_title
#: quests/main/phase4/4_40_debate/dlg_quest_main_4_40_debate_abdication.tres
msgid "Era 四: The Avatar's Decision"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: quests/main/phase4/4_40_debate/dlg_quest_main_4_40_debate_abdication.tres
msgid ""
"PAGE: avatar_adult(STUDIO_SECONDARY), scribe(STUDIO_PRIMARY)\n"
"avatar_adult: Father, may I speak with you?\n"
"scribe: Always, Your Holiness.\n"
"scribe: You look well today.\n"
"avatar_adult: Thank you, Father.\n"
"avatar_adult: I am.\n"
"avatar_adult: The old texts...\n"
"avatar_adult: I understand the Enlightened One's will now.\n"
"scribe: I knew the day would come!\n"
"scribe: The legacy of Scribes across the centuries, finally bearing fruit.\n"
"scribe: Tell me, Your Holiness, what must we do?\n"
"avatar_adult: Before that, I want to thank you.\n"
"avatar_adult: You have raised me with warmth, and wisdom.\n"
"avatar_adult: You gave me a home when I was just a child from a distant shard.\n"
"scribe: It has been the greatest honor of my life.\n"
"avatar_adult: Well... let me quote to you the sacred words of the Enlightened One.\n"
"avatar_adult: \"To force the ten thousand things into one is to destroy them.\"\n"
"scribe: I understand.\n"
"scribe: We must not use force.\n"
"scribe: We must gain the people's favor through the debate.\n"
"avatar_adult: No...\n"
"avatar_adult: I am going about this the wrong way.\n"
"avatar_adult: Father, I know the Enlightened One's will now.\n"
"avatar_adult: And in my heart, I know the world will not be made better if everyone follows me.\n"
"scribe: What?\n"
"scribe: But the debate is going so well!\n"
"scribe: The people are ready to follow you!\n"
"avatar_adult: Father, please...\n"
"scribe: It is my failing.\n"
"scribe: I pushed you too hard.\n"
"scribe: I placed the burden of the world on you before the spirit was ready.\n"
"avatar_adult: You did nothing wrong.\n"
"avatar_adult: You raised me to care for our people, and that is exactly why I must leave them.\n"
"avatar_adult: To stay would be to build an empire.\n"
"avatar_adult: An empire that will burn people like wood.\n"
"avatar_adult: I want to offer warmth, but burn no wood.\n"
"scribe: But the Enlightened One commanded us to put the shards back together!\n"
"scribe: That commandment has been handed down from Scribe to Scribe from the day of the Shattering.\n"
"avatar_adult: Yes, but...\n"
"avatar_adult: I hear the words of the Enlightened One.\n"
"avatar_adult: \"A fine bowl holds water even if cracked.\"\n"
"avatar_adult: Our world is a cracked bowl, true.\n"
"avatar_adult: And the cracks are big.\n"
"avatar_adult: But it's a fine, well-crafted bowl.\n"
"avatar_adult: It can hold water despite the cracks.\n"
"scribe: So the Enlightened One truly wants us to leave these shards scattered?\n"
"avatar_adult: We still have the gates.\n"
"avatar_adult: We can still be whole in spirit.\n"
"scribe: ...\n"
"scribe: I am the Scribe of the Enlightened One.\n"
"scribe: A Scribe's duty is to transmit the commandments.\n"
"scribe: If it is the Enlightened One's will, then it is not my place to object.\n"
"avatar_adult: Father, there will be no more commandments from the Enlightened One.\n"
"avatar_adult: I am leaving the Haven to walk my own path.\n"
"avatar_adult: But the people will still need your wisdom."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: record_title
#: quests/main/phase4/4_40_debate/dlg_quest_main_4_40_debate_begin.tres
msgid "Era 四: The Scribe Returns"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: quests/main/phase4/4_40_debate/dlg_quest_main_4_40_debate_begin.tres
msgid ""
"PAGE: explorer(STUDIO_SECONDARY), historian(STUDIO_PRIMARY)\n"
"explorer: Here's the latest report from the scholars.\n"
"explorer: They seemed excited.\n"
"historian: Yes...\n"
"historian: This...\n"
"historian: Oh my, this is more than I expected.\n"
"historian: With these notes I can already start translating the more recent texts.\n"
"historian: And those should help me decipher the ancient ones.\n"
"historian: I wish we had started this project sooner!\n"
"\n"
"PAGE: scribe(CONVERSATION), historian(STUDIO_PRIMARY), explorer(STUDIO_SECONDARY), avatar_adult(PEERING)\n"
"scribe: There will be no need to scrape bits of wisdom from the old texts anymore, Historian.\n"
"historian: Scribe!\n"
"historian: You finally returned.\n"
"historian: And you've brought a guest too?\n"
"scribe: This is no guest.\n"
"scribe: You look upon the Avatar of the Enlightened One, returned to guide us.\n"
"\n"
"PAGE: avatar_adult(PEERING), historian(STUDIO_PRIMARY), explorer(STUDIO_SECONDARY), scribe(CONVERSATION)\n"
"avatar_adult: It is an honor to meet you, Historian.\n"
"avatar_adult: Father has spoken often of your dedication to preserving our memories.\n"
"historian: Welcome to our little haven.\n"
"historian: But \"father\"?\n"
"historian: The Scribe can't possibly be your father...\n"
"avatar_adult: He is the one who raised me.\n"
"avatar_adult: Helped the divine spirit within me blossom.\n"
"historian: Excuse my theologic inexperience, but are you claiming to be the Enlightened One?\n"
"avatar_adult: No, I am an ordinary mortal.\n"
"avatar_adult: But the Enlightened One's spirit within me guides my actions.\n"
"avatar_adult: Inspires in me the knowledge of what is right.\n"
"\n"
"PAGE: scribe(CONVERSATION), historian(STUDIO_PRIMARY), explorer(STUDIO_SECONDARY), avatar_adult(PEERING)\n"
"scribe: The Avatar carries the wisdom of the ages, from long before the Shattering.\n"
"scribe: Once we all follow this divine mandate, the world will be reunified once more.\n"
"historian: Our ancestors followed the mandate, and their prayers and magic rituals never got them anywhere.\n"
"historian: We should learn from their mistakes, not try to repeat them.\n"
"scribe: It is different now.\n"
"scribe: The Reunification has already begun.\n"
"scribe: The shard holding the Enlightened One's Abode has had its neighbor join it.\n"
"scribe: It is what signaled the Enlightened One's rebirth.\n"
"historian: You keep going on about Reunification.\n"
"historian: It's a dream.\n"
"historian: We must work with what we have.\n"
"historian: Find ways to live in the New World.\n"
"scribe: The people are tired of accepting this fate, Historian.\n"
"scribe: They do not want to struggle for the next harvest knowing that the world will remain doomed.\n"
"scribe: They want hope.\n"
"scribe: I will summon envoys from the shards.\n"
"scribe: Once the people hear of the Enlightened One's rebirth, they will rally behind us.\n"
"historian: Very well.\n"
"historian: I will address these envoys as well.\n"
"historian: Let everyone decide for themself if they want to build a future based on reality or continue to follow a pointless dream."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: record_title
#: quests/main/phase4/4_40_debate/dlg_quest_main_4_40_debate_doubts.tres
msgid "Era 四: Doubts"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: quests/main/phase4/4_40_debate/dlg_quest_main_4_40_debate_doubts.tres
msgid ""
"PAGE: avatar_adult(STUDIO_SECONDARY), scribe(STUDIO_PRIMARY)\n"
"avatar_adult: Father, do you have a moment?\n"
"avatar_adult: My heart feels clouded today.\n"
"scribe: Always, Your Holiness.\n"
"scribe: You look as though you are carrying the weight of ten shards on your shoulders.\n"
"avatar_adult: It's just...\n"
"avatar_adult: Back home, everything felt so obvious.\n"
"avatar_adult: Now, seeing so many people...\n"
"avatar_adult: So many different voices...\n"
"avatar_adult: How can I possibly make every one of them happy?\n"
"scribe: It is a difficult task, Your Holiness.\n"
"scribe: That is why we need one steady voice to unite us.\n"
"avatar_adult: But what if my voice isn't steady?\n"
"avatar_adult: I search my heart for wisdom, but all I find is doubt.\n"
"avatar_adult: I haven't had a glimpse of the Enlightened One's memory in years.\n"
"scribe: Your Holiness, when a leader stops questioning if they are right, they become a tyrant.\n"
"scribe: The fact that you hesitate before this great responsibility is proof of divine wisdom.\n"
"avatar_adult: But maybe we could start small?\n"
"avatar_adult: What if I just traveled the shards, spoke to each town directly?\n"
"scribe: It is a very kind thought.\n"
"scribe: But the Cloud Sea is vast, and people are stubborn.\n"
"scribe: They may nod along at a lone sage, then return to their habits the moment you step back through the gate.\n"
"avatar_adult: I don't know if I feel ready...\n"
"avatar_adult: Father, let me try to read the commandments again.\n"
"scribe: Here. I wish we could understand them better...\n"
"avatar_adult: ...\n"
"avatar_adult: I was hoping the divine spirit would resonate with them somehow, now that we're here...\n"
"avatar_adult: Make me remember...\n"
"scribe: You shouldn't blame yourself, Your Holiness.\n"
"scribe: The commandments were written down by ordinary people, after all, in the language of their time.\n"
"scribe: Forget these dusty old scrolls.\n"
"scribe: I have more faith in the wisdom of your heart.\n"
"avatar_adult: Thank you, Father.\n"
"avatar_adult: Your support has always meant so much to me."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: record_title
#: quests/main/phase4/4_40_debate/dlg_quest_main_4_40_debate_teo_diary.tres
msgid "Era 四: The Oldest Texts"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: quests/main/phase4/4_40_debate/dlg_quest_main_4_40_debate_teo_diary.tres
msgid ""
"PAGE: avatar_adult(MUSEUM_SECONDARY), historian(MUSEUM_PRIMARY)\n"
"historian: Oh, that's a rare sight!\n"
"historian: Welcome to my humble museum.\n"
"historian: What brings you here today?\n"
"avatar_adult: I have something for you.\n"
"avatar_adult: I was hoping you could help me.\n"
"historian: Are those... the commandment scrolls?\n"
"historian: The Scribe has always been too protective to let me handle these before.\n"
"historian: But... he knows better than to try to bribe me, even if it [i]is[/i] a priceless treasure.\n"
"avatar_adult: Well, actually...\n"
"avatar_adult: He doesn't know I was bringing them to you.\n"
"historian: Oh?\n"
"historian: Well, that's a delightful surprise.\n"
"avatar_adult: Anyway, you can translate these, right?\n"
"historian: I would be thrilled!\n"
"historian: But I must temper your expectations.\n"
"historian: These ancient records rarely give us neat answers.\n"
"historian: They might just raise more questions.\n"
"historian: Or end up being unrelated entirely.\n"
"historian: Are you sure you are ready for that?\n"
"avatar_adult: Whatever the truth is, I want to hear it.\n"
"avatar_adult: I have stared at those scrolls my whole life and felt nothing.\n"
"avatar_adult: Maybe if I hear them in a language I understand, it would finally spark my memory.\n"
"historian: The mind is a vast room, but sometimes all it takes is a candle to illuminate it.\n"
"historian: I can't promise it will be the spark you are looking for, but I will do my best to not let my opinion color the translation.\n"
"avatar_adult: Thank you, Historian.\n"
"avatar_adult: That's all I ask.\n"
"historian: You know, I had assumed you were content being a symbol on the Scribe's banner.\n"
"historian: I'm glad to learn you are a fellow seeker of truth."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: record_title
#: quests/main/phase4/4_40_debate/dlg_quest_main_4_40_debate_translated.tres
msgid "Era 四: The Oldest Texts Translated"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
