#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name
#: stage/hauntings/types/akaname/haunting_akaname.tres
msgid "Akaname"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/akaname/haunting_akaname.tres
msgid "Sickness"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/akaname/haunting_akaname.tres
msgid "Filth Licker"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/akaname/haunting_akaname.tres
msgid "Filth-licking goblins are said to gather in these dirty ruins, spreading sickness wherever they crawl."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/akaname/haunting_akaname.tres
msgid "Illness spreads quickly among the unwashed. Poor sanitation in this settlement has turned homes and baths into breeding grounds for disease."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/akaname/haunting_akaname.tres
msgid ""
"At first, settlers only complained of sluggishness and fever. Then came the slime, a damp sheen creeping across the walls. Those who spent the night by the ruins swore they heard faint slurping sounds, as if something small and eager were licking at their bedrolls.\n"
"\n"
"In the Old World they spoke of Akaname, goblins born of neglect, living off the waste and grime of the careless. Their tongues are said to stretch across rooms, leaving behind sickness in their wake. Cleanliness alone keeps these creatures at bay."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/akashita/haunting_akashita.tres
msgid "Volcanic Ashfall"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/akashita/haunting_akashita.tres
msgid "Red Tongue"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/akashita/haunting_akashita.tres
msgid "A dark cloud with a red tongue hangs over the mountain slopes, licking away the life from every seed that dares to sprout."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/akashita/haunting_akashita.tres
msgid "Volcanic ashfall is choking the mountainside, smothering crops and wildlife."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/akashita/haunting_akashita.tres
msgid ""
"When the clouds turn black and the air tastes of metal, the settlers whisper of Akashita, the red-tongued cloud. They say it arises from the mountain when greed runs unchecked, farmers stealing water from their neighbor's fields.\n"
"\n"
"The beast hides within dark clouds, only its fanged grin and lashing tongue peeking out to drink in the land's life. Villagers claim it licks the color from leaves and the breath from beasts, leaving only gray fields and silence behind."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/amanojaku/haunting_amanojaku.tres
msgid "Polarization"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/amanojaku/haunting_amanojaku.tres
msgid "Evil Heavenly Spirits"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/amanojaku/haunting_amanojaku.tres
msgid "Corrupted divine spirits, the Amanojaku, have descended on the town, provoking people into wicked acts, counter to the plans of their comrades."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/amanojaku/haunting_amanojaku.tres
msgid "Rival teachings have torn this town apart, causing people to act out simply to spite the plans of their comrades."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/amanojaku/haunting_amanojaku.tres
msgid "Long, long ago, the Enlightened One crushed the wicked Amanojaku, but now they have returned to spread wickedness among the settlers of the New World. These little ogres look into the hearts of people, and provoke their darkest desires. Some are known to possess people outright, directing their actions to spite the common good of their community."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name
#: stage/hauntings/types/bashounosei/haunting_bashounosei.tres
msgid "Bashō no Sei"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/bashounosei/haunting_bashounosei.tres
msgid "Blight"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/bashounosei/haunting_bashounosei.tres
msgid "Banana Spirit"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/bashounosei/haunting_bashounosei.tres
msgid "A rot spirit is haunting this hill, appearing as human faces in the rot on banana leaves."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/bashounosei/haunting_bashounosei.tres
msgid "Creeping blight is spreading across the area, destroying agricultural yields."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/bashounosei/haunting_bashounosei.tres
msgid "The hills have been claimed by a creeping rot that spreads from plant to plant. It started from the banana trees, haunted by the Bashō no Sei, banana spirits who manifest as faces on the leaves. They look at the farmers with blame, and ask passing monks if even plants can attain enlightenment."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/furaribi/haunting_furaribi.tres
msgid "Extreme Heat"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/furaribi/haunting_furaribi.tres
msgid "Aimless Fire"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/furaribi/haunting_furaribi.tres
msgid "Settlers working outside risk being attacked by Furaribi, fiery birds with dog faces who dive down from the sky to steal souls from those too weak to resist their clutches."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/furaribi/haunting_furaribi.tres
msgid "Extreme heat stops settlers from spending long hours working outside."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/furaribi/haunting_furaribi.tres
msgid ""
"The area has become known for Furaribi, fiery birds with dog faces who dive down from the sky to steal souls from those too weak to resist their clutches. Even if the person manages to fight them off, they usually end up unconscious, their spirit wounded by the struggle.\n"
"\n"
"It is said that one can feel the approach of Furaribi when the air becomes unnaturally hot."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name
#: stage/hauntings/types/futakuchi_onna/haunting_futakuchi_onna.tres
msgid "Futakuchi Onna"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/futakuchi_onna/haunting_futakuchi_onna.tres
msgid "Corruption"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/futakuchi_onna/haunting_futakuchi_onna.tres
msgid "Two-Mouthed Woman"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/futakuchi_onna/haunting_futakuchi_onna.tres
msgid "Rumors speak of people with a second mouth on the back of their heads, consuming twice the resources."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/futakuchi_onna/haunting_futakuchi_onna.tres
msgid "Corruption is rife among the leaders of this settler group."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/futakuchi_onna/haunting_futakuchi_onna.tres
msgid ""
"Warehouses in this settlement turn up empty overnight. Households run out of food twice as fast.\n"
"\n"
"Whispers speak of people with mouths hiding behind their heads, covered by locks of hair. The most common story is of the Futakuchi Onna, a lady who smiles sweetly while her hair stirs behind her like a nest of living threads, feeding a hidden mouth that demands its share of every meal. Some claim she was once a leader who hoarded plenty while others starved, and that her second mouth belongs to those she wronged, forever consuming what she once denied."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: mechanics_description_override
#: stage/hauntings/types/futakuchi_onna/haunting_futakuchi_onna.tres
msgid "Lose half of all gained <term_lower:bonus>s."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name
#: stage/hauntings/types/gaki/haunting_gaki.tres
msgid "Gaki"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/gaki/haunting_gaki.tres
msgid "Insect Swarms"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/gaki/haunting_gaki.tres
msgid "Hungry Ghosts"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/gaki/haunting_gaki.tres
msgid "These lands are haunted by the Gaki, hungry ghosts cursed to devour everything yet never be filled."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/gaki/haunting_gaki.tres
msgid "Swarms of insects have infested the area, consuming every trace of food."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/gaki/haunting_gaki.tres
msgid ""
"Tales abound of ancient sinners from this land returning as Gaki, eternally hungry ghosts devouring every planted seed and stored grain. In life, they were said to have hoarded food from others. In death, their bellies swell while their throats remain narrow, dooming them to eternal hunger.\n"
"\n"
"Some settlers still leave offerings of rice and water in the night, hoping the monsters will turn elsewhere, but they never do."
msgstr ""

#: stage/hauntings/types/haunting_type.gd:200
msgid "When %s, %s."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/housougami/haunting_housougami.tres
msgid "Smallpox"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/housougami/haunting_housougami.tres
msgid "Smallpox Demon"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/housougami/haunting_housougami.tres
msgid "Settlers whisper that a crimson spirit walks among them, marking the sick with its red touch."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/housougami/haunting_housougami.tres
msgid "A contagious disease is spreading rapidly among the settlers."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/housougami/haunting_housougami.tres
msgid ""
"When fever sweeps through a camp, the people hang red ribbons and paper charms, hoping to draw away the gaze of the Hōsōgami. Legends tell of small, scarlet demons traveling from home to home, riding on shoulders and carried in hands, marking people with their red touch. They are said to test each household's kindness: those who hoard medicine fall first, while the generous recover.\n"
"\n"
"Yet the drums and prayers that once sent it away no longer bring comfort. Even the toughest begin to tremble at the sight of red skin."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name
#: stage/hauntings/types/jikininki/haunting_jikininki.tres
msgid "Jikininki"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/jikininki/haunting_jikininki.tres
msgid "Dangerous Wildlife"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/jikininki/haunting_jikininki.tres
msgid "Human-Eating Demons"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/jikininki/haunting_jikininki.tres
msgid "A ravenous spirit stalks the night, devouring all who linger too long among the dead."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/jikininki/haunting_jikininki.tres
msgid "Predatory beasts roam the night, drawn by the smell of food. Fear multiplies each time one of the settlers is injured."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/jikininki/haunting_jikininki.tres
msgid ""
"Travelers whisper of nights when the land stirs with hunger. They say the Jikininki walk these lands, monks who turned their prayers into coin and their faith into appetite. Now they haunt the scattered ruins and toppled gates, their faces pale as bone dust, their mouths full of teeth too sharp for penance.\n"
"\n"
"Those who sleep in the open find their packs torn open in the morning. The less lucky ones are woken up by vicious attacks from the darkness. While some claim the Jikininki only feed on corpses, they seem to see little difference between the sleeping and the dead."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/kamikiri/haunting_kamikiri.tres
msgid "Envy"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/kamikiri/haunting_kamikiri.tres
msgid "Hair Cutter"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/kamikiri/haunting_kamikiri.tres
msgid "Beautiful settlers here wake up to find their hair and clothes cut up by the mysterious Kamikiri."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/kamikiri/haunting_kamikiri.tres
msgid "Envy among settlers is causing widespread theft and vandalism."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/kamikiri/haunting_kamikiri.tres
msgid ""
"A mysterious monster with scissor-shaped claws and beak sneaks around at night, hiding among the roof beams. It waits for settlers to fall asleep, before descending on them and cutting off their beautiful locks. At times it doesn't stop there, but proceeds to ruin all the clothes in the victim's closet as well.\n"
"\n"
"The Kamikiri seems to only target the most beautiful and well-off townspeople, perhaps as a punishment for their excessive ostentation."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/kappa/haunting_kappa.tres
msgid "Slippery Rocks"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/kappa/haunting_kappa.tres
msgid "Children of the River"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/kappa/haunting_kappa.tres
msgid "Settlers blame the mischievous Kappa for dragging their goods and children into the river."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/kappa/haunting_kappa.tres
msgid "Algae and moss have made the river stones slick, causing folks to lose their footing."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/kappa/haunting_kappa.tres
msgid ""
"Work by the river has become treacherous. People slip and tumble into the rapids, coming back soaked and shivering, claiming webbed hands grabbed at their ankles from just beneath the surface.\n"
"\n"
"The locals say the Kappa have claimed the banks. These river children have a hollow dish of water set into the top of their heads, granting them the strength to drag humans into the rushing stream. Tradition dictates that offering them a cucumber might buy safe passage, but priests suggest bowing instead. The creatures are compelled to bow in return, spilling the life-giving water from their heads and losing their strength."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/kasukurai/haunting_kasukurai.tres
msgid "Vermin Infestation"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/kasukurai/haunting_kasukurai.tres
msgid "Leftover Eaters"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/kasukurai/haunting_kasukurai.tres
msgid "The expedition is haunted by Kasukurai, little gluttons said to creep in after meals to devour anything left behind."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/kasukurai/haunting_kasukurai.tres
msgid "A growing rodent infestation is spoiling stored provisions and reducing available food."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/kasukurai/haunting_kasukurai.tres
msgid ""
"At night, settlers whisper of soft chewing behind the walls and footprints around the grain stores. Nothing is ever stolen, but radishes are nibbled, and beans go missing.\n"
"\n"
"The locals blame the Kasukurai, spirits of waste and negligence. They say these sneaky figures crawl out from beneath discarded scraps, their thin lips smacking for every morsel left after a meal. Every careless waste draws more of them, until the storerooms echo with a thousand unseen feasts.\n"
"\n"
"Some tales claim they were once cooks who squandered food while others starved, doomed now to consume what no one wants."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/kodama/haunting_kodama.tres
msgid "Thick Vegetation"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/kodama/haunting_kodama.tres
msgid "Tree Spirits"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/kodama/haunting_kodama.tres
msgid "The forest is said to be guarded by Kodama, tree spirits who punish anyone who fells a tree."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/kodama/haunting_kodama.tres
msgid "The forest's growth has turned uncontrollable. Dense underbrush and creeping vines choke the trails, making work slow and hazardous."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/kodama/haunting_kodama.tres
msgid ""
"These woods are watched over by mysterious guardians. Settlers speak of glowing lights with faint faces surrounding the ancient trees. Wherever they pass, roots surge from the soil, grasping at ankles, and trails vanish overnight.\n"
"\n"
"Some swear these are Kodama, spirits of ancient trees driven from their trunks to defend the forest against any who dare harm it. Though not malicious, they punish humans who forget that nature is not a plaything to be toyed with."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/kotengu/haunting_kotengu.tres
msgid "Rockfalls"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/kotengu/haunting_kotengu.tres
msgid "Lesser Heavenly Hounds"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/kotengu/haunting_kotengu.tres
msgid "Travelers claim the Kotengu are dropping rocks from the cliffs above, punishing anyone who disturbs their mountain domain."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/kotengu/haunting_kotengu.tres
msgid "Loose stones and unstable cliffs are causing frequent rockfalls."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/kotengu/haunting_kotengu.tres
msgid ""
"The cliffs shower passers-by with loose stones, followed by mocking laughter from the clifftops.\n"
"\n"
"Folks say it is the work of Kotengu, the lesser bird-like spirits of the peaks. They fiercely guard their domain from the growing village, viewing every new building as an insult. They perch where human eyes cannot reach, waiting for careless settlers to pass beneath the cliff before sending boulders down to crush their efforts."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name
#: stage/hauntings/types/koto_furunushi/haunting_koto_furunushi.tres
msgid "Koto Furunushi"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/koto_furunushi/haunting_koto_furunushi.tres
msgid "Melancholy"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/koto_furunushi/haunting_koto_furunushi.tres
msgid "Old Koto Masters"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/koto_furunushi/haunting_koto_furunushi.tres
msgid "Whispers tell of a koto that plays itself at night, weeping for the songs the world has forgotten."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/koto_furunushi/haunting_koto_furunushi.tres
msgid "A sense of melancholy grips these buildings; joy fades quickly, and even small successes leave the people weary."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/koto_furunushi/haunting_koto_furunushi.tres
msgid ""
"In the empty halls of this settlement, faint music drifts through the rafters, strings trembling with longing, plucked by no visible hand. Some attribute this to the Koto Furunushi, a spirit possessing an old koto, once beloved, now abandoned.\n"
"\n"
"They say it remembers every song once played upon it, and grieves for every joyful gathering it once entertained. When its melodies echo, hearts grow heavy, and even good fortune feels tinged with sorrow."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name
#: stage/hauntings/types/kurobouzu/haunting_kurobouzu.tres
msgid "Kurobōzu"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/kurobouzu/haunting_kurobouzu.tres
msgid "Epidemic"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/kurobouzu/haunting_kurobouzu.tres
msgid "Black Monks"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/kurobouzu/haunting_kurobouzu.tres
msgid "Settlers whisper of dark monks that slip into homes at night to steal the breath from people's lips."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/kurobouzu/haunting_kurobouzu.tres
msgid "An epidemic of respiratory illness is sweeping through the settlement, spreading among people who have weakened their bodies from excessive labor."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/kurobouzu/haunting_kurobouzu.tres
msgid "The hardest-working settlers are waking up with pale faces and rattling coughs. Their breaths are stolen by the Kurobōzu, shadowy monks drawn to the exhausted and the ambitious, slipping into homes to lick the sweat from tired brows and steal the breath from those sleeping too deeply. Tales claim the monsters were once greedy priests who traded their health for worldly success, and are now cursed to wander the night."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/kyuuso/haunting_kyuuso.tres
msgid "Rodent Infestation"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/kyuuso/haunting_kyuuso.tres
msgid "Giant Rodents"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/kyuuso/haunting_kyuuso.tres
msgid "An enormous, chubby rat spirit is said to haunt these steppes, devouring everything in its path."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/kyuuso/haunting_kyuuso.tres
msgid "A severe rodent infestation is consuming all yields produced in these steppes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/kyuuso/haunting_kyuuso.tres
msgid ""
"At first, settlers blamed thieves for their vanishing harvests. Then they began finding bite-marks the size of fists and tracks larger than a badger's. The elders remembered the Kyūso, a rat so old it perfected gluttony and forgot fear.\n"
"\n"
"They say it waddles from granary to granary on moonless nights, its stubby tail leaving a trail in the dirt, its mouth wide enough to swallow a rice sack whole. Unafraid of cats or dogs, it will even chase foxes away.\n"
"\n"
"In some tellings it was once a farmer, cursed for hoarding food through a famine."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/nigawarai/haunting_nigawarai.tres
msgid "Animosity"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/nigawarai/haunting_nigawarai.tres
msgid "Bitter Smiles"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/nigawarai/haunting_nigawarai.tres
msgid "Settlers whisper of the Nigawarai, spirits born from forced smiles that turn neighborly faces bitter."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/nigawarai/haunting_nigawarai.tres
msgid "Resentment spreads among settlers, causing inefficiency and discord."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/nigawarai/haunting_nigawarai.tres
msgid ""
"The Nigawarai is said to arise wherever smiles hide resentment. When meals are shared without joy, and apologies ring untrue, something begins to stir. A hulking figure with a grin stretched too wide wanders between homes, licking the air for bitterness, its constant snickering an ugly hum that unsettles the heart. Those who hear it wake the next morning ready to quarrel with the first person they see.\n"
"\n"
"Some say the Nigawarai was once a kindly elder who smiled through years of unspoken grievances until his mask hardened into a curse. Now he roams, reminding all that swallowed words and polite deceit rot faster than open anger."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name
#: stage/hauntings/types/nojukubi/haunting_nojukubi.tres
msgid "Nojukubi"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/nojukubi/haunting_nojukubi.tres
msgid "Wildfires"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/nojukubi/haunting_nojukubi.tres
msgid "Wild Living Fires"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/nojukubi/haunting_nojukubi.tres
msgid "These plains are haunted by Nojukubi, fiery spirits of ancient inhabitants."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/nojukubi/haunting_nojukubi.tres
msgid "Wildfires are ravaging these plains."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/nojukubi/haunting_nojukubi.tres
msgid ""
"In the stillness of lands long abandoned, faint streaks of fire begin to wander the grass, reliving the warmth of the people who once lived there. Settlers say these flickering embers murmur snatches of poetry and laughter, the voices of past gatherings echoing through the air.\n"
"\n"
"Legends call them Nojukubi, fires born of memory, igniting even damp ground in flames. They need no fuel, feeding on the restless traces of joy left behind."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: mechanics_description_override
#: stage/hauntings/types/nojukubi/haunting_nojukubi.tres
msgid "Prevents any <term_lower:spot_upgrade> in this <term_lower:spot> from being activated."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name
#: stage/hauntings/types/nopperabou/haunting_nopperabou.tres
msgid "Nopperabō"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/nopperabou/haunting_nopperabou.tres
msgid "Dense Fog"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/nopperabou/haunting_nopperabou.tres
msgid "Flat Faced Monks"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/nopperabou/haunting_nopperabou.tres
msgid "Thick mists hide the Nopperabō, faceless wanderers who steal people's faces, turning them blind."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/nopperabou/haunting_nopperabou.tres
msgid "A thick fog frequently rolls into the area, severely limiting visibility and making work hazardous."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/nopperabou/haunting_nopperabou.tres
msgid "These lands are swallowed by a fog so thick that workers can barely see their own hands. Settlers report meeting the Nopperabō within the fog, figures who turn around to reveal large, blank faces lacking eyes, noses, or mouths. When the victims report the sightings, whoever they talk to tends to respond \"Oh, you mean like this?\" before wiping their face away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/nurarihyon/haunting_nurarihyon.tres
msgid "Bureaucracy"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/nurarihyon/haunting_nurarihyon.tres
msgid "Slippery Gourd"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/nurarihyon/haunting_nurarihyon.tres
msgid "The town is under the influence of Nurarihyon, a peppet-master with a gourd-shaped head who demands that the leaders of the settlement bring every plan to him for approval."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/nurarihyon/haunting_nurarihyon.tres
msgid "Stagnant bureacracy is drowning projects in endless permits and approval requirements."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/nurarihyon/haunting_nurarihyon.tres
msgid "The leaders of this settlement are afraid to approve any plan that the townspeople offer until they receive the blessing of Nurarihyon, a mysterious spirit who appears in the guise of a wizened old man with a gourd-shaped head. He is often seen at night wearing rich silks and being carried on a palanquin, too busy to bother with the plight of the common people. Folks whisper that he is in fact the leader of all the hauntings, and displeasing him will bring great misfortune to the shard."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name
#: stage/hauntings/types/okiku/haunting_okiku.tres
msgid "Okiku"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/okiku/haunting_okiku.tres
msgid "Contaminated Wells"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/okiku/haunting_okiku.tres
msgid "Lady Chrysanthemum"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/okiku/haunting_okiku.tres
msgid "People whisper of a ghost who counts dishes from the bottom of the well, her grief souring the water and the hearts of all who drink it."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/okiku/haunting_okiku.tres
msgid "Poor maintenance has poisoned the town's well, spreading illness among the settlers."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/okiku/haunting_okiku.tres
msgid ""
"The well at the square has turned murky, something unseen clinging to its depths. Each night, villagers claim to hear faint counting rising through the stone: one, two, three... nine. Some swear they saw a pale hand break the surface.\n"
"\n"
"The old tales recall Okiku, a servant falsely accused of losing a precious plate and thrown into the town's well. They say she returns to count what was lost, her sorrow spreading through the well's water.\n"
"\n"
"Since her whispers began, people have started to fall ill after drinking, and the square smells faintly of rot."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name
#: stage/hauntings/types/onibi/haunting_onibi.tres
msgid "Onibi"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/onibi/haunting_onibi.tres
msgid "Peat Fires"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/onibi/haunting_onibi.tres
msgid "Demon Fires"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/onibi/haunting_onibi.tres
msgid "Flickering lights drift over the wetlands, feeding on the breath of the living."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/onibi/haunting_onibi.tres
msgid "Slow-burning peat fires smolder beneath the wetlands, releasing toxic gases that sap strength and ruin the soil."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/onibi/haunting_onibi.tres
msgid ""
"At night, the swamp awakens with soft glowing lanterns that dance above the ponds. Settlers know these as Onibi, demon fires born from the grudges of the dead. They hover in flocks, swarming any who stray too near, drawing warmth and will alike.\n"
"\n"
"Old tales say they are the souls of the drowned, escaping from their torment beneath the mud."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name
#: stage/hauntings/types/oomukade/haunting_oomukade.tres
msgid "Ōomukade"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/oomukade/haunting_oomukade.tres
msgid "Sinkholes"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/oomukade/haunting_oomukade.tres
msgid "Big Centipede"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/oomukade/haunting_oomukade.tres
msgid "The ground here is said to be infested with Ōomukade, giant centipedes that dig their burrows beneath careless feet."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/oomukade/haunting_oomukade.tres
msgid "The ground here is unstable and riddled with sinkholes, making development impossible until the soil is reinforced."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/oomukade/haunting_oomukade.tres
msgid "Some scrublands are home to Ōomukade, giant centipedes that sleep in tunnels beneath the ground. Their burrows weaken the soil until it suddenly collapses, swallowing homes, roads, and shrines whole. Some claim to hear muffled drums beneath the ground, the skittering of giant legs. Tales are told of brave scouts who drove stakes into the trembling earth, only for the stakes to vanish overnight. Arcane masters often mark the soft ground with glyph-carved pillars, hoping to trap the monsters in their sleep."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name
#: stage/hauntings/types/oonamazu/haunting_oonamazu.tres
msgid "Ōnamazu"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/oonamazu/haunting_oonamazu.tres
msgid "Floods"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/oonamazu/haunting_oonamazu.tres
msgid "Giant Catfish"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/oonamazu/haunting_oonamazu.tres
msgid "Settlers warn of a monstrous catfish sleeping beneath the mud, whose restless thrashing turns the shores into an endless expanse of mud."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/oonamazu/haunting_oonamazu.tres
msgid "The lake is subject to flash floods that turn the whole area into a muddy mess."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/oonamazu/haunting_oonamazu.tres
msgid ""
"The clear waters of the lake have turned a thick, churning brown. Settlers who live on the shores claim to feel a deep thumping through the soles of their feet.\n"
"\n"
"This is the work of Ōnamazu, a catfish of impossible size sleeping beneath the waves. When humans grow arrogant and build their homes too close to the water, the beast wakes to remind them of their proper place. Its angry thrashing stirs up the lake, sending its waters out across the plains."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name
#: stage/hauntings/types/oonyuudou/haunting_oonyuudou.tres
msgid "Ōnyūdō"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/oonyuudou/haunting_oonyuudou.tres
msgid "Earthquake"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/oonyuudou/haunting_oonyuudou.tres
msgid "Giant Priests"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/oonyuudou/haunting_oonyuudou.tres
msgid "Settlers warn of a towering, shadowy priest whose heavy footsteps make the very foundations of the world tremble."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/oonyuudou/haunting_oonyuudou.tres
msgid "Regular earthquakes shake the area, disrupting construction and daily life."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/oonyuudou/haunting_oonyuudou.tres
msgid ""
"It begins with tea spilling from cups and tools rattling on workbenches. Soon, the tremors grow stronger. Every time a new beam is raised or a great task is undertaken, the ground shudders violently, throwing workers to their knees.\n"
"\n"
"The elders speak of the Ōnyūdō, the Giant Priests. They say these towering monks appear when a settlement grows too proud, building their homes taller than the ancient trees and forgetting their humility. The giant's massive feet stomp the earth, reminding the settlers that the ground they stand on is not theirs to control."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/raijuu/haunting_raijuu.tres
msgid "Thunderstorms"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/raijuu/haunting_raijuu.tres
msgid "Thunder Beasts"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/raijuu/haunting_raijuu.tres
msgid "Settlers warn of beasts made of lightning that ride the storm clouds, striking the earth wherever a ritual is held."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/raijuu/haunting_raijuu.tres
msgid "Severe thunderstorms frequently pass over the region, bringing lightning strikes that ignite sudden fires."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/raijuu/haunting_raijuu.tres
msgid ""
"The air grows heavy and smells of burning before the storms hit. Lightning strikes with an uncanny precision, targeting high temple spires where the most holy rituals are performed.\n"
"\n"
"In the Old World, they spoke of the Raijū. These beasts of thunder sleep in the bellies of dark clouds, taking the shapes of wild dogs or badgers wrapped in crackling energy. When divine powers are invoked, these creatures are drawn to strike, leaving a trail of fire in their wake."
msgstr ""

