#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name
#: stage/hauntings/types/shuten_douji/haunting_shuten_douji.tres
msgid "Shuten Dōji"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/shuten_douji/haunting_shuten_douji.tres
msgid "Alcoholism"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/shuten_douji/haunting_shuten_douji.tres
msgid "Little Lord Drunkard"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/shuten_douji/haunting_shuten_douji.tres
msgid "Settlers have started honoring Shuten Dōji, the Drunken King, whose revels never end, and neither does the hangover."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/shuten_douji/haunting_shuten_douji.tres
msgid "Alcohol abuse has spread among the settlers, sapping morale and productivity."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/shuten_douji/haunting_shuten_douji.tres
msgid ""
"In the nights when work is done, settlers speak of deep laughter rolling down from the tents. They say it is Shuten Dōji, once a man too proud for company, now the demon king of endless drink. He tempts the weary to raise their cups and forget their tasks, promising courage that burns away before morning.\n"
"\n"
"It is said that his head was once severed but never silenced, its grin still whispering of comfort in every bottle. Where his name is remembered, work slows, words slur, and spirits of both kinds run dry."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/tsuchigumo/haunting_tsuchigumo.tres
msgid "Dissent"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/tsuchigumo/haunting_tsuchigumo.tres
msgid "Earth Spiders"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/tsuchigumo/haunting_tsuchigumo.tres
msgid "Multiple leaders in this settlement have gone missing and or have been found poisoned. The prime suspect is the Tsuchigumo, giant spiders that ambush powerful people with poison and trap them in their nets."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/tsuchigumo/haunting_tsuchigumo.tres
msgid "The people are in open dissent against the leaders of this settlement, constantly sabotaging their efforts."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/tsuchigumo/haunting_tsuchigumo.tres
msgid "When people rise to power, they become the target of Tsuchigumo, giant spiders that sleep in tunnels beneath the ground. They come out at night, using illusion to hide their bulk, to challenge people who have obtained too much influence. They ambush their victims with poison that no medicine can heal, and drag them into their underground burrows, to be kept captive in silk cocoons."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/umibouzu/haunting_umibouzu.tres
msgid "High Waves"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/umibouzu/haunting_umibouzu.tres
msgid "Sea Monks"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/umibouzu/haunting_umibouzu.tres
msgid "Settlers refuse to go near the seashore, terrified of the Umibōzu, a giant shadow that rises from the waves to smash their efforts."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/umibouzu/haunting_umibouzu.tres
msgid "Unpredictable tides and dangerously high waves are constantly battering the coastline, threatening to wash away any new structures."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/umibouzu/haunting_umibouzu.tres
msgid ""
"The sea has grown violently restless, with sudden swells crashing against the shore. Those who work near the water tell frantic stories of a massive, pitch-black figure rising from the sea, its smooth, rounded head blocking out the stars before it brings the waves crashing down.\n"
"\n"
"They call it the Umibōzu, the sea monk. Legends say it is born from the drowned souls of the Old World, a creature of pure resentment that demands the sea remain untamed. It rises to test the courage of the settlers, punishing any attempt to claim the shoreline by overwhelming them with the sea's fury."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name
#: stage/hauntings/types/uwabami/haunting_uwabami.tres
msgid "Uwabami"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/uwabami/haunting_uwabami.tres
msgid "Quicksand"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/uwabami/haunting_uwabami.tres
msgid "Giant Snakes"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/uwabami/haunting_uwabami.tres
msgid "The desert is said to hide Uwabami, great serpents that swallow travelers whole without leaving a trace."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/uwabami/haunting_uwabami.tres
msgid "Treacherous quicksand pockets have formed beneath the dunes. Travelers who cross carelessly are lost to the shifting earth."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/uwabami/haunting_uwabami.tres
msgid ""
"The desert sands are home to the Uwabami, vast serpents swimming beneath the dunes, their scales shimmering like heat on the horizon. They coil themselves around anything they encounter, pulling it deep into the sands.\n"
"\n"
"Some say they were driven mad by betrayal, when a mountain god tricked such a serpent into tying itself into a knot."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/uwan/haunting_uwan.tres
msgid "Paranoia"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/uwan/haunting_uwan.tres
msgid "Waah!"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/uwan/haunting_uwan.tres
msgid "Settlers are being scared half to death by the grotesque Uwan, who appear out of the darkness and simply shout \"uwan!\"."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/uwan/haunting_uwan.tres
msgid "Settlers have become paranoid, quaking in fear and suspecting evil intent whenever plans don't go their way."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/uwan/haunting_uwan.tres
msgid "Little is known about the Uwan, but these grotesque hauntings suddenly appear late at night and scare people with their shouts. They don't seem to be actively harmful, but the fear they spread grips the town, causing people to always be on guard against unexpected assailants."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/yamabiko/haunting_yamabiko.tres
msgid "Landslides"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/yamabiko/haunting_yamabiko.tres
msgid "Mountain Boys"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/yamabiko/haunting_yamabiko.tres
msgid "Settlers claim that little mocking mountain spirits are sliding down the canyon walls, crumbling the stone in their wake."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/yamabiko/haunting_yamabiko.tres
msgid "The canyon walls are unstable, with even minor disturbances triggering dangerous landslides."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/yamabiko/haunting_yamabiko.tres
msgid ""
"Settlers working in the canyon are often ambushed by debris sliding down the walls, starting with a snapping sound and followed by a stream of echoes.\n"
"\n"
"The old tales speak of the Yamabiko, the mountain boys. These little beasts look like a mix between dogs and monkeys, and thrive on mimicking humans. When the settlers make too much racket, the Yamabiko eagerly join in, clapping and jumping up and down, breaking off pieces of the canyon walls."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/yume_no_seirei/haunting_yume_no_seirei.tres
msgid "Disenchantment"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: name_translation
#: stage/hauntings/types/yume_no_seirei/haunting_yume_no_seirei.tres
msgid "Dream Ghost"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/hauntings/types/yume_no_seirei/haunting_yume_no_seirei.tres
msgid "The dream spirit, Yume no Seirei, is feasting on the dreams of the settlers in this town, rendering them unable to find beauty in their life."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_realistic
#: stage/hauntings/types/yume_no_seirei/haunting_yume_no_seirei.tres
msgid "Excessive intellectualism has caused many of the settlers to be disenchanted with the mysteries of life, finding beauty in neither nature nor human activities."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description_long
#: stage/hauntings/types/yume_no_seirei/haunting_yume_no_seirei.tres
msgid "Many settlers in this town have found their life force drained after a visit from Yume no Seirei, a ghastly spirit appearing as a decrepit old man by their bedsides and stealing their dreams. When they awake, they find their days turning into an endless cycle of drudgery, bereft of higher meaning."
msgstr ""

