msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_abandoned_gate.tres
msgid ""
"The survey team arrives at what remains of an old pre-Shattering village. Grass grows between the stones on the path, and mosses have completely taken over the village square.\n"
"\n"
"Most of the buildings have long since fallen into ruin, but the gatehouse and a few huts still stand, as does the shrine at the center of the village."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_abandoned_gate.tres
msgid "Search the gatehouse."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_abandoned_gate.tres
msgid "The group searches the gatehouse. Among the crumbling furniture they manage to find several spears. They collect their iron tips for blacksmiths to reforge later."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_abandoned_gate.tres
msgid "Explore the huts."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_abandoned_gate.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts split up and search the huts. Some find the huts empty, save for earthen pots among the ashes in the hearths.\n"
"\n"
"However, most of the huts contain human remains, bones stripped by time and beast. They take a few of the bones for scholars to study in the future."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_abandoned_gate.tres
msgid "Investigate the shrine."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_abandoned_gate.tres
msgid ""
"As the scouts approach the weathered shrine, they spot rows of wooden prayer tablets hanging on the walls. The ones outside have been worn smooth by the elements, but ones hanging from the rafters inside the shrine are still legible.\n"
"\n"
"The language is too old to understand full sentences, but they recognize a few familiar characters, the most frequent being Disease, Cough, and Cure."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_abandoned_gate.tres
msgid "Catalog useful resources."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_abandoned_gate.tres
msgid "The scouts walk through the village, carefully recording the amount of timber that could be scavenged, the depth of the well, and the area of the nearby fields. These records will be of use if the expedition decides to settle in the vicinity."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bamboo_grove.tres
msgid "The Dense Bamboo"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bamboo_grove.tres
msgid "The survey team follows an old path into a bamboo grove, only for it to become fainter and fainter, until they find themselves lost among the stalks."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bamboo_grove.tres
msgid "Cut a straight path."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bamboo_grove.tres
msgid "The team decides to use brute force. They spend the day cutting a path through the bamboo, leaving ready building materials for the rest of the expedition."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bamboo_grove.tres
msgid "Navigate by the canopy."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bamboo_grove.tres
msgid "By carefully observing which way the stalks lean, the scouts figure out the sunniest direction and manage to find their way out."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bamboo_grove.tres
msgid "Backtrack to the edge."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bamboo_grove.tres
msgid "The team decides to turn back before they get completely lost. It takes a while to find the way out, and they emerge long after the sun has set."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bear_temple.tres
msgid "The Abandoned Temple"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bear_temple.tres
msgid ""
"After a tiring all-day hike, the survey team stumbles upon an old, pre-Shattering temple, abandoned but in surprisingly good repair.\n"
"\n"
"The scouts are happy to find shelter for the night, especially knowing that boars and bears frequent the area.\n"
"\n"
"Some among the group feel hesitant, though, claiming that they hear strange creaking noises and feel an eerie presence in the air inside."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bear_temple.tres
msgid "Camp despite misgivings."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bear_temple.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts disregard the naysayers and camp inside the temple anyway.\n"
"\n"
"During the night, they wake up to scratching noises, and as they raise their torches, they find a group of brown bear cubs ransacking their packs, spilling supplies everywhere.\n"
"\n"
"After the commotion dies down and the scouts are safe outside, they realize that they had to leave most of their supplies behind."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bear_temple.tres
msgid "Look for anything unusual."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bear_temple.tres
msgid ""
"A few brave members of the team climb the stairs to the temple's upper level, hoping to investigate the strange noises before setting up camp. Afraid to ignite the dry wood, they conduct the search in the dark.\n"
"\n"
"Although they fail to find the source of the alleged noises, they return with a little statuette, surprisingly unlike the image of the Enlightened One they are used to."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bear_temple.tres
msgid "Perform a cleansing ritual."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bear_temple.tres
msgid ""
"One of the scouts, the most familiar with sacred rites, performs a simple cleansing ritual to pacify any restless spirits, chanting and spraying water on the ground.\n"
"\n"
"The night passes without incident, and in the morning, as they are leaving, they spot an auspicious omen: a bear cub walking towards the temple grounds."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bear_temple.tres
msgid "Post guards and camp outside."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bear_temple.tres
msgid ""
"The team decides to be extra careful and camp outside the temple.\n"
"\n"
"Two of the scouts stand guard all night, and spot no danger.\n"
"\n"
"In the morning, they can't stop complaining about forgoing sleep for no good reason."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_beautiful_valley.tres
msgid "The Picturesque Vista"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_beautiful_valley.tres
msgid "One of the scouts is struck by the beauty of the valley over which the surveyors are passing. She asks to stay behind to sketch the landscape, promising to catch up as soon as she is done."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_beautiful_valley.tres
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_scary_climb.tres
msgid "Wait for her."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_beautiful_valley.tres
msgid "The team calls a break to let the artist draw. The finished sketch is a striking work of art: not only does it show the distant mountain and the valley below, but even the members of the team are immortalized within the sketch."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_beautiful_valley.tres
msgid "Have everyone sketch a version."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_beautiful_valley.tres
msgid ""
"The team calls a break and rather than letting the artist draw alone, they split the charcoal and each scout sketches their own take on the landscape.\n"
"\n"
"The result is surprisingly varied - some have drawn the valley alone. Others have focused on the distant peak rising from the clouds. One man drew a portrait of the artist instead, and now shyly presents it to her before resuming the trip."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_beautiful_valley.tres
msgid "Let the artist catch up."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_beautiful_valley.tres
msgid "The team moves on, leaving the artist to sketch. By nightfall she has still failed to catch up, so they backtrack. It turns out the poor woman had sprained her ankle, and decided to rest for the night rather than walk the treacherous path in the dark."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_beautiful_valley.tres
msgid "Continue on together."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_beautiful_valley.tres
msgid "The team refuses to split up and forges ahead. The artist keeps on grumbling about tyrannical leadership, but the rest pay her no mind."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bell_tower.tres
msgid "The Bell Tower"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bell_tower.tres
msgid ""
"Deep in the forest the survey team finds an ancient bell tower, its bronze bell still hanging at the top.\n"
"\n"
"On closer inspection, the scouts realize that the bell is barely attached, and may soon fall."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bell_tower.tres
msgid "Detach the bell."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bell_tower.tres
msgid "<term:relic.wisdom_bell> or <term:card.wound>"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bell_tower.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts cut through the corroded ring attaching the bell to the roof of the tower and safely detach it.\n"
"\n"
"They bring it with them, intending to leave it at a museum."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bell_tower.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts hit the bell with a staff and watch as the forest explodes with birds.\n"
"\n"
"Even after the bell falls silent, rustling can be heard from every direction as animals hurry to flee the frightening sound.\n"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bell_tower.tres
msgid "Study the bell."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bell_tower.tres
msgid ""
"One of the scouts sketches the bell and copies the designs decorating its surface.\n"
"  \n"
"She also marks the tower's location on the map before the team departs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bell_tower.tres
msgid "Leave the tower alone."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bell_tower.tres
msgid "The scouts move on, not wanting to disturb the ancient tower."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_big_tree.tres
msgid "The Towering Tree"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_big_tree.tres
msgid ""
"The team finds themselves standing in a clearing dominated by the biggest tree they'd ever seen.\n"
"\n"
"One of the scouts, a priest, insists that it must be inhabited by a powerful spirit. Another, a scholar's apprentice, wants to measure it and study the factors that have let it grow so large. An adventurous fellow suggests climbing it.\n"
"\n"
"The rest of the group just wants to stay a while and marvel at the size."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_big_tree.tres
msgid "Study the tree."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_big_tree.tres
msgid "The budding scholar takes a string and measures the circumference of the tree. She measures the shadow to estimate its height. Finally, she records the distance to other nearby trees and takes their measurements too. Having recorded all her findings, she signals to the group to move on."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_big_tree.tres
msgid "Pay respects to the spirit."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_big_tree.tres
msgid "The priest draws glyphs in the dirt around the tree. He bows deeply and chants several prayers while the rest of the group stand back, respectfully. Finally, the priest is satisfied with the ritual and the group moves on from the clearing."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_big_tree.tres
msgid "Climb the tree."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_big_tree.tres
msgid "Chance of <term:relic.pine_curl> or <term:card.wound>"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_big_tree.tres
msgid "Set up camp under the tree."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_big_tree.tres
msgid "The scouts set up camp under the giant tree. One composes a poem, proclaiming the tree a witness to the Shattering. Someone paints a sketch. The group is inspired by the wonder they encountered."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bitter_water.tres
msgid "The Bitter Water"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bitter_water.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts have been rationing water for days. They finally reach a stream so clear that every stone beneath the water is visible.\n"
"\n"
"Three thirsty travelers rush ahead of the group and, dipping their vessels into the flowing water, take a drink.\n"
"\n"
"They immediately spit it out. The water is unbearably bitter.\n"
"\n"
"Some suspect that the stream has been cursed by spirits. Others worry it was contaminated upstream."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bitter_water.tres
msgid "Boil the water."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bitter_water.tres
msgid ""
"The group boils several pots of water, but the heat does nothing to remove the bitter taste.\n"
"\n"
"Their fuel and time are wasted."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bitter_water.tres
msgid "Drink it despite the taste."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bitter_water.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts decide that they are too thirsty to wait.\n"
"\n"
"They fill their vessels with the clear water and drink deeply.\n"
"\n"
"Several hours later, everyone is violently sick."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bitter_water.tres
msgid "Search downstream."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bitter_water.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts walk several miles downstream and try the water again.\n"
"\n"
"It is still clear, and the taste is clearly better.\n"
"\n"
"They fill their vessels and drink deeply, refreshed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bitter_water.tres
msgid "Search upstream."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_bitter_water.tres
msgid ""
"A small party walks towards the stream's source.\n"
"\n"
"They discover a mineral spring gushing from pale rock into the main water source.\n"
"\n"
"They confirm it to be the source of bitterness and mark the point on their map."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_burden.tres
msgid "The Heavy Burden"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_burden.tres
msgid ""
"One of the surveyors is lagging behind, having filled two large boxes with extra rations and first aid supplies to deal with every possible eventuality.\n"
"\n"
"The rest of the team is growing impatient, demanding that their slow teammate leave some of his load behind."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_burden.tres
msgid "Leave the extra rations."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_burden.tres
msgid "The overburdened scout finally submits to the social pressure and leaves behind his box of rice balls and pickled burdock root. Perhaps the wildlife will find it appetizing."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_burden.tres
msgid "Leave the first aid supplies."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_burden.tres
msgid "The overburdened scout finally submits to the social pressure and leaves behind his box of bandages and ointments. He's sure the team will regret it the next time someone is injured."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_burden.tres
msgid "Split the load."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_burden.tres
msgid "The surveyors decide to repack the load, splitting it evenly among the team. The burden is much lighter when split among many shoulders."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_burden.tres
msgid "Insist on keeping everything."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_burden.tres
msgid "The overburdened scout stubbornly insists that he will need every item in both of his boxes, and refuses to budge. The rest of the team heaves heavy sighs and carries on."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_buried_monument.tres
msgid "The Odd Rock"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_buried_monument.tres
msgid ""
"The survey team comes upon an odd boulder in the middle of a path. It is unnaturally round and smooth, a little dome rising from the ground.\n"
"\n"
"On closer inspection, it appears to have faint carvings on the surface."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_buried_monument.tres
msgid "Dig it up."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_buried_monument.tres
msgid "The scouts start digging and discover that the boulder is the tip of an ancient building. They clear enough of the earth to find several relics to carry back to the scholars, and record the site for future excavations."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_buried_monument.tres
msgid "Take a rubbing of the carvings."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_buried_monument.tres
msgid "The team takes a charcoal rubbing of the inscriptions for future scholars to decipher."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_buried_monument.tres
msgid "Mark it with a signpost."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_buried_monument.tres
msgid "The scouts leave a little signpost warning the rest of the expedition that the stone is special and deserves further study. Considering their job accomplished, they move on."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_buried_monument.tres
msgid "Ignore the boulder."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_buried_monument.tres
msgid "The survey team ignores the boulder and marches on, ready to stumble upon more interesting things."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_campfire.tres
msgid "Chatting by the Fire"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_campfire.tres
msgid "As the team settles down to camp for the night, they gather around a campfire, intent on discussing the plan for the next day."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_campfire.tres
msgid "Discuss how to avoid inefficiencies."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_campfire.tres
msgid "The team spends the evening discussing ways to pack lighter and to find better shortcuts. They compare the weights of different foods, and the advantages of using a single tool to do multiple tasks. By the end of the discussion, they are certain that they can achieve more with less."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_campfire.tres
msgid "Compare maps."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_campfire.tres
msgid "The scouts take out the maps they've been sketching and compare them, correcting discrepancies and adding in bits others have noticed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_campfire.tres
msgid "Play music instead."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_campfire.tres
msgid "One of the scouts takes out a flute and starts playing an old melody, one that everybody recognizes. Another joins by drumming on a hollow log. The group grows closer, though no words are exchanged."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_campfire.tres
msgid "Tell ghost stories instead."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_campfire.tres
msgid "The scouts go around in a circle telling stories of spirits haunting the woods and ghosts coming back to claim revenge. They speak of Lady Chrysanthemum and the Black Monk, of the Two-Mouthed Woman and the Bitter Smile, as well as countless others. Each story is more chilling than the last one, and more than a few of the scouts end up waking up from nightmares that night."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_canyon_shrine.tres
msgid "The Canyon Shrine"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_canyon_shrine.tres
msgid ""
"As the scouts make their way through a canyon pass, their attention is drawn toward a great grey mountain towering on the horizon.\n"
"\n"
"Admiring its imposing height, they almost miss the bright red shrine gate sitting on the cliff above them.\n"
"\n"
"Beyond the gate stands a stone shrine, its sloped roof covered with moss."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_canyon_shrine.tres
msgid "Search the shrine."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_canyon_shrine.tres
msgid ""
"Inside the shrine the scouts find a collection of animal masks hanging on the walls. The best preserved one appears to be carved to resemble a boar's face.\n"
"\n"
"One of the scouts dons the mask, laughing, and watches his companions suddenly turn white, pointing behind him. When he looks, he sees nothing but a copse of trees.\n"
"\n"
"His companions explain that they saw a giant boar staring at them, then disappearing into the trees."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_canyon_shrine.tres
msgid "Investigate surroundings."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_canyon_shrine.tres
msgid ""
"Eager to explore, a scout walks beyond the shrine, his foot stepping on a pinecone with a loud crunch.\n"
"\n"
"A boar suddenly appears from behind the trees and lowers its head, preparing to charge. The surveyors flee, hurriedly scrambling down the canyon wall."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_canyon_shrine.tres
msgid ""
"A nun among the surveyors makes a crude altar out of the nearby pinecones.\n"
"\n"
"She leaves a small inscribed blessing on top."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_canyon_shrine.tres
msgid "Admire the scenery."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: preview_description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_canyon_shrine.tres
msgid "Gain 1 maximum <term:inspiration>"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_canyon_shrine.tres
msgid "Gained 1 maximum <term:inspiration>."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_canyon_shrine.tres
msgid ""
"Exhausted from the steep climb, the surveyors bow before the shrine.\n"
"\n"
"They stand by the red shrine gate for a while, directing their gaze toward the grey mountain in the distance."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cart.tres
msgid "The Hapless Carter"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cart.tres
msgid ""
"The survey team comes upon a cart stuck before a little stream.\n"
"\n"
"The settler pulling the cart had decided to go ahead of the expedition, and is now stuck, unable to get the wide cart over the narrow bridge."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cart.tres
msgid "Carry the cart over."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cart.tres
msgid "Three scouts join the settler and raise the whole cart onto their shoulders. Together, they carefully carry it over the bridge and leave it safely on the other end. The whole team finds such shared physical effort inspiring."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cart.tres
msgid "Dismantle the cart first."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cart.tres
msgid "One of the scouts suggests taking the cart apart and carrying it piece by piece. The plan works perfectly until someone manages to drop one of the wheels, which is quickly carried off by the current. The settler is left heartbroken, waiting for the rest of the expedition to catch up."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cart.tres
msgid "Take the settler along instead."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cart.tres
msgid "It is a waste to leave all these supplies behind, but that cart was never going to fit over the bridge. The settler decides to let it go and join the survey team. At least they'll always have someone around to help."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cart.tres
msgid "Leave the settler alone."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cart.tres
msgid "The survey team bows an apology and carries on, certain that their mission is too important to stop and help bystanders."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cliff_shrine.tres
msgid "The Little Cliff Shrine"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cliff_shrine.tres
msgid ""
"The air is oppressively hot and humid as the survey team makes its way to the top of a cliff.\n"
"\n"
"As they crest the final rise, they see an old bridge crossing over a stream ending in a roaring waterfall.\n"
"\n"
"A tiny shrine overlooks the site, sheltering a little stone pillar wrapped in a beautiful jade necklace."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cliff_shrine.tres
msgid "Clean the shrine."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cliff_shrine.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts wipe away layers of moss that had started to grow on the shrine's roof, and brush decades of dust from the necklace.\n"
"\n"
"Carved in the rock behind the pillar they find the image of a shrine maiden, whirling with the necklace held in her hand."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cliff_shrine.tres
msgid "Pray at the shrine."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cliff_shrine.tres
msgid "The scouts bow to the shrine, each saying a brief prayer, before they continue on their way."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cliff_shrine.tres
msgid "Take the necklace."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cliff_shrine.tres
msgid ""
"One of the scouts takes a liking to the necklace and decides to keep it as a memento. She rinses it in the stream, watching it glimmer bright green in the cool water.\n"
"\n"
"Before she can stuff the necklace into her sleeve, one of her teammates demands she hand it over, claiming that he had spotted the shrine first. The others, hearing the commotion, likewise protest.\n"
"\n"
"By the time they resolve the disagreement, the necklace is torn apart, each scout keeping a few of the stones."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cliff_shrine.tres
msgid "Rest by the stream."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cliff_shrine.tres
msgid ""
"The team ignores the shrine, instead spending an hour basking in the cool spray.\n"
"\n"
"They fill their canteens, rinse their headbands, and continue on fully refreshed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cloud_shapes.tres
msgid "The Shape of a Cloud"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cloud_shapes.tres
msgid ""
"At the shard's edge, the scouts stop to watch the clouds below. They twist then separate, briefly forming into shapes before dissolving again.\n"
"\n"
"The shapes look different to each person. Soon the entire group is pointing at the same cloud, calling out details to support their interpretation."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cloud_shapes.tres
msgid "It's a dragon."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cloud_shapes.tres
msgid "After a heated discussion, the majority is finally convinced that the curling cloud looks like a magnificent dragon, its shifting body shimmering orange and purple."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cloud_shapes.tres
msgid "It's an ox."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cloud_shapes.tres
msgid "After a heated discussion, the majority is finally convinced that the dense cloud looks like a strong ox, with two horns protruding from its head."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cloud_shapes.tres
msgid "It's a ship."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cloud_shapes.tres
msgid "After a heated discussion, the majority is finally convinced that the cloud looks like a ship, floating on waves of blue, white mist forming its sails. It seems to be heading toward a distant shard."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cloud_shapes.tres
msgid "It doesn't matter."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_cloud_shapes.tres
msgid "The scouts fail to agree and give up, deciding that these are random shapes not worth pay attention to."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_deep_forest.tres
msgid "Deep in the Forest"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_deep_forest.tres
msgid ""
"The survey team has found itself deep in the forest. The trees grow close here, the canopy blocking all but a few rays of sunshine.\n"
"\n"
"They decide to rest for a while, but a few of the members want to make better use of their time."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_deep_forest.tres
msgid "Research the plant life."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_deep_forest.tres
msgid "One of the scholars catalogues the local plant life, recording her findings."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_deep_forest.tres
msgid "Look for local animals."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_deep_forest.tres
msgid "One of the scouts spends the afternoon walking among the trees and noting every animal she encounters."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_deep_forest.tres
msgid "Paint the trees."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_deep_forest.tres
msgid "A particularly artistic member of the team paints the forest onto a sheet of paper. Someday they will get it printed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_deep_forest.tres
msgid "Gather edible plants."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_deep_forest.tres
msgid "Several members of the team walk the camp perimeter gathering berries and wild roots. Just enough for a humble dinner."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_desert_edge.tres
msgid "The Desert's Edge"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_desert_edge.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts are crossing a stretch of desert, the edge of it now only hours away.\n"
"\n"
"The afternoon sun is at its worst, and the heat feels unbearable.\n"
"\n"
"Water is running low, and two of the surveyors are beginning to show signs of heat exhaustion."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_desert_edge.tres
msgid "Carry them."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_desert_edge.tres
msgid ""
"Eager to leave the desert behind, the scouts haul their sick companions onto their backs and trudge onward.\n"
"\n"
"By the time they reach the edge of the desert, most of the team collapses from exhaustion."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_desert_edge.tres
msgid "Construct shelter."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_desert_edge.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts set up the tents and let the two who are sick lie down inside.\n"
"\n"
"The recovery is slow, and the group is forced to spend the night in the desert, but by morning everyone is well again."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_desert_edge.tres
msgid "Use up the water."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_desert_edge.tres
msgid ""
"The sick explorers are given the rest of the group's water, which keeps them well enough for the team to reach the edge of the desert safely.\n"
"\n"
"This willingness to sacrifice binds the team together."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_desert_edge.tres
msgid "Keep going."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: preview_description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_desert_edge.tres
msgid "Lose 2 maximum <term:inspiration>"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_desert_edge.tres
msgid "Lost 2 maximum <term:inspiration>."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_desert_edge.tres
msgid ""
"The explorers are so close to leaving the desert behind them that they decide to press forward despite their companions' pale faces and trembling limbs.\n"
"\n"
"The plan quickly falls apart when one of the two sick people faints, and the other begins to hallucinate.\n"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_empty_desert.tres
msgid "Visions in the Desert"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_empty_desert.tres
msgid ""
"The surveyors have been traveling the desert for days, the sun beating down on their backs.\n"
"\n"
"One afternoon, a scout suddenly points into the distance and describes what she sees there: a beautiful oasis with glittering water and green trees. Her teammate shakes his head, disagreeing with her vision. He claims to see a tall, snow-white fortress surrounded by a moat instead.\n"
"\n"
"The group can't come to a consensus on what they are looking at, the shapes seeming to shift and shimmer in the sun."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_empty_desert.tres
msgid "Follow the visions."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_empty_desert.tres
msgid ""
"The group decides to divert from their original route and investigate the vision instead.\n"
"\n"
"They spend several hours walking in the direction the two scouts indicated, but the visions only seem to fade the closer they get.\n"
"\n"
"By the time they reach the indicated location, the visions are gone, and they find themselves in the same empty desert they had been traversing for days."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_empty_desert.tres
msgid "Observe the visions."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_empty_desert.tres
msgid ""
"Fascinated by the phenomenon, the surveyors decide to take a break and spend an hour observing the mirage.\n"
"\n"
"They see the images shifting and glimmering in the sunlight. A few of the scouts take out paper and sketch what they see, then compare their drawings, finding each of them entirely unlike the others.\n"
"\n"
"By the time the sun sets, the visions fade away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_empty_desert.tres
msgid "Investigate the dessert."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_empty_desert.tres
msgid ""
"The team leader, who has been sharing her food too freely and has ended up particularly hungry, becomes convinced that the mirage resembles an enormous white mochi.\n"
"\n"
"It takes the efforts of the entire team to convince her to give up on the idea of pursuing the confection. The group spends the next few hours joking about desserts and imagining all the delicious foods awaiting them when they rejoin the expedition."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_empty_desert.tres
msgid "Ignore the visions."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_empty_desert.tres
msgid ""
"Many of the scouts, although tired and thirsty, have seen mirages before and refuse to be distracted.\n"
"\n"
"It proves difficult to persuade the younger teammates to continue their original path, and they lose precious time arguing that finding a glittering castle in the middle of the desert is highly unlikely."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_flying_papers.tres
msgid "A Thieving Wind"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_flying_papers.tres
msgid ""
"A fierce gust of wind sweeps across the field, bending the long grasses wildly.\n"
"\n"
"Suddenly, the survey team's logs and maps fly from the note-keeper's satchel and scatter into the sky.\n"
"\n"
"Loose pages tumble through the air, chasing a scout's lost hat."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_flying_papers.tres
msgid "Chase the papers."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_flying_papers.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts drop their packs and break into a run, dodging trees and vaulting over ditches, their eyes never leaving the flying sheets.\n"
"\n"
"They would surely have recovered their collection, if it weren't for the nest of hornets they dislodged in their wake."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_flying_papers.tres
msgid "Follow the wind."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_flying_papers.tres
msgid ""
"The group decides not to chase each paper individually, but to follow the direction the wind is blowing.\n"
"\n"
"Their restraint is rewarded when they reach a line of bushes whose branches have gathered most of the papers."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_flying_papers.tres
msgid "Follow the hat."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_flying_papers.tres
msgid ""
"The surveyors give up on the papers, but chase the straw hat as it vanishes over a hill.\n"
"\n"
"The hat leads them to a sheltered hollow, the ground completely covered in wildflowers."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_flying_papers.tres
msgid "Let the papers go."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_flying_papers.tres
msgid ""
"The surveyors accept that the wind has taken their records.\n"
"\n"
"They will have to let the past go."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_foggy_highlands.tres
msgid "The Foggy Highlands"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_foggy_highlands.tres
msgid ""
"The temperature is dropping as the surveyors march through a steep pass across the highlands.\n"
"\n"
"Ahead, a thick cloud of fog has descended over the slopes. Soon, they will find themselves swallowed up by it if they continue on the same path."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_foggy_highlands.tres
msgid "Tie everyone together."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_foggy_highlands.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts tie themselves together with a long rope before the fog reaches them. This way, no one can become separated from the group.\n"
"\n"
"The plan goes awry when one of the scouts stumbles off the path and starts sliding down the slope, pulling the rest of the group behind her.\n"
"\n"
"Crisis is averted when her teammates manage to pull her back up, but everyone is left shaken by the mishap.\n"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_foggy_highlands.tres
msgid "Camp right here."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_foggy_highlands.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts decide to camp right where they are before the fog catches up to them.\n"
"\n"
"Mist gathers on their eyelashes and on the brims of their hats as they wait.\n"
"\n"
"They are uncomfortable and chilly, but at least they are at no risk of tumbling down the slopes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_foggy_highlands.tres
msgid "Look for shelter."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_foggy_highlands.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts scatter, looking for places to shelter. One gasps and points at the ground.\n"
"\n"
"Hundreds of spiderwebs glitter with dewdrops among the grass.\n"
"\n"
"Following the webs leads the scouts to the mouth of a cave, empty but for the skittering of thousands of tiny legs."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_foggy_highlands.tres
msgid "Continue walking."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_foggy_highlands.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts decide to stay on the path.\n"
"\n"
"Soon, the fog becomes so dense that they can only see a few paces ahead, making the path indistinguishable from its surroundings.\n"
"\n"
"When the fog finally lifts, they find themselves right where they started."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_fork.tres
msgid "The Fork in the Road"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_fork.tres
msgid ""
"The surveyors are trying to pass over a hill when they reach a fork in the road.\n"
"\n"
"One path looks smooth, well-trodden by animals, but it goes all the way around the hill.\n"
"\n"
"The other is steep and covered with loose stones, but is much more direct."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_fork.tres
msgid "Take the animal trail."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_fork.tres
msgid "Following the long path takes up much of the day, but the scouts get well acquainted with the local fauna."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_fork.tres
msgid "Climb the steep path."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_fork.tres
msgid "The climb up is grueling, but that gives the surveyors time to identify many of the minerals composing the loose rocks."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_fork.tres
msgid "Search for alternative options."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_fork.tres
msgid "The scouts split up and search the surroundings. One of them returns having found a trail they had missed earlier that offers a shortcut bypassing the hill entirely."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_frozen_pack.tres
msgid "The Frozen Pack"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_frozen_pack.tres
msgid ""
"As the survey team is climbing a steep ridge high among the icy peaks, they notice a traveler's pack, frozen solid to the rock.\n"
"\n"
"The design suggests that the pack was made before the Shattering."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_frozen_pack.tres
msgid "Dig the pack out with chisels."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_frozen_pack.tres
msgid "The scouts use mallets to hammer in chisels and free the pack from the ice. It takes some time for the pack itself to thaw, but when it's finally warm enough to unpack, they find inside an ancient map of the whole region that used to include this shard."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_frozen_pack.tres
msgid "Melt the ice with fire."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_frozen_pack.tres
msgid "Chance of finding a map"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_frozen_pack.tres
msgid "The fire has to be refueled several times until its heat is enough to melt the ice, but eventually the pack is freed. Inside the scouts find an ancient map of the whole region that used to include this shard."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_frozen_pack.tres
msgid "Mark the location on a map."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_frozen_pack.tres
msgid "The scouts mark the location of the pack on their maps and move on. Let this be a quest for some future adventurer."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_frozen_pack.tres
msgid "Ignore the pack."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_frozen_pack.tres
msgid "The survey team decides not to waste time on forgotten luggage, and moves on."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_fruits.tres
msgid "Wild Fruits"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_fruits.tres
msgid ""
"The team stumbles upon a grove of trees drooping under the weight of plump fruit.\n"
"\n"
"They look a bit like Old World persimmons, but they have grown wild since the Shattering.\n"
"\n"
"The scouts are quite hungry, but they find it suspicious that no birds or insects seem to be touching the fruit."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_fruits.tres
msgid "Try the fruit raw."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_fruits.tres
msgid "<term:bonus.food> gain or <term:bonus.safety> loss"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_fruits.tres
msgid "One of the scouts takes a tiny bite of the fruit, and the team waits to see the effects. Not half an hour later, the scout is bent over with a stomach ache. It's bad enough that the team has to stop and rest for the night to wait it out."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_fruits.tres
msgid "Cook the fruit."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_fruits.tres
msgid "The team sets up a campfire and boils the fruit into a sweet, nutritious paste. They leave with their bellies full and their rations replenished."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_fruits.tres
msgid "Find something the wildlife does eat."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_fruits.tres
msgid "The scouts search the area and find several gnawed-upon roots. These prove safe, but the taste leaves much to be desired."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_fruits.tres
msgid "Leave the fruit alone."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_fruits.tres
msgid "The team moves on, their hunger unsatisfied, unwilling to take a risk."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_glass_beach.tres
msgid "The Secluded Cove"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_glass_beach.tres
msgid ""
"A secluded cove surrounded by cliffs opens out onto the vast sea.\n"
"\n"
"Although the open water is too dangerous to cross in tiny boats, the sheltered cove and its surrounding beaches could offer their own discoveries."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_glass_beach.tres
msgid "Rest on the beach."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_glass_beach.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts decide to stay on the beach and relax for a while. They lie on the warm sand and watch the clouds pass.\n"
"\n"
"Once they have time to pay attention, they notice that many of the pebbles are made of glass, a luxury even in the Old World. The edges have been polished perfectly smooth by the sea."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_glass_beach.tres
msgid "Explore the cliffs."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_glass_beach.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts climb the cliffs surrounding the cove. The grass there smells sweet, and bees buzz back and forth among the scattered wildflowers.\n"
"\n"
"At the top of the hill, the group finds a clear pool. One of the surveyors dips her hand into it and instantly recoils as a fierce burning pain spreads across her skin.\n"
"\n"
"Once they take a moment to pay attention, they see that the surrounding stone has been eaten away, and nothing grows within two paces of the pool."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_glass_beach.tres
msgid "Row along the shore."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_glass_beach.tres
msgid ""
"The surveyors get into their boats and let the current carry them along the shoreline.\n"
"\n"
"As they watch the cliffs drift by, they spot a nearly perfect hole cut into the stone, too regular to be natural. The inside of the hole appears to be covered in rusted, barnacle-clad metal."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_glass_beach.tres
msgid "Leave the cove."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_glass_beach.tres
msgid "The explorers decide to continue their journey elsewhere, leaving the secluded beach unexplored."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_glum_swamp.tres
msgid "Lost in the Swamp"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_glum_swamp.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts' sandals cling to the muck as they swat at clouds of insects. They have been circling the same pools and arguing over the same landmarks under the overcast sky all day.\n"
"\n"
"At last, they come upon something new: a small blooming cherry tree alone in the swamp.\n"
"\n"
"\"Probably the last tree we'll ever see,\" mutters one of the scouts."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_glum_swamp.tres
msgid "Follow the pessimist."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_glum_swamp.tres
msgid ""
"\"I don't expect we'll all arrive in one piece,\" the scout says glumly. Still, he traces the tree's roots and finds a narrow ridge of solid ground beneath the water.\n"
"\n"
"He predicts lost sandals, unfriendly wildlife, and death, but the group follows his lead anyway. The first two predictions come to pass, but the last one does not."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_glum_swamp.tres
msgid "Challenge the pessimist."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_glum_swamp.tres
msgid ""
"Exhausted by the gloomy surveyor's constant predictions of disaster, the group demands he prove he knows where he is going.\n"
"\n"
"The resulting argument takes up the rest of the day.\n"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_glum_swamp.tres
msgid "Camp by the tree."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_glum_swamp.tres
msgid ""
"The group decides that they are too tired to continue. The gloomy scout grumbles that they will probably drown in their sleep, but then digs drainage ditches around the camp and stays up all night to watch for rising water.\n"
"\n"
"By morning, everyone else is well rested and the supplies are still dry."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_glum_swamp.tres
msgid "Ignore the pessimist."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_glum_swamp.tres
msgid ""
"The group decides to ignore the gloomy man's grumbling. They take the tree as a sign of drier land nearby. They rush ahead towards the next tree, letting their glum teammate trail behind.\n"
"\n"
"The ground seems firmer at first, but then rapidly gives way under their feet.\n"
"\n"
"The rescue takes up the rest of the day."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_hawk_chick.tres
msgid "The Baby Hawk"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_hawk_chick.tres
msgid ""
"As the survey team hikes up a steep path, they see a hawk racing overhead. It lands on a pine tree and cries out sharply.\n"
"\n"
"The scouts hear another cry, and looking down, see a small nestling stuck in a thorny shrub, helplessly flapping its wings."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_hawk_chick.tres
msgid "Return it to its nest."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_hawk_chick.tres
msgid "Much <term:bonus.harmony> or <term:card.wound>"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_hawk_chick.tres
msgid ""
"Fearing for the chick's odds of survival, the surveyors decide to return it to the nest.\n"
"\n"
"One of them gently picks up the chick, wraps it in a cloth, and climbs up the tree.\n"
"\n"
"The adult hawk flies away and starts circling above, letting the scout safely deposit the chick."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_hawk_chick.tres
msgid "Move it to a safe spot."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_hawk_chick.tres
msgid ""
"Fearing for the chick's odds of survival, the surveyors gently move the nestling so it lies sheltered among the roots of the tree.\n"
"\n"
"Perhaps that will keep it out of harm's way for a time."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_hawk_chick.tres
msgid ""
"The group decides to take the nestling with them.\n"
"\n"
"They gently wrap it into a soft cloth, and feed it regularly throughout the day.\n"
"\n"
"Soon a young hawk will follow them everywhere."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_hawk_chick.tres
msgid ""
"The group decides to leave the nestling where it is.\n"
"\n"
"As they walk away, they see the adult hawk circling overhead."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_hay_fever.tres
msgid "The Itch"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_hay_fever.tres
msgid ""
"The sunny skies and warm breeze have made travelling across the plains pleasant. The surveyors whistle and sing merrily as they hike.\n"
"\n"
"By late afternoon, however, the sky has become strangely hazy and several scouts have begun to sneeze. Many more complain of itchy, watery eyes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_hay_fever.tres
msgid "Use damp cloths."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_hay_fever.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts place damp cloths over their faces and continue hiking.\n"
"\n"
"Although a few still sneeze once in a while, most seem to be cured for the time being."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_hay_fever.tres
msgid "Flee to the forest."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_hay_fever.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts blame the bad air on angry spirits haunting the plains, and retreat to a nearby cedar grove.\n"
"\n"
"Unfortunately, their symptoms only worsen there.\n"
"\n"
"Finally, someone notices pollen falling from the canopy in thick yellow clouds, the wind carrying it across the plains."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_hay_fever.tres
msgid "Wash in the stream."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_hay_fever.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts wash their faces in a cold stream.\n"
"\n"
"The symptoms abate, but their relief is only temporary.\n"
"\n"
"Not an hour later, they go back to sneezing and scratching their eyes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_hay_fever.tres
msgid "Continue hiking."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_hay_fever.tres
msgid "The explorers continue onward, though they cannot stop sneezing and scratching their eyes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_komusou.tres
msgid "The Monk of Emptiness"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_komusou.tres
msgid ""
"As the survey team is walking through an ancient, overgrown road, they spot a figure on the horizon.\n"
"\n"
"The figure turns out to be a man wearing a basket as a hat. He introduces himself as a monk of Emptiness, an order none of the scouts had heard of.\n"
"\n"
"A few scouts whisper that it must be a trickster spirit taking human form."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_komusou.tres
msgid "Ask about his order."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_komusou.tres
msgid ""
"The man explains that theirs is not an order that follows the Enlightened One, but one that seeks enlightenment in meditating on the void which they believe is the true nature of self.\n"
"\n"
"In pursuit of this goal, they cover their heads to dull their senses, play haunting music on the flute to block out sounds, and travel unexplored shards to escape human contact."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_komusou.tres
msgid "Invite him along."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_komusou.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts offer to take the man along, as solitary travel on a wild shard is bound to be dangerous.\n"
"\n"
"The man refuses, but takes out a flute and invites everyone to meditate with him on emptiness.\n"
"\n"
"The tune he plays is haunting and loud, but also strangely beautiful."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_komusou.tres
msgid "Present an offering."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_komusou.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts offer the man a share of their supplies, in case it's a spirit testing their generosity, but the man refuses.\n"
"\n"
"Instead, he asks the explorers to take his flute. He claims to have grown beyond needing it as a meditation aid, able now to block out the whole world by mere thought."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_komusou.tres
msgid "Ignore the strange man."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_komusou.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts nod a polite bow and move on.\n"
"\n"
"The man appears to be perfectly content to be left alone."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_lonely_steppe.tres
msgid "The Lonely Steppe"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_lonely_steppe.tres
msgid ""
"The surveyors make their way through a lonely steppe. The wind howls mournfully in the tall grasses, rustling the leaves of the few scattered trees.\n"
"\n"
"The days pass with no sign of the bleak landscape ending, and melancholy spreads among the group.\n"
"\n"
"One of the explorers has grown increasingly withdrawn. He begins lagging behind, walking with his head down."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_lonely_steppe.tres
msgid "Keep him company."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_lonely_steppe.tres
msgid ""
"One scout walks beside the gloomy teammate, offering a friendly ear.\n"
"\n"
"Soon, the lonely man begins to talk of the family he left behind, and of his fear that he will never return home.\n"
"\n"
"The two become close over the next few days."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_lonely_steppe.tres
msgid "Confront him."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_lonely_steppe.tres
msgid ""
"The group forms a circle around the downcast man.\n"
"\n"
"A few scouts demand to know why he keeps such a slow pace. Embarrassed, the man apologizes and rejoins the group.\n"
"\n"
"The next morning, they find his mat empty. After calling for him for hours, they realize that he isn't returning."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_lonely_steppe.tres
msgid "Sing to raise morale."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_lonely_steppe.tres
msgid ""
"The group begins to sing a cheerful walking song.\n"
"\n"
"The happy tune sounds hollow at first, lost in the wide expanse, but soon verses are interspersed with bouts of laughter and faces begin to brighten.\n"
"\n"
"The lagging scout can't help but join in when he recognizes a song from his childhood.\n"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_lonely_steppe.tres
msgid "Let him be."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_lonely_steppe.tres
msgid ""
"Not wanting to pry and thinking it best to leave the man in peace, the group continues on without stopping.\n"
"\n"
"As the day wears on and the shadows grow longer, the scouts realize that the familiar lonely figure is nowhere to be seen.\n"
"\n"
"The explorers make camp for the night and wait for him, but he does not return."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_lotus_pond.tres
msgid "The Lotus Pond"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_lotus_pond.tres
msgid ""
"The surveyors are slowly paddling through a lake, their long bamboo poles touching the ground, disturbing the silt below.\n"
"\n"
"They carefully bend over the water, plucking the broad, green lotus leaves. They will be used for food wrappings and medicine later.\n"
"\n"
"As one gatherer reaches for a leaf, she falls into the water with a sudden splash. She cannot swim well, and begins flailing wildly."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_lotus_pond.tres
msgid "Dive in after her."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_lotus_pond.tres
msgid ""
"The strongest swimmer jumps into the lake and helps guide her to shore.\n"
"\n"
"As they wade through the mud, they discover a large cluster of edible lotus roots beneath their feet."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_lotus_pond.tres
msgid "Offer her a bamboo pole."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_lotus_pond.tres
msgid ""
"One of the surveyors extends her pole to the struggling woman.\n"
"\n"
"She grasps it thankfully as the group rows towards shore."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_lotus_pond.tres
msgid "Try to calm her."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_lotus_pond.tres
msgid ""
"One of the group members speaks calmly to the drowning woman.\n"
"\n"
"She instructs her to stop flailing, float on her back, and breathe in and out.\n"
"\n"
"They are able to rescue her, and she learns a valuable new skill."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_lotus_pond.tres
msgid "Drag her back onto the boat."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_lotus_pond.tres
msgid ""
"The group quickly rows the boat close to the struggling woman.\n"
"\n"
"The strongest among them reaches into the water to grab her arm, but their combined weight tips the boat to one side, spilling baskets of supplies and the freshly gathered leaves."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_many_birds.tres
msgid "The Uncountable Flock"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_many_birds.tres
msgid ""
"A few scouts break away from the group to examine the banks of a stream.\n"
"\n"
"As they approach the water, a flock of tiny white birds flies up from the reeds.\n"
"\n"
"Before they can react, more and more birds emerge, filling the air with sharp, piping calls."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_many_birds.tres
msgid "Identify the birds."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: preview_description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_many_birds.tres
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_seashore_pines.tres
msgid "Gain 2 maximum <term:inspiration>"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_many_birds.tres
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_seashore_pines.tres
msgid "Gained 2 maximum <term:inspiration>."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_many_birds.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts watch carefully as the birds fly around them.\n"
"\n"
"From their white breasts, black head markings, and sharp calls, they recognize the little birds as plovers. An auspicious omen."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_many_birds.tres
msgid "Count the birds."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_many_birds.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts try to count the birds surrounding them.\n"
"\n"
"After losing count again and again, they finally give up.\n"
"\n"
"There must be at least a thousand."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_many_birds.tres
msgid "Listen to their calls."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_many_birds.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts stay silent, listening to the birds crying over the water.\n"
"\n"
"Their voices seem chaotic at first, but in time they merge into a strangely soothing cacophony."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_many_birds.tres
msgid "Flee."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_many_birds.tres
msgid "The scouts run away, disoriented by the seemingly endless number of birds erupting from their surroundings."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_missing_rations.tres
msgid "The Missing Rations"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_missing_rations.tres
msgid ""
"When the team stops to have their meal, one of the scouts notices that half of her rice is missing from her pack.\n"
"\n"
"After a brief investigation, one of the younger team members admits that he had forgotten to pack his rations and ate hers instead during yesterday's meal.\n"
"\n"
"The woman is furious and threatening to beat up the thief."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_missing_rations.tres
msgid "Settle for an apology."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_missing_rations.tres
msgid "The rest of the team intervenes to break up the argument. They convince the victim to empathize with the inexperienced youth, and she eventually settles for a sincere apology, agreeing to forgive the poor fool."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_missing_rations.tres
msgid "Make the thief carry her pack."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_missing_rations.tres
msgid "The young scout has no choice but to accept the extra burden, but the rift remains unhealed, and is sure to lead to trouble down the road."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_missing_rations.tres
msgid "Compensate her from others' rations."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_missing_rations.tres
msgid "The rest of the survey team offers to share their rations as compensation, and the woman's anger dissipates by the time she finishes the meal."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_missing_rations.tres
msgid "Let her have revenge."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_missing_rations.tres
msgid "The woman lands one kick on the thief's behind and walks away. It isn't enough to cause damage, but enough to leave a traumatic memory."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_misty_lake.tres
msgid "The Foggy Lake"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_misty_lake.tres
msgid ""
"A thick fog has rolled in as the team is crossing a lake. It won't be long before the shores are lost in the whiteout.\n"
"\n"
"The scouts are worried that they will end up rowing in circles if they don't take countermeasures."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_misty_lake.tres
msgid "Measure the depth to navigate."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_misty_lake.tres
msgid "One of the scouts ties a mallet to a rope and drops it into the water. By repeating this as the group rows around the lake, they are able to find the direction in which the depth decreases, and make their way to shore."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_misty_lake.tres
msgid "Judge direction by a trailing string."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_misty_lake.tres
msgid "A scout ties a long string to the stern and watches it as the others row. By keeping the trailing string straight, the group ensures that they are rowing in a straight line, and they eventually make their way to the shore."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_misty_lake.tres
msgid "Head towards animal sounds."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_misty_lake.tres
msgid "The surveyors listen carefully. They are quickly able to determine the direction from which frog croaks the loudest and find their way to shore."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_misty_lake.tres
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_storm.tres
msgid "Wait it out."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_misty_lake.tres
msgid "The scouts decide to wait out the fog. They spend the night in the boat, and by noon the next day find the fog has lifted, letting them row safely to the distant shore."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_mudslide.tres
msgid "The Mudslide"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_mudslide.tres
msgid ""
"A recent landslide has deposited a massive pile of loose earth and uprooted shrubbery across the pass.\n"
"\n"
"The mud has already settled, but it's still a major obstacle."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_mudslide.tres
msgid "Clear the path."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_mudslide.tres
msgid "The surveyors clear the mud slowly and methodically, careful to not trigger any further slides."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_mudslide.tres
msgid "Scramble over the top."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_mudslide.tres
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_rain_shelter.tres
msgid "Chance of <term:inspiration> loss"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_mudslide.tres
msgid "The scramble quickly descends into chaos, with the scouts constantly slipping and sliding. By the time everyone gets across, there are more than a few scraped knees and spilled packs."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_mudslide.tres
msgid "Build a causeway over it."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_mudslide.tres
msgid "The surveyors lay logs over the mud and pack the gaps with smaller branches until the mud is barely visible underneath. They get across safely, and the causeway will help the rest of the expedition once they catch up."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_mudslide.tres
msgid "Try a different route."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_mudslide.tres
msgid "The survey team gives up and backtracks out of the pass. That's a whole day wasted."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_ocean_cliff.tres
msgid "The Coastal Route"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_ocean_cliff.tres
msgid ""
"The group comes upon a part of the coast where tall cliffs rise above the sea.\n"
"\n"
"They could try walking along the narrow ledge at the bottom of the cliff, but they risk falling in and getting swept away by the waves."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_ocean_cliff.tres
msgid "Hug the cliff face."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_ocean_cliff.tres
msgid "The team presses flat against the rock and slowly shuffles across. Unfortunately, just as most of them reach the other side, one scout slips and falls into the sea. He is eventually rescued, but not before suffering minor injuries."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_ocean_cliff.tres
msgid "Hammer handholds into the rock."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_ocean_cliff.tres
msgid "One scout leads the way, hammering stakes into cracks in the rock for others to use as handholds. It is slow work, but eventually everyone makes it across safely."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_ocean_cliff.tres
msgid "Make a rope team."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_ocean_cliff.tres
msgid "The scouts attach themselves to one long rope and shuffle across. Whenever one of them loses their footing, the others brace themselves to keep their teammate from falling, and everyone makes it across safely."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_ocean_cliff.tres
msgid "Hike up to the top of the cliff."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_ocean_cliff.tres
msgid "The safe hike up to the top takes a whole day, but completely avoids the treacherous ledges, ensuring that no one gets hurt."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_pace_setter.tres
msgid "The Pace Setter"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_pace_setter.tres
msgid ""
"A naturally athletic surveyor has taken the lead and is setting a blistering pace, completely oblivious to the fact that half the team is panting and struggling to keep up.\n"
"\n"
"When asked to slow down, he argues that moving fast will save them days of travel."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_pace_setter.tres
msgid "Enforce a slower pace."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_pace_setter.tres
msgid "The team convinces the fast walker to slow down and stay with the group. He reluctantly complies, but keeps accusing his teammates of being weak and unfit for the mission."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_pace_setter.tres
msgid "Rotate the lead position."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_pace_setter.tres
msgid "The scouts agree to take turns walking in the lead, naturally evening out the pace. When a slow person is leading, the fast walker keeps running ahead and coming back, unable to restrain himself."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_pace_setter.tres
msgid "Let him carry a heavier load."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_pace_setter.tres
msgid "The athletic scout refuses, complaining that such an arrangement wouldn't be fair. The other scouts try to convince him for a while, but eventually grow tired of the argument and let it go."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_pace_setter.tres
msgid "Keep the faster pace."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_pace_setter.tres
msgid "The fast walker convinces the rest of the group to keep pace. The result is a tired, unhappy team prone to making mistakes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_path_ahead.tres
msgid "The Path Ahead"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_path_ahead.tres
msgid ""
"The team has gotten into an argument trying to decide where to go next.\n"
"\n"
"Three of the scouts disagree, each pointing in a different direction and completely refusing to budge."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_path_ahead.tres
msgid "Appeal to their camaraderie."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_path_ahead.tres
msgid "The other scouts convince the arguers that harmony among the team is more important than choosing an optimal path, and eventually two of them back down."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_path_ahead.tres
msgid "Resolve it over a meal."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_path_ahead.tres
msgid "The team decides that arguments are best resolved over a meal and a drink. With their bellies full, the three scouts are a lot less prone to arguments."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_path_ahead.tres
msgid "Resolve it with logic."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_path_ahead.tres
msgid "The team asks each of the scouts to outline their reasons, and after a brief debate, they end up finding a new choice that they all agree on."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_path_ahead.tres
msgid "Leave it up to chance."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_path_ahead.tres
msgid "The team convinces the scouts to draw lots. They follow the path of the one who drew the 正 glyph."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_rain_shelter.tres
msgid "Caught in the Rain"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_rain_shelter.tres
msgid ""
"A sudden downpour catches the survey team on an exposed ridge.\n"
"\n"
"Just ahead is a small pine grove, full of natural hollows.\n"
"\n"
"They seem perfect for sheltering a small group, but the ground is strewn with animal bones and bits of hide."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_rain_shelter.tres
msgid "Shelter in the hollows."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_rain_shelter.tres
msgid "Soon after the team takes shelter, several wolves show up. The scouts raise a racket and posture wildly, roaring and jumping. The wolves observe the display for some time, but eventually decide that the strange creatures are not worth attacking. Nonetheless, the entire team is shaken by the experience."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_rain_shelter.tres
msgid "Construct lean-tos."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_rain_shelter.tres
msgid "Instead of sheltering in what are clearly animal dens, the scouts construct simple lean-tos. Enough to shelter from the rain, even if they won't last much longer."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_rain_shelter.tres
msgid "Brave the rain."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_rain_shelter.tres
msgid "The scouts press on through the miserable weather. At least they are safe from the wildlife."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_rest_hill.tres
msgid "The Restful Hill"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_rest_hill.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts have climbed a gently sloping hill, where a light breeze stirs the leaves and the morning sun warms their faces. The smell of crushed pine needles fills the air, and the soft grass looks inviting.\n"
"\n"
"The day has only just begun, but this seems like a perfect place to rest."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_rest_hill.tres
msgid "Take a nap."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_rest_hill.tres
msgid "Gain <term:bonus.beauty> or lose <term:inspiration>"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_rest_hill.tres
msgid ""
"The surveyors stretch out in the sun and fall asleep. \n"
"\n"
"When they awake, the trees are casting long shadows across their faces in the afternoon sun.\n"
"\n"
"A herd of deer is grazing only steps away from them. When one of the scouts rises, the whole herd takes off in a rush."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_rest_hill.tres
msgid "Explore the grove."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_rest_hill.tres
msgid ""
"The explorers walk through the little pine grove, looking for anything worth recording in their logs.\n"
"\n"
"All they find is a beehive in a fallen log."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_rest_hill.tres
msgid "Rest briefly."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_rest_hill.tres
msgid ""
"The explorers stop for a brief rest, relaxing in the sun.\n"
"\n"
"Someone plays a flute. A few people sketch the landscape. The rest just sit down, taking in the beautiful view."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_rest_hill.tres
msgid "Keep hiking."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_rest_hill.tres
msgid ""
"The group decides to move on, not wanting to waste any time.\n"
"\n"
"As they march past the grove, a few surveyors can't help but look back at the sunny hill."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_river_bridge.tres
msgid "The Old Bridge"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_river_bridge.tres
msgid ""
"As the scouts travel along the riverbank, they come across a beautiful old bridge spanning the quiet water.\n"
"\n"
"Moss clings to the railing, and years of rain and sun have weathered the boards. Though decayed now, it is clear that it was once made with great care."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_river_bridge.tres
msgid "Repair the bridge."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_river_bridge.tres
msgid ""
"The group sets out to fix the crumbling beams.\n"
"\n"
"They carefully remove the rotten boards, then chop down timber to fashion replacements. By the end of the day, the bridge is sturdy again.\n"
"\n"
"The scouts take pride in having helped preserve the work of the unknown builders."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_river_bridge.tres
msgid "Cross it."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_river_bridge.tres
msgid "<term:bonus.adventure> or <term:card.soak>"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_river_bridge.tres
msgid ""
"The surveyors attempt to cross the bridge, testing each board carefully before stepping down.\n"
"\n"
"On the other side, they find crumbling walls which must have once surrounded a grove. The space is now choked with weeds, but the old trees still grow in unnaturally straight rows.\n"
"\n"
"It is clear that this place was once special."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_river_bridge.tres
msgid "Sketch it."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_river_bridge.tres
msgid ""
"Several scouts sketch the peaceful scene.\n"
"\n"
"One focuses on the graceful curve of the bridge.\n"
"\n"
"Another sketches the weathered beams and moss in detail."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_river_bridge.tres
msgid "Leave it undisturbed. "
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_river_bridge.tres
msgid "The group pauses by the bridge, appreciating the beautiful artisanship and unwilling to risk damaging it."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_ruined_castle.tres
msgid "The Fort in the Wastes"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_ruined_castle.tres
msgid ""
"The surveyors are trudging through the wasteland when they spot a crumbling fort in the distance.\n"
"\n"
"By the time they reach it, night has fallen.\n"
"\n"
"The wind picks up as they draw near, whistling through the cracks in the walls, and drowning out the thunder rumbling in the distance."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_ruined_castle.tres
msgid "Search for treasure."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_ruined_castle.tres
msgid "With torches lit, the scouts stumble through the halls and storerooms, but it appears that the castle had been looted long ago. All they find are empty chests, shattered remnants of pottery, and a few crows that scatter off into the darkness."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_ruined_castle.tres
msgid "Investigate the inner rooms."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_ruined_castle.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts explore deep into the fort until they reach a cellar that must have served as a workshop. Minute metal tools are stored on marble shelves, and metal boxes are stacked in the corner, not rusted despite the passage of centuries.\n"
"\n"
"Most of the boxes contain little more than dust, but one seems to have been sealed particularly well. It contains sheets of cracked, yellowed paper, with writing in a language unlike any the scouts had seen before. One of the sheets, instead of writing, contains schematics for some sort of complicated machinery."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_ruined_castle.tres
msgid "Climb the keep."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_ruined_castle.tres
msgid "The explorers climb the worn stone stairs to the top of the fort. From the roof, they watch the storm passing through the barren wasteland. As the lightning flashes, they catch glimpses of iron wrecks littering the horizon."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_ruined_castle.tres
msgid "Take shelter in the entryway."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_ruined_castle.tres
msgid "The team decides to spend the night by the entrance, afraid to explore deeper. The place has an odd, eerie feeling in the darkness, with the approaching storm."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sandal.tres
msgid "The Broken Sandal"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sandal.tres
msgid ""
"One of the scouts had accidentally torn the strap of her sandal and, out of embarrassment, tried to hide it.\n"
"\n"
"Now she is limping and slowing the pace of the group.\n"
"\n"
"The team is frustrated that the scout hid the problem, while the scout is defensive about not wanting to be seen as a burden."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sandal.tres
msgid "Repair the sandal."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sandal.tres
msgid "One of the other scouts uses some thread to repair the sandal, leaving it as good as new. The injury could have been easily avoided if the problem hadn't been hidden."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sandal.tres
msgid "Take turns with the good sandals."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sandal.tres
msgid "The group decides to take turns walking without sandals, so the pain is distributed more evenly. Although the injured scout is still limping, at least she is no longer ashamed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sandal.tres
msgid "Use an ointment."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sandal.tres
msgid "One of the scouts digs out an ointment from her pack, and helps her injured teammate apply it. The medicine doesn't heal the sprain outright, but it certainly eases the pain."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sandal.tres
msgid "Let the injured woman rest."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sandal.tres
msgid "The group halts to let their teammate rest her feet. Unfortunately she had already pushed herself too hard, and she will probably keep limping until she visits a healer and takes proper rest at home."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_scary_climb.tres
msgid "The Anxious Descent"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_scary_climb.tres
msgid ""
"The sun is setting behind the rocky peaks as the survey team makes its way down an ancient mountain path. The trail is steep and narrow, making for a daunting descent.\n"
"\n"
"As the evening mist surrounds them, they can just barely make out the shadowy pine forest below.\n"
"\n"
"Suddenly, a scout looks over the edge and freezes in fear, overwhelmed by the sheer drop."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_scary_climb.tres
msgid "Calm her down."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_scary_climb.tres
msgid ""
"The two scouts closest to the frightened woman speak soothingly to her.\n"
"\n"
"They remove her pack and, holding her hands, walk down the rest of the slope together."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_scary_climb.tres
msgid "Carry her."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_scary_climb.tres
msgid ""
"The two scouts closest to the frightened woman remove her pack and gently pick her up. \n"
"\n"
"The group moves slower than before, but they still complete their descent by nightfall.\n"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_scary_climb.tres
msgid "Use a blindfold."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_scary_climb.tres
msgid ""
"A scout comes up with the bright idea of tying a blindfold around the woman's head, to spare her the frightening sight.\n"
"\n"
"Miraculously, she manages to complete the descent safely."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_scary_climb.tres
msgid "None of the scouts is willing to offer concrete help. They stand around and wait, hoping the woman will recover by herself. She does, eventually."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_seashore_pines.tres
msgid "The Gnarled Pines"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_seashore_pines.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts are gathering reeds when they pass a scattered grove of gnarled pines.\n"
"\n"
"Over the years, the harsh coastal winds have twisted the branches into wild shapes, and the sea spray has crusted the bark with layers of salt."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_seashore_pines.tres
msgid "Collect pine resin."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_seashore_pines.tres
msgid ""
"The surveyors scrape resin from the trunk, the thick, gummy material sticking to their hands.\n"
"\n"
"It will prove useful for starting fires or repairing packs."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_seashore_pines.tres
msgid "Gather kindling."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_seashore_pines.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts gather the dry twigs and the dead branches that have fallen from the trees.\n"
"\n"
"They assemble these into a large bonfire on the beach, and stay late into the night reminiscing about all the adventures they have experienced over their lifetimes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_seashore_pines.tres
msgid "Sketch the pines."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_seashore_pines.tres
msgid "While most of the scouts continue gathering reeds, an artist among them puts brush to paper and paints a passable depiction of the coast with its gnarled pines standing out against the clear sunset sky."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_seashore_pines.tres
msgid "Rest by the pines."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_seashore_pines.tres
msgid ""
"The surveyors rest against the sturdy trunks and let the sun wash over their faces.\n"
"\n"
"The rush of sea wind and salt spray is invigorating."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_arch.tres
msgid "The Seashore Arch"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_arch.tres
msgid ""
"The survey team has stopped under a naturally formed stone arch rising above the seashore. As they are busy mapping the coastline, a voice comes calling from above.\n"
"\n"
"One of the scouts has climbed the arch to win a bet, and is now regretting that decision. His triumphant smile faded the moment he tried to descend. It seems climbing down the slick rocks is proving a lot more difficult than getting to the top."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_arch.tres
msgid "Use rope."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_arch.tres
msgid ""
"The whole group works together, tying a long rope into knots, and throwing it up to the stranded scout.\n"
"\n"
"He ties the rope around his waist, secures it to a large boulder, then uses the knots as footholds to descend safely."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_arch.tres
msgid "Use a tree trunk."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_arch.tres
msgid ""
"The group works together, picking up a large dead tree they find lying in the sand and dragging it to the arch.\n"
"\n"
"The stranded scout descends safely, using branches as footholds."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_arch.tres
msgid "Dare him to jump."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_arch.tres
msgid ""
"Knowing their friend to be a strong swimmer, the other scouts encourage him to jump into the water. \n"
"\n"
"Slightly embarrassed, the stranded scout glances at the smiling faces of his comrades then jumps into the water with a splash, emerging unharmed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_arch.tres
msgid "Let him deal with it."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_arch.tres
msgid ""
"The scout makes it two thirds of the way down before his foot slips on the wet rocks and he comes hurtling down.\n"
"\n"
"He is only a little bruised, but he will remember this fall for a while."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_caves.tres
msgid "The Sea Caves"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_caves.tres
msgid ""
"As the scouts are walking along the shore, they approach a huge cave.\n"
"\n"
"Waves crash unceasingly into the entrance, filling the main chamber with a layer of seawater.\n"
"\n"
"Old World legends claim such caves used to be inhabited by many-headed dragons who ruled the seas."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_caves.tres
msgid "Examine the main chamber."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_caves.tres
msgid "A chance of one of five relics"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_caves.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts spread out, searching the main chamber.\n"
"\n"
"They quickly find an alcove carved into the wall. The inscription above it has long since eroded, but a relic still lies intact on a raised dais."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_caves.tres
msgid "Delve deep into the cave."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_caves.tres
msgid "Get one of four relics"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_caves.tres
msgid ""
"The survey team ties a rope to a nearby rock and slowly descends into the depths.\n"
"\n"
"Their torches are too smoky to keep lit in the narrow tunnel, so they navigate mostly by touch.\n"
"\n"
"The bottom of the shaft is filled with rubble, some of which they haul back up.\n"
"\n"
"Among the rocks is a relic."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_caves.tres
msgid "Pray to the dragon spirit."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_caves.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts kneel by the entrance, their backs exposed to the waves.\n"
"\n"
"They clap their hands and each whispers an old prayer.\n"
"\n"
"Perhaps the dragon will favor this expedition."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_caves.tres
msgid "Ignore the cave."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_caves.tres
msgid "The scouts decide that delving into a deep, slippery cave is too much of a risk, and continue on their way."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_storm.tres
msgid "The Stormy Sea"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_storm.tres
msgid ""
"The survey team is camping by the seashore when they are woken up by a fierce gale.\n"
"\n"
"It howls, ripping through their tents and blowing out their fire. The nearby pines groan as huge waves crash against the rocks."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_storm.tres
msgid "Make a palisade."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_storm.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts work together to tie driftwood into a makeshift palisade and take shelter behind it.\n"
"\n"
"It doesn't take long for the waves to shatter their work in an explosion of splinters.\n"
"\n"
"The scouts take the hint and rush away from the shore, but by then several are already injured."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_storm.tres
msgid "Rush inland."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_storm.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts abandon their campsite and rush away from the shore.\n"
"\n"
"They find a sheltered ditch, where they lie flat and watch in terror as trees crash around them.\n"
"\n"
"By morning, they are thoroughly soaked, but at least they are safe."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_storm.tres
msgid "Hide behind a rock."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_storm.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts head to the large boulders strewn across the beach and shelter behind the largest one they can find. \n"
"\n"
"The boulder blocks the wind and the waves, but they spend the rest of the night shivering."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_storm.tres
msgid "<related_term:card.wound><related_term:card.soak><related_term:card.frozen>Get hurt, soaked, and shivering"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_storm.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts stay in their tents and wait out the storm. They pray to the Enlightened One, yet the wind continues to rage.\n"
"\n"
"A wave tears one tent from its stakes, and carries away their packs.\n"
"\n"
"Another fells a tree, which lands next to the scouts, its sharp branches scratching several of them.\n"
"\n"
"By morning, they are hurt, soaked, and shivering, but grateful to have survived."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_sunrise.tres
msgid "The Serene Sunrise"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_sunrise.tres
msgid ""
"The sea is calm this morning, the grey rocks painted a coral red by the magnificent sunrise.\n"
"\n"
"The scouts contemplate the scene, taking in the gentle waves lapping against the shore and the grass-covered hills further ahead."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_sunrise.tres
msgid "Admire the view."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_sunrise.tres
msgid ""
"The surveyors stay for a while to breathe in the briny scent of seaweed and marvel at the divine beauty of the landscape.\n"
"\n"
"They watch the rocks turn orange, then yellow as the sun rises higher and higher. Seagull calls reach them from beyond the rocks, as the sea spray leaves little crystals of salt on their skin."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_sunrise.tres
msgid "Gather seashells."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_sunrise.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts walk along the shoreline as the sun rises.\n"
"\n"
"This shore has not seen people for a long, long time, and the ground is covered in a layer of seashells, each a different shape.\n"
"\n"
"They take a colorful scallop shell with them as a memento."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_sunrise.tres
msgid "Climb the rocks."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_sunrise.tres
msgid "A few of the scouts venture out onto the rocks. It is a dangerous climb, but the view from above is magnificent, revealing a honeycomb of tide pools, teeming with sea life."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_sunrise.tres
msgid "Move on."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_sea_sunrise.tres
msgid "The group decides to continue along their route without stopping."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_shard_edge.tres
msgid "The White Dog"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_shard_edge.tres
msgid ""
"The survey team is approaching the edge of a shard one evening, as the setting sun sets the Cloud Sea on fire, turning it the color of ripe persimmons. Clouds are gathering around their feet, obscuring the path ahead.\n"
"\n"
"As they stop to refresh themselves by a tiny waterfall, a patch of fog detaches from the clouds further up the path and resolves into the shape of a white dog.\n"
"\n"
"Its fur blends into the floating wisps and every few moments it disappears, only to reappear farther ahead on the path."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_shard_edge.tres
msgid "Call out to the dog."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_shard_edge.tres
msgid ""
"One of the scouts calls out softly to the animal.\n"
"\n"
"For a moment the dog looks back at the group with intelligent eyes, then quickly vanishes back into the clouds."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_shard_edge.tres
msgid "Follow the dog."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_shard_edge.tres
msgid ""
"Two scouts break apart from the rest of the group and cautiously approach the animal.\n"
"\n"
"The dog looks back at them, then continues walking ahead.\n"
"\n"
"A few minutes later, they see the familiar vermilion of a gate peek out from the cloud, and a moment later they watch the dog run through the gate and disappear."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_shard_edge.tres
msgid "Observe from a distance."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_shard_edge.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts take a break and sit down to watch the animal. The dog likewise settles down, directing its gaze towards the setting sun. They spend the time in silence, watching the sun sink lower and lower, until it finally disappears below the horizon.\n"
"\n"
"As the team finally begins to make camp, they realize that the dog had vanished into the night."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_shard_edge.tres
msgid "Ignore the dog."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_shard_edge.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts shrug at the strange sight, but continue their hike without investigating further.\n"
"\n"
"The dog follows briefly, then disappears, never to be seen again.\n"
"\n"
"The strange encounter becomes a topic of conversation as the explorers sit around the campfire, though, each surveyor offering a different explanation for the dog's origin."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_shard_edge_fog.tres
msgid "Distant Shards"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_shard_edge_fog.tres
msgid ""
"The air is cold when the scouts reach the edge of the shard.\n"
"\n"
"The wind howls against them, as if telling them to stay away from the dangerous edge, but they look on in wonder.\n"
"\n"
"The Cloud Sea stretches into the horizon, scattered shards peeking through the clouds ahead. On one of them rises a staggeringly tall mountain."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_shard_edge_fog.tres
msgid "Sketch the scene."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: preview_description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_shard_edge_fog.tres
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_winter_wonderland.tres
msgid "Gain 3 maximum <term:inspiration>"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_shard_edge_fog.tres
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_winter_wonderland.tres
msgid "Gained 3 maximum <term:inspiration>."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_shard_edge_fog.tres
msgid ""
"One of the surveyors, an artist, sketches the scene.\n"
"\n"
"She takes liberties with the colors, painting the clouds a pale azure and giving the distant mountain a purple hue, with a blush of rose at the peak.\n"
"\n"
"The group crowds around her, admiring her work just as much as the scene itself."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_shard_edge_fog.tres
msgid "Build a marker."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_shard_edge_fog.tres
msgid ""
"The explorers erect a stone cairn at the very edge of the shard.\n"
"\n"
"Once they position the last stone into place, they pause to thank the Enlightened One for the success of their journey thus far."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_shard_edge_fog.tres
msgid "Camp here."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_shard_edge_fog.tres
msgid ""
"The group decides to camp at the edge.\n"
"\n"
"They are unusually somber as they gather around the fire for their meal, contemplating the distant shards.\n"
"\n"
"As they lie down for the night, they are lulled to sleep by the howling wind."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_shard_edge_fog.tres
msgid "Shout into the void."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_shard_edge_fog.tres
msgid ""
"One of the scouts yells into the distance with all his might.\n"
"\n"
"Instead of the echo he expects, he hears his voice muted, swallowed by the dense clouds below."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_slippery_hill.tres
msgid "The Slick Slope Slide"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_slippery_hill.tres
msgid ""
"The surveyors grumble as they trudge through a pass. It has been raining for two days in a row, and the slopes have turned slick with mud. \n"
"\n"
"Most of the group has made their way down a steep incline when they hear a yelp from above.\n"
"\n"
"A scout, struggling to lift her pack, has suddenly lost her footing and is now hurtling down the slope."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_slippery_hill.tres
msgid "Cling to a rock."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_slippery_hill.tres
msgid ""
"The scout spots a large boulder protruding from the slope.\n"
"\n"
"She reaches out and grabs it tightly, safely stopping her slide."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_slippery_hill.tres
msgid "Aim for the bushes."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_slippery_hill.tres
msgid "<term:card.poison> or choice of plant <term_lower:glyph>s"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_slippery_hill.tres
msgid ""
"The scout spots a clump of shrubs halfway down the slope. She steers herself towards them, hoping to gently break her fall.\n"
"\n"
"She crashes into the dense bushes, the springy branches softening her landing."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_slippery_hill.tres
msgid "Roll."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_slippery_hill.tres
msgid ""
"The scout makes an instant decision to stretch out her limbs and roll sideways down the grassy slope.\n"
"\n"
"As she rolls, her body picks up speed and she is unable to slow down.\n"
"\n"
"She arrives at the bottom of the hill within seconds, muddy, dizzy, but laughing."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_slippery_hill.tres
msgid "Embrace the fall."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_slippery_hill.tres
msgid ""
"The surveyor accepts that she can't stop now.\n"
"\n"
"She relaxes her limbs, leans backward, and coasts on her back down the muddy grass.\n"
"\n"
"She arrives at the bottom with a torn robe and a serene smile."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_snowy_castle.tres
msgid "The Highland Fort"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_snowy_castle.tres
msgid ""
"An unexpected sight appears before the scouts one morning. An old fort stands at a snowy peak, its broad eaves laden with a thick covering of snow.\n"
"\n"
"Inside the lavish veranda hang little golden ornaments, their luster hidden by a thick layer of dust.\n"
"\n"
"Stairs lead to a second level, where a heavy sword rests on a raised pedestal, a large blue gemstone embedded in its hilt."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_snowy_castle.tres
msgid "Take the ornaments."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_snowy_castle.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts fill their satchels with golden treasure, snatching every trinket within their reach.\n"
"\n"
"The next day the group finds two of their teammates missing, along with all the gold."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_snowy_castle.tres
msgid "Take the sword."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_snowy_castle.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts rush towards the stairs, eyes set on the shiny weapon.\n"
"\n"
"As three of them crowd onto the narrow steps, the planks finally give way with a tired groan, the stairs suddenly collapsing.\n"
"\n"
"Several people are injured, and the sword remains out of reach."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_snowy_castle.tres
msgid "Search the basement."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_snowy_castle.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts, with lanterns held aloft, descend into the stone basement.\n"
"\n"
"Among the cobwebs and dust, they find a yellowed piece of paper. Its edges are weathered and eaten by worms, but it is still recognizable as a portrait.\n"
"\n"
"It depicts a richly dressed man in a palanquin, surrounded by servants."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_snowy_castle.tres
msgid "Clear the dust."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_snowy_castle.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts decide to pay their respects to the old ruins.\n"
"\n"
"They use sticks and leaves to fashion brooms, and sweep the dust off the steps, walls, and ornaments, before leaving the fort in peace."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_statued_ledges.tres
msgid "The Statued Ledges"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_statued_ledges.tres
msgid ""
"The team comes up to a jagged cliff. On its ledges are dozens of little statues, their features worn smooth by time.\n"
"\n"
"Most of the scouts agree that this part of the cliff face is by far the easiest to climb, but one objects, afraid to disturb the spirits that surely inhabit these statues."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_statued_ledges.tres
msgid "Scramble up together."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_statued_ledges.tres
msgid "Chance of <term:card.guilt>"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_statued_ledges.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts scramble up the cliff, the ledges acting as convenient hand-holds.\n"
"\n"
"Before they are halfway up, one of them knocks a statue off its ledge and watches as it shatters at the bottom.\n"
"\n"
"He is now wracked with guilt for not listening to his teammate."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_statued_ledges.tres
msgid "Send a scout to secure a rope."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_statued_ledges.tres
msgid ""
"To minimize the chance of damaging the statues, the team sends only one person up, equipped with a long rope.\n"
"\n"
"Once at the top, she ties the rope to a boulder and dangles it down, letting the rest of the team climb up safely."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_statued_ledges.tres
msgid "Split the party."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_statued_ledges.tres
msgid ""
"The majority refuses to budge, and suggests that the objector make his own way.\n"
"\n"
"He catches up days later. He is safe, but trust among the group has been seriously eroded."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_statued_ledges.tres
msgid "Find another route."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_statued_ledges.tres
msgid "The team spends days finding a path that bypasses the cliff, dipping dangerously low into their supplies."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_stream_crossing.tres
msgid "Stream Crossing"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_stream_crossing.tres
msgid ""
"The team approaches a creek that has swelled into a wide stream rushing across the landscape.\n"
"\n"
"The water is chest-high and moving at a dangerous speed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_stream_crossing.tres
msgid "Swim across."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_stream_crossing.tres
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_swamp_bridge.tres
msgid "Chance of <term:bonus.safety> loss"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_stream_crossing.tres
msgid "Most of the surveyors manage to swim over the stream, but a few get carried downstream, emerging bruised, soaked and shivering."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_stream_crossing.tres
msgid "Scout for a narrow point."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_stream_crossing.tres
msgid "It takes an hour of searching, but the scouts find a safe fallen log upstream."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_stream_crossing.tres
msgid "Build a makeshift bridge."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_stream_crossing.tres
msgid "The team lays a few logs across and everyone manages to cross safely. The bridge will serve the rest of the expedition when it reaches the stream."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_stream_crossing.tres
msgid "Wade through the current."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_stream_crossing.tres
msgid "The team manages to cross the stream, but now they are soaked and shivering."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_swamp_boat.tres
msgid "The Sinking Boat"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_swamp_boat.tres
msgid ""
"As the scouts row down a stream winding its way through the swamp, one of their boats springs a leak.\n"
"\n"
"As water begins to flood the bottom of the boat, they scramble to find the source and quickly discover a small hole in the hull."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_swamp_boat.tres
msgid "Plug the hole."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_swamp_boat.tres
msgid ""
"One of the scouts reacts quickly, shedding his robe and wedging the cloth into the hole.\n"
"\n"
"This keeps the boat afloat long enough to reach the shore, where the rest of the survey team helps them fashion a more permanent wooden plug."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_swamp_boat.tres
msgid "Get into another boat."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_swamp_boat.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts call to their teammates in the nearest boat, who row over as quickly as they can. They all crowd into one boat, which becomes dangerously weighed down by the extra passengers.\n"
"\n"
"Together, they watch as the leaking boat is swallowed by the swamp."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_swamp_boat.tres
msgid "Row to land."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_swamp_boat.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts quickly row to a nearby clump of thickly growing reeds. They disembark just as the boat finally sinks.\n"
"\n"
"They find themselves knee-deep in the oozing muck, where they stay, cursing their fate, until the other boats catch up."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_swamp_boat.tres
msgid "Abandon the boat."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_swamp_boat.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts jump overboard, scattering in all directions.\n"
"\n"
"Some of them, unable to swim, begin to panic until they realize that the water is only chest-deep."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_swamp_bridge.tres
msgid "The Biting Swarm"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_swamp_bridge.tres
msgid ""
"The survey team has reached a particularly treacherous swamp.\n"
"\n"
"In order to prepare for the rest of the expedition, they have spent several days constructing a narrow bridge raised on bamboo stilts above the muck.\n"
"\n"
"As they are nearing the end of their construction, a thick swarm of biting insects descends on the area, making the work unbearable."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_swamp_bridge.tres
msgid "Try to finish quickly."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_swamp_bridge.tres
msgid "Banish insects with fragrant herbs."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_swamp_bridge.tres
msgid ""
"It turns out that one of the scouts had prepared for this situation. She takes out a bundle of fragrant herbs and instructs the group to rub them on their skin.\n"
"\n"
"Within minutes, the swarm thins as the insects flee the potent smell, and the team is able to finish their work in peace."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_swamp_bridge.tres
msgid "Use mud to protect skin."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_swamp_bridge.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts slather mud on their exposed skin, successfully protecting themselves from insect bites.\n"
"\n"
"However, by the time they are done, the whole group is walking in a cloud of musty stench and stale sweat."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_swamp_bridge.tres
msgid "Ward insects off with torches."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_swamp_bridge.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts light torches, hoping to fend off the swarm.\n"
"\n"
"To their surprise, this only seems to attract the insects, and by the time the work is finished everyone is covered in dozens of bug bites."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tanuki_canyon.tres
msgid "The Haunted Canyon"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tanuki_canyon.tres
msgid ""
"Darkness is gathering between the canyon walls. The scouts light their torches and press on, hoping to find shelter soon, or cross the canyon before night falls.\n"
"\n"
"They have heard tales of spirits haunting such canyons, carving messages on the walls and driving people mad.\n"
"\n"
"Suddenly the light from their torches catches the gleam of a pair of eyes, low to the ground.\n"
"\n"
"Sitting in the middle of the path is a lone tanuki."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tanuki_canyon.tres
msgid "Watch closely."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tanuki_canyon.tres
msgid "Gain or lose <term:bonus.safety>"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tanuki_canyon.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts watch the critter as it stares back at them with an unflinching gaze.\n"
"\n"
"Eventually it gets up and walks away, then looks back at the group as if expecting them to follow.\n"
"\n"
"The tanuki leads them off the path through a narrow passage, which ends in a small cave, safe from the elements.\n"
"\n"
"As they prepare their camp, the tanuki skitters off into the dark."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tanuki_canyon.tres
msgid "Honor the spirit."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tanuki_canyon.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts and the tanuki regard each other for a long moment.\n"
"\n"
"Unsure whether it's a simple critter or something stranger, the scouts offer it a deep, long bow.\n"
"\n"
"When they look up, the tanuki is gone."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tanuki_canyon.tres
msgid "Offer food."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tanuki_canyon.tres
msgid ""
"One of the scouts kneels down and places a rice ball on the ground. The tanuki sniffs cautiously, then approaches, greedily eating the morsel.\n"
"\n"
"Once its meal is finished, the tanuki scampers away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tanuki_canyon.tres
msgid "Continue on."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tanuki_canyon.tres
msgid "The scouts don't let fear delay them, and ignore the critter, who scampers halfway up a leaning tree trunk and watches them pass."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tigers.tres
msgid "The Tigers"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tigers.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts begin to notice an unusual silence in the air. The birds and insects have suddenly grown quiet.\n"
"\n"
"As they press forward, a tigress emerges through the tall grass with three nearly-grown cubs behind her. She growls, watching the surveyors intently."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tigers.tres
msgid "Throw provisions at the tigers."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tigers.tres
msgid ""
"One of the scouts removes some food from his pack and hurls it towards the tigers' feet.\n"
"\n"
"The cubs step forward, sniffing, to investigate, and the group slowly retreats.\n"
"\n"
"The tigress follows them for a distance, waiting for more food, but eventually gives up, returning to her cubs."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tigers.tres
msgid "Light a torch."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tigers.tres
msgid ""
"The explorers quickly light their torches. The tigers, wary, back up.\n"
"\n"
"One scout, her hands trembling, accidentally drops hers.\n"
"\n"
"The dry grass begins to smoulder and the group is forced to abandon their route and race ahead of the spreading fire."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tigers.tres
msgid "Watch the tigers' behavior."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tigers.tres
msgid ""
"The group remains motionless, cautiously observing the beasts.\n"
"\n"
"One scout slowly points behind him. Lying on top of a patch of flattened grass is a fresh animal carcass. \n"
"\n"
"The group slowly moves out of the tigers' way, and are ignored as a reward."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tigers.tres
msgid "Run away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tigers.tres
msgid ""
"Panicked, the scouts run, all scattering in different directions.\n"
"\n"
"The tigress immediately pursues the slowest moving surveyor. \n"
"\n"
"He ends up injured, but is rescued when the rest of the scouts fling stones to scare the tigers away."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tranquil_bay.tres
msgid "The Tranquil Bay"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tranquil_bay.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts find themselves under a sunset sky full of pink clouds. A tranquil bay spreads before their eyes.\n"
"\n"
"Two of the surveyors get into a small boat and row towards a tiny pine-covered tidal islet, where a weathered gate stands solemnly in the cooling sand.\n"
"\n"
"As they draw nearer, they notice a small wooden box hiding among the roots."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tranquil_bay.tres
msgid "Dig the box out."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tranquil_bay.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts tear up the earth, slashing at the roots with their knives.\n"
"\n"
"They eventually manage to dig the box out from among the tangled mass.\n"
"\n"
"When the lid is pried open, the scouts find jars of a sweet-smelling liquid, which shimmers golden-amber in the setting sun once poured out."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tranquil_bay.tres
msgid ""
"The surveyors dock their boat and walk onto the islet, their feet sinking into the sand.\n"
"\n"
"As they approach the gate, the woody fragrance of fresh pine fills their nostrils.\n"
"\n"
"The scouts leave a bowl of dried fruit behind the gate, content with the knowledge that they've paid their respects to the local spirits."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tranquil_bay.tres
msgid "Smash the box open."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tranquil_bay.tres
msgid ""
"Not wanting to disturb the roots of the trees, the surveyors find a large stone and strike the corner of the box.\n"
"\n"
"The wood splinters, followed by the sound of shattering clay. A sweet-smelling golden liquid oozes out, soaking into the sand."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tranquil_bay.tres
msgid "Leave the box."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tranquil_bay.tres
msgid "The surveyors paddle their boat past the tiny islet, letting the box remain undisturbed."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tree_bridge.tres
msgid "The Tree Bridge"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tree_bridge.tres
msgid ""
"As the group is walking along the edge of a ravine, they find a living tree growing on the edge, its thick, bent trunk forming a bridge across to the other side.\n"
"\n"
"Crossing it would act as a shortcut, but some of the scouts hesitate, not trusting the tree to hold their weight."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tree_bridge.tres
msgid "Reinforce the tree bridge."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tree_bridge.tres
msgid ""
"The group nails pegs to the tree trunk, and ties safety ropes around it, attaching them to nearby trees.\n"
"\n"
"Having done this, they make it across safely, but leave the tree marked and scarred."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tree_bridge.tres
msgid "Verify the trunk's sturdiness."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tree_bridge.tres
msgid ""
"The group decides to check how sturdy the tree is. They carefully try placing heavier and heavier packs on the trunk, and find it able to support everything they could pile upon it.\n"
"\n"
"In the process they notice that the bark is thicker in some areas. On closer examination, it becomes clear that at some point in the past, footholds had been carved into the trunk. Apparently they aren't the first to consider using it as a bridge."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tree_bridge.tres
msgid "Camp overnight and deliberate."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tree_bridge.tres
msgid ""
"Unable to decide which path to take, the team sets up a camp by the tree bridge.\n"
"\n"
"In the early morning, the first people to wake up are greeted with a group of woolly mountain goats all standing on the tree trunk, staring at the sleeping scouts.\n"
"\n"
"This sight is enough to convince the group of the bridge's safety, and their trust in the goats proves well-earned."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tree_bridge.tres
msgid "Take the long path."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_tree_bridge.tres
msgid "The team decides to avoid the risk and take the long path around the ravine. It is safe, but costs them extra time."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_valley_path.tres
msgid "The Valley Path"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_valley_path.tres
msgid ""
"The explorers find themselves in a narrow valley with steep, high walls. The path twists through exposed stone and small groves, occasionally opening onto patches of grass.\n"
"\n"
"The valley branches out into several nearly identical paths. The scouts worry that choosing the wrong path could strand them in a dead end, or leave the group wandering in circles."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_valley_path.tres
msgid "Climb the valley wall."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_valley_path.tres
msgid ""
"A scout scales the steep valley wall to get a better view of the landscape.\n"
"\n"
"The climb is difficult, but when he makes it to the top, he sees that one path curves toward open grassland, and the others move farther into the hills.\n"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_valley_path.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts notice the smell of damp earth and hear the sound of moving water echoing off the walls of the narrowest path.\n"
"\n"
"They decide to follow these clues and soon arrive at a bubbling spring."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_valley_path.tres
msgid "Explore separate paths."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_valley_path.tres
msgid ""
"The team sends several scouts down two different paths. \n"
"\n"
"One group finds a route out of the valley.\n"
"\n"
"The other group quickly reaches a dead end, but there they find a burrow. As they approach, an orange tail disappears into its depths."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_valley_path.tres
msgid "Choose the widest path."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: preview_description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_valley_path.tres
msgid "1 Maximum <term:inspiration>"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_valley_path.tres
msgid "Gained 1 Maximum <term:inspiration>"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_valley_path.tres
msgid ""
"The explorers decide to follow the widest path. The trail gradually becomes narrower while the walls on either side become steeper.\n"
"\n"
"Soon, the passage becomes so narrow that the sun is only shining through a thin opening in the rock above.\n"
"\n"
"By nightfall, the path finally widens again, revealing a circle of starry clear sky."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_wasteland_camp.tres
msgid "Preparing for a Storm"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_wasteland_camp.tres
msgid ""
"As evening falls and the group prepares dinner, the surveyors notice dark clouds gathering in the distance.\n"
"\n"
"Most of the team argues that they should seek shelter somewhere more secluded, but a few of the scouts think that the storm will probably pass them by."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_wasteland_camp.tres
msgid "Climb a ridge."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_wasteland_camp.tres
msgid ""
"The team decides to climb a nearby rocky ridge to scout out the weather. They watch the dark, ominous clouds drift ever closer, their tops growing taller by the minute.\n"
"\n"
"By the time the group returns to the camp to report that the storm is headed in their direction, it has already begun to rain."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_wasteland_camp.tres
msgid "Seek shelter elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_wasteland_camp.tres
msgid "The group ignores the minority who believe that the storm will miss them. They break camp and walk back the way they came, seeking shelter under rocky overhangs. Although they remain dry, the team loses valuable time and misses dinner."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_wasteland_camp.tres
msgid "Reinforce the camp."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_wasteland_camp.tres
msgid "The group decides to stay in the camp, but not to ignore the storm. They layer extra cloth over their tents, secure them with pegs, and bring the firewood inside to keep it dry. The work is tiring, but when the storm arrives, they easily withstand the worst of the wind and rain."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_wasteland_camp.tres
msgid "Ignore the clouds."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_wasteland_camp.tres
msgid "One member of the group, confident in his weather-watching abilities, assures the rest that the storm will pass far to the north. The scouts continue their meal and settle in for the night. Soon, however, the winds shift and the group wakes up to soaked supplies and dead fires."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_wasteland_wall.tres
msgid "The Endless Wall"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_wasteland_wall.tres
msgid ""
"Last night, the survey team had taken shelter from one of the violent storms that are so common in the wastelands.\n"
"\n"
"As they emerge in the morning, they are astonished to see an enormous white wall stretching across the horizon in both directions.\n"
"\n"
"It appears strangely undamaged despite the centuries it must have stood there."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_wasteland_wall.tres
msgid "Look for a way through."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_wasteland_wall.tres
msgid ""
"The explorers search the wall for cracks or gates.\n"
"\n"
"By sunset, they discover a tiny metal door that leads to a short tunnel inside the wall. Inside, they can see a cross-section of the wall: a layer of thick stone, followed by a layer of an odd, dull metal covered in white dust, and finally a thick layer of packed earth.\n"
"\n"
"The tunnel ends abruptly, without an exit, so the scouts turn back, but they pick up a chunk of the odd metal, finding it surprisingly heavy."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_wasteland_wall.tres
msgid "Climb the wall."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_wasteland_wall.tres
msgid ""
"Several surveyors reach the top of the wall after a prolonged struggle.\n"
"\n"
"From the top, they can see the vast wasteland stretching out before them in both directions. To their surprise, the landscape beyond appears almost identical to the side they came from."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_wasteland_wall.tres
msgid "Investigate the construction."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_wasteland_wall.tres
msgid ""
"After examining the wall, one surveyor notices that in the few places where the white stone has cracked away, there appears to be a strangely smooth, dull grey layer.\n"
"\n"
"This metallic material is unlike any they have ever seen. When they attempt to scratch its surface, they find it yields easily under the blade."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_wasteland_wall.tres
msgid "Follow along the wall."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_wasteland_wall.tres
msgid ""
"The surveyors decide to walk along the wall looking for where it ends.\n"
"\n"
"Hours of walking later, there's still no end in sight, and the group decides to turn in a different direction."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_waterfall_cave.tres
msgid "The Hidden Recess"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_waterfall_cave.tres
msgid ""
"The day's trek has exhausted the survey team.\n"
"\n"
"As they stop by a swift waterfall to refill their water, a scout notices a dark recess behind the waterfall.\n"
"\n"
"The curtain of water may be concealing a cave, but reaching it would require crossing the slippery rocks."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_waterfall_cave.tres
msgid "Walk on the stones."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_waterfall_cave.tres
msgid ""
"Several scouts attempt to approach the waterfall, stepping carefully onto the stones.\n"
"\n"
"The result is chaos. One scout loses both her footing and her pack to the rushing water. Another topples face-first into the stream, thrashing wildly until his teammate pulls him out.\n"
"\n"
"The group quickly realizes the folly of this approach."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_waterfall_cave.tres
msgid "Look for another entrance."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_waterfall_cave.tres
msgid "Chance of <term:relic.firefly_lantern>"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_waterfall_cave.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts climb the cliffs looking for another entrance to the cave. \n"
"\n"
"At the top they find an opening, partially blocked by a fallen tree trunk.\n"
"\n"
"Working together, the scouts heave the tree aside, just enough to squeeze into the opening .\n"
"\n"
"They find the cave filled with fireflies, their lights casting a pale green glow on the walls."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_waterfall_cave.tres
msgid "Swing in."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_waterfall_cave.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts tie a rope to tree branches hanging over the fall, and send a surveyor swinging through the curtain of rushing water.\n"
"\n"
"Safely inside the cave, he looks on in wonder. Fireflies fill the half-darkness, their light casting a pale green glow on the walls.\n"
"\n"
"Unsure whether the others will believe him, the scout lures one of the insects into an unfolded lantern before leaving through a small opening in the rock.\n"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_waterfall_cave.tres
msgid "Leave it unexplored."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_waterfall_cave.tres
msgid ""
"The group, tired from hiking all day, decides to move on.\n"
"\n"
"Night falls as they leave the waterfall behind.\n"
"\n"
"Looking back, they can see it glowing in the dark."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_water_goat.tres
msgid "The Goat"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_water_goat.tres
msgid ""
"As the scouts round a narrow bend in the trail, they come face to face with a shaggy goat.\n"
"\n"
"It startles and jumps away, its hooves scraping against loose stones. With a sharp bleat, it falls into the water below.\n"
"\n"
"The scouts look down, and though the animal should be able to swim, it seems to be panicking."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_water_goat.tres
msgid "Jump in."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: description
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_water_goat.tres
msgid "Gain <term:bonus.harmony> or lose <term:bonus.safety>"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_water_goat.tres
msgid ""
"A strong scout jumps into the waves below.\n"
"\n"
"He tries to guide the goat toward land, and it finally calms down and swims back. As soon as its hooves find purchase, it runs off."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_water_goat.tres
msgid "Pray."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_water_goat.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts bow their heads and ask the Enlightened One to assist the drowning animal.\n"
"\n"
"By the time they raise their heads, the goat has managed to calm down and swim back to shore."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_water_goat.tres
msgid "Race to the beach."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_water_goat.tres
msgid ""
"The group rushes to the beach, watching the goat struggle in the water.\n"
"\n"
"Three of the scouts swim to the animal and guide it safely to shore."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_water_goat.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts decide to let nature take its course, and walk away.\n"
"\n"
"They hear the goat struggling and splashing in the waves below.\n"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_winter_wonderland.tres
msgid "Playing in the Snow"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_winter_wonderland.tres
msgid ""
"Waking up before dawn high in the mountains, the explorers blink as they look at the landscape stretching before them.\n"
"\n"
"The entire mountain range has gained a thick blanket of fresh snow overnight.\n"
"\n"
"Standing in front of the campfire, they warm their hands and discuss how to spend the morning."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_winter_wonderland.tres
msgid "Throw snowballs."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_winter_wonderland.tres
msgid ""
"A scout cups some snow into her hands and hurls it towards one of her teammates.\n"
"\n"
"The retaliation is swift, and others are quick to join in.\n"
"\n"
"Soon the entire survey team is covered in snow as their laughter echoes through the valley below."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_winter_wonderland.tres
msgid "Go sledding."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_winter_wonderland.tres
msgid ""
"The scouts gather their straw hats.\n"
"\n"
"Each of them plants themself in the center of their hat and slides down the little icy slope leading down to their camp.\n"
"\n"
"A few crash into trees or each other, but it isn't enough to stop them from going back up the slope again and again."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_winter_wonderland.tres
msgid "Make a snow fort."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: outcome_text
#: stage/survey/episodes/episode_winter_wonderland.tres
msgid ""
"One of the surveyors suggests that they build a little fort out of the snow.\n"
"\n"
"\"It's practice for when we need emergency shelter,\" she declares. The others are happy enough with this excuse, and set to work.\n"
"\n"
"By noon they have transformed a pile of snow into a miniature castle, complete with several tunnels and a central hall.\n"
"\n"
"It is surprisingly cozy."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: label
