#: tutorial/starter/starter_tutorial.gd:127
msgid "Drag <term:glyph>s to <term:aspect_slot>s with a matching <term:aspect> to activate the <term:spot_upgrade>."
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/starter/starter_tutorial.gd:130
msgid "A <term:glyph> with multiple <term_lower:aspect>s can <term_lower:fill> any matching <term_lower:aspect_slot>, but a single glyph can only fill one slot."
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/starter/starter_tutorial.gd:144
msgid "You can <term_lower:redraw> your <term_lower:hand> once."
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/starter/starter_tutorial.gd:165
msgid ""
"<term:glyph>s have <term_lower:card_ability>s. Hover the <term_lower:glyph> to learn more.\n"
"\n"
"%s the <term_lower:glyph> to cast all of its <term_lower:card_ability>s."
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/starter/starter_tutorial.gd:186
msgid "You are now ready to start your first <term:run>!"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: line_start
#: tutorial/starter/starter_tutorial.tscn
msgid ""
"Oh Enlightened One, your prophecy told us that after the Shattering, we are to put the shards back together, one expedition at a time.\n"
"\n"
"      Let's begin, then, by rebuilding a torii gate."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: line_redraw
#: tutorial/starter/starter_tutorial.tscn
msgid ""
"We're done with building, but we'll need to redouble our efforts to open the gateway.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"      Guide us with a sign, oh Enlightened One!"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: line_open
#: tutorial/starter/starter_tutorial.tscn
msgid ""
"We are ready to resume the preparations now.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"      Let's open the gate to a new shard!"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: line_opened
#: tutorial/starter/starter_tutorial.tscn
msgid ""
"Excellent! We'll need enough people to found a settlement when we get to the shard.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"      Let's gather everyone at the gate!"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: line_gathered
#: tutorial/starter/starter_tutorial.tscn
msgid ""
"We are exhausted, but you are always with us, oh Enlightened One. Grant us one last bit of will to embark!\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"      Let's invoke this glyph's blessing!"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: tutorial/starter/starter_tutorial.tscn
msgid "Build Torii Gate"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: tutorial/starter/starter_tutorial.tscn
msgid "Open Gateway"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Property: title
#: tutorial/starter/starter_tutorial.tscn
msgid "Gather Expedition"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/harmonization/tutorial_capital_location.gd:21
msgid "Our first task is to choose a location for the <term_lower:capital>."
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/harmonization/tutorial_capital_provisions.gd:31
msgid ""
"\n"
"If you have accumulated enough of a given <term_lower:bonus>, you can <term_lower:fill> these <term_lower:aspect_slot>s to have the <term:capital> provide it automatically.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/harmonization/tutorial_carryover.gd:21
msgid ""
"\n"
"The state of all your <term_lower:settlement>s and the <term:capital> carries over to the next <term_lower:season>.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/harmonization/tutorial_connection.gd:32
msgid ""
"\n"
"Another way to <term_lower:satisfy_lack> a <term_lower:lack> is to <term_lower:connect_settlement> <term_lower:settlement>s to the <term:capital>.\n"
"\n"
"This settlement provides %s. If you <term_lower:connect_settlement> it to the <term:capital>, %s will be shared with all other connected <term_lower:settlement>s.\n"
"\n"
"If you then <term_lower:connect_settlement> a <term_lower:settlement> that has a %s <term_lower:lack>, that <term_lower:lack> will be <term_lower:satisfy_lack>ed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/harmonization/tutorial_craft_connection.gd:31
msgid ""
"\n"
"<term:connect_settlement>ing <term_lower:settlement>s requires <term:aspect.connection> <term_lower:aspect>.\n"
"\n"
"If you don't have enough, <term_lower:fill> these <term_lower:aspect_slot>s to gain a random <term_lower:glyph> with <term:aspect.connection> <term_lower:aspect>.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/harmonization/tutorial_harmonization_end.gd:22
msgid ""
"\n"
"Each <term:lack> left un<term_lower:satisfy_lack>ed by the end of the <term:harmonization> will reduce your <term:inspiration> by %d points.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/harmonization/tutorial_harmonization_start.gd:26
msgid ""
"\n"
"Now, at the end of the <term_lower:season>, it's time to establish the <term:capital>.\n"
"\n"
"This final step is called the <term:harmonization>.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/harmonization/tutorial_lacks.gd:33
msgid ""
"\n"
"The goal of <term:harmonization> is to <term_lower:satisfy_lack> <term_lower:settlement> <term_lower:lack>s.\n"
"\n"
"For example, this <term_lower:settlement> has a <term_lower:lack> of %s.\n"
"\n"
"To <term_lower:satisfy_lack> a <term_lower:lack>, <term_lower:fill> these <term_lower:aspect_slot>s.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/harmonization/tutorial_settlements.gd:23
msgid ""
"\n"
"These are your <term:settlement>s. Clicking on one of these will take you to it on the map. You can also zoom and pan the map freely during <term:harmonization>!\n"
"\n"
"Each <term_lower:settlement> has a [b]<term_lower:lack>[/b] of one type of <term_lower:bonus>.\n"
"\n"
"For example, your [b]%s[/b] settlement has a <term_lower:lack> of %s.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/hub/tutorial_capital_skills.gd:27
msgid ""
"\n"
"You can find alternative ways to complete the <term:harmonization>  in the <term:capital> <term_lower:skill> tree!\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/hub/tutorial_craft_cards.gd:47
msgid ""
"\n"
"This list contains all the <term_lower:glyph>s you have encountered during your <term_lower:run>s.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/hub/tutorial_craft_strokes.gd:23
msgid ""
"\n"
"<term:glyph>s require <term_lower:stroke>s to be <term_lower:craft>d.\n"
"\n"
"These are acquired when you <term_lower:salvage> <term_lower:glyph>s at the end of each completed <term_lower:season>.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/hub/tutorial_debate.gd:26
msgid ""
"\n"
"The Scribe and the Historian will now hold speeches to sway the people's opinion.\n"
"\n"
"To do so, %s Hold Speech and choose a topic.\n"
"\n"
"This topic choice determines who will give the speech and how the public opinion is affected.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/hub/tutorial_enable_japanese.gd:29
msgid "This game has minigames for practicing Japanese."
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/hub/tutorial_enable_japanese.gd:30
msgid " They are completely optional and assume basic familiarity with the language."
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/hub/tutorial_enable_japanese.gd:32
msgid "Would you like to enable learning minigames now?"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/hub/tutorial_enable_japanese.gd:34
msgid "You can always change learning options in the game settings."
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/hub/tutorial_enable_japanese.gd:36
msgid "Are You Learning Japanese?"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/hub/tutorial_enable_japanese.gd:36
msgid "Enable Minigames"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/hub/tutorial_explorer_trips.gd:27
msgid ""
"\n"
"The Explorer can now visit previously settled shards.\n"
"\n"
"Such trips may discover historical developments, reveal new <term_lower:skill>s, or advance the story.\n"
"\n"
"It will take one <term_lower:season> of an <term_lower:run> to visit one shard.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/hub/tutorial_hub_gate.gd:19
msgid "You can use this gate to launch a new <term_lower:run>."
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/hub/tutorial_hub_intro.gd:22
msgid ""
"\n"
"This is the <term:hub> from which we launch our <term_lower:run>s.\n"
"\n"
"It will continue to evolve as we resettle the shards.\n"
"\n"
"You can zoom with the %s and pan with %s.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/hub/tutorial_insights.gd:18
msgid ""
"\n"
"These are your <term:insight> points.\n"
"\n"
"<term:insight>s are gained during <term_lower:run>s, with each established <term_lower:settlement>.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/hub/tutorial_museum.gd:20
msgid ""
"\n"
"This museum keeps track of everything you've encountered during your <term_lower:run>s.\n"
"\n"
"It also contains hints about things you're yet to discover.\n"
"\n"
"Visit it to learn more, or %s the exhibits to customize what they display.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/hub/tutorial_practice_minigame.gd:28
msgid ""
"\n"
"This is the scroll on which the original survivors had written their names.\n"
"\n"
"Nowadays novices read it to practice their glyphs.\n"
"\n"
"%s on the scroll to start a kanji practice minigame!\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/hub/tutorial_settler_quests.gd:48
msgid ""
"\n"
"You can now accept <term:settler_quest>s.\n"
"\n"
"Settlers around the <term:hub> are looking to join expeditions with specific plans.\n"
"\n"
"If you accept them into the next expedition, they will offer a task that grants a reward.\n"
"\n"
"Settler quests only apply to the next <term_lower:run>, and add a difficulty modifier, but increase <term:insight> gains.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/hub/tutorial_shard_pinning.gd:35
msgid ""
"\n"
"This button pins the <term_lower:shard_type> to your quest list.\n"
"\n"
"If you start an <term_lower:run> with a culture pinned, settlers will try to pick a shard appropriate for fulfilling the requirements.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/hub/tutorial_shard_types.gd:26
msgid ""
"\n"
"This is a list of potential <term_lower:shard_type>s.\n"
"\n"
"Some are part of the main story, but most can arise on any shard under certain conditions.\n"
"\n"
"Over time, each <term_lower:shard_type> will develop its own history.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/hub/tutorial_shard_type_reqs.gd:35
msgid ""
"\n"
"These are the conditions under which the selected <term_lower:shard_type> will arise.\n"
"\n"
"If they are fulfilled during an <term_lower:run>, that shard will develop this culture.\n"
"\n"
"If the conditions for multiple <term_lower:shard_type>s are fulfilled in the same <term_lower:run>, only one culture will be chosen.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/hub/tutorial_skills.gd:19
msgid ""
"\n"
"You can spend <term:insight>s here to permanently unlock new <term:skill>s.\n"
"\n"
"Skill can provide numerical bonuses or unlock completely new gameplay systems.\n"
"\n"
"More <term_lower:skill>s will become available as you continue the story.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/hub/tutorial_skill_quest.gd:33
msgid ""
"\n"
"This is the [b]%s[/b] skill.\n"
"\n"
"It will allow you to <term_lower:craft> <term_lower:glyph>s to start with on future <term_lower:run>s.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/hub/tutorial_studio.gd:26
msgid ""
"\n"
"You can <term_lower:craft> new <term_lower:glyph>s here.\n"
"\n"
"<term:craft>d <term_lower:glyph>s can be chosen as your <term:signature_card>.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/hub/tutorial_tower.gd:25
msgid ""
"\n"
"You can view previously resettled <term:world_shard>s here, as well as explore potential <term_lower:shard_type>s.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/misc/tutorial_add_cards.gd:22
msgid ""
"\n"
"\tThe <term_lower:glyph>s you choose here stay for the rest of the <term_lower:run>.\n"
"\n"
"Ones with more <term_lower:aspect>s are usually better, but sometimes the <term_lower:card_ability>s matter more.\n"
"\n"
"Pay attention to your <term_lower:aspect> counts, as keeping them balanced is important. Sometimes removing a weak <term_lower:glyph> is the best choice.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/misc/tutorial_art_credits.gd:30
msgid ""
"\n"
"These icons indicate usages of historical artwork.\n"
"\n"
"%s on one to open the Art Viewer, which contains uncropped, high-resolution versions of the art, as well as relevant historical details.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/misc/tutorial_art_viewer_run.gd:18
msgid ""
"\n"
"This is the Art Viewer.\n"
"\n"
"It contains details of all historical artwork used in the game, as well as uncropped high resolution images.\n"
"\n"
"If you are unfamiliar with Japanese art, a brief introduction is available in the Intro tab.\n"
"\n"
"Most pages have a link icon in the title leading to a web resource with more information.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/misc/tutorial_aspect_balance.gd:57
msgid ""
"\n"
"Your <term_lower:card_deck> has {advanced_count} {advanced_type} <term_lower:aspect>s, and {basic_count} {basic_type} <term_lower:aspect>s.\n"
"\n"
"{basic_type} is a <term:basic_aspect>, which is crucial for starting initial <term_lower:spot_upgrade>s.\n"
"\n"
"Having too many <term:advanced_aspect>s may leave you unable to activate desired <term_lower:spot_upgrade>s before redrawing.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/misc/tutorial_card_removal.gd:26
msgid ""
"\n"
"Your <term_lower:card_deck> has %d <term_lower:glyph>s.\n"
"\n"
"Having too many <term_lower:glyph>s can make it harder to draw the really good ones.\n"
"\n"
"Consider removing <term_lower:glyph>s that have only one <term_lower:aspect>.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/misc/tutorial_landmark.gd:41
msgid ""
"\n"
"You have unlocked a <term:shop>. These have various uses, such as getting rare <term_lower:glyph>s or restoring <term:inspiration>. You can use each <term_lower:shop> once between <term_lower:stage>s.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/misc/tutorial_legacy_event.gd:22
msgid ""
"\n"
"You have encountered a Legacy Event.\n"
"\n"
"Choices made during such events have long-term story consequences!\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/misc/tutorial_negative_bonuses.gd:27
msgid ""
"\n"
"The shard is now experiencing a global shortage of %s. For each type of <term_lower:bonus> that is\n"
"below zero at the end of a <term_lower:foray>, the expedition will lose %d <term:inspiration>.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/misc/tutorial_retry.gd:23
msgid ""
"\n"
"If you find yourself wondering if you could've played this <term_lower:stage> differently, you can try restarting it from the pause menu (%s).\n"
"\n"
"It's for you to decide if that counts as cheating.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/misc/tutorial_salvage.gd:27
msgid ""
"\n"
"At the end of each <term_lower:season>, you can select a <term_lower:glyph> to <term_lower:salvage>. This will remove it from your <term_lower:card_deck> and add its <term_lower:stroke>s to your inventory for <term_lower:craft>ing new <term_lower:glyph>.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/misc/tutorial_survey.gd:23
msgid ""
"\n"
"After 3 <term_lower:foray>s, a <term_lower:survey> team will go out to map a region of the shard.\n"
"\n"
"They will have to deal with a variety of <term_lower:encounter>s, both challenges and opportunities.\n"
"\n"
"You can choose to end their trip at any time, but the further you advance, the more of the map you will reveal.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/season/tutorial_season.gd:27
msgid ""
"\n"
"After 6 <term_lower:foray>s, the <term:season> will end and you will establish the <term:capital> starting a <term:harmonization>.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/stage/tutorial_companion.gd:22
msgid ""
"\n"
"This is your <term:companion>.\n"
"\n"
"If you <term_lower:fill> the companion's <term_lower:aspect_slot>s, you will activate their ability.\n"
"\n"
"Every companion has a unique ability, with different slots and benefits.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/stage/tutorial_companion_events.gd:21
msgid ""
"\n"
"<term:spot_upgrade>s outlined with green glimmers will trigger <term_lower:event>s that may start or continue a quest to unlock a <term:companion>, but only if your choice aligns with the companion's wellbeing and cultural symbolism.\n"
"\n"
"If it doesn't, you'll get to try again on a different <term_lower:run>.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/stage/tutorial_events.gd:21
msgid ""
"\n"
"<term:spot_upgrade>s outlined with glimmers will trigger <term_lower:event>s.\n"
"\n"
"<term:event>s are little vignettes that can grant powerful <term_lower:glyph>s and <term_lower:relic>s, but could also lead to negative outcomes.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/stage/tutorial_haunting.gd:21
msgid ""
"\n"
"You have encountered your first <term:haunting>!\n"
"\n"
"These spirits will pose extra challenges during <term_lower:foray>s from now on.\n"
"\n"
"Hauntings connected to a <term_lower:spot> by a red thread affect only that <term_lower:spot>, while unconnected hauntings affect the whole settlement.\n"
"\n"
"You can pacify these spirits by <term_lower:fill>ing their associated <term_lower:aspect_slot>s.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/stage/tutorial_haunting_harmonization.gd:27
msgid ""
"\n"
"Starting from <term:season> %d, <term_lower:settlement>s can have <term_lower:haunting>s during <term:harmonization>.\n"
"\n"
"Most of these will trigger even on actions unrelated to the <term_lower:settlement> they appear in.\n"
"\n"
"All <term_lower:haunting>s also appear at the top of the screen for reference.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/stage/tutorial_haunting_scaling.gd:22
msgid ""
"\n"
"This <term:haunting> has extra <term_lower:aspect_slot>s.\n"
"\n"
"<term:haunting>s increase in difficulty as you gain more <term_lower:bonus>s. This particular <term_lower:haunting> gains an extra slot for every %d %s the shard produces.\n"
"\n"
"The chance of encountering any <term_lower:haunting> in a <term_lower:spot> increases by 1%% for every %d of total shard yields.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/stage/tutorial_negative_cards.gd:25
msgid ""
"\n"
"You have encountered a <term:negative_glyph>.\n"
"\n"
"Any such <term_lower:glyph>s remaining in your <term_lower:hand> at the end of a <term_lower:turn> are <term_lower:cast_card> automatically.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/stage/tutorial_spots_scroller.gd:27
msgid ""
"\n"
"There are more <term_lower:spot>s than can fit on one screen in this <term_lower:foray>.\n"
"\n"
"You can scroll this list using the %s.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tutorial/steps/stage/tutorial_universal_slots.gd:32
msgid ""
"\n"
"This is a universal <term_lower:aspect_slot>.\n"
"\n"
"It will accept any kind of <term_lower:aspect>.\n"
msgstr ""

#: utils/bug_reporter/bug_reporter.gd:34
